COLLDATA("darimi","en",[[1,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will a person be held accountable for what they did in pre-Islamic times?\" He replied, \"Whoever does good in Islam will not be held accountable for what they did in pre-Islamic times, and whoever does evil in Islam will be held accountable for both the past and present.\""],[2,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we were people of ignorance and idol worship. We used to kill children. I had a daughter of mine, and when she could respond—she was happy when I called her—I called her one day and she followed me. I went on until I came to a well belonging to my family, not far away. I took her by the hand and threw her into the well. The last thing I knew of her was her saying, ‘O my father, O my father.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept until tears overflowed from his eyes. A man from among those sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “You have made the Messenger of Allah ﷺ grieve.” He said to him, “Stop, for he is asking about what concerns him.” Then he said to him, “Repeat your story to me.” He repeated it, and he wept until tears overflowed from his eyes onto his beard. Then he said to him, “Allah has lifted from the ignorance what they did, so start your work anew.”"],[3,"That his family sent with him a bowl containing butter and milk to their gods. He said, “It prevented me from eating the butter out of fear of them.” He said, “Then a dog came, ate the butter, drank the milk, and then urinated on the idol—and it was Isāf and Nāʾilah.”"],[4,"“In the time of ignorance, when we found a good stone, we would worship it. If we did not find a stone, we would gather a heap of sand, then bring a choice she-camel, make her stand over it with her legs spread, and milk her over the heap until we had watered it. Then we would worship that heap as long as we stayed in that place.”"],[5,"We find a written inscription that says: Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He is not harsh, nor rude, nor does he shout in the markets. He does not repay evil with evil, but forgives and pardons. His followers are those who praise Allah the Almighty in every valley and thank Him in every situation. They gather together and perform ablution over their extremities. Their caller calls out in the air, their lines in battle are equal to their lines in prayer. They are no different during the night than the buzzing of bees, and their place of birth is Makkah, their migration is to Ṭaybah, and their rule is in Shām.\""],[6,"“Indeed we find the description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ‘We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of good tidings, and a warner, and a protection for the unlettered. You are My servant and My messenger. I have named him the one who trusts. He is not harsh, nor coarse, nor loud in the markets. He does not repay evil with evil, but he pardons and overlooks. And I will not take him until he has straightened the crooked religion by bearing witness that there is no god but Allah. Through him We open blind eyes, deaf ears, and covered hearts.’”"],[7,"In the first line: “Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, My chosen servant. Not harsh, nor coarse, nor loud in the markets. He does not repay evil with evil, but he pardons and forgives. His birthplace is Makkah, his migration is to Taybah, and his dominion is in Syria.” And in the second line: “Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah. His community are the praisers: they praise Allah in ease and hardship, they praise Allah in every station, and they magnify Him on every height. They are watchers of the sun. They perform the prayer when its time comes, even if they were on the top of a rubbish heap. They tie their lower garments around their waists, they wash their limbs, and their voices in the night are in the expanse of the sky like the voices of bees.”"],[8,"That he asked Kaʿb al-Aḥbār, “How do you find the description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Torah?” Kaʿb said, “We find him as Muhammad son of ʿAbdullāh: he will be born in Makkah, migrate to Ṭābah, and his dominion will be in Syria. He is not obscene, nor loud in the markets. He does not repay evil with evil, but he pardons and forgives. His community are the praisers: they praise Allah in every ease, and they magnify Allah on every highland. They wash their limbs, tie their lower garments around their waists, and form rows in their prayer just as they form rows in battle. Their hum in their mosques is like the hum of bees. Their caller is heard in the expanse of the sky.”"],[9,"“A messenger has come to you, not weak, nor lazy, to revive covered hearts, open blind eyes, and make deaf ears hear, and to straighten the crooked way until it is said: there is no god but Allah alone.”"],[10,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ had a need from him, so he walked with him until he entered. He said: One of his legs was inside the house and the other outside, as if he were conversing privately. He turned and said, “Do you know whom I was speaking to? This is an angel I have never seen before this day. He asked his Lord permission to greet me.” He said, “We have given you—or sent down—the Qurʾan as a decisive criterion, tranquility as patience, and discernment as connection.”"],[11,"The Prophet ﷺ was approached and it was said to him: “Let your eye sleep, let your ear hear, and let your heart understand.” He said, “My eyes slept, my ears heard, and my heart understood.” He said, “It was said to me: A master built a house, prepared a feast, and sent an inviter. Whoever answered the inviter entered the house, ate from the feast, and the master was pleased with him. Whoever did not answer the inviter did not enter the house, did not eat from the feast, and the master was angry with him.” He said, “Allah is the master, Muhammad is the inviter, the house is Islam, and the feast is Paradise.”"],[12,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to al-Batha with Ibn Masud. He seated him and drew a line around him, then said, \"Do not leave; men will come up to you, so do not speak to them, for they will not speak to you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then went on to wherever he wished, and they began coming up to the line without crossing it, then departing toward the Prophet ﷺ. When it was near the end of the night, he came to me and rested his head on my thigh. When he slept, he would breathe audibly in his sleep. While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting his head on my thigh, asleep, men came to me as though they were camels, wearing white garments—Allah knows best how beautiful they were—until one group of them sat by his head and another group by his feet. They said among themselves, \"We have never seen a servant given the like of what this Prophet ﷺ has been given. His two eyes sleep, but his heart remains awake. Set forth a parable for him: a master built a palace, then prepared a banquet and invited people to his food and drink.\" Then they rose up and departed. At that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up and said, \"Do you know who these were?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"They were the angels.\" He said, \"Do you know what parable they set forth?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"The Most Merciful built Paradise and invited His servants to it. Whoever responds to Him enters His Paradise, and whoever does not respond, He punishes and chastises him.\""],[13,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “How was the beginning of your affair, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “My caretaker was from Banū Saʿd b. Bakr. I went out with a son of hers among some lambs of ours, and we did not take any provisions with us. I said, ‘O my brother, go and bring us some provisions from our mother.’ My brother went, and I stayed with the lambs. Then two white birds came, like two eagles. One of them said to the other, ‘Is it he?’ The other said, ‘Yes.’ They came hastening to me, took me, and laid me on my back. They split my belly, then took out my heart and split it. They removed from it two black clots. One of them said to the other, ‘Bring me snow water,’ and he washed my inside with it. Then he said, ‘Bring me cool water,’ and he washed my heart with it. Then he said, ‘Bring me tranquility,’ and he sprinkled it in my heart. Then one of them said to the other, ‘Sew it up,’ and he sewed it up and sealed it with the seal of prophethood. Then one of them said to the other, ‘Put him in one scale and put a thousand of his community in the other scale.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Then I looked at the thousand above me, fearing that some of them might fall on me. He said, ‘If his community were weighed against him, he would outweigh them.’ Then they left and left me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I was extremely terrified. Then I went to my mother and told her what I had encountered. She feared that something had confused me, so she said, ‘I seek refuge for you in Allah.’ She saddled a camel of hers, placed me on the saddle, and rode behind me until we reached my mother. She said, ‘I have fulfilled my trust and my duty,’ and told her what I had encountered. That did not alarm her, and she said, ‘When he came out of me, I saw something—meaning a light—that illuminated the palaces of Syria.’”"],[14,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, how did you know that you were a prophet until you became certain?” He said, “O Abū Dharr, two angels came to me while I was in a part of the valley of Makkah. One of them fell to the ground, and the other was between heaven and earth. One of them said to the other, ‘Is it he?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Weigh him against a man.’ I was weighed against him, and I outweighed him. Then he said, ‘Weigh him against ten.’ I was weighed against them, and I outweighed them. Then he said, ‘Weigh him against a hundred.’ I was weighed against them, and I outweighed them. Then he said, ‘Weigh him against a thousand.’ I was weighed against them, and I outweighed them. It was as if I could see them scattering over me from the lightness of the scale.” He said, “Then one of them said to the other, ‘If you weighed him against his community, he would outweigh them.’”"],[15,"The Prophet ﷺ used to call them: “O people, I am only a mercy that is guided.”"],[16,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when a bedouin came. When he drew near, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Where do you want [to go]?\" He said, \"To my family.\" He said, \"Would you like [something] good?\" He said, \"What is it?\" He said, \"That you bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" He said, \"Who will bear witness to what you say?\" He said, \"This salamah tree.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it while it was on the bank of the valley, and it came plowing through the earth until it stood before him. He asked it to testify three times, and it testified three times that he was as he said. Then it returned to its place of growth, and the bedouin returned to his people and said, \"If they follow me, I will bring them to you; otherwise I will return and stay with you.\""],[17,"\"I went on a journey with the Prophet ﷺ, and he used to not relieve himself until he disappeared, so he couldn't be seen. We descended into an area without trees or landmarks. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Jabir, make water in your waterskin and then set out with us.' So we set out until we couldn't see anything, and suddenly there were two trees with a four-arm gap between them. He said, 'O Jabir, go to that tree and say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to give me shade for my companions and me.'' So I did, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat behind us. Then we returned to our place, and we rode with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was between us, as if birds were shading us. A woman came with a child and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the devil takes my son every day three times.' He took the child and placed him between himself and the front of the camel saddle, and he said, 'Get away, O enemy of Allah! I am the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, get away, O enemy of Allah! I am the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' three times. Then he handed the child back to her. When we finished our journey and passed by that place, the woman came to us with her child and two rams that were pulling them. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, accept my gift. I swear by the One who sent you with the truth, he has not returned to that condition since you treated him.' He said, 'Take one and return the other.' Then we continued and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was between us, as if birds were shading us. Suddenly, a camel called out until it knelt down between two rocks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and said, 'Who is the owner of this camel?' Some young Ansar men said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it belongs to us.' He asked, 'What is its condition?' They replied, 'We have been tending it for twenty years, and it has a cataract. We wanted to slaughter it and divide it amongst ourselves, but it escaped from us.' He said, 'Sell it to me.' They said, 'No, rather it is for you, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'No, treat it well until its time comes.' The Muslims said at that time, 'O Messenger of Allah, we should be the ones to prostrate to you, not animals.' He said, 'It is not appropriate for anything to prostrate to anything else, even if it were so, women would be prostrating to their husbands.'\""],[18,"We accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached a wall in the Tribe of Najjar. There was a camel there that no one could enter the wall except by pulling it aside. We mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ , so he came and called it. It came and kneeled down in front of him until he patted its head. Then he said, \"Bring me a rope.\" He tied it and handed it over to its owner. Then he turned and said, \"There is no one from the heavens to the Earth who does not know that I am the Messenger of Allah, except for the rebellious among the jinn and humans.\""],[19,"A woman brought her son to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my son has madness, and it seizes him at our lunch and dinner, and he defiles us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped his chest and supplicated, and he vomited, and something like a black puppy came out of his belly and ran off."],[20,"\"I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me before I was sent; indeed I know it now.\""],[21,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in Makkah, and we went out with him to some of its outskirts. We passed between mountains and trees, and we did not pass by any tree or mountain but that it said, \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[22,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Fajr prayer when suddenly he saw a pack of nearly a hundred wolves approaching. The wolves' fangs were bared and their eyes were red with hunger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"Will you give up some of your food to satisfy them and ensure safety for everything else?\" They complained about their need to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he said, \"Give them permission.\" So they allowed the wolves to come forward, and the wolves left while howling."],[23,"Gabriel came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting in distress, with blood on him from the actions of the people of Mecca from the Quraysh. Gabriel, peace be upon him, said, \"O Messenger of Allah, would you like me to show you a sign?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he looked at a tree behind him and said, \"Call it.\" So he called it and it came and stood in front of him. He said, \"Turn it back.\" So he commanded it and it returned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, \"That is enough for me, that is enough for me.\""],[24,"A man from Banu Amir came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Shall I show you a sign?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Go and call that palm tree.\" So he called it, and it came jumping until it stood before him. He said, \"Tell it to return.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to it, \"Return,\" and it returned until it went back to its place. He said, \"O Banu Amir, I have never seen a man as skilled in magic as him today.\""],[25,"The Prophet ﷺ called Bilal, and Bilal sought water then came and said, \"No, by Allah, I did not find water.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Is there a waterskin?\" So he brought him a waterskin, and he spread his palms in it, and a spring gushed forth beneath his hands. Ibn Mas'ud drank, and others performed ablution."],[26,"We raided or traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we were that day some two hundred and ten men. The prayer time came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Is there any water for purification among the people?\" A man came running with a small vessel containing a little water; the people had no water other than it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ poured it into a bowl, then performed ablution and did it well. Then he left and left the bowl, and the people crowded around that bowl and said, \"Wipe yourselves, wipe yourselves.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Gently,\" when he heard them saying that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his palm in the water and the bowl, and said, \"In the name of Allah.\" Then he said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly.\" By the One who tested me with my sight, I saw the springs—springs of water—coming out from between his fingers, and he did not lift them until they all had performed ablution."],[27,"We were afflicted with thirst, and we were distressed, and we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He placed his hand in a basin, and it began to gush as if springs were from between his fingers, and he said, \"Mention the name of Allah.\" So we drank until we were satisfied, and it sufficed us."],[28,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of thirst. He called for a large cup, and water was poured into it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand in it. He said, \"I began to look at the water springing forth as springs from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people were drawing water until all the people had drawn.\""],[29,"Abdullah heard of an earthquake, and he said, \"We, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, used to count the signs as blessings, but you count them as intimidation. While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and had no water with us, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Seek someone who has extra water.' Water was brought, and he poured it into a vessel, then placed his palm in it, and the water began to come out from between his fingers. Then he said, 'Come to the blessed purification; blessing is from Allah, exalted is He.' So we drank.\" Abdullah said, \"We used to hear the glorification of food while it was being eaten.\""],[30,"The earth quaked during the time of Abdullah, and he was told of that, and he said, \"We, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, used to see the signs as blessings, but you see them as intimidation.\""],[31,"He used to deliver the sermon leaning on a palm trunk. When the pulpit was made, the trunk yearned until he came to it and wiped it."],[32,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he delivered a sermon, would stand and prolong the standing, and it was hard for him to stand for so long. A trunk of a palm tree was brought, a hole was dug for it, and it was set upright beside him for the Prophet ﷺ. Whenever the Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon and the standing became long for him, he would lean on it and support himself against it. A man who had come to Madinah saw him standing beside that trunk and said to the people near him, 'If I knew that Muhammad would thank me for something that would give him comfort, I would make for him a seat on which he could stand; then if he wished he could sit as long as he liked, and if he wished he could stand.' This reached the Prophet ﷺ and he said, 'Bring him to me.' They brought him, and he ordered him to make for him these three or four steps that are now on the pulpit of Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ found relief in that. When the Prophet ﷺ left the trunk and went to this thing that had been made for him, the trunk grieved and yearned as a she-camel yearns when the Prophet ﷺ parted from it."],[33,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand by a trunk before the pulpit was made. When the pulpit was made, that trunk yearned until we heard its yearning, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on it and it became still."],[34,"The Prophet ﷺ used to deliver sermons by a piece of wood. When the pulpit was made and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on it, it yearned with the yearning of a ten-month pregnant she-camel, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on it and it became still."],[35,"The piece of wood yearned like the yearning of a she-camel whose young has been taken from her."],[36,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray facing a trunk and deliver sermons by it when the mosque was a trellis. One of his companions said to him, 'Shall we not make for you a trellis on which you can stand so that the people can see you on Friday and hear your sermon?' He said, 'Yes.' So three steps were made for him, the ones that are on the pulpit. When the pulpit was made and placed in the position where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed it, he said, 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came heading to the pulpit, he passed by it. When he moved beyond it, the trunk bellowed until it split and cracked. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to it and wiped it with his hand until it became still, then he went back to the pulpit.' He said, 'When he prayed, he prayed facing it. When the mosque was demolished, Ubayy b. Ka'b took that trunk, and it remained with him until it decayed and was eaten by termites and turned to dust.'"],[37,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver sermons next to a trunk. A Roman man came to him and said, 'Shall I make for you a pulpit to deliver sermons on?' He made for him this pulpit that you see. He said, 'When the Prophet ﷺ stood on it to deliver a sermon, the trunk yearned like the yearning of a she-camel for her young. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came down to it and embraced it, and it became still. Then he ordered that a hole be dug for it and it be buried.'"],[38,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, he used to lean his back against a piece of wood and speak to the people. They became numerous around him, and the Prophet ﷺ wanted to make them hear him, so he said, 'Build for me something to stand on.' They said, 'How, O Prophet of Allah?' He said, 'A trellis like the trellis of Musa.' When they built it for him, al-Hasan said, 'By Allah, the piece of wood yearned.' Al-Hasan said, 'Glory be to Allah! Are the hearts of people who heard this being sought?'"],[39,"He used to deliver sermons by a trunk before he took the pulpit. When he took the pulpit and moved to it, the trunk yearned, so he embraced it and it became still. He said, 'If I had not embraced it, it would have kept yearning until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[40,"The piece of wood by which he used to stand yearned, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to it and placed his hand on it, and it became still."],[41,"that the Prophet ﷺ used to stand on Fridays, leaning his back against the trunk of a palm tree in the mosque, and he would address the people. Once, a Roman came and said, \"Shall I not make something for you to sit on, so it would appear as if you are standing?\" So, he made a minbar (pulpit) with two steps, and the Prophet ﷺ sat on the third step.When the Prophet ﷺ sat on that pulpit, the palm tree trunk moaned like a grieving camel, to the extent that the mosque seemed to shake in sorrow [longing] for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pulpit and embraced the trunk, which continued to moan. The Prophet ﷺ consoled it until it became still. Then he said, \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if I had not embraced it, it would have continued moaning like this until the Day of Resurrection, out of longing for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Then he ordered that it be removed, and it was buried."],[42,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, did you hear it from him? I narrate it from you. Jabir said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the Trench, digging it. We remained three days without tasting food and could not get any. A hard patch appeared in the trench, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this hard patch has appeared in the trench.' We sprinkled water on it. The Prophet ﷺ stood up, his belly wrapped with a stone, and took the pickaxe or the shovel. Then he pronounced the name of Allah three times and struck, and it turned into a pile of loose sand. When I saw that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to go.' He said, 'So he permitted me. I went to my wife and said, 'May your mother lose you! I have seen something from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I cannot bear to keep secret. Do you have anything?' She said, 'I have a sa' of barley and a young she-goat.' He said, 'We ground the barley, slaughtered the goat, skinned it, put it in the pot, and kneaded the barley.' He said, 'Then I returned to the Prophet ﷺ and stayed for a while. Then I asked his permission a second time, and he permitted me. I came and found the dough ready, so I told her to bake, and I placed the pot on the stones.' Abu Abd al-Rahman said, 'It is only the athafi (stones), but this is how he said it.' Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'We have a little food. If you see fit, come with me, you and one man or two men with you.' He said, 'How much is it?' I said, 'A sa' of barley and a young she-goat.' He said, 'Return to your family and tell her not to remove the pot from the stones and not to take the bread out of the oven until I come.' Then he said to the people, 'Get up and go to the house of Jabir.' He said, 'I felt ashamed with a shame that only Allah knows, and I said to my wife, 'May your mother lose you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come to you with all his companions.' She said, 'Did the Prophet ﷺ ask you how much food there was?' I said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best. You told him what we had.' He said, 'Some of what I had been feeling left me, and I said, 'You have spoken the truth.' The Prophet ﷺ came and entered, then said to his companions, 'Do not crowd.' Then he invoked blessing over the oven and the pot. He said, 'We began taking bread from the oven and meat from the pot, crumbling and ladling for them. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Let seven or eight sit at each platter.' When they ate, we uncovered the oven and the pot, and they were fuller than before. We kept doing that; each time we opened the oven and uncovered the pot, we found them fuller than before, until all the Muslims were full and a portion of food remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, 'The people have been stricken with hunger, so eat and feed others.' We continued that day eating and feeding.' He said, 'And he informed me that they were eight hundred or he said three hundred.' Ayman said, 'I do not know which of the two.'"],[43,"Abu Talha commanded Umm Sulaim to prepare food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he could eat. Then Abu Talha sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I went to him and said, \"Abu Talha has sent me to you.\" He ordered the people to stand up, so they stood up and Abu Talha said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have made this food specifically for you.\" He replied, \"No, go ahead.\" So I left and the people left with me. Abu Talha said, \"Bring the food.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on it and invoked Allah's blessings upon it, then he said, \"Give permission to ten people.\" He gave them permission and said, \"Eat in the name of Allah.\" They ate until they were full and then they got up. He placed his hand on it as he had done previously, invoked Allah's blessings upon it, and then said, \"Give permission to ten people.\" He gave them permission and said, \"Eat in the name of Allah.\" They ate until they were full and then they got up. He did this with eighty men. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate, and the people of his household ate, and they left some food.\""],[44,"He cooked a pot for the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him, 'Hand me its foreleg,' and he liked the foreleg. He handed him the foreleg, then said, 'Hand me the foreleg,' and he handed him a foreleg. Then he said, 'Hand me the foreleg,' and I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, how many forelegs does a sheep have?' He said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had remained silent, I would have been given forelegs for as long as I called for them.'"],[45,"Narrated by Nubayh Al-Anzi, who narrated from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went out to confront the polytheists in battle. My father, Abdullah, said to me, 'O Jabir, it's best for you to stay with the people of Medina to keep an eye on the situation until we know how things turn out. By Allah, if it weren't for leaving behind my daughters, I would have preferred for them to be killed in front of me.'While I was with the people of Medina, my paternal aunt came to me with my father and my uncle to bury them in our graves. Suddenly, a man approached and announced, 'The Prophet (peace be upon him) commands you to return the corpses and bury them in their own beds where they were killed.' So we exhumed their bodies and buried them in their beds where they were killed.During the caliphate of Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, a man came to me and said, 'O Jabir ibn Abdullah, your father has stirred up some trouble regarding the dues owed to Muawiya.' Some of them set out to come to me, so I went to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my father was wounded on such-and-such a day, and he left a debt from dates. Some of his creditors are pressing me, and I would like you to help me with it so that perhaps some of his dates might be paid from it.'He replied, 'Yes, I will come to you, if Allah wills, close to midday.' He came later with his companions and sat down in the shade. The Prophet (peace be upon him) greeted us and sought permission to enter. After entering, he said, 'I had told my wife earlier not to disturb me when I came to you, and not to hurt the feelings of anyone in your house.' So she had spread a bed for him and put a pillow on it, and he lay down and slept.I said to my servant, 'Slaughter some camels from the camels for me and prepare them quickly before the Prophet (peace be upon him) wakes up.' We did not finish preparing the food until the Prophet (peace be upon him) woke up. I thought that he would order us to slaughter the camels again and that we would be rebuked, but he didn't ask for that. Instead, he asked, 'Bring me some water for ablution.' I brought it to him, and he performed ablution.When he wanted to wash his face, I thought he would go to a nearby water-skin, but he washed his face in the basin I had brought. Then he wiped over his head and said, 'Bring me the food you prepared.' We brought the food, and he placed his hand in the food saying, 'In the name of Allah, eat.' They all ate till they were fully satisfied, and the meat was more than before.He said, 'By Allah, for whom I have my life, I was about to leave with my companions but I thought that I should not go until I have eaten from the meal of my brothers.' He said, 'O Jabir! Invite all the people who are present with you.' So I invited them, and they ate of the meal and thanked Allah.The Prophet (peace be upon him) remained sitting with his companions, and they moved closer to him, and they surrounded him, and he said, 'I am your predecessor at the Lake-Fount (Kauthar) and some men amongst you will be brought to me, and when I will try to hand them some water, they will be pulled away from me by force whereupon I will say, 'O Lord, my companions!' Then the Almighty will say, 'You do not know what they did after you left, they introduced new things into the religion after you."],[46,"Indeed, Allah favored Muhammad ﷺ over the prophets (peace be upon them) and over the inhabitants of the heavens. They said, “O Ibn Abbas, by what did He favor him over the inhabitants of the heavens?” He said, “Allah said to the inhabitants of the heavens: {And whoever of them says, ‘I am a god besides Him,’ that one We will recompense with Hell. Thus We recompense the wrongdoers} [al-Anbiya 29] to the end of the verse, while Allah, Exalted is He, said to Muhammad ﷺ: {Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you what preceded of your sin and what will follow} [al-Fath 2].” They said, “Then what is his virtue over the prophets (peace be upon them)?” He said, “Allah, Exalted is He, said: {And We did not send any messenger except with the language of his people, so that he might make clear to them} [Ibrahim 4] to the end of the verse, while Allah, Exalted is He, said to Muhammad ﷺ: {And We have not sent you except comprehensively to all people} [Saba 28]. So He sent him to the jinn and mankind.”"],[47,"Some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ sat waiting for him. He came out until when he drew near them, he heard them discussing, and he listened to their talk. One of them said, “It is amazing that Allah took from His creation a close friend, for Ibrahim is His close friend.” Another said, “What is more amazing than {And Allah spoke to Musa directly} [al-Nisa 164]?” Another said, “Isa is the word of Allah and His spirit.” Another said, “And Adam was chosen by Allah.” He came out to them, greeted them, and said, “I have heard your words and your amazement that Ibrahim is the close friend of Allah, and he is indeed so; that Musa is His confidant, and he is indeed so; that Isa is His spirit and His word, and he is indeed so; and that Adam was chosen by Allah, Exalted is He, and he is indeed so. Indeed, I am the beloved of Allah, and no boast. I am the bearer of the banner of praise on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I am the first to move the ring of Paradise, and no boast. Allah will open it and admit me into it, and with me will be the poor among the believers, and no boast. I am the most honorable of the first and the last in the sight of Allah, and no boast.”"],[48,"“I am the first of them to come out, and I am their leader when they come as delegations. I am their speaker when they fall silent. I am their intercessor when they are held back. I am their bearer of good tidings when they despair. Honor and the keys that day are in my hand. I am the most honorable of the children of Adam in the sight of my Lord. A thousand servants will go around me, as if they were hidden eggs or scattered pearls.”"],[49,"“I am the leader of the messengers, and no boast. I am the seal of the prophets, and no boast. I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted, and no boast.”"],[50,"“I am the first to take hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise and rattle it.” Anas said, “It is as if I am looking at the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moving it.” Sufyan described it to us like that, and Abu Abdullah gathered his fingers and moved them. Thabit said to him, “Did you touch the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with your hand?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then give it to me so I may kiss it.”"],[51,"“I am the first intercessor in Paradise.”"],[52,"“I am the first of people for whom the earth will split open from my skull on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I will be given the banner of praise, and no boast. I am the master of people on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I am the first to enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I will come to the gate of Paradise and take hold of its ring. They will say, ‘Who is this?’ I will say, ‘I am Muhammad.’ They will open for me, and I will enter and find the Compeller facing me. I will prostrate to Him, and He will say, ‘Raise your head, O Muhammad. Speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be granted; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.’ I will raise my head and say, ‘My community, my community, O Lord.’ He will say, ‘Go to your community, and whoever you find with a barley grain’s weight of faith in his heart, admit him to Paradise.’ I will go, and whomever I find with that weight, I will admit them to Paradise. Then I will find the Compeller facing me, and I will prostrate to Him. He will say, ‘Raise your head, O Muhammad. Speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be granted; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.’ I will raise my head and say, ‘My community, my community, O Lord.’ He will say, ‘Go to your community, and whoever you find with a mustard seed’s weight of faith in his heart, admit him to Paradise.’ I will go, and whomever I find with that weight, I will admit them to Paradise. Then the reckoning of people will be finished, and those of my community who remain will be admitted to the Fire with the people of the Fire. The people of the Fire will say, ‘What did it avail you that you used to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him?’ The Compeller will say, ‘By My might, I will surely free them from the Fire.’ He will send for them, and they will come out of the Fire, charred. They will be admitted into the river of life, and they will grow in it as a seed grows in the scum of a flood. It will be written between their eyes, ‘These are the freed ones of Allah.’ They will be taken and enter Paradise. The people of Paradise will say, ‘These are the Hellfire people.’ The Compeller will say, ‘Rather, these are the freed ones of the Compeller.’”"],[53,"Jibril ﷺ came down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and split open his belly. Then Jibril said, “A sound heart, containing two hearing ears and two seeing eyes. Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the one who follows and the gatherer. Your character is upright, your tongue is truthful, and your soul is tranquil.”"],[54,"“Allah brought to me the appointed term of mercy and made it short for me, so we are the last and we are the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. I will say a saying without boast: Ibrahim is the close friend of Allah, Musa is the chosen one of Allah, and I am the beloved of Allah. With me is the banner of praise on the Day of Resurrection. Allah, Exalted is He, promised me regarding my community and protected them from three things: He will not afflict them all with a year of drought, an enemy will not uproot them all, and He will not gather them all upon misguidance.”"],[55,"“Yes, I was brought food.” He said, “O Prophet of Allah, was there any surplus in it?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “What was done with it?” He said, “It was raised to the sky. It was revealed to me that I will not remain among you except for a little while. Then you will remain until you say, ‘When, when?’ Then you will come to me in groups, destroying one another. Before the Hour there will be a severe death, and after it years of earthquakes.”"],[56,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a bowl of tharid, and it was placed before the people. They took turns with it from morning until noon; one group would get up and another would sit. A man said to Samurah b. Jundub, “Was it not being replenished?” Samurah said, “At what do you marvel? It was not replenished except from here,” and he pointed with his hand toward the sky."],[57,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a moonlit night, wearing a red suit. I began to look at him and at the moon.” He said, “He was more beautiful in my eyes than the moon.”"],[58,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a gap between his front teeth. When he spoke, light was seen as if emerging from between his front teeth."],[59,"I have never seen anyone more helpful, more generous, more courageous, or more radiant than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[60,"I said to Rabi'ah, the daughter of Mu'awwidh ibn 'Afra', \"Describe to us the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" She replied, \"Oh my son, if you had seen him, you would have seen the rising sun.\""],[61,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a fair complexion, as if his sweat were pearls. When he walked, he leaned forward slightly. I never touched silk or brocade softer than his palm, nor did I ever smell any fragrance more pleasant than his scent—not musk or anything else."],[62,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he never said 'Uff' to me at all, nor did he ever say to me about something I did, 'Why did you do such and such?' or 'Why didn't you do such and such?'"],[63,"I was with my father when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned Ma'iz b. Malik. When the stones struck him, I was terrified, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced me. Then some of his underarm sweat flowed onto me, like the fragrance of musk."],[64,"A man asked him, 'Did you see whether the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was like a sword?' He said, 'No, it was like the moon.'"],[65,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was recognized at night by the scent of perfume."],[66,"The Prophet ﷺ never traveled a path—or rather, he would not travel a path—that anyone followed him except that he would know he had traveled it from the pleasantness of his fragrance, or he said, from the scent of his sweat."],[67,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to accept gifts but not charity. A Jewish woman of Khaybar gifted him a roasted sheep. He took some of it, and Bishr b. al-Bara' took some. Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hand and said, 'This informs me that it is poisoned.' Bishr b. al-Bara' died. The Prophet ﷺ sent to her, asking, 'What made you do what you did?' She said, 'If you are a prophet, nothing will harm you; if you are a king, I have relieved the people of you.' During his illness he said, 'I have never ceased to feel the effects of the morsel I ate at Khaybar. This is the time when my aorta is severed.'"],[68,"A Jewish woman of Khaybar poisoned a roasted sheep and gifted it to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ took the foreleg and ate from it, and a group of his companions ate with him. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to them, 'Raise your hands.' The Prophet ﷺ sent for the Jewish woman and summoned her. He asked her, 'Did you poison this sheep?' She said, 'Yes. Who told you?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'This foreleg in my hand informed me.' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What did you intend by that?' She said, 'I thought: if he is a prophet, it will not harm him; and if he is not a prophet, we will be rid of him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pardoned her and did not punish her. Some of his companions who ate from the sheep died. The Prophet ﷺ was cupped on his upper back because of what he ate from the sheep. Abu Hind, the freedman of Banu Bayadah, cupped him with a horn and a blade; he was from Banu Thumamah, a clan of the Ansar."],[69,"He said, 'Did you put poison in this sheep?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What made you do that?' They said, 'We intended that if you are a liar, we would be rid of you; and if you are a prophet, it will not harm you.'"],[70,"The Prophet ﷺ was never asked for anything at all and said no."],[71,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was modest; he was never asked for anything but that he gave it."],[72,"I crowded against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and on my feet were thick sandals, and I stepped with them on the foot of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He gave me a light blow with a whip in his hand and said, \"In the name of Allah, you have hurt me.\" He said: So I spent the night blaming myself, saying, \"I have hurt the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: So I spent a night such as Allah knows. When morning came, suddenly a man was saying, \"Where is so-and-so?\" He said: I said, \"This, by Allah, is what happened from me yesterday.\" He said: So I went off while I was afraid, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Indeed you stepped with your sandal on my foot yesterday and hurt me, so I gave you a light blow with the whip. Here are eighty ewes, so take them for it.\""],[73,"Jibril said, \"There is no household of ten dwellings on earth but that I have turned them over, and I have not found anyone more generous in spending this wealth than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[74,"The Prophet ﷺ used to remember Allah much, speak little idle talk, lengthen the prayer, and shorten the sermon; and he did not disdain or deem himself above walking with a widow or a poor person to fulfill their need."],[75,"I wanted to know how long the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would remain among us. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I see that they have harmed you and their dust has distressed you; if only you had taken a shelter from which to address them. He said, \"I will not cease to be among them while they tread on my heels and contend with me over my cloak until it is Allah who gives me rest from them.\" He said: Then I knew that his remaining among us was short."],[76,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall we screen you from them?\" He said, \"No, leave them to tread on my heel and I tread on their heels until Allah gives me rest from them.\""],[77,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us during the illness in which he died, while we were in the mosque, his head bound with a cloth, until he made his way toward the pulpit and sat upon it, and we followed him. He said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am looking at the Hawd from this place of mine.\" Then he said, \"A servant was offered the world and its adornment, and he chose the Hereafter.\" He said: No one understood it except Abu Bakr, ؓ , so his eyes overflowed and he wept. Then he said, \"Rather, may we ransom you with our fathers, our mothers, ourselves, and our wealth, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: Then he descended, and he did not stand upon it again until this hour."],[78,"On the authority of Abu Muwayhibah, the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"I have been commanded to seek forgiveness for the people of Al-Baqi', so come with me.\" So I went with him in the middle of the night. When he stood near them, he said, \"Peace be upon you, O people of the graves! May Allah honor you with what He honors those who have passed before you. If you knew what Allah has saved you from, the trials (and tribulations) to come would appear to you like the darkest part of the night. It (the trials) will follow one after another, each worse than the previous one.Then he turned towards me and said, 'O Abu Muwayhibah, I have been given the keys to the treasures of the world, and the keys to eternal life in it, then Paradise. I was given the choice between that and meeting my Lord.' I said, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, take the keys to the treasures of the world, and the keys to eternal life in it, then Paradise.' He said, 'No, by Allah, O Abu Muwayhibah, I have chosen to meet my Lord.' Then he sought forgiveness for the people of Al-Baqi' and left. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to feel the pain in which he died."],[79,"When {When comes the help of Allah and the victory} [al-Nasr 1] was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Fatimah and said, \"My death has been announced to me.\" So she wept. He said, \"Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me.\" So she laughed. Some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ saw her and said, \"O Fatimah, we saw you weep and then laugh.\" She said, \"He told me that his death had been announced to him, so I wept. Then he said to me, 'Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me,' so I laughed.\""],[80,"The Prophet ﷺ returned to me one day from a funeral at al-Baqi' and found me suffering from a headache and saying, \"O my head!\" He said, \"Rather I, O 'A'ishah, O my head!\" He said, \"What harm would it do you if you died before me, and I washed you, shrouded you, prayed over you, and buried you?\" I said, \"It is as if I can see you, by Allah, if you did that, you would return to my house and consummate marriage therein with one of your wives.\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled. Then the pain in which he died began."],[81,"The Prophet ﷺ said during his illness, \"Pour over me seven waterskins from seven different wells so that I may go out to the people and give them my final instructions.\" He said: So we seated him in a basin belonging to Hafsah and poured water over him—or we sprinkled it on him—the doubt is from Muhammad b. Ishaq. He felt relief, so he went out and ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, sought forgiveness for the martyrs among the companions of Uhud, and supplicated for them. Then he said, \"Now then, the Ansar are my closest inner circle to whom I turned for refuge. Honor their noble ones and overlook their wrongdoers except in legal penalties. Indeed, a servant from among the servants of Allah has been given the choice between this world and what is with Allah, and he has chosen what is with Allah.\" Abu Bakr wept, thinking that he meant himself."],[82,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was notified of the prayer during his illness, so he said, \"Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" Then he lost consciousness, and when he came to, he said, \"Did I tell you to have Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer?\" I said, \"Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man; if only you would order 'Umar.\" He said, \"You are the companions of Yusuf. Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Many a wisher wishes, but Allah and the believers refuse.\""],[83,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died on Monday, and he was kept for the rest of that day, its night, and the next day until he was buried on Wednesday night. They said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has not died, but his soul was taken up as the soul of Musa was taken up.\" 'Umar stood and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has not died, but his soul was taken up as the soul of Musa was taken up. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will not die until he cuts off the hands and tongues of some people.\" 'Umar kept speaking until foam gathered at the corners of his mouth from his threats and words. Then al-'Abbas stood and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has died, and he is a human being, and he will decompose as human beings decompose. O people, bury your companion, for he is too noble to Allah for Him to cause him to die twice. Would He cause one of you to die once and cause him to die twice, while he is nobler to Allah than that? O people, bury your companion. If it is as you say, it is not difficult for Allah to remove the soil from over him. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until he left the way as a clear path: he made lawful what is lawful, forbade what is forbidden, married, divorced, waged war, and made peace. No shepherd of sheep, whose owner follows with them over the mountain tops, striking the thorny trees with his stick and plastering their watering trough with his hand, was more tireless or more diligent than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among you. O people, bury your companion.\" He said: Umm Ayman began to weep, and it was said to her, \"O Umm Ayman, are you weeping for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said, \"By Allah, I am not weeping for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because I do not know that he has gone to what is better for him than this world, but I am weeping because the news from heaven has ceased.\" Hammad said: Tears choked Ayyub when he reached this point."],[84,"When a calamity befalls one of you, let him remember his calamity of my loss, for it is among the greatest of calamities."],[85,"When a calamity befalls one of you, let him remember his calamity of my loss, for it is among the greatest of calamities."],[86,"I never heard Ibn 'Umar mention the Prophet ﷺ except that he wept."],[87,"O Anas, how could you find it in yourselves to heap dust upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: O my father, from his Lord how near he is! O my father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode. O my father, to Jibril we announce his death. O my father, he answered a Lord who called him."],[88,"I witnessed the day he entered Madinah, and I never saw a day more beautiful or more radiant than the day on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered to us. And I witnessed the day of his death, and I never saw a day more ugly or darker than the day on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died."],[89,"'Abdullah b. Salam said to the Prophet ﷺ: O Messenger of Allah, we find you on the Day of Resurrection standing before your Lord, your cheeks red, ashamed before your Lord because of what your ummah introduced after you."],[90,"From the Prophet ﷺ that when this surah was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: {When the victory of Allah comes and the conquest, and you see the people entering Allah's religion in multitudes} [al-Nasr 2], the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They will certainly leave it in multitudes just as they entered it in multitudes.\""],[91,"To proceed: Allah created the creation without need of their obedience and secure from their disobedience. People then were divided in stations and opinion: the Arabs were in the worst of those stations, the people of stone and the people of hair and the people of dung, passing by the good things of this world and the ease of its life, not asking Allah as a community nor reciting a Book to Him; their dead were in the Fire and their living were blind and impure, along with what cannot be counted of that which is shunned and despised. When Allah willed to spread His mercy upon them, He sent to them a messenger from among themselves: grievous to him is your suffering, keen for you, to the believers kind and merciful—may Allah bless him and upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. That did not prevent them from wounding him in his body and nicknaming him in his name, though with him was a speaking Book from Allah, not undertaken except by His command and not journeyed to except by His leave. When he was commanded with resolve and charged with jihad, he unrolled his scroll for Allah's command, and Allah made his proof succeed, made his word prevail, and made his call manifest. He departed this world pious and pure. Then Abu Bakr succeeded him, following his sunnah and taking his path. The Arabs apostatized—or those of them who did so—and he refused to accept from them after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ anything except what was acceptable before. He drew swords from their sheaths and lit fires in their torches, then attacked the people of falsehood with the people of truth. He did not cease cutting their limbs and watering the earth with their blood until he brought them back into what they had left and settled them with what they had fled from. He had taken from Allah's wealth a young camel to ride and an Abyssinian woman who suckled a son of his; he saw that at his death as a lump in his throat, so he returned it to the caliph after him. He departed this world pious and pure, upon the path of his companion. Then after him 'Umar b. al-Khattab arose: he founded the garrison towns, blended severity with gentleness, rolled up his sleeves, tucked up his garment, prepared for affairs their equals and for war its tools. When the young man of al-Mughira b. Shu'ba struck him, he commanded Ibn 'Abbas to ask the people whether they could identify his killer. When it was said it was the young man of al-Mughira b. Shu'ba, he began praising his Lord that no one with a right in the fay' had struck him, lest he might argue that he had made his blood lawful by what he had deemed lawful of his right. He had taken from Allah's wealth seventy-some thousand, and for it he broke his teeth and disliked thereby the suretyship of his children, so he returned it to the caliph after him. He departed this world pious and pure, upon the path of his two companions. Then as for you, O 'Umar, you are the child of this world: its kings gave birth to you and gave you their breasts to suck. You grew up in it seeking its places of favor. When you were given charge of it, you cast it where Allah cast it; you abandoned it, shunned it, and loathed it except what you took as provision from it. Praise be to Allah who cleared our sin through you and removed our distress through you. Go ahead and do not turn back, for nothing is too mighty for truth, and nothing is too low for falsehood. I say this statement of mine, and I ask Allah's forgiveness for me and for the believing men and women. Abu Ayyub said: 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz would say about something: Ibn al-Ahtam said to me: Go ahead and do not turn back."],[92,"The people of Madinah suffered a severe drought and complained to 'A'ishah. She said: Look at the grave of the Prophet ﷺ and make an opening from it to the sky so that there is no roof between it and the sky. He said: They did so, and we were rained upon until grass grew and camels became fat until they split from fat. It was called the year of splitting."],[93,"During the days of al-Harrah, the call to prayer was not made in the mosque of the Prophet ﷺ for three days, nor was the prayer established. Sa'id b. al-Musayyab did not leave the mosque, and he would know the time of prayer only by a murmur he heard from the grave of the Prophet ﷺ."],[94,"Ka'b entered to 'A'ishah and they mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ka'b said: Every day when it dawns, seventy thousand angels descend until they surround the grave of the Prophet ﷺ, beating their wings and praying for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When evening comes, they ascend, and the like of them descend and do the same. When the earth splits open from him, he will emerge among seventy thousand angels escorting him."],[95,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer for us, then admonished us with an eloquent admonition that made eyes weep and hearts tremble. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, it seems like the admonition of one bidding farewell, so advise us. He said: \"I enjoin you to fear Allah and to hear and obey, even if a slave of Abyssinia is in charge. Whoever lives after me will see much disagreement; so you must keep to my sunnah and the sunnah of the rightly guided and rightly guiding caliphs, biting on it with the molar teeth. Beware of newly introduced matters, for every newly introduced matter is an innovation.\""],[96,"Those of our scholars who have passed used to say: Holding fast to the Sunnah is salvation. Knowledge will be seized quickly, so the revival of knowledge is the stability of the religion and the world, and in the disappearance of knowledge is the disappearance of all of that."],[97,"It has reached me that \"the first of the disappearance of the religion is the abandonment of the Sunnah. The religion will go away Sunnah by Sunnah just as a rope frays strand by strand.\""],[98,"No people innovate an innovation in their religion except that Allah removes from their Sunnah its like, then He does not restore it to them until the Day of Resurrection."],[99,"\"A man who introduces an innovation has only allowed the sword.\""],[100,"Truly the people of desires are the people of misguidance, and I do not see their fate except to be in the Fire. So test them: not one of them adopts a saying or relates a narration but that the matter ends with him short of the sword. Indeed hypocrisy was of various kinds—then he recited: {And among them are those who made a covenant with Allah, \"If He gives us from His bounty, we will surely give charity and be among the righteous\"} [al-Tawbah: 75], {And among them are those who criticize you concerning the charities. If they are given from them, they are pleased; but if they are not given from them, at once they become angry} [al-Tawbah: 58], {And among them are those who harm the Prophet and say, \"He is an ear.\" Say, \"An ear of good for you\"} [al-Tawbah: 61]. Their statements differed, but they agreed in doubt and denial. Indeed these—their statements differed, but they agreed in the sword, and I do not see their fate except to be in the Fire."],[101,"They were both sitting when a man came and asked them about something. Ibn Mas'ud said to Hudhayfah, \"What do you think they keep asking me about this for?\" He said, \"They learn it and then abandon it.\" So Ibn Mas'ud turned to him and said, \"Whatever you ask us about from the Book of Allah, the Exalted, that we know, we will inform you of it; or a Sunnah from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, we will inform you of it. But we have no capacity for what you have innovated.\""],[102,"Abdullah never delivered a sermon in al-Kufah except that I attended it. One day I heard him, when he was asked about a man who divorces his wife eight times and the like of that, he said, \"It is as he said.\" Then he said, \"Indeed Allah sent down His Book and made clear its explanation. So whoever comes to the matter from its proper angle, it has been made clear to him; and whoever opposes, then by Allah, we cannot endure your opposition.\""],[103,"I witnessed Abdullah when a man and a woman came to him concerning prohibition (tahrim). He said, \"Indeed Allah has made clear. So whoever comes to the matter from its proper angle, it has been made clear; and whoever opposes, then by Allah, we cannot endure your opposition.\""],[104,"He would not give his opinion except about something he had heard."],[105,"I never heard Ibrahim give his opinion about anything at all."],[106,"I have not given my opinion for thirty years.\" Abu Hilal said: \"For forty years."],[107,"Someone said to him, \"Will you not give your opinion about it?\" He said, \"I am too shy of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, for the world to be judged by my opinion.\""],[108,"A man came to him asking about something, so he said, \"Ibn Mas'ud used to say such and such about it.\" The man said, \"Tell me your own opinion.\" He said, \"Are you not amazed at this man? I told him from Ibn Mas'ud, and he asks me for my opinion. My religion is dearer to me than that. By Allah, to undergo hardship is more beloved to me than to inform you of my opinion.\""],[109,"Beware of reasoning by analogy. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, if you adopt analogical reasoning, you will surely make lawful what is unlawful and make unlawful what is lawful. But whatever reaches you from those who preserved the knowledge of the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, then act upon it."],[110,"A man came to 'Abdullah and said, \"He divorced his wife last night eight times.\" He said, \"With a single statement?\" He said, \"With a single statement.\" He said, \"Do they want to make your wife unlawful for you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then another man came to him and said, \"He divorced his wife a hundred times.\" He said, \"With a single statement?\" He said, \"With a single statement.\" He said, \"Do they want to make your wife unlawful for you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then 'Abdullah said, \"Whoever divorces as Allah has commanded, Allah has made the divorce clear. But whoever confuses himself, we entrust him to his confusion. By Allah, you will not confuse yourselves while we bear it. It is as you say.\""],[111,"For a man to live ignorant after knowing the right of Allah upon him is better for him than to say what he does not know."],[112,"I heard al-Qasim being asked, and he said, \"By Allah, we do not know everything you ask about. And if we knew, we would not conceal it from you, nor would it be lawful for us to conceal it.\""],[113,"Al-Qasim was asked about something he had named, and he said, \"I am not forced to give an opinion, and I am not in any position regarding it.\""],[114,"I said to al-Qasim, \"How hard it is for me that you are asked about something you do not know, while your father was an imam.\" He said, \"Harder than that, in the sight of Allah and in the sight of anyone who understands from Allah, is that I give a fatwa without knowledge or narrate from someone who is not trustworthy.\""],[115,"When a matter came to them for which there was no report from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they would gather for it and reach consensus. So the truth is in what they deemed right. The truth is in what they deemed right."],[116,"Do not hasten toward a calamity before it descends. For if you do not hasten it before it descends, the Muslims will never lack among them, when it does descend, someone who, if he speaks, is guided aright and directed. But if you hasten it, the whims will pull you in different directions, and you will take this way and that way.\" And he gestured before him, to his right, and to his left."],[117,"That the Prophet ﷺ was asked about a matter that occurs which is not in a book or a Sunnah, he said, \"The pious believers will consider it.\""],[118,"You ask us about things we never used to ask about, and you pry into things we never used to pry into. You ask about things I do not know what they are. If we knew them, it would not be lawful for us to conceal them from you."],[119,"People will come who argue with you using the ambiguities of the Qur'an. So take hold of them with the sunan, for the people of the sunan know the Book of Allah ﷻ best."],[120,"The affair of the Children of Israel remained upright, with nothing wrong in it, until there grew up among them the muwalladun, sons of captives of other nations, sons of women whom the Children of Israel had taken captive from others. Then they spoke among them with opinion, and led them astray."],[121,"He curses the one who asks about what has not happened."],[122,"Zayd b. Thabit al-Ansari ؓ used to say, when asked about a matter, \"Has this happened?\" If they said, \"Yes, it has happened,\" he would speak about it with what he knew and what he deemed correct. If they said, \"It has not happened,\" he would say, \"Then leave it until it happens.\""],[123,"Ammar b. Yasir was asked about a matter and said, \"Has this happened yet?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Leave us until it happens; when it happens, we will undertake it for you.\""],[124,"Umar ؓ said from the pulpit: \"I adjure by Allah any man who asks about what has not happened, for Allah has made clear what is to happen.\""],[125,"I have not seen a people better than the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They did not ask him except about thirteen matters until he passed away, all of them in the Qur'an. Among them: \"They ask you about the sacred month\" [al-Baqarah 217] and \"They ask you about menstruation\" [al-Baqarah 222]. He said: \"They would not ask except about what benefited them.\""],[126,"Those of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whom I met are more than those who preceded me from them. I have not seen a people of easier conduct or less strictness than them."],[127,"I heard Ubadah b. Nusayy al-Kindi, when asked about a woman who died among a people with no guardian, say: \"I met people who would not be as strict as you are, nor would they ask the questions you ask.\""],[128,"I was with Ibn Muhayriz at Marj al-Dibaj and saw him alone, so I asked him about a matter. He said to me, \"What will you do with these questions?\" I said, \"Were it not for questions, knowledge would be lost.\" He said, \"Do not say knowledge is lost. Knowledge will not be lost as long as the Qur'an is recited. But if you were to say, 'Understanding is lost,' that would be correct.\""],[129,"O people, we do not know; perhaps we command you with things that are not lawful for you, and perhaps we forbid you things that are lawful for you. The last thing revealed of the Qur'an was the verse of riba, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not explain it to us before he died. So leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt."],[130,"I left Ibrahim's presence and Hammad met me and loaded me with eight questions. I asked him and he answered four and left four."],[131,"I never asked Ibrahim about anything except that I saw dislike in his face."],[132,"I have not seen anyone more likely to say, when asked about something, 'I have no knowledge of it,' than al-Sha'bi."],[133,"Al-Sha'bi, when something came to him, would be cautious, while Ibrahim would speak and speak and speak."],[134,"I said to Sa'id b. Jubayr, \"What is the matter with you that you do not say anything about divorce?\" He said, \"There is nothing about it except that I have asked concerning it, but I dislike making lawful what is unlawful or making unlawful what is lawful.\""],[135,"I met in this mosque one hundred and twenty of the Ansar, and there was not one of them who would narrate a hadith except that he wished his brother would spare him the hadith, and none was asked for a legal opinion except that he wished his brother would spare him the legal opinion."],[136,"I asked al-Sha'bi, \"How did you act when you were asked?\" He said, \"You have come to one who knows. When a man was asked, he would say to his companion, 'Give them a ruling,' and it would continue until it returned to the first.\""],[137,"\"The scholar enters between God and His servants, so let him seek a way out for himself.\""],[138,"By the One besides whom there is no god, \"I have not seen anyone harsher against the nitpickers than the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I have not seen anyone harsher against them than Abu Bakr, and I think Umar was the most fearful for them or of them.\""],[139,"Yes, \"upon you is fear of God and uprightness. Follow and do not innovate.\""],[140,"\"They used to consider that one is on the path as long as he follows the trace.\""],[141,"\"As long as he follows the trace, he is on the path.\""],[142,"\"Learn knowledge before it is taken away, and its taking away is that its people depart. Beware of nitpicking, delving too deep, and innovations, and keep to the ancient.\""],[143,"\"Upon you is knowledge before it is taken away, and its taking away is that its companions are taken away. Upon you is knowledge, for one of you does not know when he will need it or need what he has. You will find people who claim they are calling you to the Book of God while they have cast it behind their backs. So upon you is knowledge, and beware of innovation, beware of nitpicking, beware of delving too deep, and keep to the ancient.\""],[144,"A man called Sabigh came to Madinah and began asking about the ambiguous verses of the Quran, so Umar sent for him and had prepared palm branches for him. He said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am the servant of God, Sabigh.\" Umar took one of those palm branches and struck him, saying, \"I am the servant of God, Umar,\" and he beat him until his head bled. Then he said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, enough; what I used to find in my head has gone.\""],[145,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “It is He who has sent down to you the Book; in it are verses that are precise—they are the foundation of the Book—and others unspecific” [Āl ʿImrān 7]. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see those who follow what is unspecific of it, beware of them.”"],[146,"ʿAbdullāh was asked about something, and he said: “I would hate to make lawful for you something that Allah has forbidden for you, or to forbid something that Allah has made lawful for you.”"],[147,"“That I turn him back with his own inadequacy is more beloved to me than that I impose upon myself for him what I do not know.”"],[148,"Ṣabīgh al-ʿIrāqī began asking about certain matters of the Qurʾān among the armies of the Muslims until he arrived in Egypt. ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ sent him to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb. When the messenger brought the letter, ʿUmar read it and said: “Where is the man?” The messenger said: “In the camp.” ʿUmar said: “Make sure he has not gone, or you will receive from me a painful punishment.” So he brought him to ʿUmar. ʿUmar said: “You ask about something unheard of?” Then ʿUmar sent for fresh palm branches and beat him with them until he left his back raw. Then he left him until he healed, then repeated it. Then he left him until he healed, then called for him to repeat it again. Ṣabīgh said: “If you intend to kill me, kill me in a good manner; and if you intend to cure me, then by Allah I have already healed.” So ʿUmar permitted him to return to his land and wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī that no Muslim should sit with him. That became hard on the man, so Abū Mūsā wrote to ʿUmar that his repentance had become good. ʿUmar wrote back: “Allow the people to sit with him.”"],[149,"A man asked Ubayy b. Kaʿb for a ruling and said: “O Abū al-Mundhir, what do you say about such and such?” He replied: “O my son, has what you ask me about occurred?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then leave me until it occurs, and we will exert ourselves and then inform you.”"],[150,"I was walking with Ubayy b. Kaʿb when a young man said: “What do you say, O uncle, about such and such?” He said: “O son of my brother, has this occurred?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then excuse us until it occurs.”"],[151,"Ibrāhīm, when asked about something, would only answer with the answer of the one who was asked about it."],[152,"He would not give a ruling about the private parts in any matter about which there was disagreement."],[153,"I asked Ṭāwūs about a question, and he said to me: “Has this occurred?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “By Allah?” I said: “By Allah.” Then he said: “Our companions informed us from Muʿādh b. Jabal that he said: ‘O people, do not hasten to calamity before it descends, lest it lead you here and there. If you do not hasten to calamity before it descends, the Muslims will never cease to have among them someone who, when asked, is guided aright; and when he speaks, he is granted success.’”"],[154,"I asked him about a man who had two Ramaḍāns overtake him (i.e., with missed fasts). He said: “Has it occurred or not yet?” I said: “It has not yet occurred.” He said: “Leave his calamity until it descends.” Then we concealed a man for him, and he said: “It has occurred.” So he said: “He feeds thirty poor people for the first of them, one poor person for each day.”"],[155,"I would sit in Makkah with Ibn ʿUmar one day and with Ibn ʿAbbās another day. Ibn ʿUmar’s saying “I do not know” in response to what he was asked was more frequent than his giving a ruling."],[156,"“Learn, for one of you does not know when he will be needed.”"],[157,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The bravest among you in battle is the bravest among you in facing the Fire.\""],[158,"Whoever introduces an opinion that is not in the Book of Allah and no Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has established, he will not know where he stands regarding it when he meets Allah ﷻ."],[159,"Whoever is given a fatwa without certainty, its sin is only upon the one who gave the fatwa."],[160,"Whoever issues a fatwa that is not clear to him, its sin is upon him."],[161,"When a dispute came to Abu Bakr, he would look into the Book of Allah. If he found in it something by which to judge between them, he judged by it. If it was not in the Book and he knew a Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning that matter, he judged by it. If it eluded him, he went out and asked the Muslims, saying: \"Such and such has come to me. Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged in that matter with a judgment?\" Sometimes a group would gather to him, each mentioning a judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning it. Abu Bakr would say: \"Praise be to Allah who has placed among us those who preserve the Sunnah of our Prophet ﷺ.\" If finding a Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eluded him, he gathered the leaders and the best of the people and consulted them. When their opinion agreed on a matter, he judged by it."],[162,"My wife had a vow of i'tikaf for three days in the Sacred Mosque. I asked Umar b. Abd al-Aziz while Ibn Shihab was with him. I said: \"Is fasting due upon her?\" Ibn Shihab said: \"There is no i'tikaf except with fasting.\" Umar b. Abd al-Aziz said to him: \"From the Prophet ﷺ ?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"From Abu Bakr?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"From Umar?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"From Uthman?\" He said: \"No.\" Umar said: \"I do not think she owes fasting.\" I left and found Tawus and Ata b. Abi Rabah. I asked them. Tawus said: \"Ibn Abbas ؓ did not consider fasting due upon her unless she imposed it on herself.\" He said: Ata said: \"That is my opinion.\""],[163,"When Abu Salama came to Basra, I and al-Hasan went to him. He said to al-Hasan: \"You are al-Hasan? No one in Basra was more beloved to me to meet than you, because it reached me that you give fatwas by your opinion. So do not give fatwa by your opinion unless it is a Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or a revealed Book.\""],[164,"Ibn Umar ؓ met him during tawaf and said to him: \"O Abu al-Sha'tha, you are among the fuqaha of Basra, so do not give fatwa except by a speaking Quran or an established Sunnah. If you do otherwise, you will perish and cause others to perish.\""],[165,"A time passed over us when we did not judge, and we were not in that position. Allah has decreed that we have reached what you see. Whoever is presented with a judgment after today, let him judge in it by what is in the Book of Allah ﷻ. If there comes to him what is not in the Book of Allah, let him judge by what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged. If there comes to him what is not in the Book of Allah and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not judge it, let him judge by what the righteous judged. Let him not say: 'I fear' or 'I think'. The haram is clear and the halal is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. So leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt.\""],[166,"He was asked about a matter. If it was in the Quran, he informed about it. If it was not in the Quran and there was a Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he informed about it. If it was not, then he referred to Abu Bakr and Umar. If it was not, he gave his opinion on it.\""],[167,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ wrote to him: 'If something comes to you that is in the Book of Allah, judge by it and do not let men divert you from it. If there comes to you what is not in the Book of Allah, look to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and judge by it. If there comes to you what is not in the Book of Allah and there is no Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in it, look to what the people have agreed upon and take it. If there comes to you what is not in the Book of Allah and is not in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and no one before you has spoken about it, then choose whichever of the two matters you wish: if you wish to exercise ijtihad with your opinion and then proceed, proceed; and if you wish to delay, then delay, and I do not consider delay except better for you.'"],[168,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he said: 'Consider: if a judgment is presented to you, how will you judge?' He said: 'I will judge by the Book of Allah.' He said: 'If it is not in the Book of Allah?' He said: 'Then by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'If it is not in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'I will exercise ijtihad with my opinion and will not fall short.' He said: He struck his chest and said: 'Praise be to Allah who has guided the envoy of the Messenger of Allah to what pleases the Messenger of Allah.'"],[169,"A time passed over us when we were not asked and we were not in that position. Allah has decreed that I have reached what you see. If you are asked about something, look into the Book of Allah. If you do not find it in the Book of Allah ﷻ, then in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah. If you do not find it in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, then what the Muslims have agreed upon. If it is not in what the Muslims have agreed upon, then exercise ijtihad with your opinion. Do not say: 'I fear and I am wary.' The halal is clear and the haram is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. So leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt."],[170,"\"O people, you will initiate things and things will be initiated for you. When you see a newly initiated matter, hold fast to the original command.\""],[171,"'Umar said to Ibn Mas'ud, \"Have I not been informed—or I have been informed—that you give legal opinions when you are not an amir? Hand over the hot part of it to the one who undertakes the cool part of it.\""],[172,"\"The one who gives legal opinions to people on everything he is asked about is indeed insane.\""],[173,"Only three give legal opinions to people: a man who is a leader or a ruler, and a man who knows the abrogating verses of the Quran from the abrogated. They said, \"O Hudhayfah, who is that?\" He said, \"'Umar b. al-Khattab,\" or a foolish pretender."],[174,"Only one of three gives legal opinions to people: a man who knows the abrogating verses of the Quran from the abrogated. They said, \"Who is that?\" He said, \"'Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He said, \"And a ruler who has no alternative, or a foolish pretender.\" Then Muhammad said, \"I am not one of these two, and I hope not to be the third.\""],[175,"Whoever among you has knowledge, let him speak by it, and whoever does not know, let him say about what he does not know, 'Allah knows best.' For when a scholar is asked about what he does not know, he says, 'Allah ﷻ knows best.' And Allah said to His Messenger: {Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it, and I am not of the pretenders} [Sad 86]."],[176,"Abu Musa said in his sermon, \"Whoever has knowledge, let him teach it to people, and let him beware of saying what he has no knowledge of, lest he depart from the religion and be among the pretenders.\""],[177,"'Ali, ؓ , said: \"How cool it is for the liver, when I am asked about what I do not know, to say, 'Allah knows best.'\""],[178,"\"How cool it is for the liver to say about what you do not know, 'Allah knows best.'\""],[179,"\"When you are asked about what you do not know, flee.\" It was said, \"How is the fleeing, O Amir al-Mu'minin?\" He said, \"You say, 'Allah knows best.'\""],[180,"Ali placed it on the liver three times. They asked, \"What does that mean, O Prince of the Believers?\" He said, \"It means that a person should not be asked about something they do not know, and they should say, 'Allah knows best.'\""],[181,"\"I have no knowledge of it. So, when the man turned away, Ibn Umar said, 'Yes, that's what Ibn Umar said when he was asked about something he didn't know. He would say, 'I have no knowledge of it.'\""],[182,"“I do not know is half of knowledge.”"],[183,"A man came to Ibn ʿUmar asking him about something, and he said, “I have no knowledge of it.” Then, after the man had turned away, he said, “Ibn ʿUmar said well: he was asked about what he does not know and said, ‘I have no knowledge of it.’”"],[184,"Whenever ʿĀmir was asked about something, he would say, “I do not know.” If they insisted, he would say, “I swear to you by Allah, I have no knowledge of it.”"],[185,"I do not care whether I am asked about what I know or what I do not know, for if I am asked about what I know, I say what I know, and if I am asked about what I do not know, I say I do not know."],[186,"I heard Ibrahim saying, \"A cat is neither halal (permissible) nor haram (forbidden). He only used to say, 'They (the companions) used to dislike it while they used to prefer (keeping other animals).'\""],[187,"\"Abdullah, how are you when you wear a temptation in which the great ones become disoriented and the small ones grow up and people take it as a tradition? And when it is changed, they say, 'The tradition has changed.' They say, 'And when will that be, O Abu Abdur Rahman?' He said, 'When your readers become numerous, your scholars become few, your leaders become many, and your trustworthy ones become few, and when the worldly life is sought through the actions of the Hereafter.'\""],[188,"How will you be when a trial envelops you in which the old grow senile and the young grow up, and when something of it is abandoned, it is said, “The Sunnah has been abandoned”? They said, “And when will that be?” He said, “When your scholars pass away, your ignorant ones increase, your reciters increase, your jurists decrease, your rulers increase, your trustworthy ones decrease, the worldly life is sought by the deeds of the Hereafter, and understanding is sought for other than the religion.”"],[189,"It used to be said, “Woe to those who seek understanding for other than worship and those who make permissible what is sacred through ambiguities.”"],[190,"“No year comes upon you except that it is worse than the one before it. Indeed, I do not mean a year more fertile than a year, nor a ruler better than a ruler, but your scholars, your best ones, and your jurists will pass away, and you will not find successors from among them. Then a people will come who will measure matters by their own opinions.”"],[191,"“The first to use analogy was Iblīs, and the sun and the moon were not worshiped except by means of analogies.”"],[192,"He recited this verse: “You created me from fire and created him from clay” [al-Aʿrāf: 12], and said, “Iblīs used analogy, and he was the first to use analogy.”"],[193,"“I fear, or I am afraid, that if I use analogy, my foot will slip.”"],[194,"By Allah, “If you adopt analogies, you will surely make lawful what is unlawful and make unlawful what is lawful.”"],[195,"He used to say, “How hateful to me is ‘Do you think? Do you think?’ – a man asks his companion and says, ‘Do you think?’” And he would not use analogy."],[196,"Abu Wa'il forbade me from sitting with the people of \"Have you seen?\" (i.e., those who engage in excessive hypothetical questioning)."],[197,"If these people had been in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, most of the Quran would have been revealed: \"They ask you… They ask you…\""],[198,"\"O Abu Hamza, by Allah, I have spoken the truth even if I may have found trouble in doing so. And indeed, there is a time when I may become a scholar amongst the people of Kufa, during a time of adversity.\""],[199,"Beware of measuring out (i.e., engaging in excessive debate) in speech."],[200,"I witnessed Shurayh when a man from Murad came to him and said, \"O Abu Umayyah, what is the blood money for the fingers?\" He said, \"Ten each.\" He said, \"Glory be to Allah! Are these two equal?\" He brought together the little finger and the thumb. Shurayh said, \"Glory be to Allah! Are your ear and your hand equal? For the ear is covered by hair, the cap, and the turban, and it has half the blood money, while the hand has half the blood money. Woe to you! The Sunnah precedes your analogy, so follow and do not innovate, for you will not go astray as long as you hold to the tradition.\" Abu Bakr said: Al-Sha'bi said to me, \"O Hudhali, if your most eloquent man were killed along with this infant in his cradle, would their blood money be equal?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then where is analogy?\""],[201,"Mu'adh ibn Jabal said, \"The Quran will be spread among the people until women, children, and men read it. A man will say, 'I have read the Quran, yet I am not followed. By Allah, I will act upon it in their midst so that I may be followed.' So he acts upon it among them, but he is not followed. Then he says, 'I have read the Quran, yet I have not been followed. I have acted upon it in their midst, yet I have not been followed. I will create a mosque in my house so that I may be followed.' So he makes a mosque in his house, but he is not followed. Then he says, 'I have read the Quran, yet I have not been followed. I have acted upon it in their midst, yet I have not been followed. I have made a mosque in my house, yet I have not been followed. By Allah, I will bring them a hadith that they will not find in the Book of Allah, Glorious and Exalted, and they have not heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that I may be followed.' Mu'adh said, 'Beware of what he brings, for what he brings is misguidance.'\""],[202,"al-Shabi said to me, \"Whatever they tell you about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [said] then take it, but whatever they say based on their own opinions, then cast it aside.\""],[203,"I am content with these people of my time that they do not ask me and I do not ask them. One of them only says, \"Have you seen? Have you seen?\""],[204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line for us one day and said, \"This is the way of Allah.\" Then he drew lines to his right and left and said, \"These are various paths, on each of them there is a devil who calls to it.\" Then he recited, \"And that this is My path, which is straight, so follow it; and do not follow [other] ways, for they will separate you from His way.\" [Surah Al-An'am: 153]"],[205,"From Mujahid: {and do not follow the [other] ways} [Al-An'am: 153] - he said: \"Innovations and doubtful matters.\""],[206,"We were sitting at the door of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud before the morning prayer. When he came out, we walked with him to the mosque. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came to us and said, \"Has Abu Abdur-Rahman come out to you?\" We said, \"No, not yet.\" So he sat with us until he came out. When he came out, we all stood up to go with him. Abu Musa said to him, \"O Abu Abdur-Rahman, I have just seen something in the mosque that I rejected, but thanks to Allah, I saw only good.\" Abdullah ibn Mas'ud asked, \"What is it?\" Abu Musa replied, \"If you live, you will see it.\" Then he said, \"In the mosque, I saw some people sitting in circles waiting for prayer. In each circle, there was a man and in their hands were pebbles. He would say, 'Say Allahu Akbar (Takbir) a hundred times,' so they would say it a hundred times. Then he would say, 'Say La ilaha illallah (Tahlil) a hundred times,' so they would say it a hundred times. And he would say, 'Say Subhanallah (Tasbih) a hundred times,' so they would say it a hundred times.\" Abdullah ibn Mas'ud asked, \"What did you say to them?\" He replied, \"I didn't say anything to them, waiting for your opinion or your order.\" Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, \"You should have ordered them to count their evil deeds and assured them that their good deeds would not be lost.\" Then he proceeded, and we accompanied him until he came to one of those circles. He stood over them and said, \"What is this I see you doing?\" They said, \"O Abu Abdur-Rahman, these are pebbles we are using to count the Takbir, Tahlil, and Tasbih.\" He said, \"Count your bad deeds, and I assure you nothing will be lost from your good deeds. Woe to you, O nation of Muhammad! How quickly you have perished! These are the Companions of your Prophet ﷺ, abundant still. His garments have not worn out and his vessels are not broken. By the One in Whose Hand my soul is, you are either following a way more guided than the way of Muhammad ﷺ or you are opening a door of misguidance.\" They said, \"By Allah, O Abu Abdur-Rahman, we only intended good.\" He said, \"How many intend good but do not achieve it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us that there would be people who recite the Quran, and it does not go past their throats. By Allah, I do not know, perhaps most of them are from you.\" Then he turned away from them. Amr ibn Salamah commented, \"We saw most of those circles fighting against us on the day of Nahrawan with the Khawarij.\""],[207,"Follow and do not innovate, for you have been sufficed."],[208,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"The best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and the worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance.\""],[209,"The most truthful speech is the speech of Allah ﷻ, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ. The wretched is he who is wretched in his mother's womb. The worst of narrations are the narrations of falsehood, and the worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and everything that is coming is near."],[210,"No man adopts an innovation and then returns to a Sunnah."],[211,"I only fear for my nation the misleading leaders."],[212,"A man entered upon us at midday. I said, \"O servant of Allah, from where have you come?\" He said, \"I and a companion of mine came in search of something for us. My companion went off searching, and I entered to shade myself in the shade and drink from the drink.\" So I went to some sour milk—or she said, I went to some sour diluted milk—and gave him to drink from it. He drank, and I drank. She said: I studied his features and said, \"O servant of Allah, who are you?\" He said, \"I am Abu Bakr.\" I said, \"Are you Abu Bakr, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, of whom I have heard?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She said: Then I recalled our raids against Khath'am, and our raids against one another in the pre-Islamic era, and the affection and the ropes of the tents that Allah brought. Ibn 'Awn interlaced his fingers and Mu'adh described it to us, and Ahmad interlaced. I said, \"O servant of Allah, until when do you see this affair of the people?\" He said, \"As long as the leaders remain upright.\" I said, \"Who are the leaders?\" He said, \"Have you not seen the chief who is in the encampment, and they follow him and obey him? So as long as those remain upright.\""],[213,"The most fearful thing I fear for you is the misguided leaders.\""],[214,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon a woman from Ahmas called Zaynab. He saw her not speaking, so he said: \"What is the matter with her that she does not speak?\" They said: \"She has intended a Hajj while keeping silent.\" He said to her: \"Speak, for this is not lawful; this is from the deeds of the Jahiliyyah.\" So she spoke and said: \"Who are you?\" He said: \"I am a man from the Muhajirin.\" She said: \"From which Muhajirin?\" He said: \"From Quraysh.\" She said: \"From which Quraysh are you?\" He said: \"You are certainly inquisitive. I am Abu Bakr.\" She said: \"How long will we remain upon this righteous affair that Allah brought after the Jahiliyyah?\" He said: \"You will remain upon it as long as your leaders keep you upright.\" She said: \"And what are the leaders?\" He said: \"Did your people not have chiefs and nobles who commanded them and they obeyed them?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then they are like those over the people.\""],[215,"I saw Ibn Mas'ud giving advice to men and women, saying, \"Whoever meets a man or a woman, the first greeting should be the first greeting, as you are upon the primordial nature.\" Abdullah said, \"The first greeting is the correct way.\""],[216,"\"Do you know what demolishes Islam?\" He said: I said: \"No.\" He said: \"The slip of the scholar, the disputation of the hypocrite with the Book, and the judgment of the misguided leaders.\""],[217,"\"Do not sit with the people of disputes, for they plunge into the verses of Allah.\""],[218,"Your Sunnah, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is between the two: between the excessive and the harsh. So be patient upon it, may Allah have mercy on you. For the people of the Sunnah were the fewest of people in what has passed, and they are the fewest of people in what remains – those who did not go along with the people of extravagance in their extravagance, nor with the people of innovations in their innovations, and they were patient upon their Sunnah until they met their Lord. So be like that, if Allah wills; so be it."],[219,"\"Moderation in the Sunnah is better than striving in innovation.\""],[220,"\"I have met people for whom if one of them did not exceed a fingernail's length, I would not exceed it. It is enough of a disparagement of a people that their actions be opposed.\""],[221,"From Ata, regarding {Obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [an-Nisa 59]: He said: \"Those of knowledge and understanding. And obedience to the Messenger is following the Book and the Sunnah.\""],[222,"I asked Ibn Shubrumah about something – and I had a difficult question. I said: \"May Allah have mercy on you, look into it.\" He said: \"When the path becomes clear to me and I find the report, I do not hold back.\""],[223,"\"Learn knowledge and teach it to the people. Learn the obligations of inheritance and teach them to the people. Learn the Quran and teach it to the people. For I am a man who will be taken, and knowledge will decrease, and trials will appear until two people differ over an obligatory share and do not find anyone to judge between them.\""],[224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muadh b. Jabal and Abu Musa to Yemen. He said: \"Support one another, yield to one another, make things easy, and do not repel.\" They arrived in Yemen, and Muadh addressed the people, urging them to Islam and commanding them to seek understanding of the Quran. He said: \"When you have done that, ask me and I will inform you about the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.\" They remained as long as Allah willed them to remain, then they said to Muadh: \"You commanded us, when we have gained understanding and read, to ask you so that you inform us of the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.\" Muadh said to them: \"When a man is mentioned with good, he is from the people of Paradise; and when he is mentioned with evil, he is from the people of the Fire.\""],[225,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is noblest?\" He said: \"The most God-fearing of them.\" They said: \"It is not about this that we ask you.\" He said: \"Then Yusuf b. Ya'qub, the Prophet of Allah, son of the Prophet of Allah, son of the Friend of Allah.\" They said: \"It is not about this that we ask you.\" He said: \"Then about the origins of the Arabs you ask me? The best of them in the Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam if they gain understanding.\""],[226,"\"Whomever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.\""],[227,"\"Whomever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.\""],[228,"\"Whomever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.\""],[229,"He witnessed the sermon of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of ʿArafah during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"O people, by Allah, I do not know whether I will meet you after this day of mine in this place of mine. May Allah have mercy on whoever hears my words today and retains them, for many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him.\""],[230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at al-Khayf in Minā and said: \"May Allah brighten the face of a servant who hears my words, retains them, then conveys them to one who has not heard them. For many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him.\""],[231,"So I said, \"I did not leave Marwan except that he asked me about something, so I went to him and asked him. He said, 'Yes, he asked me about a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him.' He said, 'May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and memorizes it, then conveys it to someone who has better understanding of it. There are many carriers of fiqh (knowledge) who are not scholars, and there are many carriers of fiqh who convey it to someone who has better understanding than them.'\""],[232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and said: \"May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for many a one to whom it is conveyed is more retentive than the one who heard it.\""],[233,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[234,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[235,"\"Whoever narrates a lie from me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[236,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[237,"Were it not that I fear making a mistake, I would narrate to you things I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. That is because I heard him ﷺ say: \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[238,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[239,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the minbar: \"O people, beware of narrating many hadiths from me. Whoever says something on my behalf should say only the truth, or only what is true. And whoever says on my behalf what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[240,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[241,"Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it away from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars. When no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give legal opinions without knowledge, so they go astray and lead others astray."],[242,"\"Take knowledge before it departs.\" They said, \"How does knowledge depart, O Prophet of Allah, while the Book of Allah is among us?\" He became angry and said, \"May your mothers be bereaved of you! Were not the Torah and the Gospel among the Children of Israel, and they did not avail them anything? Indeed, the departure of knowledge is the departure of its bearers. Indeed, the departure of knowledge is the departure of its bearers.\""],[243,"I asked Sa'id b. Jubayr, saying, \"O Abu Abdullah, what is the sign of the destruction of people?\" He said, \"When their scholars perish.\""],[244,"People will remain in good as long as the first remains, until the last learns or teaches. When the first perishes before the last learns or is taught, people perish."],[245,"\"Do you know what the departure of knowledge is?\" We said, \"No.\" He said, \"The departure of the scholars.\""],[246,"\"Do you know how knowledge is decreased?\" He said: I said, \"Like a garment is shaken out, and like a dirham becomes hard.\" He said, \"No. Indeed, that is part of it: the taking away of knowledge is the taking away of the scholars.\""],[247,"\"Why do I see your scholars departing while your ignorant do not learn? Learn before knowledge is lifted, for the lifting of knowledge is the departure of the scholars.\""],[248,"\"People are either scholars or learners, and there is no good in what is beyond that.\""],[249,"\"The teacher of good and the learner are equal in reward, and there is no good for the rest of people after that.\""],[250,"\"Be a scholar, or a learner, or a listener, and do not be the fourth, lest you perish.\""],[251,"People will remain in good as long as the first remains until the last learns. When the first perishes before the last learns, the people perish."],[252,"Acquire understanding before you become leaders."],[253,"People became excessive in building during the time of Umar, so Umar said: 'O assembly of Arabs, the land, the land! Indeed there is no Islam except with a community, and no community except with leadership, and no leadership except with obedience. So whoever his people make a leader based on understanding, it is life for him and for them. And whoever his people make a leader without understanding, it is destruction for him and for them.'"],[254,"I do not accept every word of the wise, but I accept his concern and his desire. If his concern and desire are in obedience to Me, I make his silence praise of Me and dignity, even if he does not speak."],[255,"I will spread knowledge in the end of time until the man, the woman, the slave, the free, the young, and the old know it. When I do that to them, I will take them by My right upon them."],[256,"\"Whoever seeks something from this knowledge and intends with it what is with Allah, he will attain it if Allah wills. And whoever intends with it worldly gain, then that is his portion from it by Allah.\""],[257,"Do not learn knowledge for three: to dispute with the foolish, to argue with the scholars, or to turn people's faces toward you. Seek with your saying what is with Allah, for it lasts and remains, while everything else perishes."],[258,"Be springs of knowledge, lamps of guidance, homebodies, night lights, fresh hearts, worn garments. You will be known among the people of heaven and hidden from the people of earth."],[259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No one seeks this knowledge except for worldly gains, but Allah will prohibit them from entering Paradise on the Day of Judgment.\""],[260,"A man said to al-Sha'bi: 'Give me a ruling, O scholar.' He replied: 'The scholar is the one who fears Allah' ﷻ."],[261,"Learn knowledge so that you are known by it, and act upon it so that you become among its people. For after this there will come a time when nine-tenths of their people will not recognize the known, and none will escape from it except every quiet one. Those are the leaders of guidance and the lamps of knowledge, not the prattlers, nor the broadcasters, nor the gossips."],[262,"Do whatever you wish after you have learned, for Allah, may He be exalted, will never reward you for knowledge until you act."],[263,"He came to Ibn Munabbih and asked him about al-Hasan, saying: 'How is his intellect?' He informed him, then said: 'We find in the books that Allah, glorified be He, does not give a servant knowledge by which he acts upon the path of guidance, then snatch away his intellect until Allah takes him to Himself.'"],[264,"Among the worst of people in rank with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a scholar who does not benefit from his knowledge."],[265,"Whoever increases in knowledge increases in pain."],[266,"Studying knowledge for an hour at night is better than spending it in prayer."],[267,"I divide the night into three parts: one third I sleep, one third I stand in prayer, and one third I recall the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[268,"Whoever seeks something of knowledge by which he seeks the face of Allah, glorified be He, Allah grants him from it what suffices him."],[269,"I asked al-Sha'bi about a hadith, and he narrated it to me. I said, 'It is attributed to the Prophet ﷺ.' He said, 'No, upon those below the Prophet ﷺ is more beloved to us. If there is addition or omission, it is upon those below the Prophet ﷺ.'"],[270,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muhaqala and muzabana."],[271,"When Abu al-Darda' narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say: 'This or its like, or its similar, or its form.'"],[272,"When Abu al-Darda' narrated a hadith, he would say: 'O Allah, except thus, or like its form.'"],[273,"I never missed a Thursday evening except that I would come to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud in it. I never heard him say for anything at all, 'The Messenger of Allah said' until one evening, when he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.' He said: His eyes filled with tears and his jugular veins swelled. I saw him with his buttons undone, and he said: 'Or its like, or its similar, or resembling it.'"],[274,"When Ibn Mas'ud narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the days, his face would darken and he would say: 'Thus or its like, thus or its like.'"],[275,"Al-Sha'bi said to me: 'Have you seen so-and-so who says, \"The Messenger of Allah said, the Messenger of Allah said\"? I sat with Ibn 'Umar for two years, or a year and a half, and I never heard him narrate anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except this hadith.'"],[276,"I sat with Ibn 'Umar for a year and did not hear him mention a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[277,"Abdullah used to narrate to us two or three hadiths in a month."],[278,"Anas b. Malik passed by us, so we said, 'Narrate to us some of what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'And would I be absolved?'"],[279,"Anas narrated little from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say, 'or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.'"],[280,"When Anas narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say, 'or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.'"],[281,"I went out with Sa'd to Makkah, and I did not hear him narrate any hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we returned to Madinah."],[282,"\"When Umar joined the Ansar as they were leaving the city, he said, 'Do you know why I have accompanied you?' We replied, 'For the sake of the Ansar.' He said, 'Indeed, you are going to meet a people whose tongues are fluent with the recitation of the Quran, like the shaking of palm trees. Do not argue with them by talking about the Prophet's ﷺ sayings, for I am a partner with you.' I refrained from talking about anything, while having heard as my companions heard.\""],[283,"Umar b. al-Khattab sent a group of the Ansar to Kufah, and he sent me with them. He walked with us until he reached Sirar, and Sirar is water on the road to Madinah. He began to shake the dust from his feet, then said, 'You are going to Kufah, and you will come to a people who have a humming with the Quran. They will come to you and say, \"The companions of Muhammad have arrived! The companions of Muhammad have arrived!\" They will come to you and ask you about hadith. Know that the most complete ablution is three times, and two suffice.' Then he said, 'You are going to Kufah, and you will come to a people who have a humming with the Quran. They will say, \"The companions of Muhammad have arrived! The companions of Muhammad have arrived!\" They will come to you and ask you about hadith. So narrate little from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I am your partner in that.' Qarazah said, 'I used to sit among a group who would mention hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was among those who had memorized it best, but when I remembered Umar's instruction, I remained silent.'"],[284,"He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said...' Then he trembled, then he said, 'something like that or more than that.'"],[285,"I accompanied Ibn Umar to Madinah, and I did not hear him narrate any hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he said, 'I was with the Prophet ﷺ when some palm hearts were brought, and he said, \"Among trees there is a tree like the Muslim man.\" I wanted to say that it was the date palm, but I looked and saw that I was the youngest of the people, so I remained silent.' Umar said, 'I wished you had said it, and I would have owed such and such.'"],[286,"I never heard Jabir b. Zayd ever say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' out of reverence and caution against lying about him."],[287,"Abu Hurayrah came to Ka'b asking about him while Ka'b was among the people. Ka'b said, 'What do you want from him?' He said, 'Indeed, I do not know anyone among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who has better memorization of his hadith than me.' Ka'b said, 'Indeed, you will not find anyone seeking something but that he will eventually be satiated with it at some time, except a seeker of knowledge or a seeker of this world.' He said, 'Are you Ka'b?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'It is for something like this that I came.'"],[288,"It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which people are most knowledgeable?' He said, 'One who gathers the knowledge of the people to his own knowledge, and every seeker of knowledge is hungry for more knowledge.'"],[289,"I was in a circle where the elders were, and they were exchanging narrations among them, including Abid b. Amr. A young man at the edge of the group said, 'Engage in the remembrance of Allah, may Allah bless you.' The people looked at one another, wondering, 'In what way did he see us?' Then one of them said, 'Who commanded you to do this? If you do it again, we will certainly do such and such.'"],[290,"“The best gathering is a gathering in which wisdom is spread and in which mercy is hoped for.”"],[291,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he looked up at the sky and then said, “This is the time when knowledge will be snatched away from people until they are able to get nothing of it.” Ziyad b. Labid al-Ansari said, “O Messenger of Allah, how will it be snatched away from us when we have read the Qur’an? By Allah, we will certainly keep reading it and will make our women and children read it.” He said, “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ziyad! I used to count you among the jurists of the people of Madinah. This Torah and Gospel are with the Jews and Christians, but what do they avail them?” Jubayr said: Then I met Ubadah b. al-Samit and said, “Will you not listen to what your brother Abu al-Darda’ says?” I informed him of what he had said. He said, “Abu al-Darda’ spoke the truth. If you wish, I will tell you of the first knowledge to be removed from people: it is humility. Soon you will enter the congregational mosque and not see a single humble man in it.”"],[292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like my superiority over the least of you.” Then he recited this verse: “Only those of His servants who have knowledge fear Allah” [Fatir 28]. Then he said, “Indeed Allah, His angels, the inhabitants of His heavens and His earths, and the whale in the sea send blessings upon those who teach people good.”"],[293,"“A man will not be a scholar until he does not envy those above him, does not despise those below him, and does not seek a price for his knowledge.”"],[294,"I heard Abd al-A‘la al-Taymi say: “Whoever is given knowledge that does not make him weep is hardly likely to have been given knowledge that benefits him, because Allah, Exalted is He, described the scholars,” then he recited: “Indeed those who were given knowledge” [al-Isra’ 107] up to “they weep” [al-Isra’ 109]."],[295,"“You will not be a scholar until you have three qualities: you do not oppress those above you, you do not despise those below you, and you do not take worldly compensation for your knowledge.”"],[296,"“You will not be a scholar until you are a learner, and you will not be a scholar through knowledge until you act upon it. It is enough of a sin for you that you never cease disputing, and it is enough of a sin for you that you never cease arguing, and it is enough of a lie for you that you never cease speaking about other than the sake of Allah ﷻ.”"],[297,"I said to al-Hasan one day regarding something he said, “O Abu Sa‘id, this is not what the jurists say.” He said, “Woe to you! Have you ever seen a true jurist? The true jurist is the one who renounces this world, desires the Hereafter, is insightful in the affairs of his religion, and is constant in the worship of his Lord.”"],[298,"He was asked, “Who is the most knowledgeable in jurisprudence among the people of Madinah?” He said, “The one among them who is most God-fearing toward his Lord ﷻ.”"],[299,"“The true jurist is the one who fears Allah, Exalted is He.”"],[300,"“The jurist, the true jurist, is the one who does not make people despair of Allah’s mercy, does not permit them to commit disobedience to Allah, does not make them feel secure from Allah’s punishment, and does not abandon the Qur’an out of aversion to it in favor of something else. Indeed, there is no good in worship without knowledge, no knowledge without understanding, and no recitation without reflection.”"],[301,"“The jurist, the true jurist, is the one who does not make people despair of Allah’s mercy, does not make them feel secure from Allah’s punishment, and does not permit them to commit disobedience to Allah. Indeed, there is no good in worship without knowledge, no good in knowledge without understanding, and no good in recitation without reflection.”"],[302,"I verily find the description of a people who learn for other than acting, and acquire understanding for other than worship, and seek the world by the work of the Hereafter, and wear the skins of sheep while their hearts are more bitter than aloes. Is it in Me that they are deceived, or is it Me that they would beguile? I swear by Myself that I will surely bring upon them such a trial as will leave the forbearing among them bewildered."],[303,"Beware of the sinful scholar. This reached ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, and he wrote to him, being alarmed by it: What is the sinful scholar? He said: So he wrote back to him: Hirm, O Commander of the Believers, by Allah I intended nothing but good by it. It is an imam who speaks with knowledge but acts with sin, and he confuses the people, so they go astray."],[304,"\"Whoever wants his religion to be honored, should not enter the presence of the ruler, should not spend time with women, and should not argue with people of desires.\""],[305,"Beware of disputation and argumentation in religion. Do not argue with a scholar or an ignorant person. As for the scholar, he will withhold his knowledge from you and not care what you do. As for the ignorant person, he will harden your heart and not obey you."],[306,"Sulaymān b. Dāwūd ﷺ said to his son: \"Abandon contentious argumentation, for its benefit is little and it stirs up enmity between brothers.\""],[307,"\"Whoever makes his religion a target for disputes will frequently change his position.\""],[308,"\"ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz wrote to the people of Madinah: Whoever worships without knowledge, what he corrupts is more than what he sets right. Whoever counts his speech as part of his action, his speech becomes little except in what concerns him. Whoever makes his religion a target for disputes, his shifting will become frequent.\""],[309,"A man asked him about something from the desires, and he said: \"Keep to the religion of the Bedouin and the boy in the Qur'anic school, and turn away from anything besides that.\""],[310,"\"If you see a people producing something without their common people, then they are upon the foundation of misguidance.\""],[311,"Iblīs said to his allies: \"From what thing do you come to the children of Adam?\" They said: \"From everything.\" He said: \"Do you come to them from the direction of seeking forgiveness?\" They said: \"Far from it. That is something joined with tawḥīd.\" He said: \"I will surely sow among them something from which they will not seek Allah's forgiveness.\" He said: So he sowed among them the desires."],[312,"\"I do not know which of the two favors upon me is greater: that He guided me to Islam, or that He protected me from these desires.\""],[313,"\"If a man were to fast for all eternity and stand in prayer for all eternity, then were killed between the Corner and the Station, Allah would raise him on the Day of Resurrection with those whom he thought were upon guidance.\""],[314,"\"If a man were to place his head upon the Black Stone and fast by day and stand in prayer by night, Allah would raise him on the Day of Resurrection with his desire.\""],[315,"Ali, be like the bee among people, for there is nothing in birds that does not belittle it. If birds knew the blessings within their innards, they would not do this to it. Mix with people with your tongues, bodies, and enrich them with your actions and hearts. Indeed, a person will have what he has earned, and he will be on the Day of Judgment with those whom he loves."],[316,"How excellent a minister of knowledge is sound judgment."],[317,"\"To be pleased with his knowledge.\""],[318,"When we narrate a hadith to you according to its meaning, that is sufficient for you."],[319,"\"He would neither hasten nor delay when he spoke, and Al-Hasan would both precede and postpone when he spoke.\""],[320,"Al-Hasan used to speak with one original saying, while conversations differed."],[321,"The likeness of a hypocrite is that of a sheep between two folds or between two flocks.\" Ibn Umar said: \"No, he only said such-and-such.\" He said: \"When Ibn Umar heard the Prophet ﷺ, he did not add to it, subtract from it, exceed it, or fall short of it."],[322,"Al-Sha'bi, al-Nakha'i, and al-Hasan used to narrate a hadith sometimes one way and sometimes another. I mentioned that to Muhammad b. Sirin, and he said: \"If only they had narrated it as they heard it, that would have been better for them.\""],[323,"I hear a hadith with a grammatical error, and I deliberately make the same error, following what I heard."],[324,"Mujahid saw Tawus in a dream as if he was in the Ka'bah praying with his face covered, and the Prophet ﷺ was at the door of the Ka'bah. He said to him: \"O servant of Allah, uncover your face and make your recitation audible.\" He said: \"It was as if he interpreted it as knowledge, and after that he became expansive in hadith.\""],[325,"The world is accursed, and accursed is whatever is in it, except one who learns good or teaches it."],[326,"People are [of two types]: the scholar and the student, and between that is ignorance, with no goodness in it."],[327,"They used to say: \"The death of a scholar is a breach in Islam that nothing can fill as long as night and day alternate.\""],[328,"\"A gathering in which knowledge is disputed is more beloved to me than the amount of salah (prayer) I can perform. Perhaps someone will hear a word and benefit from it for a year or for the rest of their life.\""],[329,"I do not know of any deed more virtuous than seeking knowledge and preserving it for one by whom Allah Almighty intends good."],[330,"Abu Darda said, \"Learn before knowledge is taken away, because the taking away of knowledge is the taking away of scholars. And the scholar and the learner are equal in reward.\""],[331,"From al-Dahhak regarding {But be rabbaniyyun because you teach the Book} [Al 'Imran: 79], he said: \"It is incumbent upon everyone who recites the Quran to be a faqih.\""],[332,"From al-Hasan: {Were it not that the rabbis and the priests forbade them} [al-Ma'idah: 63]. He said: \"The wise, the learned.\""],[333,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr, who said: {Be rabbaniyyun} [Al 'Imran: 79]. He said: \"Learned, skilled in jurisprudence.\""],[334,"\"For knowledge, what is required is memorization, acting upon it, listening, attentiveness, and dissemination.\""],[335,"\"The most ignorant of people is the one who abandons what he knows; the most knowledgeable of people is the one who acts upon what he knows; and the best of people is the one most humble before Allah, Mighty and Sublime.\""],[336,"Those who are obsessed are never satisfied: (1) those who are obsessed with [sacred and salvific] knowledge are never satisfied with it, and (2) those who are obsessed with worldly possessions are never satisfied with them.So, whoever makes the hereafter his concern, and devotes himself to it and focuses on it, Allah will take care of his worldly affairs, and He will put contentment in his heart. But whoever makes this world his concern, and devotes himself to it and focuses on it, Allah will expose his ruin, and He will make him [obsess over] his needs: such that he will not wake up except as a needy person, and he will not reach evening [while having pursued his needs] except as a needy person [anxious, feeling unfulfilled]."],[337,"The one who possesses knowledge and the one who possesses worldly possessions are not equal, and both of them cannot be satisfied. As for the person of knowledge, their contentment with the Merciful (Allah) increases. But as for the person of the world, they indulge in transgression. Then Abdullah recited, \"No! Indeed, man transgresses because he sees himself self-sufficient.\" (Quran, Surah Al-Alaq: 7) Someone else said, \"Indeed, only the scholars fear Allah among His servants.\" (Quran, Surah Fatir: 28)"],[338,"\"Who fears Allah is knowledgeable.\""],[339,"Two are insatiable and never have enough: a seeker of knowledge and a seeker of this world."],[340,"\"Whoever seeks knowledge and attains it will have a double portion of reward; if he does not attain it, he will have a single portion of reward.\""],[341,"It has reached me that Dawud the Prophet ﷺ used to say in his supplication: \"Glory be to You, O Allah, You are my Lord, exalted above Your Throne, and You have placed fear of You upon those in the heavens and the earth. The closest of Your creation to You in station is the one most fearful of You. What knowledge does one have who does not fear You? And what wisdom does one have who does not obey Your command?\""],[342,"\"Abdullah bin Mas'ud said, 'Tomorrow, be either a scholar or a student, for there is no good in anything else.'\""],[343,"\"There will be trials in which a man will wake up a believer and become an disbeliever by evening, except the one whom Allah gives life through knowledge.\""],[344,"\"Go forth as a scholar or a student, and do not go forth as anything in between, for what is between that is ignorance. Indeed, the angels spread their wings for a man who goes out seeking knowledge, out of pleasure with what he is doing.\""],[345,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about two men among the Children of Israel: one was a scholar who would pray the prescribed prayer, then sit and teach people goodness; the other would fast during the day and stand in prayer at night. Which of them is better? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The superiority of this scholar who prays the prescribed prayer, then sits and teaches people goodness, over the worshipper who fasts during the day and stands in prayer at night is like my superiority over the least of you.\""],[346,"I entered the mosque and saw Al-Aswad bin Suray' narrating and Humaid bin Abdul Rahman mentioning knowledge in one corner of the mosque. So, I inclined towards which of them should I sit with. I felt sleepy, then someone approached me and said, \"Towards which of them did you incline to sit? If you wish, I can show you the place where Gabriel ﷺ used to sit from Humaid bin Abdul Rahman.\""],[347,"I was sitting with Abu al-Darda' in the mosque of Damascus when a man came to him and said: \"O Abu al-Darda', I have come to you from al-Madinah, the city of the Messenger ﷺ, for a hadith that reached me from you, which you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"Did you come for trade?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Did anything else bring you?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever travels a path seeking knowledge therein, Allah makes easy for him thereby a path to one of the paths of Paradise. Indeed, the angels lower their wings out of pleasure for the seeker of knowledge, and indeed the seeker of knowledge is asked forgiveness for by whoever is in the heavens and the earth, even the fish in the water. Indeed, the superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like the superiority of the moon over all the stars. Indeed, the scholars are the heirs of the prophets; the prophets did not leave behind a dinar or a dirham, but they left behind knowledge. Whoever takes hold of it has taken an abundant share.'\""],[348,"\"The teacher of good is sought forgiveness for by everything, even the fish in the sea.\""],[349,"There is no man who treads a path seeking knowledge therein but Allah makes easy for him thereby a path to Paradise. And whoever is slowed down by his deeds is not hastened forward by his lineage."],[350,"No man treads a path seeking knowledge therein but Allah makes easy for him thereby a path to Paradise. And whoever is slowed down by his deeds is not hastened forward by his lineage."],[351,"About rain, \"And We have certainly made the Qur'an easy for remembrance, so is there any who will remember?\" [Al-Qamar 17] He said, \"Is there anyone who seeks goodness that I may guide him towards it?\""],[352,"Abu al-Darda', when he saw students of knowledge, would say: Welcome to the seekers of knowledge. And he would say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined good upon you."],[353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by two gatherings in his mosque and said: 'Both are upon good, and one of them is superior to the other. As for these, they call upon Allah and desire Him, so if He wills He gives them and if He wills He withholds from them. As for these, they learn fiqh and knowledge, and teach the ignorant, so they are superior. I was only sent as a teacher.' He said: Then he sat among them."],[354,"That he said to his son: O my son, 'knowledge is better than action.'"],[355,"There is no gift better than a word of wisdom that you give to your brother."],[356,"The superiority of the scholar over the devoted worshipper is one hundred degrees, between each two degrees a distance of five hundred years of the running of a swift, lean horse."],[357,"Allah raises those who have been given knowledge above those who believe by degrees."],[358,"Whoever death comes to while he is seeking knowledge to revive Islam thereby, between him and the Prophets there is one degree in Paradise."],[359,"\"Umar's knowledge decreased by two thirds,\" I said to Ibrahim. He replied, \"Umar's knowledge decreased by nine tenths.\""],[360,"\"Whenever a group of people gather in one of the houses of Allah to study and discuss the Book of Allah among themselves, the angels lower their wings in humility and tranquility. They encompass them with their wings until they are immersed in their discussions. If someone traverses a path seeking knowledge, Allah makes their path to Paradise easy. And those whose actions are slow in progressing, their lineage will not hasten them.\""],[361,"I went early to Safwan b. 'Assal al-Muradi intending to ask him about wiping over the leather socks. He said: What has brought you? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: Shall I give you glad tidings? I said: Yes. He said: He traced the hadith back to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks.'"],[362,"I heard Sufyan forty years ago say: 'Seeking hadith was never more excellent than it is today.' They said to Sufyan: They seek it without intention? He said: 'Their seeking it is an intention.'"],[363,"We sought this knowledge while we had no great intention in it, then Allah granted us intention in it afterward."],[364,"“Some people sought knowledge, not intending thereby Allah Almighty nor what is with Him.” He said: “But knowledge did not cease to accompany them until they intended thereby Allah and what is with Him.”"],[365,"“The scholars are three: a man who lived in his knowledge and people lived with him in it; a man who lived in his knowledge and no one lived with him in it; and a man in whose knowledge people lived, and it was a burden against him.”"],[366,"Musa ﷺ said: “O Lord, which of Your servants is most wise?” He said: “The one who judges for people as he judges for himself.” He said: “O Lord, which of Your servants is richest?” He said: “The one most content with what I have apportioned for him.” He said: “O Lord, which of Your servants is most fearful of You?” He said: “The one most knowledgeable of Me.”"],[367,"It used to be said: The scholars are three: a scholar of Allah who fears Allah but is not a scholar of Allah’s command; a scholar of Allah and a scholar of Allah’s command who fears Allah – that is the complete scholar; and a scholar of Allah’s command who is not a scholar of Allah and does not fear Allah – that is the wicked scholar."],[368,"Knowledge is of two types: knowledge in the heart – that is the beneficial knowledge; and knowledge on the tongue – that is Allah’s proof against the son of Adam."],[369,"“Learn, learn; and when you know, act.”"],[370,"Whoever seeks knowledge for four things will enter the Fire – or words to that effect: to vie with the scholars thereby, to argue with the foolish thereby, to turn people’s faces toward him thereby, or to receive something from the rulers thereby."],[371,"I read in a book that I was told was from the words of ‘Isa ﷺ : You work for this world while you are provided for in it without working; and you do not work for the Hereafter while you are not provided for in it except by working. Woe to you, evil scholars! You take the wage and you neglect the deed. Soon the Lord of the deed will seek His deed, and soon you will depart from the wide world into the darkness and narrowness of the grave. Allah forbids you from sins just as He commanded you to pray and fast. How can one be among the people of knowledge when he resents his provision and disdains his station, while he knows that that is from Allah’s knowledge and power? How can one be among the people of knowledge when he suspects Allah in what He has decreed for him and is not pleased with anything that befalls him? How can one be among the people of knowledge when his world is more favored by him than his Hereafter, and he is more desirous of this world? How can one be among the people of knowledge when his destination is his Hereafter, yet he is turning toward his world and what harms him is more desirable to him – or he said: more beloved to him – than what benefits him? How can one be among the people of knowledge when he seeks speech to report it and does not seek it to act upon it?"],[372,"It is said, \"Learn knowledge and benefit from it, and do not learn it for the purpose of showing off, for it is very likely that if your life span is prolonged, the person with knowledge will show off with his knowledge just as the person with a fine garment shows off with his garment.\""],[373,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about evil, and he said: “Do not ask me about evil; ask me about good,” saying it three times. Then he said: “Indeed, the worst of evil is the wicked scholars, and the best of good is the best scholars.”"],[374,"Only one in whom two qualities were combined used to seek this knowledge: intellect and devotion. If he was devout but not intelligent, he said: “This is a matter that none but the intelligent attain,” so he did not seek it. If he was intelligent but not devout, he said: “This is a matter that none but the devout attain,” so he did not seek it. Al-Sha‘bī said: “I fear that today it is sought by one who has neither of the two: neither intellect nor devotion.”"],[375,"“A man would not seek knowledge until he had worshiped for forty years before that.”"],[376,"Whoever seeks knowledge to argue with the foolish, to vie with the scholars, or to turn people's faces to him, he is in the Fire of Hell."],[377,"Whoever seeks knowledge to vie with the scholars, to argue with the foolish, or to attract people's attention to himself, Allah will admit him to Hell."],[378,"A man's hadith is only preserved according to the measure of his intention."],[379,"I certainly think that a man forgets knowledge he used to know because of a sin he committed."],[380,"It has reached me that Luqman the Wise used to say to his son: 'O my son, do not learn knowledge to vie with the scholars, to argue with the foolish, or to show off in gatherings. And do not abandon knowledge out of indifference to it and desire for ignorance. O my son, choose gatherings with your own eyes. When you see people remembering Allah, sit with them, for if you are knowledgeable, your knowledge will benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will teach you. Perhaps Allah will look upon them with His mercy, and it will reach you along with them. And when you see people not remembering Allah, do not sit with them, for if you are knowledgeable, your knowledge will not benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will increase you in error. Perhaps Allah will look upon them with punishment, and it will reach you along with them.'"],[381,"Do not tell falsehood to the wise, lest they hate you. Do not tell wisdom to the foolish, lest they deny you. Do not withhold knowledge from its people, lest you sin. Do not place it with other than its people, lest you be considered ignorant. Indeed, you have a duty regarding your knowledge just as you have a duty regarding your wealth."],[382,"Jesus son of Mary ﷺ used to say: 'Do not withhold knowledge from its people, lest you sin. Do not spread it among other than its people, lest you be considered ignorant. Be a gentle physician who places his medicine where he knows it will benefit.'"],[383,"Do not feed your food to one who does not desire it."],[384,"Luqman said to his son: 'O my son, do not learn knowledge to vie with the scholars, to argue with the foolish, or to show off in gatherings. And do not abandon knowledge out of indifference to it and desire for ignorance. When you see people remembering Allah, sit with them: if you are knowledgeable, your knowledge will benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will teach you. Perhaps Allah will look upon them with His mercy, and it will reach you along with them. And when you see people not remembering Allah, do not sit with them: if you are knowledgeable, your knowledge will not benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will increase you in error or inability. Perhaps Allah will look upon them with displeasure, and it will reach you along with them.'"],[385,"O bearers of knowledge, act upon it. For the scholar is only one who acts upon what he knows and whose knowledge matches his action. There will be people who carry knowledge that does not go beyond their collarbones: their actions contradict their knowledge, and their inner state contradicts their outward appearance. They sit in circles, each one vying with the other, until a man becomes angry with his companion for sitting with someone else and leaving him. Those are people whose deeds do not ascend to Allah, the Exalted, from those gatherings of theirs."],[386,"It is enough knowledge for a man that he fears Allah, and enough ignorance for a man that he is impressed with his own knowledge."],[387,"If the least knowledgeable person of this Ummah had his knowledge taken by a nation among the nations, that nation would be rightly guided."],[388,"If a man were to attain a chapter of knowledge and act upon it, it would be better for him than the world and all that is in it, if it were his and he made it for the Hereafter."],[389,"No servant increases in knowledge and increases in desire for the world except that he increases in distance from Allah."],[390,"No servant increases in knowledge of Allah except that people increase in closeness to the mercy of Allah through him."],[392,"O my son, hold fast to wisdom, for all good lies in wisdom. It elevates the young over the old, the slave over the free, increases a master in mastery, and seats the poor in the assemblies of kings."],[393,"What would we be were it not for the words of the scholars?"],[394,"Do not sit with people of desires and do not argue with them, for I do not feel safe that they might immerse you in their misguidance or confuse you regarding what you used to know."],[395,"Sa'id b. Jubayr saw me sitting with Talq b. Habib and said to me, 'Did I not see you sitting with Talq b. Habib? Do not sit with him.'"],[396,"He has innovated, so if he has innovated, do not convey the greeting of peace to him."],[397,"Ibrahim did not consider backbiting an innovator to be backbiting."],[398,"It is only called desire (hawā) because it causes its possessor to fall."],[399,"Beware of disputation, for it is an hour of the scholar's ignorance, and through it Satan seeks to make him slip."],[400,"Two men from the people of desires entered upon Ibn Sīrīn and said, 'O Abū Bakr, shall we narrate a hadith to you?' He said, 'No.' They said, 'Then shall we recite to you a verse from the Book of Allah?' He said, 'No. Either you two leave me or I will leave.' Then they left. Some of the people said, 'O Abū Bakr, what harm would it have done if they recited to you a verse from the Book of Allah, exalted is He?' He said, 'I feared that they would recite a verse to me and distort it, and that would settle in my heart.'"],[401,"A man from the people of desires said to Ayyūb, 'O Abū Bakr, may I ask you about a word?' He said, 'He turned away while gesturing with his finger, and not even half a word.' Saʿīd gestured to us with his right little finger."],[402,"A man asked Saʿīd b. Jubayr about something, and he did not answer him. It was said to him, and he said, 'A fidgeter.'"],[403,"Do not sit with the people of disputes, for they are the ones who plunge into the signs of Allah."],[404,"Do not sit with the people of desires, do not argue with them, and do not listen to them."],[405,"They are only called the people of desires because they fall into the Fire."],[406,"I have not seen anyone among the people, the noble and the lowly, with whom they are equal, except Ṭāwūs, and he swears by it."],[407,"We used to dislike writing down knowledge until the authorities compelled us to do so; then we disliked withholding it from anyone."],[408,"They spoke to Muhammad about a man, meaning he was narrating to him, and he said, 'If he were a man from the Zanj, with me he and ʿAbdullāh b. Muḥammad would be equal in this.'"],[409,"Salm b. Qutayba asked Ṭāwūs about a question, and he did not answer him. It was said to him, 'This is Salm b. Qutayba.' He said, 'That makes him even lighter in my sight.'"],[410,"“I did not fear anyone among the people as much as I feared Khalid b. Ma‘dan.”"],[411,"“We used to hold Ibrahim in awe like the awe of a ruler.”"],[412,"Sa‘id b. Jubayr one day related a hadith, so I stood up to him and asked him to repeat it. He said, “Not every hour do I milk so that I may drink.”"],[413,"“Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman disliked relating hadith on the road.”"],[414,"We were with Sa‘id b. Jubayr and he related a hadith, so a man said to him, “Who related this to you, or from whom did you hear this?” He became angry and withheld his hadith from us until he got up."],[415,"“If I had been gentle with Ibn ‘Abbas, I would have obtained much knowledge from him.”"],[416,"“I have not seen anyone more honoring of knowledge than my father.”"],[417,"I said to Tawus, “So-and-so related to me such-and-such.” He said, “If your companion is reliable, then take from him.”"],[418,"“None should relate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except the trustworthy.”"],[419,"“They would not ask about the chain of narration. Then later they asked, so that they might know who was a person of Sunnah and take from him, and who was not a person of Sunnah and not take from him.”"],[420,"“You relate to me from two men, but they do not care from whom they took their hadith.” Abu Muhammad ‘Abdullah said, “I do not think he heard it.”"],[421,"“When you relate to me, then relate to me from Abu Zur‘ah, for he”"],[422,"Indeed this knowledge is religion, so let a man look to whom he takes his religion from."],[423,"When they came to a man to take from him, they looked at his prayer, his demeanor, and his appearance."],[424,"When they came to a man to take knowledge from him, they looked at his prayer, his demeanor, and his appearance, then they took from him."],[425,"From him, we observe when he prays. If he performs it excellently, we sit with him and say, \"He performs it better than others.\" And if he performs it poorly, we stand away from him and say, \"He performs it worse than others.\" Abu Ma'mar said that his statement is like this."],[426,"Indeed this knowledge is religion, so look to whom you take your religion from."],[427,"I said to Tawus, 'So-and-so narrated to me such-and-such.' He said, 'If your companion is reliable, then take from him.'"],[428,"Bushayr b. Ka'b came to Ibn Abbas and began narrating to him. Ibn Abbas said, 'Repeat the first hadith for me.' Bushayr said to him, 'I do not know whether you recognized all my hadith and rejected this one, or recognized this one and rejected all my hadith?' Ibn Abbas said, 'We used to narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when no lie was told against him, but when the people mounted the difficult and the tractable, we abandoned narrating from him.'"],[429,"We used to memorize hadith, and hadith was memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until you mounted the difficult and the tractable."],[430,"It is imminent that devils whom Solomon ﷺ had bound will appear, teaching people jurisprudence in religion."],[431,"\"Consider from whom you take this narration, for it is your religion.\""],[432,"One should be cautious of explaining the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as one is cautious of explaining the Quran."],[433,"Are you not afraid that you will be punished or swallowed up by the earth because you say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said' and 'So-and-so said'?"],[434,"No one has any opinion concerning the Book of Allah. The opinion of the leaders is only regarding what no Book has been revealed about and no Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been established for. And no one has any opinion concerning a Sunnah established by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[435,"\"O people, Allah has not sent a prophet after your Prophet, nor has He sent down after this Book that He revealed to him any book. So whatever Allah made lawful on the tongue of His Prophet is lawful until the Day of Resurrection, and whatever He made unlawful on the tongue of His Prophet is unlawful until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, I am not one who originates, but one who follows; I am not better than you except that I am the most burdened of you. Indeed, it is not for anyone of Allah's creation to be obeyed in disobedience to Allah. Indeed, have I made myself heard?\""],[436,"Tawus used to pray two rak'ahs after 'Asr, and Ibn 'Abbas said to him, \"Leave them.\" He said, \"It was only forbidden that it be taken as a ladder [to other prayers].\" Ibn 'Abbas said, \"Indeed, prayer after 'Asr has been forbidden, so I do not know whether you will be punished for it or rewarded, because Allah says: 'It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have any choice in their affair. And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly gone astray in clear error'\""],[437,"That 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a copy of the Torah and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is a copy of the Torah.\" He remained silent, and he began to read while the face of the Messenger of Allah changed. Abu Bakr (may Allah have mercy on him) said, \"May the bereaved women lose you! Do you not see the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" So 'Umar looked at the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger. We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if Musa appeared to you and you followed him and abandoned me, you would have gone astray from the right path. And if he were alive and reached my prophethood, he would have followed me.\""],[438,"Sa'id b. al-Musayyib saw a man praying two rak'ahs after 'Asr, making takbir, and said to him, \"O Abu Muhammad, will Allah punish me for prayer?\" He said, \"No, but Allah will punish you for opposing the Sunnah.\""],[439,"\"While a man was strutting in two garments, Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he will continue to sink in it until the Day of Resurrection.\" A young man, whom he named, who was wearing a fine garment, said to him, \"O Abu Hurayrah, is this how that young man who was swallowed by the earth used to walk?\" Then he struck with his hand and stumbled a stumble that nearly broke him. Abu Hurayrah said, \"For the nostrils and the mouth: {Indeed, We are sufficient for you against the mockers}\""],[440,"I saw a young man in the mosque throwing pebbles, and an old man said to him, \"Do not throw pebbles, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid throwing pebbles.\" The young man became heedless and thought that the old man would not notice him, so he threw pebbles. The old man said to him, \"I tell you that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding throwing pebbles, and you still throw them? By Allah, I will not attend your funeral, nor visit you in illness, nor ever speak to you.\""],[441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade throwing pebbles and said, \"It does not catch game, nor does it wound an enemy, but it breaks a tooth and gouges an eye.\""],[442,"'Abdullah b. Mughaffal saw a man from his companions throwing pebbles and said, \"Do not throw pebbles, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid throwing pebbles, or he used to dislike throwing pebbles. And he said, 'It does not wound an enemy, nor is game caught with it, but it may gouge an eye and break a tooth.'\" Then he saw him after that throwing pebbles and said to him, \"Did I not tell you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid it? Then I see you throwing pebbles. By Allah, I will never speak to you.\""],[443,"Ibn Sirin narrated a hadith from the Prophet ﷺ to a man, and a man said, \"So-and-so said such and such.\" Ibn Sirin said, \"I narrate to you from the Prophet ﷺ and you say, 'So-and-so and so-and-so said such and such'? I will never speak to you.\""],[444,"\"When one of you's wife asks permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her.\" A man named Fulān b. 'Abdullah said, \"Then by Allah, I will prevent her.\" Ibn 'Umar turned to him and insulted him with an insult I had never seen him insult anyone before, then said, \"I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you say, 'Then by Allah, I will prevent her'?\""],[445,"\"He forbade two dirhams for one dirham.\" A man said, \"I see no harm in this, hand to hand.\" 'Ubadah said, \"I say the Prophet ﷺ said, and you say, 'I see no harm in it'? By Allah, no roof will ever shelter me and you together.\""],[446,"\"Do not come to women at night.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was returning from a journey, and two men slipped away to their families, and each of them found a man with his wife."],[447,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, he would stop at the mosque and then say, 'Do not engage with women at night.' Two men who had heard his statement then went to their respective homes and found each of their wives with another man.\""],[448,"A man came to Sa'id b. al-Musayyib to bid him farewell before going for Hajj or 'Umrah. He said to him: Do not leave until you pray, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one leaves after the call to prayer from the mosque except a hypocrite, unless a man is taken out by a need while he intends to return to the mosque.\" He said: My companions are at al-Harrah. He said: So he left. He said: Sa'id did not cease speaking about him until he was informed that he fell from his riding beast and his thigh was broken."],[449,"\"Do not tire people.\""],[450,"\"Indeed hearts have vigor and responsiveness, and they have turning away and retreat. So narrate to people as long as they are attentive to you.\""],[451,"It used to be said: \"Narrate to a people as long as they are attentive to you with their faces; when they turn away, know that they have needs.\""],[452,"\"Do not write anything from me except the Qur'an. Whoever has written anything from me other than the Qur'an, let him erase it.\""],[453,"\"They asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to write from him, but he did not grant them permission.\""],[454,"He used to say: O Shibak, shall I repeat the hadith to you? I never wanted any hadith to be repeated to me at all."],[455,"Az-Zuhri brought a hadith, and I met him on some road, so I took hold of his rein and said, 'O Abu Bakr, repeat to me the hadith which you told us.' He said, 'Do you want me to repeat the hadith?' I said, 'Would you not have the hadith repeated?' He said, 'No.' I said, 'And do you not write it down?' He said, 'No.'"],[456,"Qatadah \"disliked writing; when he heard the sound of writing, he disapproved of it and groped for it with his hand.\""],[457,"Ibrahim \"disliked writing, meaning knowledge.\""],[458,"\"If I were to keep a written record, I would have kept the letters of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[459,"It is only edges."],[460,"\"To my Abdah, 'Do not make a book immortal within me.'\""],[461,"The translation of the passage is: \"I only wrote about Muhammad the conversation of the depths, and when I memorized it, I erased it.\""],[462,"\"I never wrote down any hadith at all.\""],[463,"\"I never wrote down anything at all.\""],[464,"I asked 'Abidah for a piece of leather on which to write, and he said, \"O Ibrahim, do not ever preserve a written record from me.\""],[465,"\"To write the Hadith in books and say it resembles the Qur'an.\""],[466,"'Abidah called for his books and erased them on his deathbed, saying, \"I fear that people will come after me who will not put them in their proper places.\""],[467,"\"To write knowledge in notebooks.\""],[468,"\"This knowledge remained mighty: men received it directly from one another, until it fell into the written pages, and those who were not worthy carried it—or entered into it.\""],[469,"\"Al-Hasan used to write and to have others write.\""],[470,"Indeed, there are people who have a book that they admire, and they have not ceased with it until they brought it to me, and I have erased it. Then, he said, \"The people of the book before you were destroyed because they embraced the books of their scholars and abandoned the book of their Lord.\""],[471,"I said, \"No\". If I find a book to read, he said, \"No\"."],[472,"I said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, \"Will you not have us write it down? For we do not memorize.\" He said, \"No. We will never write it down for you, nor will we make it a Qur'an. But memorize from us just as we memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[473,"\"Abu Hurayrah did not write down, nor did he have others write down.\""],[474,"He used to write down the hadith of his father, and Abu Musa saw it and erased it."],[475,"Ibn Sirin said, \"No, by Allah, I have never written a hadith.\""],[476,"\"So he set up a curtain between his council and the rest of his house.\" They said, \"Therefore, his companions used to enter upon him and discuss matters in that place. Then Marwan came to his companions and said, 'I see nothing except that we have been deceived.' Then he approached me and I said, 'And what is that?' He said, 'I see nothing except that we have deceived you.' I said, 'And what is that?' He said, 'We have appointed a man who sits behind this curtain and writes down what you dictate and what you say.'\""],[477,"I said to Ibrahim, \"Salim is more complete in hadith than you?\" He said, \"Salim used to write.\""],[478,"I traveled with my father to Yazid ibn Muawiya in Hawarin after the death of Muawiya to offer our condolences and congratulate him on the caliphate. There was a man in its mosque saying, \"Indeed, it is one of the signs of the Hour that the wicked will be elevated, and the good will be lowered. Indeed, it is one of the signs of the Hour that speech will be widespread, and actions will be concealed. Indeed, it is one of the signs of the Hour that the [mathnā] will be recited, and no one will be found has changed it.\" He was asked, \"What is the mathnā?\" He replied, \"It is what is written from books other than the Quran. So, adhere to the Quran, for with it you are guided, rewarded, and questioned.\" I did not know who the man was, and I narrated this incident later in Homs. A man from the people said to me, \"Do you not know him?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"That was Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him).\""],[479,"And he said, \"Verily, those before you perished by following their books and neglecting their own book.\" Husayn said, \"Indeed, if it was from the Quran or the Sunnah, he would not have erased it, but it was from the books of the People of the Book.\""],[480,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a shoulder blade with writing on it and said, \"It is enough misguidance for a people to turn away from what their Prophet brought toward what a prophet other than their prophet brought—or a book other than their book.\" Then Allah, Mighty and Exalted, revealed: {Is it not enough for them that We sent down to you the Book, which is recited to them? Indeed in that is a mercy and a reminder for a people who believe} [al-'Ankabut 51], the verse."],[481,"I saw a man with a page on which was written: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. I said to him, \"Copy it for me,\" but he seemed stingy with it, then promised to give it to me. I came to 'Abdullah, and there it was in front of him. He said, \"What is in this book is innovation, tribulation, and misguidance. This and its likes destroyed those before you: they wrote them down, their tongues found them pleasing, and their hearts absorbed them. I charge every person who knows the location of a book to point it out. I swear by Allah.\" Shu'bah said: Did he swear by Allah? He said: I think he swore: if it were mentioned to have been at a monastery in Hind—I think he means a place in al-Kufah far away—I would go to it, even on foot."],[482,"\"The children of Israel wrote a book, so they followed it and left the Torah.\""],[483,"\"Some people hear my words, then depart and write them down. I do not permit anyone to write down anything except the Book of Allah, Mighty and Exalted.\""],[484,"“I did not write black upon white, nor did I seek to have a hadith dictated back to me by any person.”"],[485,"“There is no one among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who has more hadith from the Prophet ﷺ than I, except what there is from ‘Abdullah b. ‘Amr, for he used to write while I did not write.”"],[486,"I used to write everything which I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I intended (by it) to memorise it. The Quraysh prohibited me saying: Do you write everything that you hear from him while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is a human being: he speaks in anger and pleasure? So I stopped writing, and mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He signalled with his finger to him mouth and said: Write, by Him in Whose hand my soul lies, only right comes out from it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3646)"],[487,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I wish to narrate from your hadith, and I want to seek help from the writing of my hand along with my heart, if you see fit.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said—if he did say it—: “Memorize my hadith, then seek help from your hand along with your heart.”"],[488,"While we were around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ writing, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, “Which of the two cities will be conquered first—Constantinople or Rome?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “No, rather the city of Heraclius first.”"],[489,"Write to me what has become established with you of hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the hadith of ‘Amrah, for I have feared the obliteration of knowledge and its passing away.”"],[490,"“‘Umar b. ‘Abd al-‘Aziz wrote to the people of Madinah: Look into the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and write it down, for I have feared the obliteration of knowledge and the passing away of its people.”"],[491,"They find fault with us for writing, though Allah, Exalted is He, has said: {Its knowledge is with my Lord in a Book}."],[492,"It used to be said, “Whoever does not write down his knowledge, his knowledge is not counted as knowledge.”"],[493,"Anas used to say to his sons, “O my sons, bind this knowledge down.”"],[494,"“I saw Aban writing in the presence of Anas on a slate.”"],[495,"He asked Abu Umamah al-Bahili about writing down knowledge, and he said, “There is no harm in that.”"],[496,"When I was about to part from him, I brought him his book, read it to him, and said to him, “Is this what I heard from you?” He said, “Yes.”"],[497,"I would hear hadith from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas at night and write it down on the middle part of the saddle."],[498,"Nothing makes life desirable to me except al-Sadiqah and al-Waht. As for al-Sadiqah, it is a scroll I wrote from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and as for al-Waht, it is land given as charity by Amr b. al-As which he used to tend."],[499,"Bind knowledge with writing."],[500,"Bind this knowledge with writing."],[501,"I was traveling with Ibn Abbas on the road to Makkah at night, and he would narrate hadith to me, so I would write it on the middle part of the saddle until morning, then I would copy it out."],[502,"I used to write in the presence of Ibn Abbas on a scroll, and I would write on my sandals."],[503,"I used to sit with Ibn Abbas and write on the scroll until it became full, then I would turn over my sandals and write on their backs."],[504,"\"I saw them writing the explanation at Mujahid's.\""],[505,"I saw them writing in the presence of al-Bara with the tips of reeds on their palms."],[506,"Ibn Abbas narrated a hadith to me, and I said, 'Shall I write it down from you?' He said, 'He gave me permission, but barely.'"],[507,"Hisham b. Abd al-Malik wrote to his governor to ask me about a hadith. Raja said, 'I had forgotten it, had it not been that it was with me written down.'"],[508,"Ata b. Abi Rabah would be asked and what he answered would be written down in front of him."],[509,"He saw Nafi, the client of Ibn Umar, dictating his knowledge and it being written down in front of him."],[510,"Sufyan would write down the hadith at night in the wall [i.e., on its surface], and when morning came he would copy it, then erase it."],[511,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz came out to us for the noon prayer with a sheet of paper, then he came out to us for the afternoon prayer and it was with him. I said to him, \"O Commander of the Faithful, what is this document?\" He said, \"This is a hadith.\""],[512,"Al-Hasan called his sons and the sons of his brother and said, \"O my sons and the sons of my brother, you are the young of a people, and soon you will be the elders of others. So learn knowledge; and whoever of you cannot narrate it\" — or he said \"memorize it\" — \"let him write it down and place it in his house.\""],[513,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever introduces a good practice that is followed, he will receive its reward and a reward equivalent to that of those who follow it, without that detracting from their reward in their slightest. And whoever introduces a bad practice that is followed, he will receive its sin and a burden of sin equivalent to that of those who follow it, without that detracting from their burden in the slightest.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 203)"],[514,"\"Whoever calls to guidance will have the like of the rewards of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever calls to misguidance will have the like of the sins of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their sins.\""],[515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and urged the people to give charity, but they were slow until anger appeared on his face. Then a man from the Ansar brought a purse, and the people followed one after another until joy was seen on his face. He said, \"Whoever establishes a good sunnah will have its reward and the like of the reward of those who act upon it, without anything being diminished from their rewards. And whoever establishes an evil sunnah will have its burden and the like of the burden of those who act upon it, without anything being diminished from their burdens.\""],[516,"\"I will have the greatest reward among you on the Day of Resurrection, because I have my reward and the like of the reward of those who follow me.\""],[517,"Whoever calls to a matter — even if a man calls a man — on the Day of Resurrection he will be made to stand with it, [with the sin] clinging to his neck. Then he recited: {And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned.}"],[518,"\"Four things are given to a man after his death: one-third of his wealth if he had it before that and was obedient to Allah, righteous children who pray for him after his death, good deeds that the man practiced and are carried out after his death, and intercession if a hundred people intercede for him.\""],[519,"\"To make him sit on a chair, but he refused.\""],[520,"\"He disliked leaning against the pillar.\""],[521,"Ibrahim would not begin the hadith until he was asked."],[522,"Al-Harith b. Qays al-Ju'fi, who was one of the companions of Abdullah, and they were impressed with him — a man or two men would sit with him and he would narrate to them, but when they became many he would get up and leave them."],[523,"It was said to him when Abdullah died, \"If you would sit and teach the people the sunnah?\" He said, \"Do you want my heel to be trampled?\""],[524,"We came to Ubayy b. Ka'b to talk to him. When he stood up, we stood up and we were walking behind him. Umar, ؓ , overtook us and followed him, and Umar struck him with the whip. He said: He protected himself with his forearms and said: O Commander of the Believers, what are we doing? He said: \"Do you not see? A trial for the one followed, and a humiliation for the follower?\""],[525,"\"They used to dislike that their heels be trampled.\""],[526,"Muhammad b. Sirin, when a man walked with him, would stop and say: \"Do you have a need?\" If he had a need, he fulfilled it. And if he returned to walking with him, he would stop and say: \"Do you have a need?\""],[527,"\"Beware of having your heels trampled.\""],[528,"He saw people following Sa'id b. Jubayr. He said: I think he said he forbade them and said: \"This act of yours, or this walking of yours, is a humiliation for the follower and a trial for the one followed.\""],[529,"I consulted Muhammad about a building I wanted to build in al-Kalla'. He said: He advised me and said: \"When you want the foundation of the building, let me know so I can come with you.\" He said: So I came to him. He said: While we were walking, a man came and walked with him. So he stopped and said: \"Do you have a need?\" He said: No. He said: \"Either no, then go.\" Then he turned to me and said: \"You too, go.\" He said: So I went until I took a different road."],[530,"Al-Rabi', when they came to him, would say: \"I seek refuge in Allah from your evil\" - meaning his companions."],[531,"We were with Khabbab b. al-Aratt, and his companions gathered around him while he was silent. It was said to him: Will you not narrate to your companions? He said: \"I fear saying to them what I do not do.\""],[532,"\"I wish I could escape from my deeds with neither for me nor against me.\""],[533,"Ibn Mas'ud was walking while people were treading on his heel. He said: \"Do not tread on my heel. By Allah, if you knew what I shut my door upon, no man among you would follow me.\""],[534,"\"A trial for the one followed, and a humiliation for the follower.\""],[535,"They walked behind Ali. He said: \"Keep away from me the slapping of your sandals, for it corrupts the hearts of foolish men.\""],[536,"The pattering of sandals behind men rarely delays the foolish."],[537,"When one or two men sat with him, he would get up and withdraw."],[538,"The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about his life and how he spent it, about his knowledge and what he did with it, about his wealth, from where he acquired it and on what he spent it, and about his body and how he wore it out."],[539,"Allah will not leave the servants on the Day of Resurrection, the day when people stand before the Lord of the Worlds, until He asks them about four things: about their lives and how they spent them, about their bodies and how they wore them out, about what they earned and on what they spent it, and about what they did with what they knew."],[540,"\"Do not depart from a servant on the Day of Judgment until he is asked about four things: his life, how he fared in it, his body, how he wore it out, his wealth, how he earned it and how he spent it, and his knowledge, what he did with it.\""],[541,"Tawus said to me: “Whatever you learn, learn it for yourself, for trustworthiness has departed from people.”"],[542,"I met people when a devout person, when he was devout, was not known by his speech, but was known by his deeds. That is beneficial knowledge."],[543,"Convey from me even if a single verse, and narrate from the Children of Israel without harm, and whoever deliberately lies against me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to be overcome in three things: that we enjoin good, forbid evil, and teach people the Sunnah."],[545,"Whenever we sat with Abu Umamah, he would bring us great matters of hadith and say to us: “Listen, understand, and convey from us what you hear.”"],[546,"I came to Abu Dharr while he was sitting at the middle jamrah, and the people had gathered around him asking for rulings. A man came and stood before him, then said: “Were you not forbidden from giving legal rulings?” He raised his head and said: “Are you a watcher over me? If you placed the sharp sword on this,” and he pointed to the back of his neck, “then I thought I could utter a word I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before you carried it out on me, I would utter it.”"],[547,"Should you be a mufti?” I said: “No, but I do not feel safe that you may depart and we remain.” He said: “Abu al-‘Aliyah has spoken the truth.”"],[548,"Abidah used to come to Abdullah every Thursday and ask him about matters he had missed. Most of what is preserved from Abdullah is from what Abidah asked him about."],[549,"“What is the matter with you that you do not ask me? Have you gone bankrupt?”"],[550,"“Knowledge is a treasure house, and the key to open it is asking.”"],[551,"“Whoever’s face becomes delicate (i.e., is shy), his knowledge becomes delicate (i.e., limited).”"],[552,"\"He who is too shy and arrogant does not learn.\""],[553,"He used to gather his sons and say, “O my sons, learn, for if you are the young ones of a people, perhaps you will be the elders of others. How ugly it is for a shaykh to be asked and not have knowledge.”"],[554,"Ibn ‘Abbas “would place the fetter on my feet and teach me the Qur’an and the Sunan.”"],[555,"“Whoever takes leadership quickly harms much knowledge, and whoever does not take leadership keeps seeking and seeking until he attains.”"],[556,"“Knowledge that is not spoken of is like treasure that is not spent from.”"],[557,"“The example of knowledge that is not benefited from is like the example of treasure that is not spent in the way of Allah.”"],[558,"“Knowledge is like springs that people come to; this one and that one draw from it, and Allah benefits many by it. A wisdom that is not spoken of is like a body without a soul. Knowledge that is not brought out is like treasure not spent from. The example of a scholar is like a man who carries a lamp on a dark road; whoever passes by benefits from its light, and everyone supplicates for him for good.”"],[559,"Three things follow a man after his death: ongoing charity after him, his child’s prayer for him, and knowledge that he spread and is acted upon after him."],[560,"When a person dies, his deeds come to an end except for three: knowledge that is benefited from, or a continuing charity for him, or a righteous child who supplicates for him."],[561,"He said when he arrived at Basra: \"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ sent me to you to teach you the Book of your Lord and your Sunnah, and to clean your roads.\""],[562,"Whoever seeks knowledge, it will be an expiation for what has passed."],[563,"I stayed in Madinah for three days, and I had no need except that I had already completed it, except that there was a man whom they were expecting, who used to narrate a hadith. So I stayed until he arrived, and then I asked him."],[564,"I would ride to one of the garrison towns for a single hadith just to hear it."],[565,"We used to hear a narration in Basra from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we were not satisfied until we rode to Madinah and heard it from their own mouths."],[566,"Dawud the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Say to the seeker of knowledge: let him take a staff of iron and two sandals of iron, and seek knowledge until the staff breaks and the sandals wear out.\""],[567,"He sleeps and then I put my cloak under my head and lay down until midday. Then he says, \"When did you come here, O cousin of the Messenger of Allah?\" I say, \"A long time ago.\" He says, \"What a terrible thing you have done! Why didn't you inform me?\" I say, \"I wanted you to come to me after you had fulfilled your need.\""],[568,"The following sentence translates to: \"The majority of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were narrated by the people of this neighborhood among the Ansar, and by Allah, if I came to a man from them and it was said that he was sleeping, I would leave him until he woke up to ask him about his hadith.\""],[569,"\"If I had accompanied Ibn Abbas, I would have acquired much knowledge from him.\""],[570,"I used to come to the door of Urwah and sit at the door. If I had wished to enter, I would have entered, but it was out of respect for him."],[571,"\"When the messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I said to a man from the Ansar, 'O so and so, come let us ask the companions of the Prophet ﷺ , for they are still numerous today.' He marveled at me and said, 'O Ibn Abbas, do you think people are in need of you? Among the people there are companions of the Prophet ﷺ , who do you see?' I left this matter and approached (the companions) to ask them. If there was a hadeeth from a person, I went to him while he was speaking, I leaned my cloak on his door, and the wind blew dust on my face. He would come out and see me, and say, 'O cousin of the Messenger of Allah, what brought you here? Did you not send for me so that I could come to you?' I would say, 'No, I am more deserving of coming to you, so I ask you about the hadeeth.' The man would then remain until he saw me, and the people had gathered around me, and he said, 'This boy was more intelligent than me.'\""],[572,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ traveled to Fadalah b. Ubayd while he was in Egypt. He came to him while he was stretching a rope for a she-camel of his. He said, \"Welcome.\" He said, \"Indeed, I have not come to you as a visitor, but I and you heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I hoped that you might have some knowledge of it.\" He said, \"Such and such.\""],[573,"He entered the market and haggled with a man over a garment. The man said, \"It is yours for such and such. By Allah, if it were anyone other than you, I would not have given it to him.\" He said, \"Would you do that?\" After that, he was not seen buying from the market or selling until he met Allah ﷻ."],[574,"He would not buy from anyone he knew."],[575,"Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr distributed wealth among the reciters of Kufa when Ramadan began, and he sent two thousand dirhams to Abd al-Rahman b. Ma'qil, saying: 'Use it to help you in this month of yours.' Abd al-Rahman b. Ma'qil returned it and said: 'We did not recite the Quran for this.'"],[576,"Umar ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Abdullah ibn Salam, 'Who are the knowledgeable ones?' He replied, 'Those who act upon what they know.' Umar then asked, 'What removes knowledge from the hearts of men?' Abdullah ibn Salam replied, 'Greed.'"],[577,"Nothing adorns anything more beautifully than forbearance adorns knowledge."],[578,"The adornment of knowledge is the forbearance of its people."],[579,"Knowledge has never been carried in the like of a vessel of forbearance."],[580,"The adornment of knowledge is the forbearance of its people."],[581,"Wisdom dwells in the calm, serene heart."],[582,"You have disgraced knowledge and removed its light. If Umar ؓ had caught us, he would have caused us pain."],[583,"Learn knowledge, and when you have learned it, restrain it and do not mix it with laughter or play, lest hearts reject it."],[584,"Whoever laughs a laugh spits out a mouthful of knowledge."],[585,"Umar said to Ka'b: 'Who are the masters of knowledge?' He said: 'Those who act upon what they know.' He said: 'Then what removes knowledge from the hearts of the scholars?' He said: 'Greed.'"],[586,"\"I was going to 'Amr ibn Nu'man when the Messenger of Mus'ab ibn Zubayr came to him. It was during the month of Ramadan, and he had one thousand dirhams with him. The Messenger said, 'Indeed, the commander (Ali) sends you his greetings, and he said, 'We have not left a noble reciter except that we have sent him something good. So, rely on these two (dirhams) for your expenses this month.' He (Mus'ab) said, 'Convey my greetings to the commander, and tell him that by Allah, we have not recited the Qur'an seeking the worldly life and its wealth.'\""],[587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade certain things on the day of Khaybar, including the domestic donkey and others. Then he said: 'A man will soon recline on his couch and be told of my hadith, and he will say: Between us and you is the Book of Allah. Whatever we find in it as lawful we will deem lawful, and whatever we find in it as unlawful we will deem unlawful. Beware, indeed what the Messenger of Allah forbids is like what Allah, exalted be He, forbids.'"],[588,"The Sunnah is a judge over the Quran, and the Quran is not a judge over the Sunnah."],[589,"Jibril used to descend upon the Prophet ﷺ with the Sunnah just as he would descend upon him with the Qur'an."],[590,"The Sunnah is of two kinds: a Sunnah whose adoption is obligatory and abandoning it is disbelief, and a Sunnah whose adoption is a virtue and abandoning it entails no blame."],[591,"One day he narrated a hadith from the Prophet ﷺ, and a man said, 'In the Book of Allah there is something that contradicts this.' He said, 'I do not think I should narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while you object to it with the Book of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew the Book of Allah, exalted be He, better than you.'"],[592,"When you are told a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, think of it in the way that is most fitting, most guided, and most God-fearing."],[593,"When you are told a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, think of it in the way that is most guided, most God-fearing, and most fitting."],[594,"When he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"],[595,"From Sulayman al-Ahwal."],[596,"Study hadith together, for hadith stimulates hadith."],[597,"Study hadith together, for hadith stimulates hadith."],[598,"Study hadith together, for hadith stimulates hadith."],[599,"Tawus said to me, \"Come with us to sit with the people.\""],[600,"\"Study this hadith together, lest it slip away from you, for it is not like the Qur'an, compiled and preserved. If you do not study this hadith together, it will slip away from you. Let none of you say, 'I narrated yesterday, so I will not narrate today.' Rather, narrate yesterday, and narrate today, and narrate tomorrow.\""],[601,"\"Repeat the hadith and review it, for if you do not remember it, it will go. Let no man say of a hadith he has narrated, 'I have narrated it once.' For whoever heard it increases in knowledge by it, and he hears it who has not heard it.\""],[602,"\"Study it together, for reviving the hadith is by reviewing it together.\""],[603,"\"Study the hadith together, for mentioning it is its life.\""],[604,"Ibn Shihab used to narrate to the bedouins."],[605,"Isma'il b. Raja' used to gather the boys of the kuttab, narrating to them, and thereby he would memorize it."],[606,"\"Narrate your hadith to whoever desires it and to whoever does not desire it, for it becomes like an imam to you which you recite.\""],[607,"\"When you hear a hadith from us, then study it among yourselves.\""],[608,"We used to come to al-Hasan, and when we left him we would discuss among ourselves."],[609,"When one of you wants to narrate a hadith, let him repeat it three times."],[610,"Abdullah bin Shaddad, may Allah have mercy on you, how many conversations have you revived in my heart that were dead."],[611,"Al-Harith b. Yazid al-Ukli, Ibn Shubrumah, al-Qa'qa' b. Yazid, and Mughirah: when they prayed the late night prayer, they would sit for fiqh and nothing would separate them until the call to the morning prayer."],[612,"There is no harm in staying up at night for fiqh."],[613,"There is no harm in staying up at night for fiqh."],[614,"Studying knowledge for an hour at night is better than spending the whole night in worship."],[615,"We used to come to Jabir b. 'Abdullah, and when we left him we would discuss, and Abu al-Zubayr was the one with the best memorization of his hadith."],[616,"Ibn Shihab remembered a hadith one night after the night prayer while he was sitting having performed ablution. He said: 'That remained his sitting place until morning.' Marwan said: 'He kept on discussing the hadith.'"],[617,"When I met 'Ubaydullah b. 'Abdullah, it was as if I had burst open a sea with him."],[618,"Al-Harith al-Ukli and his companions used to sit together at night and mention fiqh."],[619,"Discuss this hadith with one another, for its life is in its discussion."],[620,"Abdullah said to his companions when they came to him: 'Do you sit together?' They said: 'We are not left without that.' He said: 'Do you visit one another?' They said: 'Yes, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman; a man among us misses his brother and walks in search of him to the farthest part of Kufa until he meets him.' He said: 'You will remain in good as long as you do that.'"],[621,"The bane of knowledge is forgetfulness, and neglecting to review it with others."],[622,"The bane of hadith is forgetfulness."],[623,"Everything has a bane, and the bane of knowledge is forgetfulness."],[624,"The bane of knowledge is forgetfulness, and squandering it is to narrate it to those unworthy of it."],[625,"The blight of knowledge is forgetfulness."],[626,"Study this hadith together and visit one another, for if you do not, it will be effaced."],[627,"I used to think that I had acquired a good share of knowledge; then I sat with Ubayd Allah, and it was as if I had been in one of the mountain ravines."],[628,"If you were to unite the people upon a single thing? He said: It would not please me that they did not differ. He said: Then he wrote to the horizons and to the garrison cities that each people should judge by what their jurists had agreed upon."],[629,"I would not like the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to have not differed, for had they agreed upon something and a man abandoned it, he would have abandoned the Sunnah; but since they differed, if a man takes the saying of one of them, he has taken the Sunnah."],[630,"How often Ibn Abbas held an opinion and then abandoned it."],[631,"Uthman b. Affan said to me: Umar said to me: I have formed an opinion regarding the grandfather. If you see fit to follow it, follow it. Uthman said: If we follow your opinion, it is sound; and if we follow the opinion of the elder before you, what an excellent man of opinion he was. He said: Abu Bakr used to make him a father."],[632,"I presented the hadiths of jurisprudence to al-Shabi, and he approved them for me."],[633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man who passed through the mosque with arrows: “Hold them by their tips.” He said: Yes."],[634,"I said to ‘Abd al-Rahman b. al-Qasim: Did you hear your father narrate from ‘A’ishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss her while he was fasting? He said: Yes."],[635,"Mansur wrote a hadith to me. Then I met him and said: Should I narrate it from you? He said: Is it not that when I wrote to you, I had already narrated to you?"],[636,"I presented a book to him, and then I said, \"Should I tell him about you?\" He replied, \"Who else told you about it other than me?\""],[637,"Presenting the book and the hadith are the same."],[638,"Presenting the book and the hadith are the same."],[639,"Zaid ibn Aslam used to say, \"To him, the study of the Quran and Hadith are equally important.\" And the son of Abu Dhi'b used to agree with that."],[640,"He used to regard presenting and narrating as the same."],[641,"Ibrahim used to say: He stands to his left. Then I narrated to him from Sumay‘ al-Zayyat, from Ibn ‘Abbas, that the Prophet ﷺ made him stand to his right, and he accepted it."],[642,"‘Umar adjured the people, saying: Did any of you hear from the Prophet ﷺ about the fetus? Al-Mughirah b. Shu‘bah stood up and said: He ruled in it a male or female slave. Then he adjured the people again. The one in whose favor the ruling was made stood up and said: The Prophet ﷺ ruled for me in it a male or female slave. Then he adjured the people again. The one against whom the ruling was made stood up and said: The Prophet ﷺ ruled against me a ghurrah, a male or female slave. I said: Will you rule against me in it for what did not eat, nor drink, nor cry, nor speak? If such is to be made equal, then it is more worthy to be made equal. The Prophet ﷺ inclined to him with something he had and said: “Poetry?” ‘Umar said: Had I not learned of the ruling of the Prophet ﷺ, I would have made it a diyah between two diyahs."],[643,"If you want to know the mistake of your teacher, sit with someone else."],[644,"We discussed in Makkah a man who dies. I said: Her waiting period is from the day the news comes to her, according to the saying of al-Hasan, Qatadah, and our companions."],[645,"We came to Umar concerning al-musharrakah, and he did not make them sharers. Then we came to him the following year, and he made them sharers. We said to him, and he said: “That was according to what we judged then, and this is according to what we judge now.”"],[646,"In the past, scholars used to despise the knowledge of worldly people. Worldly people would aspire to their knowledge and would dedicate their lives to obtain it. However, today, scholars have dedicated their knowledge to worldly people. As a result, worldly people have lost interest in their knowledge and have belittled them by exerting their worldly possessions upon them."],[647,"Is there someone in the city who met one of the companions of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ ? They said to him, \"Abu Hazim.\" So he sent for him, and when he entered upon him, he said to him, \"O Abu Hazim, what is this harshness?\" Abu Hazim said, \"O Commander of the Believers, what harshness have you seen from me?\" He said, \"The people of Madinah came to me, but you did not come.\" He said, \"O Commander of the Believers, I swear by Allah that you should not say anything that you did not know about me before this day, nor have I seen you.\" Sulaiman turned to Muhammad bin Shihab al-Zuhri and said to him, \"The old man is right and I made a mistake.\" Sulaiman said, \"O Abu Hazim, why do we dislike death?\" Abu Hazim said, \"Because you have ruined the hereafter and"],[648,"“O possessor of knowledge, act upon your knowledge, give from the surplus of your wealth, and withhold the surplus of your speech except something of hadith that benefits you with your Lord. O possessor of knowledge, that which you have learned but not acted upon cuts off your proof and your excuse with your Lord when you meet Him. O possessor of knowledge, that which you have been commanded of obedience to Allah will surely occupy you from that which you have been forbidden of disobedience to Allah. O possessor of knowledge, do not be strong in the work of others while weak in the work of your own self. O possessor of knowledge, do not let that which belongs to others occupy you from that which belongs to you. O possessor of knowledge, honor the scholars, press close to them, listen to them, and leave off disputing with them. O possessor of knowledge, honor the scholars for their knowledge and belittle the ignorant for their ignorance, but do not distance them; rather draw them near and teach them. O possessor of knowledge, do not relate a hadith in a gathering until you understand it, and do not answer a man about his statement until you know what he said to you. O possessor of knowledge, do not be deceived by Allah and do not be deceived by people, for deception by Allah is abandoning His command, and deception by people is following their whims. And beware of Allah as He warned you of Himself, and beware of people and their trial. O possessor of knowledge, the light of day is not complete except with the sun; likewise wisdom is not complete except with obedience to Allah. O possessor of knowledge, crops are not good except with water and soil; likewise faith is not good except with knowledge and action. O possessor of knowledge, every traveler takes provision, and when he needs provision he will find what he took; likewise every worker, when he needs his work in the Hereafter, will find what he did in this world. O possessor of knowledge, if Allah wants to urge you to His worship, know that He only wants to show you your honor with Him, so do not turn to other than Him and return from His honor to His contempt. O possessor of knowledge, if you transport stones and iron, it would be easier for you than to speak to one who does not understand your speech. And the example of one who speaks to one who does not understand his speech is like one who calls out to the dead and sets a table for the people of the graves.”"],[650,"“If the Bedouin is truthful, he will enter Paradise.”"],[651,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Peace be upon you, O youth of Banu Abd al-Muttalib. He said: “And upon you.” He said: I am a man from your maternal uncles, from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr, and I am the messenger of my people to you and their delegate. I will ask you and press my question upon you, and I will adjure you and press my adjuration of you. He said: “Ask, O brother of Banu Sa'd.” He said: Who created you and created those before you, and who is the Creator of those after you? He said: “Allah.” He said: Then I adjure you by that—is it He who sent you? He said: “Yes.” He said: Who created the seven heavens and the seven earths and made provision flow between them? He said: “Allah.” He said: Then I adjure you by that—is it He who sent you? He said: “Yes.” He said: We found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that we should pray five prayers in the day and night at their times, so I adjure you by that—is it He who commanded you? He said: “Yes.” He said: Then we found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that we should take from the surplus of our wealth and return it to our poor, so I adjure you by that—is it He who commanded you with that? He said: “Yes.” Then he said: As for the fifth, I will not ask you about it, and I have no need of it. Then he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will act upon them and whoever obeys me from my people. Then he turned back, and the Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molars appeared, then said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he is truthful he will surely enter Paradise.”"],[652,"Banu Sa'd b. Bakr sent Dimam b. Tha'labah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came to him, made his camel kneel at the door of the mosque, then hobbled it, then entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among his companions. Dimam was a tough man with shaggy hair and two locks. He stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Which of you is the son of Abd al-Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib.” He said: Muhammad? He said: “Yes.” He said: O son of Abd al-Muttalib, I will ask you and be stern in questioning, so do not feel anger in yourself against me. He said: “I will not feel anger in myself, so ask whatever appears to you.” He said: I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will be after you—did Allah send you to us as a messenger? He said: “O Allah, yes.” He said: Then I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will be after you—did Allah command you that we worship Him alone, associating nothing with Him, and that we cast off these rivals which our fathers used to worship besides Him? He said: “O Allah, yes.” He said: Then I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will be after you—did Allah command you that we pray these five prayers? He said: “O Allah, yes.” He said: Then he began mentioning the obligations of Islam one by one—zakah, fasting, Hajj, and all the rites of Islam—adjuring him at each obligation as he had adjured him for the one before it. When he finished, he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and I will perform these obligations and avoid what you have forbidden me. Then he said: I will not add nor detract. Then he turned to his camel, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when he turned away: “If the one with the two locks is truthful, he will enter Paradise.” He went to his camel, released its hobble, then left until he came to his people. They gathered around him, and the first thing he said was: Evil be to al-Lat and al-Uzza! They said: Stop, O Dimam! Beware of leprosy, beware of madness, beware of elephantiasis. He said: Woe to you! By Allah, they neither harm nor benefit. Allah has sent a Messenger and revealed to him a Book by which He has rescued you from what you were in. And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I have come to you from him with what he has commanded you and forbidden you. By Allah, by the evening of that day there was not a man or woman in his settlement except as a Muslim. Ibn Abbas said: We have not heard of a delegate of a people better than Dimam b. Tha'labah."],[653,"Purification is half of faith, and al-hamdu lillah fills the scale, and la ilaha illallah and Allahu akbar fill what is between the heaven and the earth, and prayer is light, and charity is proof, and wudu is radiance, and the Quran is an argument for you or against you, and all people go out and sell themselves, either freeing themselves or destroying themselves."],[654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ counted them on my hand—or he said: he counted them on his hand while his hand was in mine: “Subhan Allah is half of the scale, al-hamdu lillah fills the scale, Allahu akbar fills what is between the heaven and the earth, wudu is half of faith, and fasting is half of patience.”"],[655,"From Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, who said that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Stay steadfast and you will not be able to count [the rewards] and know that the best of your deeds is prayer.\" Another narration states, \"Indeed, prayer is among the best of your deeds.\" And another narration states, \"No one will maintain their ablution except a believer.\""],[656,"He (Thawban, servant of the Messenger of Allah) heard that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Be sincere and approach (good deeds) closely, and the best of your deeds is prayer. No one remains constant in ablution (wudu) except a believer.\""],[657,"Sa'd used to pray all the prayers with one wudu."],[658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded to perform wudu for every prayer, whether he was pure or not. When that became difficult for him, he was commanded to use the siwak for every prayer. Ibn Umar believed he had strength for that, so he did not abandon wudu for every prayer."],[659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform wudu for every prayer until the day of the conquest of Makkah, when he prayed the prayers with one wudu and wiped over his leather socks. Umar said to him: I saw you do something you did not used to do. He said: “I did it deliberately, O Umar.”"],[660,"“I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far away.”"],[661,"“When the Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far away.”"],[662,"Whoever applies kohl, let him apply it an odd number of times. Whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no blame. Whoever cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number. Whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no blame. Whoever eats, let him pick his teeth. What he removes with the toothpick, let him spit out, and what he works loose with his tongue, let him swallow. Whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no blame. Whoever goes to relieve himself, let him conceal himself. If he finds nothing but a heap of sand, let him turn his back to it, for the devils play with the posteriors of the children of Adam. Whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no blame."],[663,"The most beloved thing with which the Prophet ﷺ would conceal himself for relieving himself was a target or a thicket of palm trees."],[664,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"You are my messenger to the people of Makkah. Say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and commands you that when you go out, do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it.\""],[665,"When you go to relieve yourselves, do not face the qiblah with feces or urine, and do not turn your backs to it.\" He said: Then Abu Ayyub said: \"We came to Syria and found latrines built facing the qiblah, so we would turn aside and seek Allah's forgiveness.\""],[666,"He would not raise his garment until he drew close to the ground."],[667,"I climbed onto the roof of our house and saw the Prophet ﷺ sitting on two bricks facing Jerusalem."],[668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a people's garbage dump and urinated while standing."],[669,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the lavatory, he would say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from male and female devils.\""],[670,"When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him take three stones with him to clean himself with, for they will suffice him."],[671,"Three stones, none of which is dung,\" meaning for cleaning oneself."],[672,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"You are my messenger to the people of Makkah. Say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and commands you that when you go out, do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it.\""],[673,"«None of you should touch his private part with his right hand, nor wipe himself with his right hand.»"],[674,"«I am to you only like a father to his child: I teach you. So do not face the qiblah, nor turn your backs to it; and when you cleanse yourself, do not cleanse yourself with your right hand.»"],[675,"He ﷺ, «when he went to relieve himself, I and a boy would bring him a small spear and a water vessel, and he would perform ablution.»"],[676,"He ﷺ, «when he came out of the privy, the boy would bring a vessel of water with which he used to clean himself.»"],[677,"Hudhayfah used to «clean himself with water.»"],[678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Bring me water for purification.\" Then, he entered the bathroom, so I brought him water. He performed istinja (cleaning after using the toilet), then rubbed his hand with soil, and then washed his hands."],[679,"When he ﷺ came out of the privy, he would say: «Your forgiveness.»"],[680,"«I have emphasized the siwak to you much.»"],[681,"«I have emphasized the siwak to you much.»"],[682,"«Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them with it at every prayer.»"],[683,"«The siwak is a purifier for the mouth, a means of pleasure to the Lord.»"],[684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, «when he stood for the night prayer, he would rub his mouth with the siwak.»"],[685,"Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from treachery."],[686,"The key to prayer is purification; its prohibition is the takbir, and its release is the taslim."],[687,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa‘."],[688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution with a makkuk and bathe with five makakik."],[689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us in our home. I would take a vessel of ours, which held a mudd and a third, or a quarter of a mudd, and pour water for him, and he would perform ablution washing each part three times."],[690,"The Messenger of Allah said: \"There is no ablution for one who does not mention the Name of Allah (before doing it).\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 397)"],[691,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and he cupped water and washed his hands three times. I said to him, \"What is 'cupped water and washed three times'?\" He said, \"He washed his hands three times.\""],[692,"Uthman performed ablution: he rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face three times, his hands three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet three times. Then he said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution as I have performed ablution.\" Then he said, \"Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then prays two rak‘ahs without letting his mind wander in them, his previous sins will be forgiven.\""],[693,"Abdullah b. Zayd called for a vessel of water and poured it over his hands, washing them three times. He washed his face three times and his hands up to the elbows twice each. Then he said, \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.\""],[694,"Shall I not tell you, or shall I not inform you, of the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He performed ablution washing each part once, or he said once each."],[695,"He performed ablution washing each part once, and he combined the rinsing of the mouth and sniffing of water into the nose."],[696,"Shall I not guide you to what Allah erases sins by and increases good deeds by?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Performing ablution thoroughly despite difficulties, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after the prayer."],[697,"“We were commanded to perform the ablution thoroughly.”"],[698,"Ali entered the courtyard after he had prayed Fajr. He sat in the courtyard, then said to a servant of his, “Bring me water for purification.” The servant brought him a vessel containing water and a basin. Abd Khayr said: We were sitting watching him. He put his right hand into it, filled his mouth, rinsed his mouth, inhaled water into his nose, and blew it out with his left hand. He did this three times, then he said, “Whoever would like to see the purification of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this is his purification.”"],[699,"“Whoever inhales water into the nose should expel it, and whoever cleans himself with stones should use an odd number.”"],[700,"I saw Uthman performing ablution and he ran his fingers through his beard, and he said, “This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.”"],[701,"“When you perform ablution, perform it thoroughly and run your fingers between your fingers.”"],[702,"“Woe to the heels from the Fire. Perform the ablution thoroughly.”"],[703,"He used to pass by us while the people were performing ablution from the water container, and he would say, “Perform the ablution thoroughly.” Abu al-Qasim ﷺ said, “Woe to the heel from the Fire.”"],[704,"I saw Uthman perform ablution and wipe his head and his ears, their outer and inner parts, then he said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do as I did, or like what I did.”"],[705,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution at al-Juhfah. He rinsed his mouth and inhaled water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed his hands three times, then wiped his head, and washed his feet until he cleaned them, then he wiped his head with water other than the leftover from his hands."],[706,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[707,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once (washing each part) once and sprinkled water over his private parts."],[708,"I asked Maymunah, my maternal aunt, about the ghusl of the Prophet ﷺ from janabah. She said: A vessel would be brought to him, and he would pour with his right hand over his left, washing his private parts and whatever had been affected. Then he would perform the ablution he performs for prayer. Then he would wash his head and the rest of his body. Then he would move and wash his feet. Then a towel would be brought to him, and he would place it in front of him and shake off his fingers, but he would not touch it."],[709,"One night I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. He asked (me), \"Have you got water with you?\" I replied, \"Yes\" So he got down from his she-camel and went away till he disappeared in the darkness of the night. Then he came back and I poured water for him from the pot (for the ablution). He washed his face and hands while he was wearing a woollen cloak (the sleeves of which were narrow), so he could not take his arms out of it. So he took them out from underneath the cloak. Then he washed his forearms and passed his wet hands over his head. Then I tried to take off his Khuffs (socks made from thick fabric or leather), but he said, \"Leave them, for I have performed ablution before putting them on.\" And so he passed his wet hands over them. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5799)"],[710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."],[711,"I saw Ali perform ablution and wipe over his two sandals, and he extended (the wiping). Then he said: Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do as you saw me do, I would think that the bottoms of the feet are more deserving of wiping than their tops."],[712,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat talking to his companions and said: Whoever stands when the sun has risen, performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak'ahs, comes out of his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him. Uqbah said: I said, Praise be to Allah who granted me to hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umar b. al-Khattab, who was sitting facing me, said: Are you amazed at this? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something more amazing than this before you came. I said: What is that, may my father and mother be your ransom? Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then raises his gaze to the sky — or he said: directs his gaze to the sky — and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger, the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes."],[713,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever performs ablution as he was commanded and prays as he was commanded, his previous deeds are forgiven. Is that so, O Uqbah? He said: Yes."],[714,"Messenger of Allah said: \"When a Muslim, or believer, performs Wudu', washing his face, every evil that he looked at with his eyes leaves with the water - or with the last drop of water, or an expression similar to that - and when he washes his hands, every evil he did with his hands leaves with the water - or with the last drop of water - until he becomes free of sin.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2)"],[715,"I was with Salman under a tree. He took a dry branch from it and shook it until its leaves fell off. He said: Will you not ask me why I do this? I said to him: Why did you do it? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did this with me, then said: When a Muslim performs ablution and does it well, and prays the five prayers, his sins fall away as these leaves fell away. Then he said: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night} [Hud 114] up to His saying {That is a reminder for those who remember} [Hud 114]."],[716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution for every prayer, and it was sufficient for any of us to keep his ablution as long as he had not broken it."],[717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If any one of you offers prayer and feels a movement between his paddocks, but is doubtful whether or not his ablution broke, he should not cease praying unless he hears a sound or perceives a smell. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 177)"],[718,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the eyes are the ropes of the mind. So when the eye sleeps, the mind is free.\" It was asked to Abu Muhammad Abdullah, do you say this? He said, \"No, when one sleeps while standing, ablution is not required for him.\""],[719,"I used to suffer greatly from madhi, so I would wash excessively because of it. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about it. He said: Ablution is sufficient for you in that case. He said: I said: What about what gets on my garment from it? He said: Take a handful of water and sprinkle it where you see that it has touched."],[720,"A man should perform ablution from touching the penis."],[721,"Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution."],[722,"Ablution is required from what the fire has touched."],[723,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cutting meat from a sheep's shoulder in his hand. Then he was called to prayer, so he threw away the knife with which he was cutting, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."],[724,"Some men from Banu Mudlij came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we are people of this sea, fishing on rafts, so we stay out on it for a night, two nights, three, and four, and we carry fresh water with us for our lips. If we perform ablution with it, we fear for our lives, but if we prefer ourselves and perform ablution from the sea, we find within ourselves something from that, so we fear it may not be purifying.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution from it, for its water is pure and its dead is lawful.\""],[725,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"We travel by sea and with us is a little water. If we perform ablution with it, we become thirsty. May we perform ablution from seawater?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the purifier; its water is purifying and its dead is lawful.\""],[726,"None of you should urinate in stagnant water and then bathe in it."],[727,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was asked about water in the open land and what comes to it from animals and beasts of prey. He said, \"When water reaches two qullahs, nothing makes it impure.\""],[728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water and what comes to it from animals and beasts of prey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When water is two qullahs, it does not carry impurity.\""],[729,"The Prophet ﷺ came to visit me while I was ill and not conscious. He performed ablution and poured some of his ablution water on me, and I regained consciousness."],[730,"A woman from among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ got up and bathed from janabah in a large basin. The Prophet ﷺ came to the leftover water to bathe, and she said, \"I bathed in it before you.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Water does not become junub.\""],[731,"Abu Qatadah entered upon her, and she poured ablution water for him. A cat came to drink from it, so Abu Qatadah tilted the vessel for it until it drank. Kabshah said, \"He saw me looking, and said, 'Are you surprised, O daughter of my brother?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not impure; it is only one of those who go around among you, male and female.\"'\""],[732,"If a dog laps in a vessel, wash it seven times, and the eighth time rub it with dust."],[733,"A mouse fell into some clarified butter and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Throw it away and what is around it, and eat the rest.\""],[734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by two graves and said, “They are both being punished in their graves, and they are not being punished for something major. One of them used to go about with malicious gossip, and the other used not to protect himself from urine—or from urine.” He said: Then he took a fresh palm branch, broke it, and stuck a piece at the head of each grave. Then he said, “Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not dry out.”"],[735,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ, and when he stood, he urinated in a corner of the mosque. He said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shouted at him, but he restrained them from him. Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over his urine."],[736,"She brought a son of hers to the Prophet ﷺ who had not reached the age of eating food. He seated him in his lap, and the child urinated on him. He called for water and sprinkled it, but did not wash it."],[737,"I am a woman who lets her garment trail, and I walk in a filthy place? Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What comes after it purifies it.”"],[738,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. Then he stopped and called for water for ablution and performed ablution. Then the call to prayer was given, and he prayed with the people. When he turned away from his prayer, he saw a man who had stayed apart and had not prayed with the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I became junub and there is no water.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Use clean earth, for it is sufficient for you.”"],[739,"Two men went out on a journey, and the prayer time came while they had no water with them. They performed tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Then they found water afterward within the time, so one of them repeated the prayer with ablution and the other did not repeat. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that. He said to the one who did not repeat, “You have followed the Sunnah and your prayer is sufficient for you.” And he said to the one who performed ablution and repeated, “You have the reward twice.”"],[740,"He used to say about tayammum: “A single strike for the face and the hands.”"],[741,"She borrowed a necklace from Asma’, and it was lost. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent some of his companions to search for it. The prayer time overtook them, and they prayed without ablution. When they came to the Prophet ﷺ, they complained to him about that, and the verse of tayammum was revealed. Usayd b. Hudayr said, “May Allah reward you with good. By Allah, no matter ever befalls you but Allah makes for you a way out of it and makes in it a blessing for the Muslims.”"],[742,"I placed water for the Prophet ﷺ. He poured it over his hands and began washing his private part with them. When he finished, he wiped them on the ground or on a wall—Sulayman was uncertain—then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, washed his face and forearms, and poured water over his head and body. When he finished, he moved aside and washed his feet. I handed him a wrap, but he refused and began shaking off with his hand. She said: So I screened him until he had washed."],[743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to begin by washing his hands, then perform the ablution for prayer, then insert his palm into the water and run it through the roots of his hair. When he thought that he had reached the skin, he scooped with his hand three scoops and poured them over his head, then washed."],[744,"I used to wash from janabah, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel."],[745,"I used to wash from janabah, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel, and it was the faraq."],[746,"Whoever leaves a spot the size of a hair of janabah that the water does not reach, such and such will be done to it in the Fire. Ali said: It is for this reason that I treated my head as an enemy, and he used to shave his hair."],[747,"\"I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying that a man was injured in the head at the time of the Messenger of Allah, then he had a wet dream. He was told to have a bath, so he took the bath, became rigid and stiff, and died. News of that reached the Messenger of Allah and he said: 'They have killed him, may Allah kill them! Is not the cure for a lack of knowledge to ask questions?'\"'Ata' said: \"We heard that the Messenger of Allah said: 'If only he had washed his body and left his head alone where the wound was.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 572)"],[748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went around to his wives in a single day."],[749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went around to his wives in a single night, all together."],[750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me up behind him one day, and he confided a secret to me that I will not tell anyone among the people. The most beloved thing for the Prophet ﷺ to shield himself with when relieving himself was a target or a palm enclosure."],[751,"Umar, ؓ , asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Janabah befalls me at night. So he commanded him to wash his private part and perform wudu, then sleep."],[752,"I asked Aishah: How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do when he wanted to sleep while he was junub? She said: He used to perform wudu as for prayer, then sleep."],[753,"\"Water is for Water.\" [1] [1] That is, water for peforming Ghusl is obligatory when the ejaculation of water (semen) occurs. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 199)"],[754,"The legal ruling that they used to give regarding his saying, 'Water is from water,' was a concession that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted in the beginning of Islam, then he commanded ghusl afterward."],[755,"The legal ruling that they used to give, 'Water is from water,' was a concession that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted in the beginning of Islam, or the time, then he performed ghusl afterward."],[756,"When he sits between her four branches and then exerts himself, ghusl becomes obligatory."],[757,"I heard Said b. al-Musayyab say: My maternal aunt Khawlah bt. Hakim al-Sulamiyyah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who has a wet dream, and he commanded her to perform ghusl."],[758,"Umm Sulaym, the mother of the sons of Abu Talhah, entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth. What do you think about a woman who sees in a dream what a man sees? Should she perform ghusl? He said: Yes. Aishah said: I said, Uff to you! Does a woman see that? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to her and said: May your right hand be dusty. From where then does resemblance come?"],[759,"Umm Sulaym entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Umm Salamah was with him, and she said: A woman sees in her dream what a man sees? Umm Salamah said: May your hands be dusty, O Umm Sulaym! You have disgraced women. The Prophet ﷺ said, defending Umm Sulaym: Rather, may your hands be dusty. The best of you is the one who asks about what concerns her. When she sees the water, let her perform ghusl. Umm Salamah said: Do women have water? He said: Yes, so how would the child resemble them? They are but the counterparts of men."],[760,"About a man who wakes up and sees wetness but does not remember a wet dream, he said: “He should perform ghusl. But if he remembers a wet dream and does not see wetness, then no ghusl is required of him.”"],[761,"“If one of you wakes up from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the ablution water until he has washed it three times.”"],[762,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he entered the privy and then came out. Food was brought to him, and it was said, “Will you not perform ablution?” He said, “Am I going to pray, so that I should perform ablution?”"],[763,"'Aishah the wife of the Prophet said: \"Umm Habibah Jahsh experienced prolonged non-menstrual bleeding for seven years when she was married to 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf. She complained about that to the Prophet and the Prophet said: 'That is not menstruation, rather it is a vein, so when the time of your period comes, leave the prayer, and when it is over, take a bath and perform prayer.'\" 'Aishah said: \"She used to bathe for every prayer and then perform the prayer. She used to sit in a washtub belonging to her sister Zainab bint Jahsh and the blood would turn the water red.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 626)"],[764,"The Prophet ﷺ used to “kiss and embrace while fasting.”"],[765,"He used to “kiss and embrace while fasting.”"],[766,"“Hand me the prayer mat.” She said, “I am menstruating.” He said, “It is not in your hand.”"],[767,"I heard a woman asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: How should she treat her garment when she becomes pure from her menses? He said: “If you see blood on it, rub it, then scratch it, then sprinkle water on the rest of your garment, then pray in it.”"],[768,"A woman from the Ansar asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstruation. He said: “Take your water and your lote-tree leaves, then wash and cleanse yourself thoroughly. Then pour water over your head until you reach the roots of the hair. Then take a piece of cloth perfumed with musk.” She said, “How should I use it, O Messenger of Allah?” He remained silent. She said, “Then how should I use it, O Messenger of Allah?” He remained silent. Aisha said, “Take a piece of cloth perfumed with musk and follow the traces of blood with it,” while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ listened and did not disapprove of what she said."],[769,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has prolonged bleeding and never becomes pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “No, that is only a vein. When the menses comes, then leave the prayer; and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself and pray.”"],[770,"It is reported that the daughter of Ja'hsh informed the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ that she used to have irregular bleeding during her period. The Prophet ﷺ instructed her to perform a ritual purification (ghusl) for every prayer. If she noticed that blood was entering her vagina while inside the mosque, and she found water inside the mosque, she should submerge herself in it and then exit. If the blood was on top of the water, she should pray without repeating the purification."],[771,"She is only so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had “commanded her to perform ghusl for every prayer, but when that became difficult for her, he commanded her to combine Zuhr and Asr with one ghusl, and Maghrib and Isha with one ghusl, and to perform ghusl for Fajr.”"],[772,"A woman had prolonged bleeding during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and was given instructions. He said: I said to Abd al-Rahman, “Did the Prophet ﷺ instruct her?” He said, “I do not narrate anything to you from the Prophet ﷺ.” He said: So she was instructed to “delay Zuhr and hasten Asr and perform one ghusl for both, delay Maghrib and hasten Isha and perform one ghusl for both, and perform one ghusl for Subh.”"],[773,"'Aishah the wife of the Prophet said: \"Umm Habibah Jahsh experienced prolonged non-menstrual bleeding for seven years when she was married to 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf. She complained about that to the Prophet and the Prophet said: 'That is not menstruation, rather it is a vein, so when the time of your period comes, leave the prayer, and when it is over, take a bath and perform prayer.'\" 'Aishah said: \"She used to bathe for every prayer and then perform the prayer. She used to sit in a washtub belonging to her sister Zainab bint Jahsh and the blood would turn the water red.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 626)"],[774,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has prolonged bleeding. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “No, that is only a vein and not the menses. When the menses comes, then leave the prayer. When its usual duration has passed, wash the blood from yourself, perform ablution, and pray.”"],[775,"A woman was flowing with blood in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Umm Salamah sought a ruling for her from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Let her note the number of nights and days that she used to menstruate before this happened to her, and their portion of the month, and let her abandon the prayer for that. When that passes and the prayer time comes, let her bathe, wrap a cloth, and then pray.'"],[776,"O Messenger of Allah, the blood has overcome me. He said: 'Bathe and pray.'"],[777,"Umm Habibah bt. Jahsh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she had been suffering from prolonged bleeding for seven years. She complained to him about that and sought his ruling about it. He said to her: 'This is not menstruation; it is only a vein. So bathe and then pray.' Aishah said: Umm Habibah used to bathe for every prayer and pray. She would sit in a large tub, and the redness of the blood would rise over the water, then she would pray."],[778,"Umm Habibah bt. Jahsh suffered from prolonged bleeding in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to bathe for every prayer. She would immerse herself in a large tub filled with water and then come out with the blood floating on top of it, then she would pray."],[779,"He asked Saeed about the woman with prolonged bleeding. He said: 'O son of my brother, no one remains more knowledgeable about this than I. When menstruation begins, let her leave the prayer; when it ends, let her bathe and pray.'"],[780,"Regarding the woman with prolonged bleeding: 'She leaves the prayer for the days of her menstrual cycles, then she bathes, then she uses a pad and wraps a cloth, then she prays.' The man said: 'Even if it flows?' He said: 'Even if it flows like this spout.'"],[781,"Yes, even if you gush it abundantly, insert (a pad), then wrap a cloth, then enter."],[782,"I asked her about the woman with prolonged bleeding. She said: 'She waits for her menstrual cycles, during which she used to leave the prayer before that. When the day of her purity comes, on which she used to become pure, she bathes, then performs wudu for every prayer and prays.'"],[783,"About the woman with prolonged non-menstrual bleeding: “She should wait for the days during which she used to abstain from prayer; when the day of her purity comes, the day on which she used to become pure, she should perform ghusl, then perform wudu for each prayer and pray.”"],[784,"“The woman with prolonged non-menstrual bleeding should refrain from prayer during the days of her menstrual period in each month; when it comes to its end, she should perform ghusl, pray, fast, and perform wudu for each prayer.”"],[785,"“Concerning the woman with prolonged non-menstrual bleeding who knows the days of her menstrual period: if she is divorced and the bleeding continues for a long time, she should observe a waiting period equivalent to the length of her menstrual cycles, three periods. As for prayer, when the time of menstruation comes in each month, she should refrain from prayer.”"],[786,"I said to Qatada, “A woman whose menstruation was known, but it increased by five days, or four days, or three days?” He said, “She should pray.” I said, “Two days?” He said, “That is part of her menstruation.” And I asked Ibn Sirin, who said, “Women know better about that.”"],[787,"Concerning a woman who sees blood during the days of her purity, he said, “I think she should perform ghusl and pray.”"],[788,"Ibn Abbas was asked about a woman who has prolonged non-menstrual bleeding. He said, “She should wait for the extent of her previous menstrual period and refrain from prayer, then perform ghusl and pray until the time of her usual period comes, then refrain from prayer, then perform ghusl. That is only from Satan, who wants to make one of them disbelieve.”"],[789,"Regarding the woman with prolonged non-menstrual bleeding: she should abstain from prayer during the days of her menstrual periods, then perform ghusl, use a piece of cotton as a barrier, and perform wudu for each prayer."],[790,"“The woman with prolonged non-menstrual bleeding should sit out the days of her menstrual periods, then perform one ghusl, and perform wudu for each prayer.”"],[791,"A woman from the family of Anas experienced prolonged non-menstrual bleeding. They sent me to ask Ibn Abbas, so I asked him. He said, “As long as she sees the abundant dark blood, she should not pray. When she sees purity, even for an hour of the day, she should perform ghusl and pray.”"],[792,"“When she sees the abundant dark blood, she should not pray. When she sees purity, she should perform ghusl and pray.”"],[793,"A woman asked him, saying, “I am a woman who has prolonged non-menstrual bleeding.” He said, “When you see fresh red blood, then refrain for the days of your menstrual periods.”"],[794,"The woman with prolonged non-menstrual bleeding “should sit out the days of her menstrual periods, then perform a single ghusl for Zuhr and Asr, delay Maghrib and hasten Isha, and that is at the time of Isha, and perform a single ghusl for Fajr. She should not fast, her husband should not have intercourse with her, and she should not touch the mushaf.”"],[795,"Regarding the woman with istihada, she performs one ghusl for Zuhr and Asr, and one ghusl for Maghrib and Isha. He used to say: she delays Zuhr and hastens Asr, and delays Maghrib and hastens Isha."],[796,"Regarding the woman with istihada: \"When she has passed her menstrual periods, then when it is time for Asr, she performs a complete wudu, then takes a cloth and binds it as a loincloth, then prays Zuhr and Asr together. Then she does the same and prays Maghrib and Isha together. Then she does the same and prays Fajr.\""],[797,"Regarding the woman with istihada: \"She performs ghusl every day for the first prayer and Asr, and prays them, and she performs ghusl for Maghrib and Isha, and prays them, and she performs ghusl for the dawn prayer.\""],[798,"\"The woman with istihada performs ghusl, then combines Zuhr and Asr. If she sees anything, she performs ghusl and combines Maghrib and Isha.\""],[799,"I asked Sa'id b. al-Musayyab about the woman with istihada. He said: \"She sits for the days of her menstrual periods, performs ghusl from Zuhr to Zuhr, binds a cloth, her husband may have intercourse with her, and she may fast.\" I asked, \"From whom is this?\" He took up pebbles."],[800,"\"She performs ghusl from Zuhr to Zuhr, and performs wudu for every prayer. If the blood overcomes her, she binds a cloth.\" Al-Hasan used to say that."],[801,"Sa'id (a boy's name) \"she washes herself from noon until the same time tomorrow for the Dhuhr prayer. If menstruation overcomes her, she seeks forgiveness and performs ablution for every prayer and prays.\""],[802,"Regarding the woman with istihada: \"She performs ghusl from the Zuhr prayer to the Zuhr prayer of the next day.\""],[803,"\"The woman with istihada leaves prayer during the days of her menstruation in the month, then performs ghusl from Zuhr to Zuhr, performs wudu at every prayer, fasts, prays, and her husband may have intercourse with her.\""],[804,"Regarding \"the woman with istihada, she performs ghusl once every day.\""],[805,"He used to say: The woman with istihada performs ghusl from Zuhr to Zuhr. Marwan said: And that is the statement of al-Awza'i."],[806,"\"The woman with istihada performs ghusl every day at the time of the first prayer.\""],[807,"Regarding the woman experiencing istihaadah: he did not see any harm in her husband having intercourse with her."],[808,"Sa'id b. Jubayr was asked, 'May one have intercourse with a woman experiencing istihaadah?' He replied, 'Prayer is greater than intercourse.'"],[809,"\"Her husband comes to her.\""],[810,"Her husband covers her."],[811,"Regarding the woman experiencing istihaadah: her husband may have intercourse with her, even if the blood drips onto the mat."],[812,"It was said to Bakr b. 'Abdullah that al-Hajjaj b. Yusuf says that a woman experiencing istihaadah should not be approached by her husband. Bakr b. 'Abdullah al-Muzani said, 'Prayer is of greater sanctity, and her husband may approach her.'"],[813,"Her husband may come to her."],[814,"Regarding the woman experiencing istihaadah: her husband may have intercourse with her. She should leave off prayer during the days of her menstruation, and when prayer becomes lawful for her, then he may have intercourse with her."],[815,"A woman experiencing istihaadah: her husband may have intercourse with her."],[816,"Regarding the woman experiencing istihaadah: she performs ghusl, prays, fasts Ramadan, and her husband may have intercourse with her."],[817,"A woman experiencing istihaadah: her husband should not have intercourse with her."],[818,"Muhammad used to dislike a man having intercourse with his wife while she was experiencing istihaadah."],[819,"A woman experiencing istihaadah: her husband should not come to her, she should not fast, and she should not touch the mushaf."],[820,"A woman experiencing istihaadah: her husband should not come to her."],[821,"The woman suffering from irregular bleeding (mustahada) is not to be sexually approached, nor is she to fast, nor to touch the mushaf; only prayer has been permitted for her. Yazid said: her husband may have intercourse with her, and what is lawful for a pure woman is lawful for her."],[822,"Regarding prayer during menstruation, if a woman becomes clean before the seventh day, then she may perform the prayer, otherwise, she should refrain from praying until she becomes clean. However, if she becomes clean before the tenth day, then she may perform the prayer. If not, she should wash herself, perform ablution, and then pray while in a state of istihadah (minor ritual impurity)."],[823,"Menstruation is ten days; anything beyond that is irregular bleeding (istihada)."],[824,"Menstruation is ten days; anything beyond that is irregular bleeding."],[825,"Menstruation is up to thirteen days; anything beyond that is irregular bleeding."],[826,"\"The menstruation lasts for ten days, then she is considered clean.\""],[827,"Menstruation is up to thirteen days; anything other than that is irregular bleeding."],[828,"When she sees blood, she should refrain from prayer and count the days of her menstruation—a day or two—then after that she is considered as having irregular bleeding."],[829,"The woman with irregular bleeding waits three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten days."],[830,"The woman with irregular bleeding waits the maximum of her usual menstrual cycles plus one day."],[831,"What exceeds ten days is irregular bleeding."],[832,"The maximum of menstruation is fifteen days."],[833,"The minimum of menstruation is three days."],[834,"The minimum of menstruation is three (days)."],[835,"The minimum of menstruation is a day."],[836,"If she sees the blood before her menstruation by a day or two, then it is from the menstruation."],[837,"Regarding the virgin, when she has postpartum bleeding and then becomes mustahada (experiencing irregular bleeding), they both said: \"She refrains from prayer the same as a woman from among her womenfolk refrains.\""],[838,"When a woman menstruates for the first time, she sits during the menstruation according to what is customary among her womenfolk."],[839,"Regarding the elderly woman who sees blood? He said: \"We do not consider it menstruation.\""],[840,"Regarding a woman whom menstruation left for thirty years, then she saw blood; he commanded concerning her the matter of the mustahada."],[841,"Regarding the elderly woman who sees blood? He said: \"She has the status of a mustahada; she does as the mustahada does.\""],[842,"Regarding the one who has ceased from menstruation, when she sees blood, she performs wudu and prays, and she does not perform ghusl. Abdullah was asked about the elderly woman; he said: \"She performs wudu and prays, and if she is divorced, she observes the waiting period with months.\""],[843,"Purity is fifteen (days)."],[844,"If a woman menstruates in a month or in forty nights three menstruations, he said: \"So if trustworthy women witnesses testify for her that she saw that which makes prayer forbidden for her, from the menstrual blood of women, which is the known menstruation, then her term has elapsed.\""],[845,"A woman came to Ali disputing with her husband who had divorced her, and she said: \"I have menstruated three menstruations in a month.\" Ali said to Shurayh: \"Judge between them.\" He said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, while you are here?\" He said: \"Judge between them.\" He said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, while you are here?\" He said: \"Judge between them.\" Then he said: \"If she brings from the inner circle of her family someone whose religion and trustworthiness are acceptable, claiming that she menstruated three menstruations, becoming pure at each period and praying, then it is permissible for her; otherwise, no.\" Ali said: \"Qalun.\""],[846,"That they should conceal what Allah has created in their wombs [al-Baqarah:228]. He said: \"Menstruation.\" It was said to Abu Muhammad: Do you hold this view? He said: No. Abdullah was asked about the hadith of Shurayh: Do you hold this view? He said: No, and he said: Three menstrual periods in a month, how can that be?"],[847,"That they should look at night at the menstrual discharge, and she says that it may be yellowness or duskiness."],[848,"Amrah used to command women not to perform ghusl until the cotton came out white."],[849,"Duskiness and yellowness during the days of menstruation are menstruation, and anything she sees after the days of menstruation of blood or duskiness or yellowness is istihadah."],[850,"A woman of Quraysh sent to Amrah a piece of cotton containing something like yellowness, asking her whether she considered that if a woman saw nothing of her menses except this, she had become pure. She said: \"No, not until she sees pure whiteness.\""],[851,"We used to be under her care, and one of us would menstruate, then become pure and perform ghusl and pray, then slight yellowness would return to her, and she would command us to abstain from prayer until we saw nothing but pure whiteness."],[852,"Duskiness and yellowness during the days of menstruation have the status of menstruation."],[853,"When she sees blood, she should refrain from prayer until she sees purity white like plaster, then she should perform ghusl and pray."],[854,"Al-Hasan did not consider yellowness and duskiness, nor anything like the washing of meat, as anything."],[855,"We used not to consider yellowness and duskiness as anything."],[856,"About a woman who sees blood during the days of her purity, he said: I think she should perform ghusl and pray."],[857,"About a woman who sees yellowness after purity? He said: That is the tarryah; she should wash it, perform wudu, and pray."],[858,"There is nothing in the yellowish discharge after the ritual bath except purification."],[859,"When a woman sees yellowish discharge a day or two after the ritual bath, she should purify herself and pray."],[860,"There is nothing in the yellowish discharge after the ritual bath except purification."],[861,"We did not count the dark discharge and yellowish discharge after the ritual bath as anything."],[862,"When a menstruating woman sees fresh blood a day or two after the ritual bath, she should refrain from prayer for a day, then after that she is a woman with istihadah."],[863,"When a woman purifies herself from menstruation and then sees something that disturbs her after the purification, it is only a kick from Satan in the womb. If she sees something like a nosebleed, or a drop of blood, or the wash water of meat, she should perform her ablution for prayer and then pray. If the blood is fresh and unmistakable, she should abandon prayer."],[864,"Regarding a woman whose menstruation lasts six or seven days, and then she sees dark discharge or yellowish discharge, or sees a drop or two of blood: that is invalid, and nothing harms her."],[865,"I asked Ata about a woman who performs the ritual bath after menstruation and then sees yellowish discharge. He said: She performs ablution and sprinkles water."],[866,"Regarding the woman with istihadah, he said: She abandons prayer during her menstrual cycles for that day or two, then performs the ritual bath. Then when the first prayer time comes, she looks: if it is a yellowish discharge, she performs ablution and prays; but if it is blood, she delays the noon prayer and advances the afternoon prayer, then prays both with one ritual bath. When the sun sets, she looks: if it is a yellowish discharge, she performs ablution and prays; but if it is blood, she delays the sunset prayer and advances the night prayer, then prays both with one ritual bath. When dawn breaks, she looks: if it is a yellowish discharge, she performs ablution and prays; but if it is blood, she performs the ritual bath and prays the morning prayer. This is three times every day and night."],[867,"The Prophet ﷺ observed seclusion in the mosque, and some of his wives observed seclusion with him while she was a woman with istihadah seeing blood. Sometimes she would place a basin beneath her because of the blood. And he claimed that Aishah saw the water of safflower and said: This was something that so-and-so used to experience."],[868,"I asked Ata about a woman who becomes pure from menstruation and then sees yellowish discharge. He said: She performs ablution."],[869,"I asked him about a woman whose menstruation was seven days and then her menstruation increased. He said: She should extend by waiting three extra days."],[870,"When a woman becomes pure at the time of a prayer and does not perform ghusl while she is able to perform ghusl, she must make up that prayer."],[871,"When a woman prays two rakʿahs and then menstruates, she does not make them up when she becomes pure."],[872,"Regarding a woman who becomes pure at ẓuhr and delays her ghusl until the time of ʿaṣr enters, they both said: “She makes up ẓuhr.”"],[873,"Regarding a woman who neglects the prayer until menstruation overtakes her, they said: “She repeats that prayer.”"],[874,"Regarding Al-Hasan's opinion about a woman who attended the prayer but missed it until she menstruated, he said, \"You can make up for that prayer once you have performed ablution.\""],[875,"When a woman wastes the prayer until she menstruates, she must make it up when she becomes pure."],[876,"When she neglects it and then menstruates, she makes it up."],[877,"When a woman menstruates at the time of a prayer, she is not required to make it up."],[878,"When she becomes pure before maghrib, she prays ẓuhr and ʿaṣr; and when she becomes pure before fajr, she prays maghrib and ʿishāʾ."],[879,"Regarding the menstruating woman who becomes pure during the time of a prayer, she prays that prayer."],[880,"When the menstruating woman becomes pure before dawn, she prays Maghrib and Isha; and when she becomes pure before sunset, she prays Zuhr and Asr."],[881,"Regarding the menstruating woman, if she sees purity at the end of the day, she prays Zuhr and Asr; and if she becomes pure at the end of the night, she prays Maghrib and Isha."],[882,"When she becomes pure at the time of Asr, she prays Zuhr and Asr."],[883,"When she becomes pure during the time of a prayer, she prays it."],[884,"When she becomes pure during the time of a prayer, she prays that prayer and does not pray any other."],[885,"I asked him about a woman who becomes pure after Asr. He said: She prays Zuhr and Asr. I said: What if her purity occurs close to sunset? He said: She prays Asr and does not pray Zuhr. And if she does not become pure until the sun has set, nothing is required of her."],[886,"A woman wrote to him: I have been suffering from istihada for such and such a time, and it has reached me that Ali said: She performs ghusl for every prayer. Ibn Abbas said: We find nothing for her other than what Ali said."],[887,"Zaynab used to observe I'tikaf with the Prophet ﷺ while she was shedding blood, so he ordered her to perform ghusl for every prayer."],[888,"The woman with istihada performs ghusl for every prayer."],[889,"Al-Awza'i, and al-Zuhri and Makhul used to say: She should perform ghusl for every prayer."],[890,"Umm Habiba bt. Jahsh was experiencing non-menstrual bleeding, and she asked the Prophet ﷺ about that. He commanded her to perform ghusl for every prayer and to pray."],[891,"About that, they said: Ali used to say, 'She should perform ghusl for every prayer.' So I read and wrote the answer with my own hand: I find nothing for her except what Ali said. It was said, 'Kufa is a cold land.' He replied, 'If Allah willed, He could have tested her with something more severe than that.'"],[892,"The daughter of Jahsh was married to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and experienced istihada. She would come out of her washtub with blood still upon it and then pray."],[893,"\"She should have a separate ghusl for every prayer.\""],[894,"\"For every two prayers one ghusl, and she should have a separate ghusl for the Fajr prayer.\""],[895,"A woman asked Ibrahim, 'I am experiencing istihada.' He replied, 'Use water and sprinkle it, for it will stop the blood from you.'"],[896,"Regarding a divorced woman about whom there is doubt: 'She should wait a year. If she menstruates, then so be it; otherwise she should wait after the completion of the year for three months. If she menstruates, then so be it; otherwise her waiting period has ended.'"],[897,"\"Abu Muhammad is the statement of Malik.\""],[898,"Jabir b. Zayd was asked about a woman who is divorced while she is young and her menstruation ceases without old age. He said, 'Without menstruation, should she consider herself menstruating?' Tawus said, 'Three months.'"],[899,"\"When a man divorces his wife and she menstruates once or twice, then her menstruation ceases: if that is due to old age, she observes an iddah of three months; and if she is young and doubtful, she observes an iddah of a year after the doubt.\""],[900,"\"The mustahada and the woman whose menstruation is irregular: she menstruates once in a month and twice in another month. Her waiting period is three months.\""],[901,"She should reckon her waiting period by menstrual cycles."],[902,"The waiting period of the mustahadah is one year."],[903,"The mustahadah should reckon her waiting period by menstrual cycles."],[904,"Abu Muhammad said: The people of the Hijaz say that “al-aqra’” means the periods of purity, while the people of Iraq said it means menstruation. Abdullah said: I say it means menstruation."],[905,"The mustahadah should reckon her waiting period by menstrual cycles."],[906,"I asked al-Zuhri about a man who divorced his wife while she was a young woman who menstruated, but her menstruation ceased when he divorced her and she saw no blood. How long should she wait? He said: “Three months.”"],[907,"About the man who buys a young girl who has not yet reached puberty or become pregnant, for how long can he keep her? He said, \"For three months.\""],[908,"That he used to say concerning the mustahadah: She should perform ghusl for every prayer and pray."],[909,"I asked al-Zuhri about a pregnant woman who sees blood. He said: “She should abandon prayer.”"],[910,"From my wife: she saw blood while I consider her pregnant. He said: That is the waning of the wombs. {Allah knows what every female carries and what the wombs wane and increase} [Al-Ra'd 8]. Whatever they wane of anything, they increase the like of it in pregnancy."],[911,"From 'Ikrimah regarding this verse: {Allah knows what every female carries and what the wombs wane and increase, and everything with Him is in measure} [Al-Ra'd 8]. He said: \"That is menstruation during pregnancy. She does not menstruate a day during pregnancy except that it adds a pure day to her pregnancy.\""],[912,"From 'A'ishah: \"The pregnant woman, when she sees blood, she should not pray until she becomes pure.\""],[913,"From 'Ikrimah: {And what the wombs wane} [Al-Ra'd 8]. He said: \"It is menstruation during pregnancy.\" {And what they increase} [Al-Ra'd 8]. He said: \"For each day she menstruates during her pregnancy, she adds a day to her purity until she completes nine months pure.\""],[914,"From Mujahid: {And what the wombs wane} [Al-Ra'd 8]. He said: \"When a woman menstruates while she is pregnant.\" He said: \"That is a decrease from the child. So if it increases beyond nine months, it is a completion for what decreased from her child.\""],[915,"\"My wife menstruates while she is pregnant.\""],[916,"\"When the pregnant woman sees blood, let her refrain from prayer, for it is menstruation.\""],[917,"Regarding the pregnant woman who sees blood: \"If it is fresh blood, she performs ghusl and prays; and if it is yellowish discharge, she performs wudu' and prays.\""],[918,"\"If she sees it as she used to see it before that in her cycles, she leaves prayer; and if it is only for a day or two, she does not leave prayer.\""],[919,"Regarding the pregnant woman who sees blood, she said: \"That does not prevent her from prayer.\""],[920,"Abdullah, I say according to the saying of Yazid."],[921,"Regarding a pregnant woman who sees blood, he said: \"She is in the position of a mustahada, except that she does not abandon the prayer.\""],[922,"Regarding a pregnant woman who sees blood, he said: \"She washes the blood from herself, performs wudu, and prays.\""],[923,"\"When a pregnant woman sees blood, she performs wudu and prays.\""],[924,"Regarding a pregnant woman who sees blood, he said: \"She performs wudu and prays.\""],[925,"She is in the state of menstruation."],[926,"\"There is no menstruation with pregnancy.\""],[927,"Regarding a pregnant woman who sees blood, he said: \"She is in the position of a mustahada.\""],[928,"\"When a pregnant woman sees blood, she does not abandon the prayer.\""],[929,"Regarding a pregnant woman and one who has ceased menstruating: \"If they see blood, they perform wudu and pray, and they do not perform ghusl.\""],[930,"\"They both perform ghusl and pray.\""],[931,"\"Indeed, a pregnant woman does not menstruate. So if she sees blood, let her perform ghusl and pray.\""],[932,"Regarding a woman when she sees blood while she is in labor? He said: \"It is menstruation. She leaves the prayer.\""],[933,"Regarding a pregnant woman: \"When labor strikes her and she sees blood upon delivery, let her refrain from prayer.\""],[934,"Regarding \"the postpartum woman is like the purification of a woman among her women.\""],[935,"Regarding the postpartum woman: \"She refrains from prayer for forty days. If she sees purity, then that is it; and if she does not see purity, she refrains from prayer for some days, five or six. If she becomes pure, then that is it; otherwise she refrains from prayer for what is between her and fifty. If she becomes pure, then that is it; otherwise she is mustahadah (a woman with prolonged bleeding).\""],[936,"That he would \"not approach postpartum women for forty days.\""],[937,"\"The time of postpartum bleeding is forty days. If she becomes pure, then it is so; otherwise do not exceed it until she prays.\""],[938,"\"If the postpartum woman has a customary period, then it is so; otherwise she sits for forty nights.\""],[939,"\"Postpartum bleeding is menstruation.\""],[940,"\"The postpartum woman waits forty days or so.\""],[941,"\"The postpartum woman would sit during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for forty days or forty nights. One of us would apply wars (a yellow dye) to her face due to the dark spots.\""],[942,"I am so-and-so, I have become pure. He kicked her with his foot and said, \"Do not deceive me regarding my religion until forty nights have passed.\""],[943,"\"The postpartum woman sits for about forty days.\""],[944,"\"The postpartum woman waits for about forty.\""],[945,"Regarding the woman in postnatal bleeding who sees blood: \"She should wait forty nights, then pray.\""],[946,"The woman waits thirty days for a boy and forty days for a girl—meaning the one in postnatal bleeding. Marwan said: This is the view of Sa'id b. 'Abd al-'Aziz. Al-Awza'i said: They are equal."],[947,"\"If she sees blood at the time of labor for a day or two, it is part of postnatal bleeding.\""],[948,"Regarding the pregnant woman who sees blood while she is in labor? He said: \"She does what the woman with istihadah does.\""],[949,"Regarding the woman who becomes junub then menstruates: He said, \"She should perform ghusl.\""],[950,"\"Menstruation is greater.\""],[951,"Regarding a man who has intercourse with his wife and then she menstruates: He said, \"She performing ghusl is more beloved to me.\""],[952,"\"She should perform ghusl from janabah.\""],[953,"Ibrahim said: \"She should perform ghusl.\""],[954,"\"She should perform ghusl.\""],[955,"\"To perform ablution for prayer, then glorify and magnify Allah at the time of prayer.\""],[956,"A menstruating woman performs ablution at the time of every prayer and remembers Allah? He said: �I do not find any basis for this.�"],[957,"He used to �command the menstruating woman at the time of prayer to perform ablution and sit in the courtyard of her mosque, remembering Allah and glorifying Him.�"],[958,"\"There is no deity but the edge of the verse, but rather, cleanse yourself at the time of every prayer, then face the qibla, and glorify and magnify, and invoke Almighty God.\""],[959,"�The menstruating woman is commanded to perform ablution at the times of prayer, face the qiblah, and remember Allah, Exalted is He.�"],[960,"�When the menstruating woman or the ritually impure person hears the prostration verse, the ritually impure person takes a bath and prostrates, but the menstruating woman does not make it up because she does not pray.�"],[961,"Regarding a menstruating woman who hears the prostration verse, he said: �She does not make it up.�"],[962,"�There is nothing upon her.�"],[963,"�We used to menstruate in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he would not command any woman among us to make up the prayers.�"],[964,"A woman asked Aishah: Does one of us make up the prayers of the days of her menstruation? She said: Are you a Haruriyyah? �One of us used to menstruate during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and she was not commanded to make up.�"],[965,"�When the menstruating woman hears the prostration verse, she should not prostrate.�"],[966,"�A menstruating woman does not prostrate when she hears the prostration verse.�"],[967,"He used to �dislike for the menstruating woman to prostrate when she hears the prostration verse.�"],[968,"About women in postnatal bleeding and menstruation: do they make up the prayers when they become pure? He said: Here are the wives of the Prophet ﷺ; if they had done that, we would have commanded our women to do it."],[969,"A woman came to Aisha and said: Do I make up the prayers I missed during menstruation when I become pure? Aisha said: Are you a Haruri? “We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; one of us would menstruate and become pure, and he did not command us to make them up.”"],[970,"I said to Fatimah, meaning the daughter of Ali: Do you make up the prayers of the days of your menstruation? She said: “No.”"],[971,"A woman asked her: Does a menstruating woman make up the prayer? She said: Are you a Haruri? “The wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ menstruated, and he commanded them to make up [fasting].”"],[972,"“The menstruating woman and the one in major ritual impurity remember Allah and say His name.”"],[973,"“The one in major ritual impurity and the menstruating woman do not read a complete verse; they may read a letter.”"],[974,"“The one in major ritual impurity and the menstruating woman do not read the Quran.”"],[975,"Umar “disliked or forbade the one in major ritual impurity from reciting.” Shuʿbah said: I found in the book: and the menstruating woman."],[976,"Four do not read the Quran: at the toilet, in the bathhouse, the one in major ritual impurity, and the menstruating woman, except a verse and the like for the one in major ritual impurity and the menstruating woman."],[977,"“The menstruating woman and the one in major ritual impurity may begin a verse but do not complete its end.”"],[978,"About the menstruating woman, he said: “She does not read the Quran.”"],[979,"Aisha used to “perform ruqyah on Asma while she was menstruating.”"],[980,"\"The person in a state of sexual impurity remembers the name of Allah the Almighty.\""],[981,"It used to be said: The junub and the menstruating woman do not recite, and recitation is not done in the bathhouse. And there are two states in which the servant does not remember Allah: at the toilet and during intercourse, except that when a man goes to his wife, he begins and mentions Allah's name."],[982,"About a menstruating woman reciting, he said: \"No, except the edge of a verse.\""],[983,"Four phrases that can be said by someone in a state of ritual impurity (junub) or menstruation (haidh): \"SubhanAllah\" (Glory be to Allah), \"Alhamdulillah\" (All praise is due to Allah), \"La ilaha illallah\" (There is no deity but Allah), and \"Allahu Akbar\" (Allah is the Greatest)."],[984,"He was asked about a menstruating woman who hears a verse of prostration, and he said: “She should not prostrate, because it is a prayer.”"],[985,"Ibrahim and Abu al-Dhuhay said, \"Do not prostrate.\""],[986,"Ibrahim and Saeed bin Jubair said, \"She does not have a greater prayer than that.\""],[987,"She has been prevented from something better than that: the obligatory prayer."],[988,"\"She does not prostrate.\""],[989,"regarding a woman who notices purity [in her self after her menstrual period], and then she hears the sajdah [of Recitation]. He said: “Do not prostrate until you have performed the ritual bath.”"],[990,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said to the women, \"Give in charity, for you are the majority of the inhabitants of Hell.\" So a woman who was not from the elite women asked, \"Why? For what reason or with what?\" He said, \"Because you frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands.\""],[991,"\"When a woman becomes pure from menstruation, let her attend to the garment that touches her skin, wash whatever impurity has touched it, then pray in it.\""],[992,"One of us would have a shift in which she menstruated and in which she became junub, then she would see a drop of menstrual blood in it and scrape it off with her saliva."],[993,"\"A drop of blood may get ahead of one of you. When that happens to one of you, let her scrape it off with her saliva.\""],[994,"\"When a woman washes the blood but it does not go away, let her change it with the yellowness of wars or saffron.\""],[995,"A woman said to her: \"Blood may be on a garment, and I wash it but it does not go away, so should I cut it off?\" She said: \"Water is purifying.\""],[996,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu al-Qasim, would be with me under a single inner garment while I was menstruating, powerfully bleeding. If anything of me touched him, he washed what had touched him and did not go beyond it to other parts, then prayed in it. Then he would return, and if anything of me touched him, he did the same: he washed that spot and did not go beyond it to other parts, then prayed in it."],[997,"\"Regarding the clothes a woman wears while menstruating: if blood touches them, she washes them; otherwise she does not have to wash them. And if she sweats in them, it suffices her to sprinkle them.\""],[998,"The menstruating woman \"prays in the clothes in which she menstruated, unless something of them is touched by blood, in which case she washes the place of the blood.\""],[999,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said: \"Scrape it off, then sprinkle it with water.\""],[1000,"A menstruating woman does not wash her garment if there is no blood on it."],[1001,"I heard a woman asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her garment when she becomes pure from her menstruation: what should she do with it? He said: \"If you see blood on it, rub it, then pinch it with water, then sprinkle water over the rest of it, and pray in it.\""],[1002,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about menstrual blood that is on a garment. He said: \"Wash it with water and lote-tree leaves, and rub it with a rib.\""],[1003,"The woman said: \"Menstrual blood gets on her garment.\" She said: \"She should wash it with water.\" She said: \"But we wash it and its trace remains.\" She said: \"Water is a purifier.\""],[1004,"Aisha ؓ would see something of menstruation on her garment, and she would rub it off with a stone, a stick, or a horn, then sprinkle it with water."],[1005,"I asked Sa'id b. Jubayr about a junub person who sweats in a garment and then wipes himself with it. He said: \"There is no harm in that.\""],[1006,"He used to see no harm in the sweat of a junub person on a garment."],[1007,"He used to see no harm in it."],[1008,"Not all of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ used to find two garments. He said: \"When you perform ghusl, do you not wear it? So that is for that.\""],[1009,"Regarding a man who has intercourse with a woman, then wears the garment and sweats in it, she saw no harm in it."],[1010,"There is no harm in a junub person or a menstruating woman sweating in a garment that is prayed in."],[1011,"Concerning the junub who sweats in his garment, he said: “It does not harm him, and he need not sprinkle it with water.”"],[1012,"Concerning the menstruating woman when she sweats in her clothes: “It suffices her to sprinkle it with water.”"],[1013,"He used to sweat in the garment while junub, then pray in it."],[1014,"He did not see any harm in the sweat of the menstruating woman or the junub."],[1015,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “What is lawful for me from my wife while she is menstruating?” He said: “She should tie her waist-wrapper tightly, then you may do what you wish with her upper body.”"],[1016,"“She should tie her waist-wrapper tightly upon her lower part, then he may touch her.”"],[1017,"“The menstruating woman: her husband may come to her upon her lower belly and between her thighs; if he ejaculates, she washes what touched her and he performs ghusl.”"],[1018,"I asked Abd al-Karim about the menstruating woman, and he said: Ibrahim said: “Indeed Umm Imran knew that I would thrust into her buttocks.”"],[1019,"A man asked Ata about the menstruating woman, and he saw no harm in what is short of the blood."],[1020,"“When I menstruated, the Prophet ﷺ would order me to wrap a waist-wrapper, and he would touch me.”"],[1021,"Aisha was asked what is permissible for a man from his wife while she is menstruating. She said, \"Anything above the waistcloth.\""],[1022,"I said to Aisha: “What is lawful for a man from his wife when she is menstruating?” She said: “Everything except intercourse.” He said: I said: “And what is forbidden to him from her when they are both in ihram?” She said: “Everything except talking with her.”"],[1023,"She said to a person: “Avoid the place where the blood flows.”"],[1024,"When the harm—meaning the blood—ceases."],[1025,"There is no harm in approaching a menstruating woman between her thighs and in her navel area."],[1026,"She may face you or turn away, except for the anus and the place of menstruation."],[1027,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a blanket, and I experienced what women experience, so I got up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with you? Have you started menstruating?\" I said, \"I have experienced what women experience.\" He said, \"That is what Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam.\" So I got up, attended to my state, then returned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Enter under the blanket,\" so I entered."],[1028,"While I was lying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a velvet cloth, my menstruation started, so I slipped away and took my menstrual garments. He said, \"Have you started menstruating?\" I said, \"Yes.\" She said, \"He called me, and I lay with him in the velvet cloth.\""],[1029,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have intimate contact with one of his wives over the waist-wrapper while she was menstruating."],[1030,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command one of us, when she was menstruating, to tie her waist-wrapper firmly, then he would have intimate contact with her."],[1031,"I used to put on a waist-wrapper while I was menstruating, then I would enter with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under his blanket."],[1032,"Ibn Jubayr was asked: What may a man have from his wife when she is menstruating? He said, \"Whatever is above the waist-wrapper.\""],[1033,"About the menstruating woman, he said: \"The bedding is one, but the blankets are separate. If they do not find any, he should throw part of his blanket over her.\""],[1034,"He may have what is above the navel—or the navel."],[1035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wrap me when I was menstruating, and he would touch my head while there was a cloth between me and him."],[1036,"The Jews, when a woman among them menstruated, would not eat with her or drink with her, and they would turn her out of the house, and she would not be with them in the houses. The Prophet ﷺ was asked about that, and Allah, the Exalted, sent down: {They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is harm} [al-Baqarah 222]. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to eat with them, and to drink with them, and to have them with them in the houses, and to do everything except intercourse. The Jews said, “This man does not want to leave anything of our affair except that he opposes us in it.” Then ʿAbbād b. Bishr and Usayd b. Ḥuḍayr came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of that, and said, “O Messenger of Allah, should we not have intercourse with them during menstruation?” The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed greatly, so much so that we thought he was angry with them. They stood up and left, and a gift of milk met them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent after them and brought them back and gave them to drink, so we knew that he was not angry with them."],[1037,"I asked Sālim b. ʿAbd Allāh about a man who lies with his wife under one blanket while she is menstruating. He said, “As for us, the family of ʿUmar, we avoid them when they are menstruating.”"],[1038,"“There is no harm in using the leftover water of a woman’s ablution as long as she is not in a state of major ritual impurity or menstruating.”"],[1039,"“She places it—meaning on the private part.”"],[1040,"He used to “touch his wives while they were menstruating, when she had a waist-wrapper that reached to the middle of her thighs or her knees, girded with it.”"],[1041,"“I used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was menstruating.”"],[1042,"\"I used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was menstruating.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 277)"],[1043,"The slave-girls of Ibn ʿUmar used to “wash his feet while they were menstruating, and hand him the prayer mat.”"],[1044,"“I would be brought a vessel and I would put my mouth to it and drink while I was menstruating, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place his mouth on the place where I had placed mine and drink. And I would be brought a bone with meat and I would bite from it, and he would place his mouth on the place where I had placed mine and bite from it. Then he would order me, and I would put on a waist-wrapper while I was menstruating, and he would touch me.”"],[1045,"It used to be said: “The menstruating woman—her menstruation is not in her hand; she may wash her hand and knead dough and prepare nabīdh.”"],[1046,"“Indeed, the menstruating woman—her menstruation is not in her hand.”"],[1047,"I asked Ibrāhīm about shaking hands with a Jew, a Christian, a Magian, and a menstruating woman, “and he did not deem it to require ablution.”"],[1048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the mosque and said to a young girl, “Hand me the prayer mat.” She said—meaning he wanted to spread it and pray on it—she said, “She is menstruating.” He said, “Her menstruation is not in her hand.”"],[1049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring his head out to me from the mosque, and I would wash it."],[1050,"He used to \"see no harm in a menstruating woman assisting a sick person in performing ablution.\""],[1051,"\"I used to wash the head of the Prophet ﷺ while I was menstruating.\""],[1052,"\"I used to wash the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was menstruating and he was in i'tikaf.\""],[1053,"Abu Zabyan sent to Ibrahim asking him about a menstruating woman assisting a sick person in performing ablution. He said: \"Yes, and she may support him.\" He said: No."],[1054,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Hand me the prayer mat.\" She said: \"I am menstruating.\" He said: \"It is not in your hand.\""],[1055,"That he was asked about a menstruating woman who drank from some water — can one perform ablution with it? He laughed and said: \"Yes.\""],[1056,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about eating with a menstruating woman. He said: \"Eat with her.\""],[1057,"That he used to order his slave girl to hand him the prayer mat from the mosque, and she would say: \"I am menstruating,\" and he would say: \"Your menstruation is not in your palm,\" so she would hand it to him."],[1058,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about eating with a menstruating woman, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Some of my family is indeed menstruating, and we are surely eating dinner together, if Allah wills.\""],[1059,"That she used to \"see no harm in a menstruating woman touching the prayer mat.\""],[1060,"Regarding \"a menstruating woman, when she becomes pure from the blood, her husband should not approach her until she performs the ritual bath.\""],[1061,"Sufyan was asked: May a man have intercourse with his wife when the blood has ceased from her before she performs the ritual bath? He said: \"No.\" It was said: What do you think if she leaves the ritual bath for two days or several days? He said: \"She is asked to repent.\""],[1062,"From Mujahid: {And do not approach them until they are pure} [al-Baqarah 222]. He said: \"Until the blood ceases.\" {Then when they have purified themselves} [al-Baqarah 222]. He said: \"When they have performed the ritual bath.\""],[1063,"\"When the blood ceases.\" {Then when they have purified themselves} [al-Baqarah 222]. He said: \"They have performed the ritual bath.\""],[1064,"I asked Mujahid about a woman who sees purity: is it lawful for her husband to come to her before she performs the ritual bath? He said: \"No, not until prayer becomes lawful for her.\""],[1065,"\"He may not have intercourse with her until she performs the ritual bath.\""],[1066,"Regarding the man who steps on his wife while she has seen her period before she takes a ritual bath (ghusl), Al-Hasan said: \"She is considered menstruating until she takes a bath, and he is required to perform the expiation (kaffarah), and he may not approach her until she takes a bath.\""],[1067,"\"Her husband does not overshadow her.\""],[1068,"By Allah, \"I do not have intercourse with my wife on the day she becomes pure until a day has passed.\""],[1069,"About a woman who sees purity: may her husband come to her before she performs the ritual bath? He said: \"No, not until she performs the ritual bath.\""],[1070,"About a woman from whom the blood has ceased. He said: \"If desire overtakes him, she washes her private part and then he may come to her.\""],[1071,"I heard Sharik when a man asked him: A woman from whom the blood has ceased, may her husband come to her before she performs the ritual bath? He said: Abd al-Malik said from Ata that he \"granted a dispensation in that for the one overcome by desire.\""],[1072,"\"I saw women among the women of Madinah praying in dyed garments.\""],[1073,"She was asked about a woman who wipes over dyed garments. She said: \"That my hand be cut off with knives is dearer to me than that.\""],[1074,"A woman asked Aishah: May a woman pray while wearing dyed garments? She said: \"Remove it, and woe to you.\""],[1075,"\"Our women used to dye their hands at night. In the morning they would open it, perform ablution, and pray; then they would dye after the prayer. When it was near noon they would open it, perform ablution, and pray with the best dye, and it did not prevent prayer.\""],[1076,"The women of Ibn Umar \"used to dye their hands while they were menstruating.\""],[1077,"\"When our women had prayed the last evening prayer, they would dye their hands. In the morning they would release it, perform ablution, and pray. When they had prayed noon, they would dye their hands. When they wanted to pray the afternoon prayer, they would release it and improve its dye, and they would not be kept from prayer.\""],[1078,"Concerning one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, they both said: \"It is a sin he has committed; let him seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, and not do it again.\""],[1079,"\"It is a sin he has committed, and there is no expiation upon him.\""],[1080,"He was asked about the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: \"He should apologize to Allah and repent to Allah.\""],[1081,"\"Seek Allah's forgiveness, and there is nothing upon you.\""],[1082,"He was asked, while I was listening, about a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: \"He should seek Allah's forgiveness.\""],[1083,"A man came to Abu Bakr and said: \"I saw in a dream as if I was urinating blood.\" He said: \"Do you have intercourse with your wife while she is menstruating?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Fear Allah and do not do it again.\""],[1084,"\"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said, 'He seeks forgiveness from Allah.'\""],[1085,"Concerning one who breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan, he said: \"He must free a slave, or offer a sacrificial camel, or give twenty sa's to forty poor people. And the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating is the same.\""],[1086,"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: “He should give half a dinar in charity.”"],[1087,"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: “He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.”"],[1088,"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: “He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.”"],[1089,"“If he comes to her while there is blood, then a dinar; and if he comes to her after the blood has ceased, then half a dinar.”"],[1090,"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: “He should give half a dinar in charity.”"],[1091,"Umar b. al-Khattab had a wife who disliked intercourse, and whenever he wanted to come to her she would excuse herself on account of menstruation. He then had intercourse with her and found that she was truthful. So he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered him “to give two-fifths of a dinar in charity.”"],[1092,"“If a man comes to his wife while she is menstruating, if the blood is fresh, let him give a dinar in charity; and if it is yellowish, let him give half a dinar in charity.”"],[1093,"He was asked about the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: “He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.”"],[1094,"“If he has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he must give a dinar in charity.”"],[1095,"Regarding a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: “He should give a dinar in charity.”"],[1096,"“He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.”"],[1097,"Regarding a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating or after she has seen purity but has not yet bathed, he said: “He should seek Allah’s forgiveness and give one-fifth of a dinar in charity.”"],[1098,"If a man has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he should give half a dinar in charity.” A man from the people said to him, “But al-Hasan says he must free a slave.” He said, “I do not forbid you from drawing near to Allah as much as you are able.”"],[1099,"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said, “He should give a dinar in charity.”"],[1100,"I asked Hafsah bt. 'Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Abi Bakr. I said to her, “I want to ask you about something, but I am too shy to ask you about it.” She said, “Ask, O son of my brother, whatever occurs to you.” He said, “I ask you about coming to women in their back passages.” She said, “Umm Salamah narrated to me: The Ansar used not to mount women from behind, while the Muhajirun did. A man from the Muhajirun married a woman from the Ansar and mounted her from behind, but the Ansari woman refused. She came to Umm Salamah and mentioned that to her. When the Prophet ﷺ came, the Ansari woman felt shy and left, so Umm Salamah mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, ‘Call her to me.’ So she was called, and he said to her, “Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish” [al-Baqarah 223], “through one opening only.” The opening is the single passage.”"],[1101,"\"To separate from them (feminine)\""],[1102,"From Mujahid: “So come to them from where Allah has commanded you” [al-Baqarah 222]. He said, “They were commanded to come from where they were forbidden.”"],[1103,"From Abu Razin: “So come to them from where Allah has commanded you” [al-Baqarah 222]. He said, “From the direction of purity.”"],[1104,"From Mujahid: “And you leave what your Lord has created for you among your wives” [al-Shu'ara' 166]. He said, “By Allah, it is the front.”"],[1105,"From 'Ikrimah: “Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish” [al-Baqarah 223]. He said, “It is only the vulva.”"],[1106,"The Jews did not stop making things difficult for the Muslims. They used to say, “O companions of Muhammad, by Allah, it is not permissible for you to come to your wives except from one direction.” He said, “So Allah revealed, “Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish” [al-Baqarah 223]. Thus Allah left the believers free to satisfy their need.”"],[1107,"“Come to her from her front or from her back, as long as it is in the place of intercourse.”"],[1108,"The people of the Jahiliyyah used to treat a menstruating woman in a manner similar to what the Magians do. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and the verse was revealed: “They ask you about menstruation. Say, ‘It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation and do not approach them until they are pure’” [al-Baqarah 222]. “And the matter regarding them only became more severe.”"],[1109,"From Mujahid: “Say, ‘It is harm’” [al-Baqarah 222]. He said, “It is the blood.”"],[1110,"From Qatadah: “Say, ‘It is harm’” [al-Baqarah 222]. He said, “It is filth.”"],[1111,"If you wish, then withdraw; and if you wish, then do not withdraw."],[1112,"However you wish, meaning: come to her in the vagina."],[1113,"The Jews said to the Muslims, 'Whoever comes to his wife while she is turned away, his child will come out cross-eyed.' So Allah, Exalted is He, revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish}."],[1114,"From 'Ikrimah: {So come to your tilth however you wish} [al-Baqarah 223]. He said: 'He may come to his wife however he wishes: standing, sitting, in front of her, or from behind her.'"],[1115,"From Ibrahim: {So come to them from where Allah has commanded you} [al-Baqarah 222]. He said: 'In the vagina.'"],[1116,"Whoever comes to his wife in her anus, then for him from the woman is the like of that from the man. Then he recited: {And they ask you about menstruation} [al-Baqarah 222]. Say: It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation and do not approach them until they are pure. And when they have purified themselves, then come to them from where Allah has commanded you: to keep away from them during menstruation, the vagina. Then he recited: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish} [al-Baqarah 223] - standing, sitting, facing, or turned away, in the vagina."],[1117,"Whoever comes to a menstruating woman, or a woman in her anus, or a soothsayer and believes what he says, has disbelieved in what Allah sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ."],[1118,"A man came to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud and said, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, may I come to my wife wherever I wish?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And from wherever I wish?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And however I wish?' He said, 'Yes.' A man said to him, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, this one intends evil.' He said, 'No, the anuses of women are forbidden to you.'"],[1119,"He used to dislike a man's coming to his wife in her anus and would severely criticize it."],[1120,"No male mounted a male until the people of Lut."],[1121,"Whoever comes to his wife in her anus, Allah, Exalted is He, will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1122,"When one of you breaks wind in prayer, let him depart, perform ablution, and then pray."],[1123,"I said to Ibn 'Umar: What do you say about female slaves when I apply ḥumayḍ to them? He said, \"What is taḥmīḍ?\" Then I mentioned the anus, so he said, \"Does any Muslim do that?\""],[1124,"We were discussing the matter of women in a gathering of the Banū Wāqif and what is done with them, so Khuzaymah b. Thābit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"O people, Allah is not shy of the truth. Do not approach women in their anuses.\""],[1125,"They used to avoid women during menstruation but would have anal intercourse with them. They asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and Allah, Exalted is He, revealed: \"They ask you about menstruation. Say, 'It is harm, so keep away from wives during menstruation and do not approach them until they are pure. And when they have purified themselves, then come to them from where Allah has ordained you'\" [2:222], meaning in the vagina, and do not go beyond it."],[1126,"About Tawus, Saeed, Mujahid, and Ata, they used to reject women coming from behind them and say, \"It is disbelief.\""],[1127,"\"The ghusl for janābah and ḥayḍ is one and the same.\""],[1128,"He said to his wife, \"Comb through your hair with water before it is combed with fire, for it has little patience.\""],[1129,"I entered with my mother and maternal aunt upon ʿĀʾishah, and one of them asked her, \"How do you perform ghusl?\" She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform ablution like his ablution for prayer, then pour water over his head three times, while we would pour over our heads five times because of the braids.\""],[1130,"He asked ʿĀʾishah about a woman who performs ghusl: does she undo her hair? She said, \"Amazing! Even if she spent an ūqiyah on it? It suffices her to pour water over her head three times.\""],[1131,"\"She combs through it with her fingers.\""],[1132,"Regarding \"the menstruating woman and the ritually impure person: they may pour water over themselves, and they need not undo their hair.\""],[1133,"\"If the water reaches the roots and ends of the hair, she need not undo it.\""],[1134,"\"The wives of Ibn ʿUmar and the mothers of his children, when they performed ghusl, would not undo their braids, whether from menstruation or janābah.\""],[1135,"She said: 'Do not undo your braids, whether due to menstruation or major ritual impurity.'"],[1136,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I tie my hair in a braid or knot tightly.' He said: 'Cup water over your head three times, then press along the trace of each cupful with a squeeze.'"],[1137,"He said to his wife: 'Remove the hair completely; a little remains on it, the Fire will not leave it out.'"],[1138,"He said to his wife: 'Remove the hair completely with water; a little remains on it, the Fire will not leave it out.'"],[1139,"When a woman performs ghusl from major ritual impurity, she should not undo her hair, but pour water onto its roots and wet it."],[1140,"Regarding a woman who has major ritual impurity and her head is tied up—should she undo it? He said: 'No, rather she should pour water over her head thoroughly until the roots of the hair are soaked.'"],[1141,"Is one of you not able, when she purifies herself from her menstruation, to fumigate with some costus; if she cannot find that, then some myrtle; if she cannot find that, then some date pits; if she cannot find that, then some salt."],[1142,"When a woman performs ghusl from menstruation, she should apply perfume to the trace of the blood."],[1143,"His wives and the mothers of his children used to perform ghusl from menstruation and major ritual impurity, then they would not undo their hair, but would be thorough in wetting it."],[1144,"There is no harm in a menstruating woman taking something from the mosque."],[1145,"A menstruating woman may take something from the mosque but not enter it."],[1146,"A person in a state of major ritual impurity may take something from the mosque but not put anything in it."],[1147,"Regarding a menstruating woman who takes something from the mosque, he said: “Yes, except the Mushaf.”"],[1148,"Regarding His saying “or junub” [al-Nisa’ 43] “except those passing through,” he said: “That is the traveler.”"],[1149,"Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ said, \"The person in a state of major ritual impurity (junub) may pass through the mosque but should not sit in it.\" (Surah An-Nisa 43)"],[1150,"“The junub may pass through the mosque but not sit in it.” Then he recited this verse: “or junub except those passing through.”"],[1151,"“He may pass but not sit in it.”"],[1152,"“We used to walk in the mosque while we were junub, and we did not see any harm in that.”"],[1154,"I asked al-Hasan and ʿAta’ about a man who is traveling with his wife and she menstruates, then becomes pure, and does not find water. They both said: “She performs tayammum and prays.” He said: I said to them: “May her husband have intercourse with her?” They both said: “Yes, the prayer is greater than that.”"],[1155,"Regarding a woman who becomes pure and does not find water, he said: “Her husband may have intercourse with her when she has performed tayammum.”"],[1156,"In the excuse of the nation, if you are not menstruating, he said, \"Forty-five.\""],[1157,"He said, \"Three months.\""],[1158,"I asked al-Zuhri about a man who buys a slave girl who has not yet menstruated and one like her cannot become pregnant: how long should he wait before intercourse? He said: “Three months.”"],[1159,"“One month.” ʿAbdullah was asked: “Which of the two do you follow?” He said: “Three months is more certain, and one month suffices.”"],[1160,"“The likeness of the prescribed prayers is like a flowing fresh river at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times every day.”"],[1161,"“Have you considered, if there were a river at the door of one of you in which he bathed five times every day, what would you say—would any of his dirt remain?” They said: “It would not leave any of his dirt.” He said: “Such is the likeness of the five prayers, by which Allah erases sins.”"],[1162,"Jabir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, Asr while it was still bright or clear, Maghrib when the sun set, and Isha sometimes he would hasten it and sometimes delay it. When the people gathered he would hasten, and when they were late he would delay. As for Subh, they would sometimes—or he would sometimes—pray it in the darkness before dawn."],[1163,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz once delayed the prayer, so Urwa b. al-Zubayr entered upon him and informed him that al-Mughira b. Shuba had once delayed the prayer, and Abu Masud al-Ansari entered upon him and said: \"What is this, O Mughira? Do you not know that Jibril descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed,\" then he said: \"With this I have been commanded.\" He said: \"Do you know what you are relating, O Urwa? Or that Jibril established the time of prayer for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Thus Bashir b. Abi Masud used to relate from his father.\" Urwa said: \"And Aisha narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Asr while the sun was in her chamber, before it appeared.\""],[1164,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz once delayed the prayer, so Urwa b. al-Zubayr entered upon him and informed him that al-Mughira b. Shuba had once delayed the prayer, and Abu Masud al-Ansari entered upon him and said: \"What is this, O Mughira? Do you not know that Jibril descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed; then he prayed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed,\" then he said: \"With this I have been commanded.\" He said: \"Do you know what you are relating, O Urwa? Or that Jibril established the time of prayer for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Thus Bashir b. Abi Masud used to relate from his father.\" Urwa said: \"And Aisha narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Asr while the sun was in her chamber, before it appeared.\""],[1165,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the use of the clapper."],[1166,"Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."],[1167,"The Prophet ﷺ had two muadhdhins, Bilal and Ibn Umm Maktum. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until you hear the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum.\""],[1168,"Bilal came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to call him to the Fajr prayer, and they said he was sleeping. So Bilal called out in his loudest voice: \"Prayer is better than sleep,\" and it was then established in the Fajr adhan."],[1169,"The adhan at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was repeated twice, and the iqama once, except that when he said \"Qad qamat al-salah\" he said it twice. When we heard the iqama, one of us would perform ablution and go out."],[1170,"\"Bilal was commanded to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 730)"],[1171,"Anas reported; Bilal was commanded to pronounce Adhan in double pairs and IQAMAH in single pairs. Hammam added in his version; “except IQAMAH”. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 508)"],[1172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded about twenty men to give the adhan, and he liked the voice of Abu Mahdhura, so he taught him the adhan: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar. Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah. Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah. Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah. Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah. Hayya ala al-salah, hayya ala al-salah. Hayya ala al-falah, hayya ala al-falah. Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar. La ilaha illa Allah. And the iqama repeated twice."],[1173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him the adhan with nineteen phrases and the iqama with seventeen phrases."],[1174,"He saw Bilal give the adhan, and he said: \"I began to follow his mouth here and there with the adhan.\""],[1175,"Bilal planted the spear, then gave the call to prayer, and placed his fingers in his ears. I saw him rotating during his call to prayer."],[1176,"Two supplications are not rejected, or seldom rejected: the supplication at the call to prayer and at the time of battle when the two sides are locked in combat."],[1177,"When you hear the muezzin, say the same as he says."],[1178,"We entered upon Mu'awiya and the caller called out: \"Allah is most great, Allah is most great.\" Mu'awiya said: \"Allah is most great, Allah is most great.\" He said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.\" Mu'awiya said: \"And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.\" He said: \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" Mu'awiya said: \"And I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" Yahya said: And one of our companions informed me that when he said: \"Hasten to prayer,\" Mu'awiya said: \"There is no might and no power except with Allah.\" Then Mu'awiya said: \"Thus I heard your Prophet say.\""],[1180,"Mu'awiya heard the muezzin say: \"Allah is most great, Allah is most great,\" so Mu'awiya said: \"Allah is most great, Allah is most great.\" The muezzin said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,\" so Mu'awiya said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,\" then \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.\" The muezzin said: \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,\" so Mu'awiya said: \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" The muezzin said: \"Hasten to prayer, hasten to prayer,\" so Mu'awiya said: \"There is no might and no power except with Allah.\" The muezzin said: \"Hasten to success, hasten to success,\" so Mu'awiya said: \"There is no might and no power except with Allah.\" The muezzin said: \"Allah is most great, Allah is most great, there is no god but Allah,\" so Mu'awiya said: \"Allah is most great, Allah is most great, there is no god but Allah.\" Then he said: \"Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[1181,"When the call to prayer is made, Satan retreats, passing wind, so that he does not hear the adhan. When the adhan is completed, he comes back. When the iqama is made, he retreats. When the iqama is completed, he comes back until he comes between a man and his own self and says: \"Remember this and that,\" things he had not remembered before."],[1182,"Abu Hurayra saw a man leave the mosque after the muezzin had called the adhan, and he said: \"As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.\""],[1183,"The Prophet ﷺ went out when the sun had declined from its zenith and led them in the noon prayer."],[1184,"When the heat is intense, delay the prayer until it is cooler, for intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[1185,"He used to pray the afternoon prayer, then a person would go to the 'Awali area and reach it while the sun was still high."],[1186,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the sunset prayer at the moment the sun set, when its edge had disappeared."],[1187,"My community will continue to be in good state as long as they do not delay the sunset prayer until the stars appear thickly."],[1188,"By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer, meaning the ʿIshāʾ prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it when the moon set on the third night."],[1189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer one night until a third of the night had almost passed or nearly so. Then he came, while the people were asleep, scattered in groups and circles, and he became angry and said: \"If a man were to call the people\"—and ʿAmr said, \"invite the people\"—\"to a bone with meat or two sheep trotters, they would respond to it, yet they stay behind from this prayer. I was determined to order a man to lead the people in prayer, and then I would go after the people of these houses who stay behind from this prayer and set their homes on fire upon them.\""],[1190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer until ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb called out to him: \"The women and children have fallen asleep.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: \"There is no one among the people of the earth who prays this prayer other than you.\" And at that time, no one prayed it except the people of Madinah."],[1191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the prayer one night until most of the night had passed and the people of the mosque fell asleep. Then he came out and prayed it and said: \"This is indeed its time, were it not that I would impose hardship on my community.\""],[1192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the prayer one night. It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the prayer—the women and children have fallen asleep.\" He came out wiping water from his side and saying: \"It is the time, were it not that I would impose hardship on my community.\""],[1193,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to pray Fajr with the Prophet ﷺ, then they would return wrapped in their cloaks, unrecognizable before it became light."],[1194,"Perform the Ṣubḥ prayer when it is bright, for that is greater in reward."],[1195,"Brighten the Fajr prayer, for that is greater in reward."],[1196,"Whoever catches one rakʿah of a prayer has caught it."],[1197,"Whoever catches one rakʿah of Ṣubḥ before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches one rakʿah of ʿAṣr before the sun sets has caught it."],[1198,"When you see a man frequenting the mosque, bear witness to his faith, for Allah says: 'Only those who believe in Allah maintain the mosques of Allah.'"],[1199,"Whoever prays ʿIshāʾ in congregation, it is as if he has stood (in prayer) for half the night. And whoever prays Fajr in congregation, it is as if he has stood (in prayer) for the entire night."],[1200,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ which deeds are most virtuous, or most beloved to Allah. He said, “Prayer at its appointed time.”"],[1201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were in the mosque, seven of us. Three of us were Arabs and four of us were non-Arabs, or four of us were Arabs and three of us were non-Arabs. The Prophet ﷺ came out from one of the corners of the mosque until he sat with us and asked, \"What made you sit here?\" We replied, \"We are waiting for the prayer.\" He then tapped the ground with his finger and turned it over for a while, then raised his head and asked, \"Do you know what your Lord says?\" We replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"He says, 'Whoever performs the prayer at its prescribed time and observes its proper limits, it will be a guarantee for him to enter Paradise. And whoever does not perform the prayer at its prescribed time and does not observe its proper limits, he will not have any guarantee from me. If I will, I will admit him to Hell, and if I will, I will admit him to Paradise.'\""],[1202,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “How will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer beyond its time?” He said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Pray the prayer at its time, then leave. If the prayer is established while you are in the mosque, then pray with them.”"],[1203,"“O Abū Dharr, how will you act when you encounter leaders who delay the prayer beyond its time?” I said, “What do you command me, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them supererogatory.”"],[1204,"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, let him pray it when he remembers it. Indeed, Allah, exalted is He, says: {And establish prayer for My remembrance}."],[1205,"The Messenger of Allah said: \"The one who misses the 'Asr prayer, it is as if he has been cheated out of his family and wealth.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 685)"],[1206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has lost his family and children.\" Abu Muhammad said, \"Or his wealth.\""],[1207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the Trench, “May Allah fill their graves and their homes with fire, just as they kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set.”"],[1208,"Between a servant and shirk, or between him and disbelief, there is nothing except abandoning the prayer."],[1209,"While the people were in the Fajr prayer at Qubāʾ, a man came to them and said, “Indeed, the Qurʾān has been revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he has been commanded to face the Kaʿbah, so face it.” The faces of the people had been toward Syria, so they turned around and faced the Kaʿbah."],[1210,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of those who died while they were praying toward Jerusalem?” Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {And Allah would never let your faith be lost}."],[1211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to open the prayer with the takbīr and open the recitation with {Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds} [al-Fātiḥah 2] and end it with the taslīm."],[1212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not stand for prayer except that he raised his hands, extended."],[1213,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started to pray, he would say Takbir, then say: \"Wajahtu wajhi lilladhi fataras-samawatiwal-arda hanifan wa ma ana minal-mushrikin. Inna salati wa nusuki wa mahyaya wa mamati lillahi rabbil-alamin, la sharika lahu, wa bidhalika umirtu wa ana min al-muslimin. Allahumma! Antal-maliku la ilaha illa ant, ana abduka zalamtu nafsi wa'taraftu bidhanbi faghfirli dhunubi jami'an, la yaghfirudhunuba illa anta, wahdini lihasanil-ahklaqi, la yahdi li ahsaniha illa anta wasrif anni sayy'aha la yasrifu anni sayy'aha illa anta, labaika wa sa'daika, wal-khairu kulluhu fi yadaika wash-sharru laisa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika tabarkta wa ta'alaita astaghfiruka wa atubu ilaik. (Verily, I have turned my face toward Him who created the Heavens and the Earth hanifa (worhsipping none but Allah Alone), and I am not of the idolaters. Verily, my salah, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the all that exists. He has no partner. And of this I have been commanded, and I am one of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the Sovereign and there is none worthy of worship but You. I am Your slave, I have wronged myself and I acknowledge my sin. Forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of manners for none can guide to the best of them but You. Protect me from bad manners for none can protect against them but You. I am at Your service, all goodness is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I rely on You and turn to You, blessed and exalted are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 897)"],[1214,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would get up at night, he would say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. Blessed is Your name and exalted is Your Majesty. There is no deity worthy of worship except You. I seek refuge in Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from Satan, the accursed, from his whispers, breaths, and blowing.' Then he would begin his prayer. Ja'far explained it as follows: 'His whispers refers to death, his breaths refers to poetry, and his blowing refers to arrogance.'\""],[1215,"\"The Prophet, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to begin reciting by saying, 'Praise be to Allah, the Lord of all the worlds' [Al-Fatiha 2].\" Abu Muhammad said, 'With this, we say, and I do not see the need to audibly say 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.'\""],[1216,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ place his right hand over his left, near the wrist."],[1217,"Whoever does not recite the Mother of the Book, there is no prayer for him."],[1218,"He used to remain silent twice: when he entered the prayer and when he finished the recitation. ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn disapproved of that, so they wrote to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, and he wrote back to them that Samurah had spoken the truth."],[1219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remain silent between the takbīr and the recitation—a moment of silence—I think he said a short while. I said to him, \"May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah! What do you say during your silence between the takbīr and the recitation?\" He said, \"I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You have distanced the east from the west. O Allah, purify me from my sins as a white garment is purified from filth. O Allah, wash away my sins with snow and cold water.\""],[1220,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When the reciter says, 'Not of those who earned wrath nor of those who went astray,' and the one behind him says 'Āmīn,' and that coincides with the inhabitants of heaven, his previous sins are forgiven.\""],[1221,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"When the imam says, 'Not of those who earned wrath nor of those who went astray,' say 'Āmīn,' for the angels say 'Āmīn' and the imam says 'Āmīn.' Whoever's saying of 'Āmīn' coincides with the angels' saying of 'Āmīn,' his previous sins are forgiven.\""],[1222,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, 'nor of those who went astray,' he said 'Āmīn' and raised his voice with it."],[1224,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbīr in every raising and lowering, standing and sitting."],[1225,"When he entered the prayer, he said the takbīr and raised his hands level with his shoulders. When he bowed, he said the takbīr and raised his hands. When he raised his head from bowing, he did the same, but he did not raise them between the two prostrations or during the prostration."],[1226,"When he said the takbīr, he raised his hands until they were level with his ears; and when he intended to bow; and when he raised his head from bowing."],[1227,"He prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he used to say the takbīr when he went down and when he came up, raise his hands at the takbīr, and greet to his right and to his left.\" He said: I asked, \"Until the whiteness of his face appeared?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[1228,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group of my people, and we were young men. We stayed with him for twenty nights. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was gentle. When he saw our longing for our families, he said, \"Return to your families, stay among them, teach them and instruct them. Pray as you have seen me pray. When the time for prayer comes, let one of you call the adhān for you, then let the oldest of you lead you.\""],[1229,"When three people are together, let one of them lead them, and the one most entitled to lead them is the one who recites the best."],[1230,"I was with my maternal aunt Maymūnah. The Prophet ﷺ came after ʿIshāʾ and prayed four rakʿahs. Then he got up and said, “Has the boy slept?” or something similar. Then he got up and prayed. I came and stood to his left, and he took my hand and placed me on his right."],[1231,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted a horse and was thrown from it, injuring his right side. He prayed one of the prayers while sitting, and we prayed with him sitting. When he finished, he said, “The Imam is appointed only to be followed, so do not differ from him. When he prays standing, pray standing; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; and when he says, ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him,’ say, ‘Our Lord, to You belongs praise.’ And if he prays sitting, then all of you pray sitting.”"],[1232,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah and said to her, “Will you not tell me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” She said, “Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became seriously ill and asked, ‘Have the people prayed?’ We said, ‘No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah.’ He said, ‘Put water for me in the basin.’ She said, “So we did, and he washed. Then he went to rise but fainted. Then he regained consciousness and asked, ‘Have the people prayed?’ We said, ‘No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah.’ He said, ‘Put water for me in the basin.’ We did so. Then he went to rise but fainted. Then he regained consciousness and asked, ‘Have the people prayed?’ We said, ‘No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah.’ She said, “And the people were remaining in the mosque, waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the last ʿIshāʾ prayer. She said, “So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Abū Bakr, ordering him to lead the people in prayer. She said, “The messenger came to him and said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you to lead the people in prayer.’ Abū Bakr, who was a tender-hearted man, said, ‘O ʿUmar, lead the people in prayer.’ ʿUmar said to him, ‘You are more entitled to that.’ She said, “So Abū Bakr led them in prayer during those days. She said, “Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some lightness in himself and came out supported by two men, one of whom was al-ʿAbbās, for the ẓuhr prayer, while Abū Bakr was leading the people in prayer. When Abū Bakr saw him, he started to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him not to step back and said to the two men, ‘Seat me next to him.’ So they seated him next to Abū Bakr. She said, “Abū Bakr prayed standing, following the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ, while the people prayed following the prayer of Abū Bakr, and the Prophet ﷺ was sitting.” ʿUbaydullāh said, “I entered upon ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās and said to him, ‘Shall I present to you what ʿĀʾishah narrated to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ He said, ‘Bring it.’ So I presented her narration to him, and he did not object to anything in it except that he said, ‘Did she name for you the man who was with al-ʿAbbās?’ I said, ‘No.’ He said, ‘It was ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib.’”"],[1233,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sit on the minbar and say the takbīr, and the people behind him said the takbīr. Then he bowed while he was on the minbar. Then he raised his head, descended backwards, and prostrated at the base of the minbar. Then he returned until he finished the rest of his prayer."],[1234,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I stay away from the dawn prayer because so-and-so makes it very long for us.” I never saw the Prophet ﷺ angrier in giving an admonition than he was that day. He said, “O people, there are some among you who drive others away. Whoever leads the people in prayer should make it brief, for among them are the old, the weak, and those with needs.”"],[1235,"The Prophet ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while still fulfilling it completely."],[1236,"When the call to prayer is given, do not stand until you see me."],[1237,"When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."],[1238,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of the perfection of prayer."],[1239,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Straighten your rows, for your hearts will not be united if your rows are not.\""],[1240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like my superiority over the least of you.” Then he recited this verse: “Only those of His servants who have knowledge fear Allah” [Fatir 28]. Then he said, “Indeed Allah, His angels, the inhabitants of His heavens and His earths, and the whale in the sea send blessings upon those who teach people good.”"],[1241,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ask forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second one once."],[1242,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say, “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Let those of you who possess maturity and understanding stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.” Abū Masʿūd said, “Today you differ even more.”"],[1243,"\"Let those of you who possess understanding and intelligence stand near me, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. And beware of the clamor of the markets.\""],[1244,"\"The best of the rows for men is the first one, and the worst is the last one. The best of the rows for women is the last one, and the worst is the first one.\""],[1245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then turned to face us and said, \"Is so-and-so present?\" They said, \"No.\" Then he said, \"Is so-and-so present?\" They said, \"No,\" referring to a group of hypocrites who had not attended the prayer. Then he said, \"Indeed, these two prayers are the heaviest of prayers upon the hypocrites. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even if they had to crawl.\""],[1246,"\"Indeed, there is no prayer heavier upon the hypocrites than the last evening prayer and the dawn prayer. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even if they had to crawl.\""],[1247,"\"I was about to order my young men to gather firewood, then order a man to lead the people in prayer, and then go to those people who stay away from this prayer and burn their houses down upon them. If it had been a fat bone with meat or two meaty bones, they would have attended it. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even if they had to crawl.\""],[1248,"He stopped at Ḍajnān on a cold night, so he ordered a caller, and he called out, \"Prayer in the dwellings.\" Then he informed that when the Prophet ﷺ was on a journey on a cold or rainy night, he would order a caller, and he would call out, \"Prayer in the dwellings.\""],[1249,"I said to Saʿīd b. al-Musayyab, \"A man prayed in his house, then caught up with the imam while he was praying—should he pray with him?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Which of the two does he count?\" He said, \"The one he prayed with the imam, for indeed Abū Hurayrah...\""],[1250,"\"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees.\""],[1251,"\"If one of you's wife asks permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her.\""],[1252,"Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out, when they go out, without perfume."],[1253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When dinner is served and the prayer is present, then begin with dinner.\""],[1254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When dinner is present and the prayer is established, then begin with dinner.\""],[1255,"\"When you come to the prayer, do not come to it running; come to it walking, and you must be calm. Whatever you catch up with, pray, and whatever you miss, complete.\""],[1256,"\"When you come to the prayer, you must be calm. Whatever you catch up with, pray, and whatever you were preceded in, complete.\""],[1257,"There was a man in Madinah—I do not know anyone in Madinah among those who pray toward the qiblah whose home was farther from the mosque than his—and he used to pray the prayers with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was said to him, \"If only you bought a donkey to ride in the heat and darkness?\" He said, \"By Allah, it does not please me that my home be adjacent to the mosque.\" The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, so he asked him about it. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, so that my footsteps and my steps may be written, and my returning to my family and my coming and my going—or as he said.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah give you all of that, and give you all that you hoped for.\""],[1258,"Ziyad b. Abi al-Ja'd took me by the hand and stood me before an old man of Banu Asad called Wabisah b. Ma'bad, and he said [then he narrated from him]:"],[1259,"That a man prayed alone behind the rows, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat."],[1260,"That his grandmother Mulaykah invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to food she had prepared, and he ate. Then he said, \"Stand up, for I will lead you in prayer.\" Anas said: I went to a mat of ours that had turned black from long use, and I sprinkled it with water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on it, and I and the orphan lined up behind him, and the old woman behind us. He prayed two rak'ahs with us, then left."],[1261,"He used to stand in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr for the length of thirty verses, and in the last two for about half of that. And in 'Asr for the length of the last two of Zuhr, and in the last two for about half of that."],[1262,"He used to recite in Zuhr and Asr: 'By the sky and the night comer' and 'By the sky with constellations.'"],[1263,"He used to recite the Mother of the Qur'an and two surahs with it in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr prayer and Asr prayer, and sometimes he would let us hear a verse, and he would lengthen the first rak'ah."],[1264,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr prayer the Mother of the Book and two surahs, and in the last two the Mother of the Book, and he would let us hear a verse, and he would make the first rak'ah longer than he would make the second, and likewise in Asr prayer and likewise in the dawn prayer."],[1265,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting in Maghrib 'By those sent forth.'"],[1266,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ recite Al-Mursalat in Maghrib. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 986)"],[1267,"Mu'adh used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he would come to his people and lead them in prayer. One night he came and prayed the 'atamah and recited al-Baqarah. A man from the Ansar came and prayed, then left. It reached him that Mu'adh was speaking ill of him, so he complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Mu'adh: 'Are you a tempter? Are you a tempter? Are you a tempter?' or 'A tempter, a tempter, a tempter?' Then he ordered him to recite two surahs from the middle of the mufassal."],[1268,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and heard him recite in one of the two rak'ahs of the dawn prayer: 'And tall date palms.'"],[1269,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting in Fajr in the first rak'ah: 'And tall date palms with layered fruit.'"],[1270,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the dawn prayer: 'When the sun is wrapped up.' When he reached this verse: 'And by the night when it departs,' I began to say to myself: What is the night when it departs?"],[1271,"I entered with my father upon Abu Barzah al-Aslami while he was on an upper room of reeds. My father asked him about the time of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ prayer. He said: 'He used to pray the midday prayer, which you call zuhr, when the sun had passed its zenith. He would pray Asr, then one of us would go to his family in the farthest part of Madinah while the sun was still bright.' He said: 'And I forgot what he mentioned about Maghrib.' He used to prefer to delay the night prayer, which you call 'atamah. He would leave the dawn prayer when a man could recognize his companion, and he would recite in it from sixty to one hundred verses."],[1272,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque while they had raised their eyes in prayer toward the sky. He said: 'Stop that, or your sight will not return to you.'"],[1273,"“What is the matter with people who raise their gazes towards the sky during their prayer?” His statement about that became severe until he said, “You must stop that, or Allah will surely snatch away your eyesight.”"],[1274,"The sons of Abdullah b. Mas'ud, when they bowed, would place their hands between their thighs. I prayed beside Sa'd and did that, and he struck my hand. When he finished, he said, “O my son, place your hands on your knees.” I did it another time after that, on a day, and prayed beside him, and he struck my hand. When he finished, he said, “We used to do this, and we were commanded to place the palms on the knees.”"],[1275,"Shall I not lead you in prayer as the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said, “He said the takbir, bowed, placed his hands on his knees, and spread his fingers until every part of him settled.”"],[1276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, “Place it in your bowing.” Then when “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” [Al-A'la 1] was revealed, he said, “Place it in your prostration.”"],[1277,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ one night, and in his bowing he would say, “Glory be to my Lord, the Great,” and in his prostration, “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” Whenever he came to a verse of mercy, he paused at it and asked, and whenever he came to a verse of punishment, he sought refuge."],[1278,"\"Abu Humaid, Abu Usaid, Sahl bin Sa'd, and Muhammad bin Maslamah were once together and they were mentioning the Salat of Messenger of Allah. Abu Humaid said: 'I am the most knowledgeable among you of the Salat of Messenger of Allah: Messenger of Allah would bow and place his hands on his knees as if he was grasping them, and he would draw his forearms to hold them away from his sides.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 260)"],[1279,"When the Prophet ﷺ began the prayer, he would raise his hands level with his shoulders. When he bowed, he did likewise, and when he raised his head from bowing, he did likewise and said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah, our Lord, and to You belongs praise.” He did not do that in prostration."],[1280,"And when the imam says, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” say, “Our Lord, and to You belongs praise.”"],[1281,"The imam is appointed only to be followed. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he says, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” say, “O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise”; and when he prays standing, pray standing; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting, all of you."],[1282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and taught us our prayer and established for us our sunnah. He said — I think he said: When the prayer is commenced, let one of you lead you. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; and when he says, “not of those who have incurred wrath, nor of those who are astray” [Al-Fatihah 7], say “Amin,” and Allah will answer you. When he says the takbir and bows, say the takbir and bow, for the imam bows before you and raises before you. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, “That corresponds to that.” When he says, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” say, “O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise,” or he said, “Our Lord, to You belongs praise,” for Allah, may He be exalted, said on the tongue of His Prophet, “Allah hears the one who praises Him.”"],[1283,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from bowing, he would say, “Our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter. O worthy of praise and glory, the truest thing a servant has said, and all of us are Your servants. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[1284,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from bowing, he would say, “Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling what is between them and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter.”"],[1285,"\"I have become heavy, so do not precede me in bowing or prostrating. For as long as I get ahead of you when I bow, you will catch up with me when I rise; and as long as I get ahead of you when I prostrate, you will catch up with me when I rise.\""],[1286,"\"Does one of you not fear—or should one of you not fear—when he raises his head before the imam, that Allah may make his head like the head of a donkey, or his form like the form of a donkey?\""],[1287,"The Prophet ﷺ urged them to pray and forbade them from preceding him when he was leading them in bowing and prostration, and from leaving before he finished the prayer. He said, \"I see you from behind me and from in front of me.\""],[1288,"\"Your Prophet was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and was commanded not to tuck up his hair or his garment.\""],[1289,"\"I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones: the forehead\"—Wuhayb said, and he pointed with his hand to his nose—\"and the two hands, the two knees, and the toes of the two feet, and not to tuck up the garments or the hair.\""],[1290,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"When he prostrated, he placed his knees before his hands, and when he rose, he lifted his hands before his knees.\""],[1291,"\"When one of you prays, he should not kneel as a camel kneels. Let him place his hands before his knees.\""],[1292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Be moderate in bowing and prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like a dog spreads them.\""],[1293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade spreading the arms like a beast of prey, pecking like a crow, and a man making a place his permanent spot as a camel does."],[1294,"He used to say between the two prostrations: \"My Lord, forgive me.\""],[1295,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew aside the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr. He said, \"O people, there remains nothing of the glad tidings of prophethood except a righteous dream which a Muslim sees or is shown. Indeed, I was forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, magnify your Lord therein, and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is worthy of being answered for you.\""],[1296,"\"I was forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, magnify the Lord therein, and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is worthy of being answered for you.\""],[1297,"A prayer in which a man does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration does not suffice."],[1298,"“The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal from his prayer?” He said, “He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration.”"],[1299,"While we were sitting around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—or the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting while we were around him, Hammam was unsure—a man entered, faced the qiblah, and prayed. When he finished the prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” The man went back and prayed, and we began watching his prayer, not knowing what defect it had. When he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” Hammam said, “I do not know whether he commanded him that twice or three times.” The man said, “I have not fallen short, so I do not know what you have found defective in my prayer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The prayer of any of you is not complete until he performs wudu thoroughly as Allah ﷻ commanded him, washing his face and his hands up to the elbows, wiping his head, and his feet up to the ankles. Then he says takbir and praises Allah. Then he recites from the Quran whatever Allah ﷻ has permitted him. Then he says takbir and bows, placing his palms on his knees until his joints are at ease and relaxed, and he says, ‘Allah hears the one who praises Him.’ Then he stands upright until he straightens his back, so that every bone takes its proper place. Then he says takbir and prostrates, pressing his face—Hammam said, and perhaps he said his forehead—to the ground until his joints are at ease and relaxed. Then he says takbir and sits upright on his seat and straightens his back.” He described the prayer in this manner for four rakʿahs until he finished. “The prayer of any of you is not complete until he does that.”"],[1300,"When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, he spread his arms so wide that whoever was behind him could see the whiteness of his armpits."],[1301,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, he spread his arms so wide that if a young lamb wanted to pass under him, it could have passed."],[1302,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, he raised his hands, meaning he spread them out, until the whiteness of his armpits was visible from behind him; and when he sat, he settled on his left thigh."],[1303,"His bowing when he bowed, his standing after raising his head from bowing, his prostration, and his sitting between the two prostrations were all nearly the same in length."],[1304,"I observed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his prayer and found that his standing, his bowing, his straightening after bowing, his prostration, his sitting between the two prostrations, his prostration, and his sitting between the taslim and leaving were all nearly the same in length."],[1305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and with him came al-Mughirah b. Shuʿbah, until they found the people had already started the Fajr prayer, and they had put ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf forward to lead them. ʿAbd al-Rahman led them in one rakʿah of the Fajr prayer before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and joined the row with the people behind ʿAbd al-Rahman in the second rakʿah. When ʿAbd al-Rahman said the taslim, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and prayed. The people were startled by that and said much tasbih. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said to the people, “You did well,” or “you did excellently.”"],[1306,"We came to the people while they had stood for prayer, with ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf leading them, and he had already led them in bowing. When he sensed the Prophet ﷺ, he started to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him with his hand to continue leading them. When he said the taslim, the Prophet ﷺ and I stood up and prayed the rakʿah that we had missed."],[1307,"We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in intense heat. If one of us could not press his forehead to the ground, he would spread his garment and pray on it."],[1308,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ supplicating like this in the prayer. Ibn ʿUyaynah pointed with his finger, and Abu al-Walid pointed with the index finger."],[1309,"When he sat in the final part of the prayer, he placed his left hand on his left knee, placed his right hand on his right knee, and pointed his finger."],[1310,"when we (prayed and) sat up during prayer along the Messenger of Allah (may peach be upon him), we said: “Peace be to Allah before it is supplicated for His servants; peace be to so and so. “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not say “Peace be to Allah ,”for Allah Himself is peace. When one of you sits(during the prayer), he should say: The adoration of the tongue are due to Allah, and acts of worship and all good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah’s mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon Allah’s upright servants. When you say that, it reaches every upright servant in heavens and earth or between heavens and earth. I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and apostle. Then he may choose any supplication which pleases him and offer it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 968)"],[1311,"\"And indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the hand of Abdullah and taught him the Tashahhud in prayer, which is: 'All greetings, prayers, and good deeds are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah.' Zuhayr said, 'I think he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.' He hesitated in these two statements; if you do this or finish it, then you have completed your prayer. If you wish to stand, then stand, and if you wish to sit, then sit.\""],[1312,"“I heard Ibn Abi Laila say: ‘Ka’b bin ‘Ujrah met me and said: “Shall I not give you a gift? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and we said: ‘We know what it means to send greetings on you, but what does it mean to send peace and blessings upon you?’ He said: ‘Say: Allahumma salli ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin, kama sallayta ‘ala Ibrahima, innaka Hamidun Majid; Allahumma barik ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin, kama barakta ‘ala Ibrahima, innaka Hamidun Majid (O Allah, send your grace, honour and mercy upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your grace, honour and mercy upon Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, send Your blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your blessings upon Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 904)"],[1313,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in the Majlis of Sa'd bin 'Ubadah and Bashir bin Sa'd said to him: 'Allah has commanded us to send Salah upon you, O Messenger of Allah; so how should we send salah upon you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until we wished that he had not asked him. Then he said: 'Say: 'Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)\" And the salam is as you know.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1285)"],[1314,"When one of you finishes the tashahhud, let him seek refuge with Allah from four things: from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."],[1315,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to greet to his right until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, then greet to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[1316,"I prayed behind a man in Makkah, and he gave two salutations. I mentioned that to 'Abdullah, and he said, 'Where did he get that from?' And al-Hakam said: The Prophet ﷺ used to do that."],[1317,"The Prophet ﷺ did not sit after the prayer except for as long as it takes to say: 'O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.'"],[1318,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to depart from his prayer, he would seek forgiveness three times, then say: 'O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.'"],[1319,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah dictated to me in a letter to Mu'awiyah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say after every obligatory prayer: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.'"],[1320,"None of you should give the devil a share of his prayer, thinking that he is obliged to depart only from his right side. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ often depart from his left side."],[1321,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ depart from his right side."],[1322,"The Prophet ﷺ departed from his right side."],[1323,"Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have taken the rewards. They pray as we pray, and fast as we fast, but they have surplus wealth with which they give charity, while we have nothing to give. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not teach you words by which you will catch up with those who preceded you, and no one who comes after you will reach you except one who does the like of your deed?' He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, magnify Him thirty-three times, and seal it with: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things.'"],[1324,"We were commanded to glorify Allah thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and exalt Him thirty-four times. Then a man, or a man from the Ansar, was shown in a dream, and it was said: 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command you to glorify Allah thirty-three times after every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and exalt Him thirty-four times?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then make them twenty-five, twenty-five, and include the tahlil with them.' The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, and he said: 'Do it.'"],[1325,"The first thing for which a servant will be held accountable is the prayer. If his prayer is found complete, it is recorded for him as complete. If there is any deficiency in it, Allah Almighty says to His angels: 'Look and see if My servant has any voluntary prayers, and complete what is deficient in his obligatory prayer from them.' Then zakah, then the rest of the deeds are judged likewise."],[1326,"I heard Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi say in the presence of ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, one of whom was Abu Qatadah: 'I am the most knowledgeable of you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They said: 'Why? You were not the most frequent of us in following him, nor the earliest of us in his company.' He said: 'Yes, I was.' They said: 'Then present it.' He said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then he said the takbir until every bone settled in its place. Then he recited. Then he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then he bowed and placed his palms on his knees until every bone returned to its place, without lowering his head or raising it. Then he raised his head and said: \"Allah hears the one who praises Him.\" Then he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders — Abu 'Asim thought he said — until every bone returned to its place, standing straight. Then he said: \"Allah is greater,\" then he descended to the ground, keeping his arms away from his sides, then he prostrated. Then he raised his head, bent his left leg and sat on it, and spread the toes of his feet when he prostrated. Then he returned and prostrated again. Then he raised his head and said: \"Allah is greater,\" bent his left leg and sat on it straight until every bone returned to its place. Then he stood up and did the same in the next rak'ah. When he stood up from the two prostrations, he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, as he did at the beginning of the prayer. Then he did the same for the rest of his prayer, until when it was the prostration or the sitting in which the taslim is given, he moved his left leg back and sat on his left side, leaning on it.' They said: 'You have spoken the truth. This is how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was.'"],[1327,"\"I said: 'I am going to watch how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prays.' So I watched him and he stood and said the takbir, and raised his hands until they were in the level with his ears, then he placed his right hand over his left hand, wrist and lower forearm. When he wanted to bow he raised his hands likewise. Then he prostrated and placed his hands in level with his ears. Then he sat up and placed his left leg under him; he put his left hand on his left thigh and knee, and he put the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, then he held two of his fingers together and made a circle, and raised his forefinger, and I saw him moving it and supplicating with it.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 889)"],[1328,"Abu Musa led us in one of the two evening prayers, and a man from the people said: 'The prayer has been combined with piety and zakah.' When Abu Musa finished the prayer, he said: 'Which of you said such-and-such a word?' The people remained silent. He said: 'Perhaps you, O Hittan, said it?' He said: 'I did not say it, and I feared you would rebuke me for it.' A man from the people said: 'I said it, and I intended nothing but good.' Abu Musa said: 'Do you not know what you are to say in your prayer? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and taught us our prayer and made our Sunnah clear to us.' He said, I think he said: 'When the prayer is established, let one of you lead you. When he says the takbir, say the takbir. When he recites \"not of those who have earned anger, nor of those who go astray\" [al-Fatihah 7], say \"Amin,\" and Allah will answer you. When he says the takbir and bows, say the takbir and bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is for that. When he says \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" say: \"O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise,\" or he said: \"Our Lord, and to You is praise,\" for Allah said on the tongue of His Prophet: \"Allah hears the one who praises Him.\" When he says the takbir and prostrates, say the takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you.' The Prophet of Allah said: 'That is for that. When it is time for the sitting, let the first thing one of you says be: \"All greetings, pure words, and prayers are for Allah. Peace, or peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace, or peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\"'"],[1329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to pray carrying Umamah, daughter of Zaynab, on his neck or shoulder. When he bowed, he put her down, and when he stood up, he carried her."],[1330,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was leading the people in prayer with Umamah daughter of Zainab daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ (in his lap). When he prostrated, he put her down and when he got up(after prostration) he lifted her up. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 917)"],[1331,"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him while he was praying, and he returned the greeting to me with a gesture. Layth said: I think he said: with his finger."],[1332,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque of Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, and the people entered and greeted him while he was praying. He said: I asked Suhayb how he returned their greeting, and he said: like this, and he gestured with his hand."],[1333,"Glorification is for men, and clapping is for women."],[1334,"If something happens to you during your prayer, let the men glorify Allah and the women clap."],[1335,"You must pray in your houses, for the best prayer of a person is in his house, except the congregational prayer."],[1336,"He prayed the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ. He said: When the Prophet ﷺ had prayed, there were two men sitting in a corner who had not prayed. He called for them, and they were brought trembling. He said: 'What prevented you from praying?' They said: 'We prayed in our homes.' He said: 'Do not do that. If you pray in your homes and then catch the imam, pray with him, for it will be a voluntary prayer for you.' He said: Then the people stood up and took his hand to wipe their faces with it. He said: I took his hand and wiped my face with it, and it was cooler than snow and more fragrant than musk."],[1337,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone and said: “Is there no man who would give charity to this one by praying with him?”"],[1338,"A man entered the mosque after the Prophet ﷺ had prayed, and he said: “Is there no man who would give charity to this one by praying with him?”"],[1339,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment? He said: “Does each of you find two garments, or do all of you have two garments?”"],[1340,"“None of you should ever pray in a single garment with nothing of it on his shoulder.”"],[1341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two ways of dressing: that one of you should wrap himself in a single garment with nothing between his private part and the sky, and the ṣammāʾ, the wrapping of the Jews."],[1342,"He used to pray on a khumrah."],[1343,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on a mat."],[1344,"He asked Umm Ḥabībah whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in the garment in which he slept with her. She said: Yes, if he did not see any impurity on it."],[1345,"He asked her whether the Prophet ﷺ used to pray in the garment in which he had intercourse with her. She said: Yes, if he did not see any impurity on it."],[1346,"I asked Anas b. Mālik: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray in his sandals? He said: Yes."],[1347,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with his companions, he removed his sandals and placed them to his left, so they removed their sandals. When he finished his prayer he said: “What made you throw off your sandals?” They said: We saw you remove yours, so we removed ours. He said: “Jibrīl came to me—or came—and told me that there was impurity or filth on them. So when one of you comes to the mosque, let him turn over his sandals; if he sees impurity on them, let him wipe it off and pray in them.”"],[1348,"He disliked sadl, and he attributed that to the Prophet ﷺ."],[1349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me while I was prostrating and I had tied back my hair—or he said, I had knotted it—and he released it."],[1350,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, the likeness of this is like the likeness of one who prays while he is bound.”"],[1351,"“When one of you yawns, let him restrain his hand, for indeed Satan enters.”"],[1352,"“When one of you feels sleepy while he is praying, let him sleep until his sleepiness goes away, for perhaps he intends to seek forgiveness but ends up cursing himself.”"],[1353,"“The prayer of a man while sitting is half of the prayer.” He said: I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying sitting, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that you said, ‘The prayer of a man while sitting is half of the prayer,’ and you are praying sitting?” He said, “Yes, but I am not like any one of you.”"],[1354,"“The prayer of a man while sitting is half of the prayer.” He said: I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying sitting, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that you said, ‘The prayer of a man while sitting is half of the prayer,’ and you are praying sitting?” He said, “Yes, but I am not like any one of you.”"],[1355,"“I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray in his voluntary prayer while sitting until one or two years before he passed away. Then I saw him pray in his voluntary prayer while sitting, and he would recite the surah slowly until it became longer than the longest of them.”"],[1356,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about wiping in the mosque, and he said, “If you must do it, then once.”"],[1357,"“When one of you stands for prayer, mercy faces him, so let him not wipe away the pebbles.”"],[1358,"“I have been given five things that no prophet before me was given: a prophet was sent to his people specifically, but I have been sent to all people; war booty has been made lawful for me, but it was forbidden to those before me; the earth has been made for me pure, a place of prostration and a means of purification; our enemy is terrified of us for a month’s journey; and I have been granted intercession.”"],[1359,"“All of the earth is a mosque except the graveyard and the bathhouse.”"],[1360,"“When the prayer becomes due and you find only sheep pens and camel enclosures, then pray in the sheep pens and do not pray in the camel enclosures.”"],[1361,"I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build a similar one for him in Paradise.\""],[1362,"“When one of you comes to the mosque, let him pray two rakʿahs before sitting down.”"],[1363,"when any of you enters the mosque he should invoke blessing on the prophet ﷺ and then he should say: O Allah, open to me the gates of thy mercy. And when he goes out, he should say: O Allah, I ask thee out of Thine abundance. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 465)"],[1364,"I said to Qatādah, “Did you hear Anas say from the Prophet ﷺ, ‘Spitting in the mosque is a sin’?” He said, “Yes, and its expiation is burying it.”"],[1365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When a person prays, they are having a private conversation with their Lord, or their Lord is addressing them directly between them and the qibla (direction of prayer). So when one of you spits, let them spit to their left or under their foot, or say, 'Like this' and spit on their garment and rub it with some of it on the other.\""],[1366,"While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon, he saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque, so he became angry with the people of the mosque and said, “Allah is before one of you when he is in his prayer, so let him not spit,” or he said, “let him not expectorate.” Then he ordered that it be removed, and its place was scraped, and he ordered that it be smeared. Ḥammād said, “I do not know but that he said, ‘with saffron.’”"],[1367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw phlegm on a wall of the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a pebble and scraped it off, then said, “When one of you expectorates, let him not expectorate in front of his face or to his right, and let him spit to his left or under his foot.”"],[1368,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was sleeping in the mosque and struck me with his foot, saying, “Do I not see you sleeping in it?” I said, “O Prophet of Allah, sleep overcame me.”"],[1369,"I used to spend the night in the mosque, and I had no family. I saw in a dream as if I was taken to a well in which there were men hanging, and it was said, “Take him to the right side.” I mentioned the dream to Ḥafṣah and said, “Tell it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She told it to him, and he said, “Who saw this?” She said, “Ibn ʿUmar.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Excellent young man,” or he said, “Excellent man, if only he would pray at night.” He said, “And when I slept, I would not get up until morning.” He said, “So Ibn ʿUmar used to pray at night.”"],[1370,"“When you see someone selling or buying in the mosque, say, ‘May Allah not profit your trade,’ and when you see someone announcing a lost item in it, say, ‘May Allah not return it to you.’”"],[1371,"I said to ʿAmr b. Dīnār, “Did you hear Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh say that a man passed carrying arrows, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, ‘Hold their tips’?” He said, “Yes.”"],[1372,"When the Prophet ﷺ was dying, he began to throw a cloak of his over his face, and when he felt distressed he uncovered his face and said while doing so, “Allah’s curse be upon the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques,” warning against the like of what they had done."],[1373,"Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah caught up with me at al-Balāṭ while I was interlacing my fingers, and he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘When one of you performs ablution and then goes out intending prayer, let him not interlace his fingers.’”"],[1374,"“When you perform ablution and then head to the mosque, do not interlace your fingers, for you are in prayer.”"],[1375,"“Whoever performs ablution and then goes out intending prayer, he is in prayer until he returns to his house, so do not do like this.”"],[1376,"The angels do not cease to send blessings upon the servant as long as he remains in his prayer place where he prayed, so long as he does not get up or break his ablution, saying: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."],[1377,"The Hour will not come until people vie with one another in (building) mosques."],[1378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to al-Baṭḥāʾ at midday and prayed Ẓuhr as two rakʿahs and ʿAṣr as two rakʿahs, with a short spear in front of him, and women's litters were passing in front of him."],[1379,"A short spear used to be planted for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he would pray facing it."],[1380,"When one of you prays, he should not let anyone pass in front of him, and if he refuses, then he should fight him, for he is only a devil."],[1381,"He used to pray facing his riding camel."],[1382,"He used to pray while she was between him and the qiblah, on his family's bed, lying crosswise like a funeral bier."],[1383,"A man's prayer is cut off if there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle: by a donkey, a black dog, and a woman. I said, 'What is it about the black one as opposed to the red or the yellow?' He said, 'I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said, \"The black one is a devil.\" '"],[1384,"A man's prayer is cut off if there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle: by a donkey, a black dog, and a woman. I said, 'What is it about the black one as opposed to the red or the yellow?' He said, 'I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said, \"The black one is a devil.\" '"],[1385,"I and al-Faḍl came on a female donkey while the Prophet ﷺ was praying at Minā or ʿArafah, and I passed by part of the row, then dismounted and left it to graze, and entered the row."],[1386,"Abū Juhaym al-Anṣārī sent me to Zayd b. Khālid al-Juhanī to ask him what he had heard from the Prophet ﷺ about the one who passes in front of a person praying. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For one of you to stand for forty is better for him than to pass in front of a person praying.\" He said: I do not know whether he meant forty years, months, or days."],[1387,"He heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the one who passes in front of a person praying. Abū Juhaym said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If the one who passes in front of a person praying knew what was upon him for that, it would be better for him to stand for forty than to pass in front of him.\" Abū al-Naḍr said: I do not know whether he meant forty days, months, or years."],[1388,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is like a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[1389,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is more excellent than a thousand prayers in any other, except the Sacred Mosque."],[1390,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is more excellent than a thousand prayers in any other, except the Sacred Mosque."],[1391,"The saddles are not to be fastened except for three mosques: the Mosque of the Kaʿbah, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque."],[1392,"Whoever walks in the darkness of night to a prayer, Allah will give him light on the Day of Resurrection."],[1393,"Allah continues to turn towards the servant as long as he does not turn away; and when he turns his face away, He turns away from him."],[1394,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, 'Which deeds are most excellent?' He said, 'Faith without doubt, and jihad without misappropriation, and an accepted Hajj.' It was said, 'Which prayer is most excellent?' He said, 'Length of standing.' It was said, 'Which charity is most excellent?' He said, 'The effort of one with little.' It was said, 'Which emigration is most excellent?' He said, 'That you abandon what Allah has forbidden to you.' It was said, 'Which jihad is most excellent?' He said, 'The one who strives against the polytheists with his wealth and his life.' It was said, 'Which killing is most noble?' He said, 'The one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed.'"],[1395,"Whoever prays the two cool prayers will enter Paradise."],[1396,"Whoever prays the morning prayer is under Allah's protection, so do not let Allah call you to account for His protection. And whoever prays the afternoon prayer is under Allah's protection, so do not let Allah call you to account for His protection."],[1397,"When the prayer is present and a man wants to relieve himself, let him begin with relieving himself."],[1398,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to pray while holding his side."],[1399,"The Prophet ﷺ disliked sleeping before the evening prayer and talking after it."],[1400,"I was with ʿAli b. Abi Talib when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him, and he called out four things until his voice became hoarse: 'Indeed, none will enter Paradise except a believing soul; and no polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year; and no one shall circumambulate the House naked; and whoever has a treaty between him and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, its term is up to four months. Then when the four months have passed, Allah is free from the polytheists, and His Messenger is too.'"],[1401,"Teach the child the prayer when he is seven years old, and strike him for it when he is ten."],[1402,"Three times the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid us to pray in them or to bury our dead in them: when the sun rises until it is high, when the sun stands at its zenith until it declines, and when the sun turns for setting until it sets."],[1403,"There is no prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rises, and no prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."],[1404,"\"She testified concerning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he never missed performing these two units of prayer except after Asr (afternoon prayer).\""],[1405,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never abandoned two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer."],[1406,"Abdullah b. Abbas, Abd al-Rahman b. Azhar, and al-Miswar b. Makhramah sent him to Aishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and they said: Convey our greetings to her all together, and ask her about the two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer, and say: We have been informed that you pray them, and it has reached us that the Prophet ﷺ forbade them. Ibn Abbas said: I used to strike people with Umar b. al-Khattab concerning them. Kurayb said: I entered upon her and conveyed to her what they sent me with. She said: Ask Umm Salamah. I went out to them and told them what she said. They sent me back to Umm Salamah with the like of what they had sent me to Aishah. Umm Salamah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding them, then I saw him praying them. As for when he prayed them, he prayed the afternoon prayer, then entered while there were women from Banu Haram of the Ansar with me, and he prayed them. I sent a slave girl to him and said: Stand beside him and say: Umm Salamah says: O Messenger of Allah, did I not hear you forbidding these two rak'ahs, and I see you praying them? If he gestures with his hand, then withdraw from him. She said: The slave girl did so, and he gestured with his hand, so she withdrew from him. When he finished he said: O daughter of Abu Umayyah, you asked about the two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer. Some people from Abd al-Qays came to me with their people's Islam, and they kept me from the two rak'ahs after the noon prayer, so these are those two."],[1407,"He used to pray two rak'ahs before the noon prayer, two rak'ahs after the noon prayer, two rak'ahs after the sunset prayer in his house, two rak'ahs after the night prayer, and two rak'ahs after the Friday prayer in his house."],[1408,"From Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ , she narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"There is no Muslim servant who prays twelve voluntary Rak'ahs every day, other than the obligatory prayers, except that Allah will build a house for him in Paradise or a palace in Paradise.\" Umm Habibah said, \"I have never ceased praying them after I heard this.\" 'Amr ibn Salamah said the same, and Nu'man said the same."],[1409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not abandon four rak'ahs before the noon prayer and two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer."],[1410,"Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, for whoever wishes."],[1411,"The mu'adhdhin would call the adhan for the sunset prayer at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the foremost of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stand and hurry to the pillars until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while they were like that. He said: And he would seldom stay long."],[1412,"The Prophet ﷺ used to hide what he would recite in them, and he mentioned, \"Say, O disbelievers\" [Surah Al-Kafirun 1] and \"Say, He is Allah, [who is] One\" [Surah Al-Ikhlas 1]. Sa'id said in the two units of Fajr prayer."],[1413,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two light rak'ahs after the dawn broke, and it was a time when I would not enter upon the Prophet ﷺ."],[1414,"When the mu'adhdhin finished the adhan for the dawn prayer and the dawn broke, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray two light rak'ahs before the iqamah was given."],[1415,"He used to pray two rak'ahs after the Friday prayer."],[1417,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the two units before dawn, if he had a need, he would speak to me about it; otherwise, he would go out to the prayer."],[1418,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray from the evening (Isha) prayer until the dawn (Fajr) prayer eleven voluntary units (raka'at), and he would conclude every two units with the Tasleem (saying Assalamu Alaikum). He would perform the Witr prayer with one unit. When the Mu'athin finished the Adhan, he would perform two light units (raka'at), then lie down until the Mu'athin comes to him and he would go out with him."],[1419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺas saying: When the iqamah is pronounced for prayer, no prayer is valid except the obligatory prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1266)"],[1420,"The prayer was established, and the Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying the two units. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, the people surrounded him, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Are you praying the morning prayer as four?\""],[1421,"\"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory.\""],[1422,"Son of Adam, pray four units for Me at the beginning of the day, and I will suffice you at its end."],[1423,"No one has told us that he saw the Prophet ﷺ praying the forenoon prayer except Umm Hāniʾ, for she mentioned that on the day of the conquest of Makkah he bathed in her house and then prayed eight units. She said, \"And I did not see him pray any prayer lighter than it, except that he completed the bowing and prostration.\""],[1424,"She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the conquest and found him bathing while his daughter Fāṭimah was shielding him with a cloth. She said, \"I greeted him, and that was in the forenoon.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Who is this?\" I said, \"I am Umm Hāniʾ.\" She said, \"When he finished his bath, he stood and prayed eight units, wrapped in a single cloth. Then he left.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the son of my mother claims that he will kill a man I have granted protection to, Fulān b. Hubayrah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We have granted protection to the one you have granted protection to, O Umm Hāniʾ.\""],[1425,"She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the conquest and said, “O Messenger of Allah, my cousin claims that he will kill a man I have granted protection to, Fulan b. Hubayrah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “We grant protection to the one you have protected, O Umm Hani’.”"],[1426,"My friend advised me of three things that I will not abandon until I die: praying the Witr prayer before I sleep, fasting three days every month, and performing two units of prayer before the Dhuha prayer."],[1427,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not observe the Duha prayer during travel or at home.\""],[1428,"His father saw people praying the forenoon prayer, and he said, \"Indeed, they are praying a prayer that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never prayed, nor did the majority of his Companions.\""],[1429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them while they were praying after sunrise, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The prayer of the returners is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun.\""],[1430,"\"The prayer of night and day is two units by two units.\""],[1431,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the night prayer, and he said, \"Two units by two units. When one of you fears the coming of dawn, he should pray one unit, making odd what he has already prayed.\""],[1432,"When the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, arrived in Medina, people gathered and said, \"The Messenger of Allah has arrived, the Messenger of Allah has arrived.\" He said, \"So I went out with those who went out, and when I saw his face, I recognized that his face was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him say was, 'O people, spread peace, feed the hungry, maintain family ties, and pray while people are asleep so that you may enter Paradise in peace.'\""],[1433,"I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw a man who was frequently performing bowing and prostration. I said to myself, \"I will not leave until I see whether he moves to the next two cycles of prayer or continues with another one.\" When he finished, I said, \"O Abdullah, did you move to the next two cycles of prayer or continue with another one?\" He replied, \"Truly, I do not know. But indeed, Allah knows.\" Then he said, \"I have heard my beloved friend, Abu Al-Qasim ﷺ , say, 'Whenever a servant prostrates to Allah, Allah elevates him by a degree and removes a sin from him.'\" I asked, \"Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?\" He said, \"I am Abu Dhar.\" At that moment, I lost consciousness."],[1434,"I saw Ibn Abī Awfā pray two units, and he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the forenoon prayer as two units when he was given the good news of the victory or of the head of Abū Jahl.\""],[1435,"I came to al-Ḥīrah and saw them prostrating to a marzubān of theirs. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, should we not prostrate to you?' He said, 'If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands because of the right Allah has placed upon them over them.'"],[1436,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to prostrate to you.' He said, 'If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.'"],[1437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited 'The Star' and prostrated in it, and no one remained except an old man who took a handful of pebbles, raised it to his forehead and said, 'This suffices me.'"],[1438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon one day and recited Ṣād. When he came to the prostration, he descended and prostrated, and we prostrated with him. He recited it another time, and when he reached the prostration, we prepared ourselves for prostration. When he saw us, he said, 'It is only the repentance of a prophet, but I see that you have prepared yourselves for prostration.' So he descended and prostrated, and we prostrated."],[1439,"Regarding the prostration in Ṣād: 'It is not among the prescribed prostrations, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate in it.'"],[1440,"I saw Abū Hurayrah prostrating in 'When the sky is split open.' It was said to him, 'You prostrate in a sūrah in which one does not prostrate?' He said, 'Indeed I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating in it.'"],[1441,"I saw Abū Hurayrah prostrating in 'When the sky is split open.' I said, 'O Abū Hurayrah, I see you prostrating in \"When the sky is split open.\"' He said, 'Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate in it, I would not have prostrated.'"],[1442,"that the Prophet ﷺ prostrated in the [Surah] \"When the sky tears apart\" (Surat al-Inshiqaq)"],[1443,"We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in 'When the sky is split open' and 'Read in the name of your Lord.'"],[1444,"I recited 'By the Star' in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not prostrate in it."],[1445,"Between the time when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the night prayer till the dawn broke, he used to pray eleven rak'ahs, uttering the salutation at the end of every two and observing the witr with a single one, and during that he would make a prostration about as long a one of you would take to recite fifty verses before raising his head. When the mu'adhdhin finished making the call for the dawn prayer, he stood up and prayed two short rak'ahs, then he lay down on his right side till the mu'adhdhin came to him (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1336)"],[1446,"He asked Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night. She said: \"He used to pray thirteen rak'ahs. He would pray eight rak'ahs then pray witr, then pray two rak'ahs sitting down. When he wanted to bow he would stand and bow, and he prayed two rak'ahs between the adhan and iqamah of subh prayer. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1781)"],[1447,"I divorced my wife. I then came to Medina to sell my land that was there so that I could buy arms and fight in battle. I met a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. They said: Six persons of us intended to do so (i.e. divorce their wives and purchase weapons), but the Prophet ﷺ prohibited them. He said: For you in the Messenger of Allah there is an excellent model. I then came to Ibn 'Abbas and asked him about the witr observed by the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I point to you a person who is most familiar with the witr observed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Go to 'Aishah. While going to her I asked Hakim b. Aflah to accompany me. He refused, but I adjured him. He, therefore, went along with me. We sought permission to enter upon 'Aishah. She said: Who is this ? He said: Hakim b. Aflah. She asked: Who is with you ? He replied: Sa'd b. Hisham. She said: Hisham son of 'Amir who was killed in the Battle of Uhud. I said: Yes. She said: What a good man 'Amir was! I said: Mother of faithful, tell me about the character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She asked: Do you not recite the Quran ? The character of Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the Qur'an. I asked: Tell me about his vigil and prayer at night. She replied: Do you not recite: \"O thou folded in garments\" (73:1). I said: Why not ? When the opening of this Surah was revealed, the Companions stood praying (most of the night) until their fett swelled, and the concluding verses were not revealed for twelve months from heaven. At last the concluding verses were revealed and the prayer at night became voluntary after it was obligatory. I said: Tell me about the witr of the Prophet ﷺ. She replied: He used to pray eight rak'ahs, sitting only during the eighth of them. Then he would stand up and pray another rak'ahs. He would sit only after the eighth and the ninth rak'ahs. He would utter salutation only after the ninth rak'ah. He would then pray two rak'ahs sitting and that made eleven rak'ahs, O my son. But when he grew old and became fleshy he observed a witr of seven, sitting only in sixth and seventh rak'ahs, and would utter salutation only after the seventh rak'ah. He would then pray two rak'ahs sitting, and that made nine rak'ahs, O my son. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not pray through a whole night, or recite the whole Qur'an in a night or fast a complete month except in Ramadan. When he offered prayer, he would do that regularly. When he was overtaken by sleep at night, he would pray twelve rak'ahs. The narrator said: I came to Ibn 'Abbas and narrated all this to him. By Allah, this is really a tradition. Has I been on speaking terms with her, I would have come to her and heard it from her mouth. I said: If I knew that you were not on speaking terms with her, I would have never narrated it to you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1342)"],[1451,"that the Prophet ﷺ said, \"The best [voluntary] ritual prayer after the farḍ (mandatory) prayer is [that which is done] in the middle of the night.\""],[1452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever sleeps away from his nightly portion or from something of it, then recites it between the Fajr prayer and the Ẓuhr prayer, it will be written for him as if he had recited it during the night.'"],[1453,"Allah, Exalted is He, descends to the lowest sky every night at the last half of the night or the last third of the night and says, 'Who is it that calls upon Me so that I may answer him? Who is it that asks of Me so that I may give him? Who is it that seeks My forgiveness so that I may forgive him?' until dawn breaks or the reciter finishes the Fajr prayer."],[1454,"Our Lord, blessed is His name, descends every night when the last third of the night remains to the lowest sky and says, 'Who calls upon Me so that I may answer him? Who seeks My forgiveness so that I may forgive him? Who asks of Me so that I may give him?' until dawn."],[1455,"Allah, the Exalted, descends every night to the lowest sky and says: Is there anyone who asks, that I may give him? Is there anyone who seeks forgiveness, that I may forgive him?"],[1456,"When half of the night has passed, or two-thirds of it, Allah descends to the lowest sky, then He says: I will not ask about My servants from anyone other than Me. Who is it that asks Me, that I may give him? Who is it that seeks My forgiveness, that I may forgive him? Who is it that calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Until the dawn rises."],[1457,"When one-third of the night remains, or half of the night, and he mentioned the descent."],[1458,"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak before every prayer, and I would have delayed the last night prayer until one-third of the night. For when the first third of the night has passed, Allah descends to the lowest sky and remains there until dawn rises, saying: Is there anyone who asks, that he may be given? Is there anyone who calls, that he may be answered? Is there anyone sick, that he may be healed? Is there any sinner seeking forgiveness, that he may be forgiven?"],[1459,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to perform the night prayer, he would say: O Allah, to You belongs all praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. To You belongs all praise. You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. To You belongs all praise. You are the King of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. You are the Truth, Your word is truth, Your promise is truth, meeting You is truth, Paradise is truth, Paradise is truth, Hellfire is truth, the resurrection is truth, the prophets are truth, and Muhammad ﷺ is truth. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have argued, and to You I have appealed for judgment. So forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have made public and what I have kept secret. You are the One who brings forward and You are the One who delays. There is no god but You, and there is no power and no strength except with You."],[1460,"Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah Al-Baqarah at night, they will suffice him."],[1461,"Allah does not listen to anything as He listens to a prophet reciting the Quran with a beautiful voice, reciting it aloud."],[1462,"The Prophet ﷺ heard Abu Musa while he was reciting, and he said: This man has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud."],[1463,"He is not one of us who does not beautify his voice with the Quran."],[1464,"Allah does not listen to anything as He listens to a prophet reciting the Quran with a beautiful voice."],[1465,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me and said, “Did Allah not say: ‘O you who believe, respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you’ [al-Anfāl 24]?” Then he said, “Shall I not teach you a sūrah greater than any sūrah in the Qur’an before I leave the mosque?” When he wanted to leave, he said, “Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. It is the Seven Oft-Repeated and the Mighty Qur’an that you have been given.”"],[1466,"“He does not understand who recites the Qur’an in less than three (days).”"],[1467,"When the call to prayer is given, Satan turns away, passing wind so that he does not hear the call. When the call is finished, he returns. When the iqāmah is given, he turns away, and when the iqāmah is finished, he returns, until he whispers between a man and his self, saying, “Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such,” something he had not been remembering, until the man remains not knowing how much he has prayed. So if one of you does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him prostrate twice while sitting."],[1468,"“If one of you does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him stand and pray a rakʿah, then afterwards prostrate twice. If he had prayed five, they make his prayer even; and if he had prayed four, they are a humiliation for Satan.”"],[1469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the two evening prayers and prayed two rakʿahs, then said the salutation and went to a piece of wood lying across the mosque and placed his hand on it. Yazīd said: Ibn ʿAwn showed us, placing his palms one on the back of the other and inserting his upper fingers into the lower ones, and he stood as if angry. The hasty people went out saying, “The prayer has been shortened, the prayer has been shortened.” Among the people were Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, who did not speak. Among the people was a man with long arms called Dhū al-Yadayn, who said, “O Messenger of Allah, did you forget or has the prayer been shortened?” He said, “I did not forget, nor has the prayer been shortened.” He said, “Then is it as you say?” They said, “Yes.” So he returned and completed what remained, then said the salutation, said the takbīr and prostrated for a long time. Then he raised his head, said the takbīr and prostrated as he had prostrated, then raised his head and departed."],[1470,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon or afternoon prayer and said the salutation after two rakʿahs of one of them. Dhū al-Shimālayn b. ʿAbd ʿAmr b. Naḍlah al-Khuzāʿī, an ally of Banū Zuhrah, said to him, “Has it been shortened, or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I did not forget, nor has it been shortened.” Dhū al-Shimālayn said, “Some of that has occurred, O Messenger of Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to the people and said, “Is Dhū al-Yadayn truthful?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and completed the prayer. None of them told me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated twice while sitting in that prayer, and that is, as it appears – and Allah knows best – because the people made the Messenger of Allah ﷺ certain until he was sure."],[1471,"“He prayed the noon prayer with five (rakʿahs), and he was told, so he prostrated twice.”"],[1472,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in two rakʿahs, then stood and did not sit. The people stood with him. When he finished the prayer, we expected his salutation, but he said the takbīr and prostrated twice while sitting before saying the salutation, then he said the salutation.”"],[1473,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up from the two rakʿahs of the noon or afternoon prayer and did not return until he finished his prayer, then he prostrated the two prostrations of inadvertence, then he said the salutation.”"],[1474,"Al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah led us in prayer. When he had prayed two rakʿahs, he stood and did not sit. Those behind him glorified Allah at him, but he gestured to them to stand. When he finished his prayer, he said the salutation, prostrated the two prostrations of inadvertence, said the salutation, and said, “Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do with us.”"],[1475,"Ṣadaqah narrated to us: Ibn ʿUlayyah and Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd informed us, from Ḥajjāj al-Ṣawwāf, from Yaḥyā, from Hilāl, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Muʿāwiyah, something similar."],[1476,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded killing the two black creatures during prayer.”"],[1477,"You may shorten the prayer if you fear [an-Nisa' 101]. People have become secure. He said: I wondered at what you wondered at. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A charity Allah has bestowed upon you, so accept it.”"],[1478,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs at Mina, Abu Bakr two rakʿahs, ʿUmar two rakʿahs, and ʿUthman two rakʿahs at the beginning of his rule; then he completed it after that.”"],[1479,"“We prayed Ẓuhr with the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah four rakʿahs, and we prayed with him at Dhul-Ḥulayfah two rakʿahs.”"],[1480,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed four rakʿahs in Madinah and two rakʿahs at Dhul-Ḥulayfah.”"],[1481,"“Prayer, when it was first prescribed, was two rakʿahs. The travel prayer remained as it was, and the resident prayer was completed.” I said, “What about her? She used to complete the prayer while traveling?” He said, “She interpreted as ʿUthman interpreted.”"],[1482,"“We set out with the Prophet ﷺ, and he kept shortening until we reached Makkah. He stayed there ten days, shortening until he returned, and that was during his ḥajj.”"],[1483,"“The stay of the emigrant after completing his rites is three days.”"],[1484,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted the emigrants permission to remain three days in Makkah after the departure.”"],[1485,"“He used to pray on his mount facing east, and when he wanted to pray an obligatory prayer, he would dismount and face the qiblah.”"],[1486,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing voluntary prayer while on his mount, nodding with his head in whatever direction he faced, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do that for the obligatory prayer.”"],[1487,"“We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the Tabuk expedition. He would combine the prayer, praying Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr together, then he entered; then he came out after that and prayed Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ together.”"],[1488,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ at Muzdalifah, combining them.”"],[1489,"He used to combine Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ when travel became urgent for him."],[1490,"Saʿīd b. Jubayr led us in prayer at Jamʿ with one iqāmah: Maghrib as three rakʿahs, then when he said salām, he stood and prayed ʿIshāʾ as two rakʿahs. Then he narrated from Ibn ʿUmar that he did the same for them in that place, and Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did the same in that place."],[1491,"He would not arrive from a journey except during the day, in the forenoon, then he would enter the mosque and pray two rakʿahs, then sit for the people."],[1492,"“I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ toward Najd. We confronted the enemy and lined up against them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to lead us in prayer. One group of us stood with him and another group faced the enemy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led those with him in one rakʿah and two prostrations, then they departed and took the place of the group that had not prayed. The group that had not prayed came, and the Prophet ﷺ led them in one rakʿah and two prostrations, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said salām. Then each Muslim man stood and prayed one rakʿah and two prostrations for himself."],[1493,"About the prayer of fear, he said: “The imam prays with one group while another group faces the enemy. He prays one rakʿah with those who are with him, then these go to the battle lines of their companions, and those come, and he prays one rakʿah with them, and they make up one rakʿah for themselves.”"],[1494,"We were detained on the Day of the Trench until a portion of the night had passed, until we were relieved—and that is the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And Allah sufficed the believers in battle, and Allah is ever Strong and Mighty} [al-Ahzāb 25]. The Prophet ﷺ called Bilāl and ordered him, so he gave the iqāmah and he prayed Ẓuhr, performing it well as he used to pray it in its time. Then he ordered him, so he gave the iqāmah for ʿAṣr and prayed it. Then he ordered him, so he gave the iqāmah for Maghrib and prayed it. Then he ordered him, so he gave the iqāmah for ʿIshāʾ and prayed it. That was before the revelation of {And if you fear, then [pray] on foot or riding} [al-Baqarah 239]."],[1495,"“The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of the death of any person, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when you see them, stand and pray.”"],[1496,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed during an eclipse eight rakʿahs in four prostrations.”"],[1497,"A Jewish woman entered upon her and said, “May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave.” When the Prophet ﷺ came, she asked him: “Will people be punished in their graves?” He said, “I seek refuge in Allah.”"],[1499,"When one of you finishes the tashahhud, let him seek refuge with Allah from four things: from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."],[1500,"The sun was eclipsed, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and his prayer was narrated by Ibn Abbas that he ﷺ prayed two units (rak'ahs) in each unit (rak'ah), then he gave them a sermon and said, \"Verily, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death or life of any person. So, when you witness that, hasten to the remembrance of Allah.\""],[1501,"The sun eclipsed, so the Prophet ﷺ prayed. She (the narrator) recounted that he prayed two rakʿahs, in each rakʿah two bowings."],[1502,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered, when the sun eclipsed, the freeing of a slave."],[1503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with the people to the muṣallá seeking rain, faced the qiblah, and turned his cloak inside out."],[1504,"The Prophet ﷺ went out with the people to the muṣallá to seek rain for them. He stood and supplicated to Allah while standing, then turned toward the qiblah and turned his cloak inside out, and they were given rain."],[1505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not raise his hands in any supplication except in the prayer for rain."],[1506,"When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[1507,"The Friday ghusl is obligatory upon every adult."],[1508,"While ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb was delivering a sermon, a man entered, and ʿUmar alluded to him. The man said, \"O Commander of the Believers, I did no more than perform wuḍūʾ when I heard the call.\" ʿUmar said, \"And wuḍūʾ as well? Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'When one of you comes on Friday, let him perform ghusl'?\""],[1509,"Whoever performs wuḍūʾ for Friday, it is acceptable and good; and whoever performs ghusl, ghusl is better."],[1510,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, purifies himself as much as he is able, then anoints himself with his oil or touches perfume from his house, then goes out and does not separate between two people, and prays what is decreed for him, and when the imam comes out, listens attentively, he will be forgiven for what is between that Friday and the next."],[1511,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the dawn prayer: Tanzīl al-Sajdah and Hal Atā ʿalā al-Insān."],[1512,"The one who hastens to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then the one who comes after him is like one who offers a cow, then the one who comes after him is like one who offers a sheep. When the imam sits on the pulpit, the records are folded up and they sit listening to the reminder."],[1513,"When it is the day of Friday, the angels sit at the doors of the mosque and record those who come to Friday. When the imam goes out, the angels fold up the records and enter to listen to the reminder."],[1515,"We used to pray Friday with the Prophet ﷺ, then we would return and race to find shade in the fortress of Banū Ghanm, and there was only enough for the places of our feet."],[1516,"We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would depart when the walls had no shade for us to seek shelter in."],[1517,"Whoever washes and bathes on Friday, then sets out early and arrives early, then sits close to the imam and listens attentively and does not engage in idle talk until the imam finishes, for every step he takes he will have the reward of a year's fasting and standing in prayer."],[1518,"If you say to your companion, 'Listen,' while the imam is delivering the sermon, you have engaged in idle talk."],[1519,"If you say to your companion, 'Listen,' while the imam is delivering the sermon, you have engaged in idle talk."],[1520,"When one of you comes while the imam is delivering the sermon or has already come out, let him pray two rakʿahs."],[1521,"Abū Saʿīd came while Marwān was delivering the sermon. He stood to pray two rakʿahs. The guards came to prevent him, and he said, 'I would not abandon them, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command them.'"],[1522,"I saw al-Ḥasan pray two rakʿahs while the imam was delivering the sermon."],[1523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us one day and recited Ṣād. When he came to the prostration, he descended and prostrated."],[1524,"A man entered the mosque on Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He said, “Have you prayed?” He replied, “No.” He said, “Then pray two rakʿahs.” Abu Muhammad said, “I hold this view.”"],[1525,"ʿAmmār b. Yāsir delivered a sermon to us, and he was eloquent yet concise. We said, “O Abu al-Yaqẓān, if only you had paused a little?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Indeed, the length of a man’s prayer and the brevity of his sermon are a sign of his understanding, so lengthen this prayer and shorten these sermons, for indeed some eloquence is sorcery.’”"],[1526,"“I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate.”"],[1527,"“He would deliver two sermons while standing, and he would separate them by sitting.”"],[1528,"“The Prophet ﷺ had two sermons, sitting between them, reciting the Quran and reminding the people.”"],[1529,"ʿUmārah b. Ruwaybah saw Bishr b. Marwān on the pulpit raising his hands, so he said, “May Allah make these two hands ugly! I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit, and he did not gesture except with his finger.”"],[1530,"He saw Bishr b. Marwān raising his hands supplicating on the pulpit on Friday, so he reviled him and said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit, and he did not indicate except with his finger like this,” and he pointed with his index finger at his waist."],[1531,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand at a palm trunk before the pulpit was made. When the pulpit was made, that trunk yearned until we heard its yearning, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on it and it became still.”"],[1532,"“He used to deliver sermons at a palm trunk before he took the pulpit. When he took the pulpit and moved to it, the trunk yearned, so he embraced it and it became still. He said, ‘Had I not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection.’”"],[1533,"When the people became numerous in Madinah, a man would come and people would come, but they could hardly hear the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they returned from his presence. So the people said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, the people have become numerous, and the one who comes arrives but can hardly hear your words.” He said, “Whatever you wish.” So he sent to a slave boy of a woman of the Anṣār, a carpenter, and to the tamarisk trees of al-Ghābah, and they made for him two or three steps. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sit on it and deliver sermons on it. When they did that, the wooden trunk by which he used to stand yearned, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood by it and placed his hand on it, and it became still."],[1534,"That al-Ḍaḥḥāk b. Qays asked al-Nuʿmān b. Bashīr al-Anṣārī what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite on Friday after Sūrat al-Jumuʿah. He said: “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming [Event]?”"],[1535,"We asked him what the Prophet ﷺ used to recite to them on Friday along with the sūrah in which Friday is mentioned. He said: “He used to recite along with it, ‘Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming [Event]?’”"],[1536,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on the two ʿĪds and on Friday: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming [Event]?’ And sometimes they coincided, so he recited both of them.”"],[1537,"Kaʿb and I met, and I began narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he began narrating to me from the Torah, until we came to the mention of Friday. I said: “Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘In it there is an hour; no Muslim servant coincides with it while praying, asking Allah for good in it, but He gives it to him.’”"],[1538,"That they both heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying while he was on the planks of his pulpit: “Let people desist from neglecting the Friday prayers, or Allah will surely seal their hearts, and then they will surely be among the heedless.”"],[1539,"“Whoever abandons Friday out of disregard for it, Allah seals his heart.”"],[1540,"“Indeed, the best of your days is Friday: in it Adam was created, in it the trumpet blast is, and in it the thunderclap is. So invoke blessings upon me abundantly in it, for your blessings are presented to me.”"],[1542,"He used to pray two rakʿahs after Friday in his house."],[1543,"He used to pray two rakʿahs after Friday."],[1544,"“Whoever among you wishes to pray after Friday, let him pray four rakʿahs after it.”"],[1545,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: “Indeed Allah has aided you with a prayer that is better for you than red camels. He made it for you between the ʿIshāʾ prayer and the rising of dawn.”"],[1546,"Ibn Muhayriz said: A man from Banu Kinanah, named al-Makhdaji, heard a person called AbuMuhammad in Syria, saying: The witr is a duty (wajib). Al-Makhdaji said: So I went to Ubadah ibn as-Samit and informed him. Ubadah said: AbuMuhammad told a lie. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There are five prayers which Allah has prescribed on His servants. If anyone offers them, not losing any of them, and not treating them lightly, Allah guarantees that He will admit him to Paradise. If anyone does not offer them, Allah does not take any responsibility for such a person. He may either punish him or admit him to Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1420)"],[1547,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with disheveled hair and said: “O Messenger of Allah, what has Allah made obligatory upon me of prayer?” He said: “The five prayers and fasting.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed him of the laws of Islam, so he said: “By the One who honored you, I will not do any voluntary act, nor will I reduce anything that Allah has obligated upon me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He will succeed, by his father, if he is truthful; or he will enter Paradise, by his father, if he is truthful.”"],[1548,"I heard Ali saying, \"Verily, Witr (a specific prayer) is not obligatory like the regular prayers, but it is a recommended act, so do not neglect it.\""],[1549,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Verily, Allah is One and loves odd numbers.\""],[1550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rak'ahs during the night, observing a witr out of that with five, he did not sit during the five except the last and then gave the salutation. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Numair reported it from Hisham recently. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1338)"],[1551,"Perform Witr with five; if you cannot, then with three; if you cannot, then with one; if you cannot, then gesture by nodding."],[1552,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the night prayer. He said: \"Two by two; and when one of you fears the coming of dawn, let him pray one rakʿah, which will make Witr what he has prayed.\""],[1553,"The translation of the given text is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray eleven units of prayer from the night prayer (Isha) until the dawn prayer (Fajr). He would make the tasleem (conclude the prayer) after every two units, and he would perform one unit of Witr prayer.\""],[1554,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr and recite: ‘Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High.’, [Al-A’la (87)] ‘Say: O you disbelievers!” [Al-Kafirun (109)] and ‘Say: Allah is One.”. [Al-Ikhlas (112)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1171)"],[1555,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Witr at all parts of the night, and his Witr ended at the pre-dawn time.\""],[1556,"The translation of the Arabic sentence \"أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ سُئِلَ عَنِ الْوِتْرِ فَقَالَ «أَوْتِرُوا قَبْلَ الْفَجْرِ»\" into English is: \"The messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Al-Witr (an odd-numbered prayer), and he said, 'Perform Al-Witr prayer before dawn.'\""],[1557,"\"In the first rak'ah of witr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: \"GLorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High;\" in the second; \"Say: O you disbelievers!\" and in the third; \"Say: He is Allah, (the) One.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1700)"],[1558,"\"Indeed, the Prophet used to perform the Witr prayer while riding a camel.\" It was said to Abu Muhammad, \"Did you follow his example?\" He replied, \"Yes.\""],[1559,"I said to al-Hasan b. ʿAli: What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He carried me on his shoulder, and I took a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth, so he said to me: \"Throw it out; do you not know that charity is not lawful for us?\" He said: And he used to supplicate with this supplication: \"O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, pardon me among those You have pardoned, turn to me among those You have turned to, bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed, You decree and none decrees against You. None is humiliated whom You befriend. Blessed and Exalted are You.\""],[1560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me words to say in the Qunut."],[1561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me some words that I say during the witr. (The version of Ibn Jawwas has: I say them in the supplication of the witr.) They were: \"O Allah, guide me among those Thou hast guided, grant me security among those Thou hast granted security, take me into Thy charge among those Thou hast taken into Thy charge, bless me in what Thou hast given, guard me from the evil of what Thou hast decreed, for Thou dost decree, and nothing is decreed for Thee. He whom Thou befriendest is not humbled. Blessed and Exalted art Thou, our Lord.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1425)"],[1562,"\"Staying up at night is hardship and burden, so when one of you performs Witr, let him pray two rakʿahs; if he gets up during the night, then well and good, otherwise they will be counted for him.\""],[1563,"When he wanted to supplicate against someone or for someone, he performed Qunut after the rukūʿ. Sometimes he would say, after saying \"Allah hears the one who praises Him; our Lord, and to You belongs praise\": \"O Allah, save al-Walid b. al-Walid, Salamah b. Hisham, ʿAyyash b. Abi Rabiʿah, and the weak among the believers. O Allah, intensify Your punishment on Mudar and make years upon them like the years of Yusuf.\" He would say it aloud, and in some of his prayers, in the Fajr prayer, he would say: \"O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so,\" referring to two tribes of the Arabs. Then Allah revealed: \"You have no part in the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers.\""],[1564,"I asked Anas b. Malik about the Qunut. He said: Before the rukūʿ. I said: So-and-so claims that you said after the rukūʿ. He said: He lied. Then he narrated that the Prophet ﷺ performed Qunut for a month after the rukūʿ, supplicating against a tribe of Banu Sulaym."],[1565,"He used to perform Qunut in the Fajr prayer."],[1566,"Anas b. Malik was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform Qunut in the Fajr prayer? He said: Yes. It was said to him: Before the rukūʿ or after the rukūʿ? He said: After the rukūʿ, briefly. Abu Muhammad said: I hold this view and adopt it, but I do not see adopting it except in war."],[1567,"He used to eat on the day of Fitr before going out. And when it was the day of sacrifice, he would not eat until he returned and then ate from his slaughtered animal."],[1568,"I attended the prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a day of Eid, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, without adhan or iqama."],[1569,"“I heard Ibn ‘Abbas say: ‘I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed before the sermon, then he delivered the sermon. And he thought that the women had not heard, so he went over to them and reminded them (of Allah) and preached to them and enjoined them to give in charity, and Bilal was spreading his hands like this, and the women started giving their earrings, rings and things.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1273)"],[1570,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman praying before the sermon on Eid."],[1571,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the day of Fitr and prayed two rak'ahs, and he did not pray before them or after them."],[1572,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say the takbir in the two Eids: in the first seven, and in the last five. And he used to begin with the prayer before the sermon."],[1573,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite at the two 'Ids (festivals) and on Friday, \"Glorify the name of your most high Lord.\" (87) and \"Has the story of the overwhelming reached you?\" (88) He said: When a festival ('Id) and a Friday coincided, he recited them both (at the two prayers). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1122)"],[1574,"I performed Hajj with my father and my paternal uncle. My father said to me, 'Do you see that owner of the red camel who is delivering the sermon? That is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[1575,"He commanded us, by my father, to bring out on the day of Fitr and the day of sacrifice, the adolescent girls and those in seclusion. As for menstruating women, they keep away from the prayer row but witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims. She said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what if one of them does not have a jilbab?' He said, 'Let her sister clothe her from her jilbab.'"],[1576,"I witnessed praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Eid. He began praying before giving the sermon, then stood leaning on Bilal until he reached the women. He gave them a sermon, reminded them, and commanded them to fear Allah. He said, \"Give charity.\" Then he mentioned something about the matter of Hellfire, and a woman from the lower class of women stood up, her face reddened. She said, \"Why, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Because you women spread gossip and curse, and you deny kinship.\" Then they began taking off their jewelry and earrings and throwing them in the garment of Bilal, giving it as charity."],[1577,"I witnessed Mu'awiyah asking Zayd b. Arqam: Did you witness with the Prophet ﷺ two Eids that coincided on one day? He said: Yes. He said: How did he do? He said: He prayed the Eid, then gave a concession regarding Jumu'ah, and said, 'Whoever wishes to pray, let him pray.'"],[1578,"He used to, when he went out for Eid, return by a different path."],[1579,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he said, 'You will come to a people of the Book, so call them to testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. If they obey you in that, then inform them that Allah has obligated upon them five prayers in every day and night. If they obey you in that, then inform them that Allah has obligated upon them charity in their wealth, taken from their rich and returned to their poor. If they obey you in that, then beware of the best of their wealth, and beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for there is no barrier between it and Allah.'"],[1580,"The needy person is not the one who is turned away by a morsel or two, a piece or two, a date or two. Rather, the needy person is the one who has no wealth to suffice him, but he is too shy to ask people persistently, or he does not ask people persistently."],[1581,"There is no owner of camels, cows, or sheep who does not pay what is due on them except that on the Day of Resurrection he will be made to sit on a vast flat plain. Those with cloven hooves will trample him with their hooves, and those with horns will gore him with their horns. On that day, none among them will be hornless or have a broken horn. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is due on them? He said: Lending the stud, lending the bucket, giving its milk, milking it at the watering place, and carrying loads on it in the way of Allah."],[1583,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of camels? He said: Milking them at the watering place, lending their bucket, lending their stud, giving their milk, and carrying loads on them in the way of Allah."],[1584,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote down the sadaqah. For sheep that graze freely: in every forty, one sheep up to one hundred and twenty. If they exceed that, then two sheep up to two hundred. If they exceed that, then three sheep up to three hundred. If they exceed that by one sheep, only three sheep are due until they reach four hundred. When they reach four hundred sheep, then in every hundred there is one sheep. Neither an old decrepit animal, nor one with a defect, nor one with a blemish may be taken as sadaqah."],[1585,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen with 'Amr b. Hazm: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad the Prophet to Shurahbil b. 'Abd Kulal, al-Harith b. 'Abd Kulal, and Nu'aym b. 'Abd Kulal. For forty sheep, one sheep, up to one hundred and twenty. If they exceed one hundred and twenty by one, then two sheep are due, up to two hundred. If they exceed that by one, then three are due, up to three hundred. Whatever exceeds that, in every hundred sheep, one sheep."],[1586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from every forty cows a musinnah, and from every thirty a tabi' or tabi'ah."],[1587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from cattle: from thirty, a tabi' that is a year old; and from forty cows, a musinnah."],[1588,"Muhammad b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Sufyan b. Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[1589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote with 'Amr b. Hazm to Shurahbil b. 'Abd Kulal, al-Harith b. 'Abd Kulal, and Nu'aym b. 'Abd Kulal: In every five awqiya of silver there are five dirhams; whatever exceeds that, then in every forty dirhams a dirham is due, and there is nothing due in what is less than five awqiya."],[1590,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have exempted the sadaqah of horses and slaves. Bring the sadaqah of silver: from every forty dirhams a dirham is due, and there is nothing due on one hundred and ninety until it reaches two hundred.\""],[1591,"The Prophet's ﷺ zakat collector came to us, so I took his hand and read in his commission: \"Do not combine what is separate, nor separate what is combined, for fear of sadaqah.\""],[1592,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he said: \"Beware of taking the best of their wealth.\""],[1593,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no sadaqah due on a Muslim's horse or on his slave.\""],[1594,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no sadaqah due on what is less than five awsuq, nor on what is less than five awqiya, nor on what is less than five camels.\""],[1595,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no sadaqah due on what is less than five awsuq of grains or dates, nor on what is less than five awqiya, nor on what is less than five camels.\""],[1596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote with 'Amr b. Hazm to Shurahbil b. 'Abd Kulal, al-Harith b. 'Abd Kulal, and Nu'aym b. 'Abd Kulal: \"In every five awqiya of silver there are five dirhams; whatever exceeds that, then in every forty dirhams a dirham is due, and there is nothing due in what is less than five awqiya.\""],[1597,"Al-'Abbas asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about paying his sadaqah in advance before it became due, and he permitted him to do that."],[1598,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, in your wealth there is a duty other than zakat.\""],[1599,"My grandfather, my father and I gave the pledge of allegiance to Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ got me engaged and then got me married. One day I went to the Prophet ﷺ with a complaint. My father Yazid had taken some gold coins for charity and kept them with a man in the mosque (to give them to the poor) But I went and took them and brought them to him (my father). My father said, \"By Allah! I did not intend to give them to you. \" I took (the case) to Messenger of Allah ﷺ . On that Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Yazid, you will be rewarded for what you intended. O Ma'n, whatever you have taken is yours.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1422)"],[1600,"the Messenger of Allah said: “Charity is not permissible for a rich person, or for one who is strong and healthy. ” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1839)"],[1601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever asks about the wealth of others will come on the Day of Judgment with marks of blackness, bruises, or scratches on his face.\" It was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is wealth?\" He said, \"Fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold.\""],[1602,"Al-Hasan took a date from the sadaqah dates and put it in his mouth, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Spit it out, spit it out! Throw it away. Do you not know that we do not eat sadaqah?\""],[1603,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and with him was al-Hasan b. Ali. He took a date from the dates of charity, so he snatched it from him and said, \"Do you not know that charity is not lawful for us?\""],[1604,"“Do not press me in asking, for by Allah, no one asks me for something and I give it to him while I dislike it, but it will be blessed for him in it.”"],[1605,"“Whoever asks people for something while he is wealthy independent of it, it will be a blemish on his face.”"],[1606,"Some people of the Ansar asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave them. Then they asked again, and he gave them until what he had was exhausted. Then he said, \"Whatever good I have, I will never withhold it from you. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste. Whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient. Whoever seeks patience, Allah will make him patient. No one is given a gift that is better and more ample than patience.\""],[1607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give me a gift, and I would say, \"Give it to someone who is more in need of it than me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Take it. Whatever Allah gives you of this wealth while you are neither coveting it nor asking for it, take it. Whatever is not so, do not let your soul pursue it.\""],[1608,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ and he gave me. Then I asked him and he gave me. Then I asked him and he gave me. Then I asked him and he said, \"O Hakim, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with a generous soul, it will be blessed for him in it. Whoever takes it with a covetous soul, it will not be blessed for him in it, and he will be like one who eats but is not satisfied.\""],[1609,"“The best charity is that given while one is wealthy, and let one of you begin with those he supports.”"],[1610,"“The upper hand is better than the lower hand.” He said, “The upper hand is the giving hand, and the lower hand is the asking hand.”"],[1611,"“The best charity is that given from surplus wealth. The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support.”"],[1612,"“O group of women, give charity, even from your jewelry.”"],[1614,"Abu Talha was the wealthiest of the Ansar in Madinah in terms of palm trees. The most beloved of his properties to him was Bayruha', which faced the mosque. He used to enter it and drink from its pleasant water. Anas said: When this verse was revealed: {You will not attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love} [Al-Imran 92], he said: 'The most beloved of my properties to me is Bayruha', and it is a charity for Allah, hoping for its righteousness and its treasure with Allah. Place it, O Messenger of Allah, wherever you wish.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Excellent! That is a profitable property - or a returning one. I have heard what you said about it, and I think you should make it for your relatives.' Abu Talha said: 'I will do so, O Messenger of Allah.' So Abu Talha divided it among his relatives and the sons of his paternal uncle."],[1615,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never delivered a sermon to us except that he commanded us therein to give charity and forbade us from mutilation."],[1616,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date; and if you do not find it, then with a good word."],[1617,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with him, he said: 'O Messenger of Allah, part of my repentance is that I abandon the abode of my people and dwell with you, and that I divest myself of my wealth as charity for Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A third is sufficient for you.'"],[1618,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , a man came to him with an egg-sized piece of gold, some of which he acquired from battles. Ahmad Ibn Hanbal stated that it is from minerals, and this is correct. The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, take this as charity from me. By Allah, I have no wealth other than this.\" The Prophet turned away from him. Then he came to him from his left side and said the same. He came to him from in front of him and said the same. Then he said, \"Give it to me,\" angrily. The Prophet threw it at him, striking him with it. If it had hit him, it would have hurt or even injured him. Then he said, \"One of you may intentionally give away his wealth when he does not own anything else, then sit amongst the people as if he is poor. Charity is only appropriate for those who possess excess wealth. Take what is rightfully yours, as we have no need for it.\" So the man took his wealth and left. Abu Muhammad stated that Malik used to say, \"When a person gives away a third of his wealth to the poor, it is considered charity.\""],[1619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to give charity, and it coincided with me having wealth. I said: 'Today I will surpass Abu Bakr, if I ever surpass him one day.' He said: So I brought half of my wealth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What have you left for your family?' I said: 'The like of it.' He said: Then Abu Bakr came with all that he had. He said: 'O Abu Bakr, what have you left for your family?' He said: 'I left for them Allah and His Messenger.' I said: 'I will never race you to anything ever.'"],[1620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made obligatory the Zakat al-Fitr of Ramadan, a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley, upon every free person and slave, male or female, among the Muslims."],[1621,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Zakat al-Fitr for every young and old, free or slave: a sa' of barley or a sa' of dates. Ibn Umar said: 'The people equated it with two mudds of wheat.'"],[1622,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, we used to give Zakat al-Fitr for every young and old, free and owned: a sa' of food, or a sa' of dates, or a sa' of barley, or a sa' of aqit (dried curd), or a sa' of raisins. It remained like that until Mu'awiya came to us in Madinah as a pilgrim or for Umrah and said: 'I think that two mudds of Syrian wheat equals a sa' of dates.' So the people adopted that. Abu Sa'id said: 'As for me, I will continue to give it as I used to give it.'"],[1623,"We used to give Zakat al-Fitr of Ramadan: a sa' of food, or a sa' of dates, or a sa' of barley, or a sa' of raisins, or a sa' of aqit (dried curd)."],[1624,"\"A toll collector will not enter Paradise.\""],[1625,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and ordered me to take a tenth from fruits watered by rainfall and half a tenth from those watered by irrigation.\""],[1626,"\"An injury caused by a beast is without liability, and a well is without liability, and a mine is without liability, and a fifth is due on buried treasure.\""],[1627,"\"The Prophet ﷺ appointed an agent over the zakah. When the agent had finished his task, he came to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is yours, and this was given to me as a gift.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Why did you not stay in the house of your father and mother and see whether you would be given a gift or not?' Then the Prophet ﷺ stood in the evening after the prayer on the pulpit, declared the shahadah, praised Allah as He deserves, and then said, 'To proceed: what is the matter with an agent whom we employ and he comes to us and says, \"This is from your work, and this was given to me as a gift\"? Why did he not stay in the house of his father and mother and see whether he would be given a gift or not? By the One in whose hand is my soul, none of you takes anything from it but he will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it on his neck. If it is a camel, he will come with it grumbling; if it is a cow, he will come with it lowing; if it is a sheep, he will come with it bleating. I have conveyed the message.'\" Abu Humayd said, \"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands until we could see the whiteness of his armpits.\" Abu Humayd said, \"Zayd b. Thabit heard that with me from the Prophet ﷺ, so ask him.\""],[1628,"\"When the collector of zakah comes to you, he should not leave you except while he is pleased.\""],[1629,"\"O Muslim women, let none of you belittle what she gives to her neighbor, even if it is a roasted sheep's trotter.\""],[1630,"\"The paternal aunt of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah was taken captive, and she was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ asked about her, and he said, 'O Sakhr, when a people embrace Islam, they protect their wealth and their blood, so return her to them.' There was a water source belonging to Banu Sulaym, and when they embraced Islam, they asked him for it. He called me and said, 'O Sakhr, when a people embrace Islam, they protect their wealth and their blood, so return it to them.' So I returned it.\""],[1631,"\"No one gives charity from good earnings—and Allah accepts only what is good—but the Most Merciful takes it in His right hand, and Allah causes the date to grow for one of you just as one of you raises his foal or young camel until it becomes like Mount Uhud.\""],[1632,"\"Charity does not decrease wealth; Allah does not increase a servant who pardons except in honor; and no one humbles himself for Allah but Allah raises him.\""],[1633,"\"For every grazing camels, for every forty, a two-year-old she-camel is due. Camels are not to be separated for the sake of accounting. Whoever gives it seeking reward, he will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it and half of his wealth as a firm obligation from the obligations of Allah. None of it is lawful for the family of Muhammad.\""],[1634,"I undertook a guarantee and came to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him regarding it. He said: “Stay, O Qabisah, until the zakāh comes to us and we will order it for you.” Then he said: “O Qabisah, begging is not lawful except for one of three: a man who has undertaken a guarantee, so begging is lawful for him, and he may ask until he obtains it, then he refrains; a man who has been struck by a calamity that destroyed his wealth, so begging is lawful for him, and he may ask until he obtains a means of livelihood — or he said: a sufficiency of livelihood; and a man stricken by poverty until three people of sound judgment among his people say, ‘So-and-so has been stricken by poverty,’ so begging is lawful for him, and he may ask until he obtains a means of livelihood or a sufficiency of livelihood, then he refrains. Whatever else of begging, O Qabisah, is unlawful earnings, which its owner consumes as unlawful earnings.”"],[1635,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about charities, which of them is the best. He said: “Upon the hostile relative.”"],[1636,"“Charity upon the poor is charity, and upon the relative it is two: charity and maintaining kinship ties.”"],[1637,"“Charity upon the poor is charity, and upon the relative it is two: charity and maintaining kinship ties.”"],[1638,"We were with ʿAmmār b. Yāsir when a roasted sheep was brought. He said: “Eat.” Some of the people drew back, and one said: “I am fasting.” ʿAmmār b. Yāsir said: “Whoever fasts the day that is uncertain has disobeyed Abu’l-Qāsim ﷺ.”"],[1639,"I woke up on a day that was ambiguous to me, whether from Shaʿbān or the month of Ramaḍān, and I woke up fasting. I went to ʿIkrimah and found him eating bread and greens. He said: “Come to lunch.” I said: “I am fasting.” He said: “I swear by Allah, you will break your fast.” When I saw that he had sworn without exception, I came forward and excused myself, but I had only eaten the pre-dawn meal shortly before that. Then I said: “Now bring what you have.” He said: ..."],[1640,"\"Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not stop fasting until you see it, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then work it out.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2121)"],[1641,"\"the Messenger of Allah said: 'Fast when you see it and stop fasting when you see it, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then count it as thirty (days). \"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2117)"],[1642,"\" I am surprised at those who anticipate the moth, when the Messenger of Allah said: 'When you see the new crescent then fast, and when you see it, then stop fasting, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then complete thirty days. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2125)"],[1643,"The translation of the given text in Arabic to English is: \"When the Prophet ﷺ saw the new moon, he used to say, 'Allah is the greatest! O Allah, let this crescent be a crescent of security, faith, safety, Islam, and success in what our Lord loves and is pleased with. And your Lord is Allah.'\""],[1644,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw the new moon, he would say: “O Allah, let it appear upon us with security, faith, safety, and Islām. My Lord and your Lord is Allah.”"],[1645,"“Do not precede Ramaḍān by one or two days [of fasting], except for a man who was already observing a fast, then let him fast it.”"],[1646,"“The month is only twenty-nine [days], so do not fast until you see it, and do not break your fast until you see it. If it is overcast for you, then estimate it.”"],[1647,"“The people looked for the new moon, and I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I had seen it. So he fasted and ordered the people to fast.”"],[1648,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I have seen the new moon.” He said: “Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “O Bilāl, announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow.”"],[1649,"“The Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, if a man was fasting and the time for breaking the fast came, and he slept before breaking his fast, he would not eat that night nor his day until evening.”"],[1650,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I placed under my pillow a white thread and a black thread, but nothing became clear to me. He said: \"Indeed your pillow is wide. That is only the night from the day, in the saying of Allah the Exalted: 'And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread of dawn. Then complete the fast until night. And do not have relations with them as long as you are staying for worship in the mosques. These are the limits of Allah, so do not approach them. Thus does Allah make clear His verses to the people that they may become righteous.'\""],[1651,"\"We had suhoor with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"Then he stood up for prayer.\" He said: I asked: \"How much time was between the adhan and the suhoor?\" He said: \"The amount of reciting fifty verses.\""],[1652,"\"Take suhoor, for in suhoor there is blessing.\""],[1653,"We would prepare food for him for suhoor, but he would not eat much of it. We said to him: \"You command us to do it, but you do not eat much of it?\" He said: \"I do not command you to do it because I crave it. Rather, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The distinction between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the eating of suhoor.'\""],[1654,"\"Whoever does not intend the fast before dawn, there is no fast for him.\""],[1655,"\"People will continue to be upon good as long as they hasten to break the fast.\""],[1656,"\"When the night approaches and the day retreats, and the sun has set, then you have broken your fast.\""],[1657,"\"When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates; if he does not find any, then with water, for water is purifying.\""],[1658,"\"Whoever provides food to a fasting person to break his fast, the like of his reward is written for him, without diminishing the fasting person's reward in the least.\""],[1659,"\"Beware of continuous fasting,\" twice. They said: \"But you practice continuous fasting.\" He said: \"I am not like you. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.\""],[1660,"\"Do not practice continuous fasting.\" It was said: \"But you do that.\" He said: \"I am not like any one of you. I am fed and given drink.\""],[1661,"\"Do not practice continuous fasting. Whoever among you wants to practice continuous fasting, let him continue until suhoor.\" They said: \"But you practice continuous fasting, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"I spend the night while there is a feeder for me who feeds me and gives me drink.\""],[1662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting. Some men among the Muslims said to him, \"But you fast continuously.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am not like you. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.\" When they refused to stop continuous fasting, he fasted continuously with them for a day, then another day. Then they sighted the new moon, and he said, \"Had it been delayed, I would have increased you,\" as if to punish them when they refused to stop."],[1664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out in the year of the conquest and fasted, and the people fasted until he reached al-Kadid. Then he broke his fast, and the people broke their fast. They used to follow the most recent of the actions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1665,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and saw a crowd and a man being shaded. He said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"This is a fasting man.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is not an act of righteousness to fast while traveling.\""],[1666,"\"It is not an act of righteousness to fast while traveling.\""],[1667,"\"It is not an act of righteousness to fast while traveling.\""],[1668,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a journey and greeted him. When I turned to leave, he said, \"Wait for the morning meal, O Abu Umayyah.\" I said, \"I am fasting, O Prophet of Allah.\" He said, \"Come, let me inform you about the traveler. Allah has relieved him of fasting and half the prayer.\""],[1669,"I boarded a ship from al-Fustat with Abu Basrah al-Ghifari during Ramadan. He set off and brought his lunch close, then said, \"Come near.\" I said, \"Do you not see the houses?\" Abu Basrah said, \"Have you turned away from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\""],[1670,"\"Whoever breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan without a concession or illness, fasting for the whole of time will never make it up for him, even if he fasts for all time.\""],[1671,"\"Whoever breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan without a concession that Allah has granted him, fasting for all time will not make it up for him.\""],[1672,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I am ruined.\" He said, \"What has ruined you?\" He said, \"I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan.\" He said, \"Free a slave.\" He said, \"I do not have one.\" He said, \"Fast two consecutive months.\" He said, \"I am not able.\" He said, \"Feed sixty poor people.\" He said, \"I cannot find the means.\" Then a basket of dates was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Where is the questioner? Give this in charity.\" He said, \"To those poorer than my family, O Messenger of Allah? By Allah, there is no household between its two lava fields poorer than us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his canine teeth showed and said, \"Then you, if that is so.\""],[1673,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"He is burned.\" He asked him what was wrong with him, and he said, \"He had intercourse with his wife in Ramadan.\" A basket called al-araq containing dates was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Where is the burned one?\" The man stood up, and he said, \"Give this in charity.\""],[1674,"He said to a woman: \"Do not fast except with his permission.\""],[1675,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A woman must not fast a voluntary day outside Ramadan while her husband is present except with his permission.\""],[1676,"\"A woman must not fast a day while her husband is present except with his permission.\""],[1677,"He used to kiss while fasting."],[1678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss when he was fasting. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1685)"],[1679,"I became amorous and kissed while I was fasting. So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have done a great thing today: I kissed while fasting.' He said, 'What do you think if you rinsed your mouth with water?' I said, 'Then it would not harm.' He said, 'So what is the problem?'"],[1680,"He used to wake up in a state of major ritual impurity from his family, then fast."],[1681,"\"Whoever forgets while fasting and eats or drinks, let him complete his fast, for Allah fed him and gave him drink.\""],[1682,"\"If one of you eats or drinks forgetfully while fasting, then remembers, let him complete his fast, for Allah fed him and gave him drink.\""],[1683,"\"The Prophet ﷺ vomited, so he broke his fast.\" He said: Then I met Thawban in the mosque of Damascus and mentioned that to him, and he said, \"He spoke the truth; I poured the water for his ablution.\""],[1684,"\"If a fasting person is overcome by vomiting without intending it, he does not have to make up the fast. But if he induces vomiting, he must make up the fast.\""],[1685,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and he saw a man being cupped. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[1686,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking in al-Baqi', there was a man being cupped, so he said, \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[1687,"Fasting is a shield as long as it is not rent."],[1688,"And my grandfather had been brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped his head and said, \"Do not apply kohl by day while you are fasting; apply kohl at night with ithmid, for it clears the sight and makes the hair grow.\""],[1689,"That he said: When this verse was revealed: {And upon those who can afford it, a ransom of feeding a poor person} [Al-Baqarah: 184], he said, \"Whoever wished to break the fast and pay the ransom did so, until the verse after it was revealed and abrogated it.\""],[1690,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was fasting. A vessel was brought and he drank, then he handed it to her and she drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If it was a makeup for Ramadan, then fast another day; and if it was voluntary, then if you wish make it up, and if you wish do not make it up.\""],[1691,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, Fatimah came and sat on the left of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Umm Hani on his right. She said: Then a servant girl came with a vessel containing a drink and handed it to him. He drank from it, then he handed it to Umm Hani, and she drank from it. Then she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have broken my fast, and I was fasting.\" He said to her, \"Were you making up anything?\" She said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then it does not harm you if it was voluntary.\""],[1692,"When one of you is invited to food while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting."],[1693,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and she called for food for him. He said to her, \"Eat.\" She said, \"I am fasting.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When food is eaten in the presence of a fasting person, the angels send blessings upon him until they finish,\" and perhaps he said, \"until they finish their eating.\""],[1694,"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fast an entire month except Sha'ban, for he used to join it to Ramadan so that they would be two consecutive months. And he used to fast in a month until we would say he does not break the fast, and he would break the fast until we would say he does not fast."],[1695,"When the middle of Sha'ban comes, then refrain from fasting."],[1696,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man, \"Did you fast any of the white days of this month?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then when you break your fast from Ramadan, fast two days.\""],[1697,"The Prophet ﷺ did not fast a complete month other than Ramadan. And when he fasted, he would fast until someone would say, \"No, by Allah, he will not break the fast\"; and when he broke the fast, he would break the fast until someone would say, \"No, by Allah, he will not fast.\""],[1698,"A man who fasted perpetually was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"He neither fasted nor broke his fast.\""],[1699,"\"He heard Abu Huraira say: 'My beloved friend advised me with three things that I will never neglect. Firstly, to never sleep except after praying Witr (an additional prayer performed after Isha prayer). Secondly, to fast three days every month. And thirdly, to never abandon the two Rak'ahs of Dhuha (a voluntary prayer performed in the morning).' \""],[1700,"\"Fasting the white days is the fasting of a lifetime and its breaking.\""],[1701,"I said to Jabir: Did the Prophet ﷺ prohibit fasting on Friday? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this House."],[1702,"\"Do not fast on Saturday except what is obligatory upon you; and if one of you finds nothing but this or the bark of a tree, let him chew it.\""],[1703,"Usamah used to ride to some property of his in Wadi al-Qura and fast on Mondays and Thursdays while traveling. So I said to him: Why do you fast on Mondays and Thursdays while traveling, when you have grown old and weak, or become thin? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays, and he said: \"Indeed the deeds of people are presented on Monday and Thursday.\""],[1704,"He used to fast on Monday and Thursday, so I asked him, and he said: \"Indeed deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday.\""],[1705,"\"The most beloved fasting to Allah ﷻ is the fasting of Dawud; he used to fast one day and break his fast the next. And the most beloved prayer to Allah ﷻ is the prayer of Dawud; he used to sleep half the night, pray a third, and observe glorification a sixth.\" Abu Muhammad said: This last wording is an error or mistake; rather, he used to sleep half the night, pray a third of it, and observe glorification a sixth of it."],[1706,"There is no fasting on two days: the day of al-Fitr and the day of al-Nahr."],[1707,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six days of Shawwal, that is like fasting for a lifetime.”"],[1708,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fasting a month is equal to ten months (30 days x 10 rewards = 300 days of reward), and fasting six days after it is equal to two months (6 days x 10 rewards = 60 days of rewards); that is a complete year (300 + 60 = 360 days of reward),” meaning the month of Ramadan and six days after it."],[1709,"A man came to Ali and asked him about a month to fast after the month of Ramadan. Ali said to him: No one has asked me about this since I heard a man ask the Prophet ﷺ: Which month of the year should one fast after the month of Ramadan? He commanded him to fast Muharram and said: \"Indeed in it there is a day on which Allah accepted the repentance of a people, and on which He will accept the repentance of another people.\""],[1710,"\"The best fasting after the month of Ramadan is the month of Allah, which you call al-Muharram.\""],[1711,"\"The best fasting after the month of Ramadan is al-Muharram.\""],[1712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while the Jews were fasting on the day of Ashura. He asked them, and they said, \"This is the day on which Musa prevailed over Pharaoh.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have more right to Musa than them, so fast it.\""],[1713,"He used to fast on the day of Ashura and command its fasting."],[1714,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a man from Aslam on the day of Ashura, saying, \"Today is the day of Ashura. Whoever has eaten or drunk, let him complete the rest of his day [in abstinence], and whoever has not eaten or drunk, let him fast it.\""],[1715,"\"This is the day of Ashura. Quraysh used to fast it in the pre-Islamic period. Whoever of you wishes to fast it, let him fast it; and whoever of you wishes to leave it, let him leave it.\" Ibn Umar used not to fast it unless it coincided with his fasting."],[1716,"\"The day of Ashura was a day that Quraysh used to fast in the pre-Islamic period. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, he fasted it and commanded its fasting, until when Ramadan was made obligatory, Ramadan became the obligation and the day of Ashura was left. Whoever wished fasted it and whoever wished left it.\""],[1717,"\"The Day of Arafah and the days of Tashriq are our festival, O people of Islam. They are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1718,"Ibn Umar was asked about fasting on the Day of Arafah. He said, \"I performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ and he did not fast it. I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and he did not fast it. I performed Hajj with Umar and he did not fast it. I performed Hajj with Uthman and he did not fast it. I do not fast it, nor do I command it, nor do I forbid it.\""],[1719,"The Prophet [SAW] commanded him to call out on the days of At-Tashriq that no one would enter Paradise except a believer, and that these were the days of eating and drinking. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4994)"],[1720,"He and Abdullah b. Amr entered upon Amr b. al-As on the day after or the day after that of the Day of Sacrifice. Amr brought food near to them, and Abdullah said, \"I am fasting.\" Amr said, \"Break your fast, for these are the days in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to break our fast and forbid us from fasting.\" So Abdullah broke his fast and ate, and I ate with him."],[1721,"A woman vowed to fast, then she died. Her brother came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"If she had a debt, would you pay it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then pay Allah, for Allah is more deserving of fulfillment.\" He said, \"So he fasted on her behalf.\""],[1722,"The change in the breath of the fasting person is more pleasant to Allah than the fragrance of musk. The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy on the Day of Resurrection."],[1723,"Every deed of the son of Adam is for him; the good deed is multiplied ten times its like up to seven hundredfold, except fasting. It is for Me, and I reward it. He leaves his food and his desire for My sake, and he leaves his drink and his desire for My sake. So it is for Me, and I reward it."],[1724,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Fasting is a shield.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2224)"],[1725,"When he broke his fast with people, he would say, \"The fasting people have broken their fast with you, the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have descended upon you.\""],[1726,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no deed that is better in the sight of Allah than the deeds performed during the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah.\" It was asked, \"Not even Jihad for the sake of Allah?\" He ﷺ replied, \"Not even Jihad for the sake of Allah, unless a person goes out with his life and wealth and does not return with anything.\""],[1727,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"There is no deed more pure in the sight of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and no deed more deserving of rewards than a good deed performed during the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah.\" It was asked, \"Not even Jihad for the sake of Allah?\" He replied, \"Not even Jihad for the sake of Allah, except for a man who went out with himself and his wealth and did not return with anything.\" It is reported that Sa'eed ibn Jubayr would exert extreme effort and strive his best during the ten days (of Dhul-Hijjah) to the extent that he could barely manage it."],[1728,"When Ramadan comes, the gates of heaven are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained."],[1729,"Whoever stands (in prayer) during Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven; and whoever stands (in prayer) on the Night of Power, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[1730,"Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Dawud, from al-Walid b. Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr b. Nufayr al-Hadrami, from Abu Dharr, something similar."],[1731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to observe i'tikaf during the last ten days. In the year in which he passed away, he observed i'tikaf for twenty days."],[1732,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ to visit him during his i'tikaf in the mosque in the last ten days of Ramadan. She spoke with him for a while, then she stood up."],[1733,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, intending to inform us of the Night of Power, but two Muslim men quarreled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I came out to you intending to inform you of the Night of Power, but there was a quarrel between so-and-so and so-and-so, so it was taken away. Perhaps that is better. So seek it in the last ten nights, on the fifth, the seventh, and the ninth.'"],[1734,"I saw the Night of Power, then some of my family woke me, and I forgot it. So seek it in the remaining ten nights."],[1735,"Seek the Night of Power in the last seven nights."],[1736,"Whoever intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten."],[1737,"Whoever is not prevented from Hajj by an evident need, a tyrannical ruler, or a confining illness, and then dies without performing Hajj, let him die, if he wishes, as a Jew, or if he wishes, as a Christian."],[1738,"The Prophet ﷺ performed one Hajj after his emigration."],[1740,"I said to Anas, 'How many times did the Prophet ﷺ perform Hajj?' He said, 'One Hajj. And he performed Umrah four times: his first Umrah, when the polytheists turned him back from the House; his second Umrah, when they made peace with him and he returned the following year; his Umrah from al-Ji'ranah, when he distributed the spoils of Hunayn in Dhu al-Qa'dah; and his Umrah along with his Hajj.'"],[1741,"“Hajj has been prescribed for you.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, every year?” He said, “No. Had I said it, it would have become obligatory. Hajj is once; whatever is more is voluntary.”"],[1742,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhul-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd at Qarn.” He said: Ibn Umar said, “As for these three, I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it reached me that he set the miqat for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam.”"],[1743,"“The Prophet ﷺ set the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhul-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd at Qarn al-Manazil, and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam. These are for them and for any other who comes upon them from elsewhere intending Hajj or Umrah. Whoever is before that, then from wherever he begins, even the people of Makkah from Makkah.”"],[1744,"Al-Miswar b. Makhramah and Ibn Abbas differed about a muhrim washing his head, so they sent me to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari: How did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wash his head while in ihram? I came to Abu Ayyub while he was between the two posts of the well, covered with a cloth. I greeted him, and he drew the cloth to himself. I said, “Your nephew Ibn Abbas sent me to you: How did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wash his head?” He passed his hands over his head, forward and back."],[1745,"“The Prophet ﷺ stripped for ihram and performed ghusl.”"],[1746,"An accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise, and two Umrahs expiate for the sins between them."],[1747,"“Whoever performs Hajj to the House and does not engage in obscenity or wickedness returns as on the day his mother gave birth to him.”"],[1748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, “Which Hajj is best?” He said, “The one with raised voices and flowing blood.”"],[1749,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, “What clothing may we wear when we enter ihram?” He said, “Do not wear shirts, trousers, turbans, hooded cloaks, or leather socks, unless someone has no sandals; then let him wear leather socks and cut them below the ankles. And do not wear any clothing touched by wars or saffron.”"],[1750,"“Whoever finds no waist wrapper, let him wear trousers; and whoever finds no sandals, let him wear leather socks.” He said: I or someone said, “Should he cut them?” He said, “No.”"],[1751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about what the pilgrim in ihram should wear. He said: “He should not wear shirts, turbans, trousers, hooded cloaks, or leather socks—except if he cannot find sandals, then he may wear leather socks, but he should cut them below the ankles.”"],[1752,"I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he entered ihram with the finest perfume."],[1753,"I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of his entering ihram with the best perfume I could find."],[1754,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ihram, and I perfumed him at Mina before he departed."],[1755,"Asma’ gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr at the tree. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Abu Bakr that she should perform ghusl and enter ihram."],[1756,"In the hadith of Asma’ bt. ‘Umays when she gave birth at Dhu al-Hulayfah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Abu Bakr to tell her to perform ghusl and enter ihram."],[1757,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram after the prayer."],[1758,"The Prophet ﷺ entered ihram and made the talbiyah after the prayer."],[1759,"Verily, the Prophet ﷺ used to say when he performed the pilgrimage, \"Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, innal hamda wani'mata laka wal mulk, la sharika laka.\" Yahya and Nafi' have mentioned that Ibn 'Umar used to add the following words to this phrase, \"Labbayka war-rahba'u ilayk, wal 'amal labbayk labbayk.\""],[1760,"Verily, the Prophet ﷺ used to say when he performed the pilgrimage, \"Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, innal hamda wani'mata laka wal mulk, la sharika laka.\" Yahya and Nafi' have mentioned that Ibn 'Umar used to add the following words to this phrase, \"Labbayka war-rahba'u ilayk, wal 'amal labbayk labbayk.\""],[1761,"‘Uthman b. Muhammad narrated to us; Ibn ‘Uyaynah narrated to us from ‘Abdullah b. Abi Bakr with his chain, similar to it."],[1762,"Duba‘ah bt. al-Zubayr b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I want to perform Hajj, so what should I say?” He said: “Say: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk, and my place of ending is wherever You detain me. For you have from your Lord what you have stipulated.”"],[1763,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj ifrad."],[1764,"I am telling you a hadith that perhaps Allah may benefit you with afterward: Greetings used to be sent upon me, and Ibn Ziyad ordered me, so I was cauterized, and the greeting was withheld from me until the trace of the cauterization disappeared. And know that mut‘ah is lawful in the Book of Allah; no prophet forbade it and no scripture was revealed concerning it. A man said, based on his own opinion, whatever appeared to him."],[1765,"I heard, in the year Mu‘awiyah performed Hajj, him asking Sa‘d b. Malik: How do you speak about tamattu‘ with ‘umrah to Hajj? He said: It is good and beautiful. He said: ‘Umar used to forbid it, so are you better than ‘Umar? He said: ‘Umar is better than me, but the Prophet ﷺ did that, and he is better than ‘Umar."],[1766,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he performed Hajj while he was making his camel kneel at al-Batḥā’. He said to me: “Have you performed Hajj?” I said: Yes. He said: “How did you enter iḥrām?” He said: I said: Labbayk, with an iḥrām like the iḥrām of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: “You have done well. Go and perform ṭawāf around the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, then come out of iḥrām.” He said: So I performed ṭawāf around the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, then I came to a woman from the women of Banū Qays, and she began to delouse my head. I began to give fatwā to the people with that. A man said to me: O ‘Abdullāh b. Qays, go slowly with some of your fatwā, for you do not know what the Commander of the Faithful has introduced in the rites after you. So I said: O people, whoever we have given a fatwā to, let him be cautious, for the Commander of the Faithful is coming to you, so follow him. When he arrived, I came to him and mentioned that to him. He said: “If we follow the Book of Allah, the Book of Allah commands completion, and if we follow the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out of iḥrām until the sacrificial animal reached its place of sacrifice.”"],[1767,"Five for which there is no sin in killing the one who kills any of them: the crow, the mouse, the kite, the scorpion, and the biting dog."],[1768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of five transgressors in the Ḥill and the Ḥaram: the kite, the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, and the biting dog."],[1769,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ underwent cupping while he was in iḥrām.”"],[1770,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ underwent cupping at Laḥy Jamal while he was in iḥrām.”"],[1771,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ underwent cupping while he was in iḥrām.”"],[1772,"“The Prophet ﷺ married while he was in iḥrām.”"],[1773,"A man from Quraysh proposed to Abān b. ‘Uthmān while he was the amīr of the season. Abān said: I consider him only an uncouth Iraqi. “The muḥrim does not marry, nor gives in marriage.”"],[1774,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me while we were both out of iḥrām, after he returned from Makkah, at Sarif.”"],[1775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while in a state of permissibility and consummated the marriage with her while in a state of permissibility, and I was the messenger between them."],[1776,"My father set out with the Prophet ﷺ in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah, and his companions entered ihram while Abu Qatadah did not enter ihram. He came upon a wild donkey and stabbed it and ate from its meat. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I came upon a wild donkey and stabbed it. He said to the people: \"Eat,\" while they were in a state of ihram."],[1777,"While we were traveling, they were in a state of ihram and Abu Qatadah was in a state of permissibility, when I saw a wild donkey. I mounted a horse and caught it, and they ate from its meat while in ihram, but I did not eat. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he said: \"Did you point or kill?\" Or he said: \"Did you strike?\" They said: No. He said: \"Then eat.\""],[1778,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought meat of a wild donkey and he returned it, saying: \"We are in a state of ihram; we do not eat game.\""],[1779,"We were with Talhah b. Ubayd Allah on a journey when a bird was gifted to him while they were in ihram and he was asleep. Some of us ate and some of us abstained out of scrupulousness. Talhah woke up and they informed him, and he agreed with those who ate it, saying: \"We ate it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[1780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was at al-Abwa' or Waddan, and I gifted him meat of a wild donkey, but he returned it to me. When he saw displeasure in my face, he said: \"It is not that we are refusing it to you, but we are in a state of ihram.\""],[1781,"He was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage when a woman from Khath'am came and said: The obligation of Allah upon His servants regarding Hajj has found my father an old man who cannot remain steady on his mount, and he has not performed Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: \"Yes.\" Abu Muhammad was asked: \"Do you hold this view?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[1782,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: My father is an old man who cannot sit upright on a camel, and the obligation of Allah has overtaken him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[1783,"A woman from Khath'am sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, while al-Fadl b. Abbas was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: O Messenger of Allah, the obligation of Allah upon His servants has found my father an old man who cannot sit upright on the mount. Is it permissible for me to perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: \"Yes.\""],[1784,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, my father or my mother is a very old person. If I carry them, they cannot remain steady, and if I tie them, I fear I might kill them. He said: \"Do you think that if your father or mother had a debt, you would pay it?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father or your mother.\""],[1785,"A man from Khath‘am came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “My father embraced Islam, but he is an elderly man who is unable to ride a camel, and hajj is obligatory upon him. Should I perform hajj on his behalf?” He asked: “Are you his eldest son?” He replied: “Yes.” He said: “Tell me, if your father owed a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would that suffice for him?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then perform hajj on his behalf.”"],[1786,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “My father is an elderly man who is unable to perform hajj.” He said: “Tell me, if your father owed a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would it be accepted from him?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Allah is more merciful. Perform hajj on behalf of your father.”"],[1787,"“I have not abandoned touching these two corners, in times of hardship or ease, since I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touching them.” I said to Nāfi‘: “Would Ibn ‘Umar walk between the two corners?” He said: “He used to walk only so that it would be easier for him to touch it.”"],[1788,"“Allah will surely resurrect the Stone on the Day of Resurrection, and it will have two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, bearing witness for whoever touched it in truth.”"],[1789,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ jogged from the Stone to the Stone for three rounds.”"],[1790,"When he circumambulated the House for the first circumambulation, he jogged three rounds and walked four, and he would hasten along the valley bed when he did sa‘y between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. I said to Nāfi‘: “Would ‘Abdullāh walk when he reached the Yemeni Corner?” He said: “No, unless he was crowded at the corner, for he would not leave it until he touched it.”"],[1791,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ jogged from the Stone to the Stone for three and walked for four.”"],[1792,"About the Prophet ﷺ , it is narrated that he performed tawaf while wearing sandals."],[1793,"“Whoever enters ihram for hajj and ‘umrah, one circumambulation suffices for both, and he does not exit ihram until he exits from both.”"],[1794,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated the House on a camel, and whenever he came to the corner he pointed to it with something in his hand and said takbīr.”"],[1795,"“I arrived in Makkah while I was menstruating, and I did not do tawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: ‘Do what the pilgrim does, except that you should not circumambulate the House.’”"],[1796,"“Circumambulation of the House is prayer, except that Allah has permitted speech during it. Whoever speaks during it, let him speak only good.”"],[1797,"I agreed with my Lord in three things. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would take the station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. Then Allah revealed: {And take the station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.}"],[1798,"Muhammad b. Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us: Hatim b. Isma'il narrated to us from Ja'far from his father from Jabir with this."],[1799,"While a man was standing with the Prophet ﷺ at Arafah, he fell from his mount, or he said: it killed him instantly. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in two garments, do not perfume him, and do not cover his head, for Allah, Exalted is He, will raise him on the Day of Resurrection uttering the talbiyah.\""],[1800,"Tawaf around the House, the stoning of the jamarat, and the sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah were only prescribed to establish the remembrance of Allah."],[1801,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is the nullification of Hajj for us specifically or for those after us? He said: \"Rather, for us specifically.\""],[1802,"\"This is an Umrah that we have enjoyed. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him fully exit ihram. Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1803,"They traveled with the Prophet ﷺ until they reached Usfan. A man from Banu Mudlij, called Malik b. Suraqah or Suraqah b. Malik, said to him: Judge for us as you would judge for people born today. He said: \"Indeed, Allah has inserted into your Hajj this Umrah. When you arrive, whoever performs tawaf around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah has exited ihram, except those who have a sacrificial animal with them.\""],[1804,"The Prophet ﷺ performed four Umrahs: the Umrah of al-Hudaybiyah, the Umrah of al-Qada', or he said the Umrah of al-Qisas - Shihab b. Ubbad was uncertain - the following year, the third from al-Ji'ranah, and the fourth that accompanied his Hajj."],[1805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a woman: \"Perform Umrah in Ramadan, for an Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj.\""],[1806,"\"An Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj.\""],[1807,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from al-Ji'ranah when he began his umrah, entered Makkah at night, completed his umrah, then left the same night and arrived at al-Ji'ranah in the morning as if he had spent the night there.»"],[1808,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told me to seat Aisha behind me and have her perform umrah from al-Tan'im.»"],[1809,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr, «Seat your sister – meaning Aisha – behind you and have her perform umrah from al-Tan'im. When you descend from the hill, tell her to enter ihram, for it is an accepted umrah.»"],[1810,"«I certainly kiss you, and I certainly know that you are a stone, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you.»"],[1811,"I saw Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far touch the Stone, then kiss it and prostrate upon it. I said to him, \"What is this?\" He said, \"I saw your maternal uncle Abd Allah b. Abbas ؓ do it,\" then he said, \"I saw Umar do it,\" then he said, «I certainly know that you are a stone, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do this.»"],[1812,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah with Usama b. Zayd riding behind him. He made his camel kneel at the base of the Kaaba. Ibn Umar said: The people rushed about. The Prophet ﷺ, Bilal, and Usama entered. I said to Bilal from behind the door, \"Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" He said, «Between the two pillars.»"],[1813,"«Were it not that your people have only recently left disbelief, I would demolish the Kaaba and rebuild it on the foundations of Ibrahim. When Quraysh built it, they made it too short, then they left out a portion.»"],[1814,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Hijr: \"Is it part of the House?\" He said, «Yes.» I said, \"Then why did they not include it in the House?\" He said, «Your people ran short of funds.» I said, \"Why is its door raised high?\" He said, «Your people did that to let in whomever they wished and keep out whomever they wished. Were it not that your people are still close to the time of ignorance, and I fear their hearts would reject it, I would incorporate the Hijr into the House and make its door level with the ground.»"],[1815,"«Tahşib is not anything; it is simply a place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ camped.»"],[1816,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five prayers in Mina.»"],[1817,"I said to Anas b. Malik, \"Tell me something you understood from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: where did he pray zuhr on the day of tarwiyah?\" He said, «In Mina.» I said, \"Where did he pray asr on the day of nafr?\" He said, «In al-Abtah.» Then he said, \"Do as your rulers do.\""],[1818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha, and slept a short sleep at Mina, then rode to the House and circumambulated it."],[1819,"Abdullah said: And he prayed with Uthman at Mina four rak'ahs. \"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this place two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs. Then the ways parted with you, so would that my share of four rak'ahs be two accepted rak'ahs.\""],[1820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at Mina two rak'ahs, Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, Umar two rak'ahs, and Uthman two rak'ahs at the beginning of his rule, then he completed it afterwards."],[1821,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Mina, and among us were those who said takbir and among us were those who said the talbiyah."],[1822,"I asked Anas b. Malik while we were going in the morning from Mina to Arafat about the talbiyah: How did you use to do with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"The one who said the talbiyah would say it and it was not objected to, and the one who said takbir would say it and it was not objected to.\""],[1823,"I lost a camel of mine, so I went to look for it, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing with the people at Arafah. I said: By Allah, this man is of the Hums; what is his business here?"],[1824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebbles, then sat for the people. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I slaughtered. He said: \"No harm.\" Then another came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated before I threw. He said: \"No harm.\" He said: He was not asked about anything but he said: \"No harm.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"All of Arafah is a standing place, all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, all of Mina is a place of sacrifice, and all the mountain passes of Makkah are a road and a place of sacrifice.\""],[1825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebbles, then sat for the people. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I slaughtered. He said: \"No harm.\" Then another came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated before I threw. He said: \"No harm.\" He said: He was not asked about anything but he said: \"No harm.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"All of Arafah is a standing place, all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, all of Mina is a place of sacrifice, and all the mountain passes of Makkah are a road and a place of sacrifice.\""],[1826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebbles, then sat for the people. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I slaughtered. He said: \"No harm.\" Then another came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated before I threw. He said: \"No harm.\" He said: He was not asked about anything but he said: \"No harm.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"All of Arafah is a standing place, all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, all of Mina is a place of sacrifice, and all the mountain passes of Makkah are a road and a place of sacrifice.\""],[1827,"He was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, so he departed from Arafah, and he was moving at a brisk pace, and when he came upon an open space he urged the camel on."],[1828,"Hajjaj informed us: Hammad narrated to us: Musa b. Uqbah narrated to us from Kurayb b. Abi Muslim from Usamah something similar."],[1829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Maghrib and Isha."],[1830,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah; he did not call the adhan for either of them except with the iqamah, and he did not pray any supererogatory prayer between them or after either of them."],[1831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to depart from Muzdalifah at night."],[1832,"Sawdah bt. Zam‘ah asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to depart before he departed, and he granted her permission. Al-Qasim said: She was a heavy woman. And al-Qasim said: “al-thabitah” means “al-thaqilah” (heavy). So she departed, and we were kept back with him until we departed with his departure. Aishah said: If I had asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Sawdah asked permission, and had departed before the people, that would be dearer to me than anything I might rejoice over."],[1833,"Sawdah bt. Zam‘ah asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to depart before he departed, and he granted her permission. Al-Qasim said: She was a heavy woman. And al-Qasim said: “al-thabitah” means “al-thaqilah” (heavy). So she departed, and we were kept back with him until we departed with his departure. Aishah said: If I had asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Sawdah asked permission, and had departed before the people, that would be dearer to me than anything I might rejoice over."],[1834,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about Hajj and said: “Hajj is Arafat—or he said ‘Arafah—and whoever reaches the night of Muzdalifah before the dawn prayer has attained it.” And he said: “The days of Mina are three days.” {So whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him}."],[1835,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about Hajj and said: “Hajj is Arafat—or he said ‘Arafah—and whoever reaches the night of Muzdalifah before the dawn prayer has attained it.” And he said: “The days of Mina are three days.” {So whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him}."],[1836,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the standing place, above the heads of the people, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come from Mount Tayyi`, I have exhausted my mount and worn out myself. By Allah, there is no mountain but I stood upon it. Is there any Hajj for me? He said: “Whoever witnesses this prayer with us, and had already come to Arafat before that, by night or by day, has fulfilled his rites and completed his Hajj.”"],[1837,"The people of the Jahiliyyah used to depart from Muzdalifah after sunrise, and they used to say: “Shine, Thabir, so that we may hasten.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ differed from them, so he departed before sunrise by the amount of the prayer of those who pray when it is light—or he said “those who are in the east”—with the dawn prayer."],[1838,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the evening of Arafah and the morning of Muzdalifah, when they departed: “You must be calm,” while he was holding back his she-camel, until when he entered the valley of Muhassir, he urged it on."],[1839,"Abdullah b. Abdullah and Salim spoke to Ibn Umar during the nights when al-Hajjaj camped against Ibn al-Zubayr, before he was killed. They said: It would not harm you not to perform Hajj this year; we fear that you will be prevented from reaching the House. He said: “We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending Umrah, but the disbelievers of Quraysh blocked us from the House. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered his sacrificial animal and shaved his head, then returned. I call you to witness that I have made Umrah obligatory upon myself. If I am allowed to reach the House, I will perform tawaf; and if I am prevented from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did when I was with him.” So he entered ihram for Umrah from Dhu al-Hulayfah, then traveled. Then he said: “Their affair is one. I call you to witness that I have made Hajj obligatory along with my Umrah.” Nafi‘ said: He performed a single tawaf for both and a single sa‘y for both. Then he did not exit ihram until the Day of Sacrifice came, and he offered a sacrificial animal. He used to say: Whoever combines Umrah and Hajj and enters ihram for both together must not exit ihram until he exits from both together on the Day of Sacrifice."],[1840,"Whoever breaks a bone or becomes lame has exited ihram, and he owes another Hajj."],[1841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, and after that at the time when the sun declines."],[1842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a concession to camel herders to throw on the Day of Sacrifice, then to throw the next day or the day after, for two days, then to throw on the day of departure."],[1843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us in the Farewell Pilgrimage to throw the pebble with the like of pebbles of throwing."],[1844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them, so they threw with the like of pebbles of throwing, and he hastened in the valley of Muhassir, and he said, \"You must maintain tranquility.\""],[1845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to throw the jamarat with the like of pebbles of throwing."],[1846,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ throwing the jamarat on a reddish-brown she-camel, with no striking there, nor driving away, nor saying 'to you, to you'."],[1847,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not stop pronouncing the talbiyah until he threw the pebble."],[1848,"When he threw the pebble that is next to the mosque, the mosque of Mina, he would throw it with seven pebbles, saying 'Allahu Akbar' with each pebble. Then he would go forward in front of it and stand facing the qiblah, raising his hands, and he would prolong the standing. Then he would come to the second pebble and throw it with seven pebbles, saying 'Allahu Akbar' each time he threw a pebble. Then he would descend to the left, toward the valley, raising his hands and supplicating. Then he would come to the pebble at the Aqabah and throw it with seven pebbles, saying 'Allahu Akbar' each time he threw a pebble. Then he would depart and not stand at it."],[1849,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending only the Hajj. When we reached Sarif, I menstruated. When it was the Day of Sacrifice, I became pure. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, and I performed the ifadah. Then cow meat was brought, and I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives.'"],[1850,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Shaving is not a duty laid on women; only clipping the hair is incumbent on them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1984)"],[1851,"May Allah have mercy on those who shave. It was said, 'And those who shorten?' He said, 'May Allah have mercy on those who shave.' He said in the fourth: 'And those who shorten.'"],[1852,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the pebble while he was being asked questions. A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before throwing?' He said, 'Throw, and there is no harm.' Another said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before slaughtering?' He said, 'Slaughter, and there is no harm.' So he was not asked about anything that was brought forward or delayed except that he said, 'Do it, and there is no harm.'"],[1853,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the pebble while he was being asked questions. A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before throwing?' He said, 'Throw, and there is no harm.' Another said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before slaughtering?' He said, 'Slaughter, and there is no harm.' So he was not asked about anything that was brought forward or delayed except that he said, 'Do it, and there is no harm.'"],[1854,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the people in the Farewell Pilgrimage. A man said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before slaughtering?' He said, 'No harm.' He said, 'I did not realize, I slaughtered before throwing?' He said, 'No harm.' So he was not asked that day about anything brought forward or delayed except that he said, 'No harm.'"],[1855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the people in the Farewell Pilgrimage. A man said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before slaughtering?' He said, 'No harm.' He said, 'I did not realize, I slaughtered before throwing?' He said, 'No harm.' So he was not asked that day about anything brought forward or delayed except that he said, 'No harm.'"],[1856,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'How should I deal with what is crippled of the sacrificial animal?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Any body of a sacrificial animal that becomes crippled, slaughter it, then place its sandal in its blood, then leave it between it and the people so they may eat it.'"],[1857,"He narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once gifted some sheep as a hady."],[1858,"He narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer at Dhu'l-Hulayfah, then called for a sacrificial camel and marked it from the right side of its hump. Then he wiped the blood from it and put two sandals around its neck. Then his riding camel was brought, and when he sat on it and it stood up straight on the desert plain, he recited the talbiyah for Hajj."],[1859,"He narrated that he came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said, \"Ride it.\" The man said, \"It is a sacrificial camel.\" He said, \"Ride it.\" The man said, \"It is a sacrificial camel.\" He said, \"Ride it, woe to you!\""],[1860,"He narrated that he saw a man who had made a sacrificial camel kneel down. He said, \"Make it stand, with its leg hobbled, according to the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[1861,"He narrated that when the Prophet ﷺ returned from the Umrah of al-Ji'ranah, he sent Abu Bakr as leader of the Hajj. We set out with him until when we were at al-'Arj, the call for the morning prayer was given. When he stood to say the takbir, he heard the grunting of a camel behind him, so he paused from the takbir and said, \"This is the grunting of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ camel al-Jad'a'. It seems that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has changed his mind about the Hajj, so perhaps it is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we may pray with him.\" But it was 'Ali on it. Abu Bakr said, \"Are you a commander or a messenger?\" He said, \"No, rather a messenger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with Bara'ah to recite to the people at the stations of Hajj.\" We arrived at Makkah, and one day before the day of Tarwiyah, Abu Bakr stood and addressed the people, teaching them their rituals. When he had finished, 'Ali stood and recited Bara'ah to the people until he completed it. Then we went out with him until the day of 'Arafah. Abu Bakr stood and addressed the people, teaching them their rituals. When he had finished, 'Ali stood and recited Bara'ah to the people until he completed it. Then on the day of sacrifice we departed. When Abu Bakr returned, he addressed the people, teaching them about their departure, their sacrifice, and their rituals. When he had finished, 'Ali stood and recited Bara'ah to the people until he completed it. On the first day of departure, Abu Bakr stood and addressed the people, telling them how to depart and how to stone, and he taught them their rituals. When he had finished, 'Ali stood and recited Bara'ah to the people until he completed it."],[1862,"He narrated that on that day the Prophet ﷺ sat on a camel—I am not sure whether it was a male or a female—and a man held its halter, or he said its reins. He said, \"Which day is this?\" We remained silent, thinking that he would call it by a different name. He said, \"Is it not the day of sacrifice?\" We said, \"Indeed.\" He said, \"Which month is this?\" We remained silent, thinking that he would call it by a different name. He said, \"Is it not Dhu'l-Hijjah?\" We said, \"Indeed.\" He said, \"Which land is this?\" We remained silent, thinking that he would call it by a different name. He said, \"Is it not the sacred city?\" We said, \"Indeed.\" He said, \"Verily, your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred among you like the sanctity of this day, in this month, in this land. Let those present convey to those absent, for the one present may convey to someone who understands better than he does.\""],[1863,"He narrated that Safiyyah menstruated. On the night of departure, she said, \"Alas, how wretched!\" in their dialect. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Did you not perform the tawaf on the day of sacrifice?\" She said, \"Indeed I did.\" He said, \"Then proceed.\""],[1864,"He said: We asked 'Ali, \"With what were you sent?\" He said, \"I was sent with four things: no one enters Paradise except a believing soul; no one may circumambulate the House naked; no Muslim and no disbeliever may gather together in the Hajj after this year; and whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, his treaty lasts until its term, and whoever has no treaty, it is four months.\" He said, \"After the day of sacrifice, their deadline is the twentieth of Dhu'l-Hijjah, so fight them after the four months.\""],[1865,"It was asked of Jabir b. 'Abd Allah about raising the hands at the House. He said, \"Only the Jews used to do that. We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and did we do that?\""],[1866,"He asked the people to be silent during the Farewell Hajj and then said, \"Do not return after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks.\""],[1867,"He narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ran between Safa and Marwah while we shielded him from the people of Makkah, lest someone hit him with a stone or a shot."],[1868,"He witnessed Ali and Uthman between Makkah and Madinah while Uthman was prohibiting mut'ah. When Ali saw that, he entered ihram for both together and said, 'Labbayk with a Hajj and an Umrah together.' Uthman said, 'You see me prohibiting it, yet you do it?' Ali replied, 'I would not abandon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the word of anyone among people.'"],[1869,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Labbayk with an Umrah and a Hajj.'"],[1870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram for both together. I met Ibn Umar and informed him of Anas's statement, and he said, 'He only entered ihram for Hajj.' I returned to Anas and informed him of Ibn Umar's statement, and he said, 'Do they consider us but children?'"],[1871,"O Banu Abd Manaf, if you are given authority over this matter, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating or praying at any hour he wishes, night or day."],[1872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the night at Dhu Tuwa until morning, then entered Makkah. And Ibn Umar used to do that."],[1873,"He would enter Makkah from the upper mountain pass and leave from the lower mountain pass."],[1874,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his foot in the stirrup and his she-camel stood upright with him, he would enter ihram from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."],[1875,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning the muhrim whose eyes hurt: 'He should bandage them with aloe.'"],[1876,"The Prophet ﷺ arrived, circumambulated the House, prayed two rak'ahs at the Maqam, then went out to al-Safa."],[1877,"The people used to go out (from Mecca after Hajj) by all sides. The Prophet ﷺ said: No one should leave (Mecca) until he performs the last circumambulation of the House (the Ka'bah). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2002)"],[1878,"Concession was given for a menstruating woman to depart if she had performed the Ifadah tawaf."],[1879,"That he heard Abdullah b. Umar while he was being asked about preventing women from the tawaf of the House when they menstruate before departing, and they had already performed the ifadah on the Day of Sacrifice. He said, 'Aishah used to mention a concession for women, and that was one year before the death of Abdullah b. Umar.'"],[1880,"That he said to Aishah, 'O Mother of the Believers, there are men one of whom sends his gift with a man and says: when you reach such-and-such a place, garland it. When he reaches that place, he remains in ihram until the people come out of ihram.' He said, 'I heard the clap of her hand from behind the screen, and she said: I used to twist the garlands for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send the gift to the Kabah, and nothing that is lawful for a man among his family became forbidden to him until the people returned.'"],[1881,"'I used to twist the garlands of the gift of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send his gift garlanded and stay in Madinah, and he would not avoid anything until his gift was slaughtered.'"],[1882,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, shall we not build for you at Mina a structure to shade you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No. Mina is the resting place of whoever arrives first.'"],[1883,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah in the year of the conquest, and on his head was a helmet. When he took it off, a man came to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is Ibn Khatal clinging to the curtains of the Kabah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Kill him.' Abdullah b. Khalid said: And it was read to Malik. He said: Ibn Shihab said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not in ihram on that day."],[1884,"'The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah when he conquered it, and on him was a black turban, without ihram.'"],[1885,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to take charge of his sacrificial camels, and to distribute all of his sacrificial camels — their meat, their hides, and their coverings — and not to give anything from them for their slaughtering."],[1886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the hyena, and he said, 'It is game, and in it is a ram if the muhrim catches it.'"],[1887,"I asked Jabir b. Abdullah about the hyena, 'May I eat it?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'Is it game?' He said, 'Yes.' I said, 'Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[1888,"That al-Abbas b. Abdul-Muttalib asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to spend the nights of Mina in Makkah because of his water-giving. He granted him permission."],[1889,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two salt-and-white horned rams. He pronounced the name of Allah and said the takbir. I saw him slaughter them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides.' I said, 'Did you hear it yourself?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[1890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two rams on the day of Eid. When he turned them [for slaughter], he said: “Indeed, I have turned my face toward the One who created the heavens and the earth, inclining to truth, and I am not of those who associate others with Allah. Indeed, my prayer, my rites of sacrifice, my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. And this I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, indeed this is from You and for You, on behalf of Muhammad and his Ummah.” Then he pronounced the name of Allah, said Allahu Akbar, and slaughtered."],[1891,"\"Ibn Al-Musayyab told me that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet told him that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever wants to offer a sacrifice, let him not remove anything from his nails or cut his hair for the first ten days Dhul-Jijjah.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4362)"],[1892,"“When the ten days (of Dhul-Hijjah) begin, and one of you wants to offer a sacrifice, let him not remove anything from his hair or skin.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3149)"],[1893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked what should be avoided in sacrificial animals. He said: “The one-eyed whose defect is obvious, the lame whose lameness is obvious, the sick whose sickness is obvious, and the emaciated one that has no marrow.”"],[1894,"I asked al-Bara' about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited among sacrificial animals. He said: “Four are not sufficient: the one-eyed whose defect is obvious, the lame whose lameness is obvious, the sick whose sickness is obvious, and the broken [or emaciated] one that has no marrow.”"],[1895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to examine the eyes and ears."],[1896,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to trim the eye and ear, and not to shave, trim, or pierce.\" So, \"trimming\" refers to cutting the edge of the ear, \"shaving\" refers to cutting from the side of the ear, \"pierced\" refers to a perforated (eared?) one, and \"split\" refers to a split one."],[1897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his Companions. A jadha' (young sheep) fell to my share. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, a jadha'a has fallen to me.” He said, “Sacrifice it.”"],[1898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me some sheep to distribute among his Companions. I distributed them, and an 'atud (young goat) remained. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Sacrifice it.”"],[1899,"On the day of Hudaybiyyah, we slaughtered seventy badanahs (camels), each badanah on behalf of seven. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Share in the sacrificial animal.”"],[1900,"We slaughtered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a cow on behalf of seven."],[1901,"He prohibited the meat of sacrificial animals, or he said: “Do not eat the meat of sacrificial animals after three [days].”"],[1902,"We had forbidden you to eat the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days so that it might suffice you. Now Allah has brought abundance, so eat, store, and seek reward."],[1903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prohibited the meat of sacrificial animals after three days. The following year, when the people sacrificed, I said, “O Messenger of Allah, these sacrificial animals used to benefit the people; they used to store their meat and fat?” He said, “What prevents them from that today?” I said, “O Prophet of Allah, did you not forbid them last year from eating their meat beyond three days?” He said, “I only forbade that because of the needy people who had come to them from the desert, so that they would distribute the meat among them. Now let them eat and store.”"],[1904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me while we were at Mina, “Prepare for us some of this meat.” I prepared some for him, and he kept eating from it until we reached Madinah."],[1905,"We used to take provision from Makkah to Madinah at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1906,"Abu Burdah b. Niyar sacrificed before he prayed, and when the Prophet ﷺ had prayed he called him and he mentioned to him what he had done, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Your sheep is only a sheep for meat.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a jadh'ah goat kid that is dearer to me than two sheep.\" He said, \"Then sacrifice it, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[1907,"That the Prophet ﷺ should leave and he ordered him to return."],[1908,"There is no fara'a and no 'atirah."],[1909,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we used to sacrifice during the month of Rajab. What do you think?\" He said, \"There is no problem with that.\" Waki said, \"I will never leave it.\""],[1910,"He said concerning the 'aqiqah, \"For a boy two sheep of equal age, and for a girl one sheep.\""],[1911,"With the boy is an 'aqiqah, so pour blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."],[1912,"For a boy two similar sheep, and for a girl one sheep."],[1913,"Every boy is held in pledge by his 'aqiqah; it is slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day, and his head is shaved and smeared with blood."],[1914,"I memorized two things from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Allah has prescribed excellence in everything. When you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and give rest to his animal.\""],[1915,"A woman used to tend sheep for the family of Ka'b b. Malik at Sal'. She feared that one of the sheep would die, so she took a stone and slaughtered it with it. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he commanded them to eat it."],[1916,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat and the upper chest?\" He said, \"If you had stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed you.\""],[1917,"I went out with Ibn 'Umar on one of the roads of Madinah, and there were some boys throwing stones at a chicken. Ibn 'Umar said, \"Who did this?\" They scattered. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed whoever mutilates animals.\""],[1918,"He forbade confining an animal to be shot."],[1919,"He prohibited al-mujaththamah.” Abu Muhammad said: “Al-mujaththamah is the animal that is tied up and shot (at).”"],[1920,"Some people said, “O Messenger of Allah, some people bring us meat and we do not know whether the name of Allah has been mentioned over it or not.” He said, “Say the name of Allah yourselves and eat.” They had only recently left the days of ignorance."],[1921,"A camel bolted, and the people had only a few horses, so a man shot it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “These beasts have wild impulses like those of wild animals. Whatever of them overpowers you, deal with it in this way.”"],[1922,"“Whoever kills a sparrow without right, Allah will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection.” It was said, “What is its right?” He said, “That you slaughter it and eat it.”"],[1923,"“The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.”"],[1924,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited eating every beast of prey that has fangs.”"],[1925,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the snatched morsel, the tied-up animal, the stolen property, and eating every beast of prey that has fangs.”"],[1926,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited eating every beast of prey that has fangs and every bird that has talons.”"],[1927,"“He prohibited using the skins of beasts of prey as floor coverings.”"],[1928,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas about water skins, and he said, “I do not know what to tell you except that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Any hide that is tanned has become pure.’”"],[1929,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas about the skins of dead animals, and he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Its tanning is its purification.’”"],[1930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the skins of dead animals be utilized when they are tanned."],[1931,"A sheep belonging to Maymunah died, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Why did you not make use of its hide?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is a dead animal.\" He said: \"Only its eating is forbidden.\""],[1932,"\"The Messenger of Allah forbade Mut'ah and the flesh of domesticated donkeys on the Day of Khaibar.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4335)"],[1933,"\"O Messenger of Allah, the donkeys have been eaten or are being slaughtered.\" Then he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the donkeys have been slaughtered or are being eaten.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man to announce, \"Indeed, Allah and His Messenger prohibit you from consuming donkey meat, as it is impure.\""],[1934,"\"We ate the meat of a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah.\""],[1935,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited on the day of Khaybar the meat of domesticated donkeys, and he permitted the meat of horses.\""],[1936,"\"He does not snatch a plunder of significant value, one in which the believers raise their eyes toward it, while he is a believer at the time he snatches it.\""],[1937,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited looting.\""],[1938,"We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where famine occurs; what of dead animals is lawful for us?\" He said: \"When you have not drunk the morning milk, nor the evening milk, nor gathered wild herbs, then you may make use of it.\" People say with a ha', but this one said with a kha'."],[1939,"I gifted a milch camel to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he commanded me to milk it. I milked it and exerted myself in milking it. He said: \"Leave the remaining milk in the udder.\""],[1940,"He prohibited killing frogs.\""],[1941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited killing four creatures: the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, and the shrike."],[1942,"It was narrated from Umm Sharik that the Prophet ﷺ told her to kill house lizards. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3228)"],[1943,"He prohibited eating animals that have been tied up and shot, and the milk of animals that eat filth, and drinking from the mouth of a water skin.\""],[1944,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the game caught by a dog. He said: “What your dog holds back for you, eat, for its taking is its slaughter. But if you find another dog with it and you fear that the other dog took it with it and killed it, then do not eat it, for you only mentioned the name of Allah over your dog, and you did not mention it over the other.”"],[1945,"“Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qīrāṭs are deducted from his reward every day.”"],[1946,"“I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘Whoever keeps a dog that he does not need for farming or herding, one Qirat will be deducted from his (good) deeds each day.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3206)"],[1947,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of dogs, then said: “What have I to do with dogs?” Then he gave a concession for the dog of cultivation and the dog of hunting."],[1948,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of dogs.”"],[1949,"“Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have commanded that all of them be killed. But kill from them every pure black one.”"],[1950,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the mi'rād. He said: “If it strikes with its edge, eat; but if it strikes with its broad side and kills, then it is a waqīdh, so do not eat.”"],[1951,"“We went on seven military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating locusts.”"],[1952,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “We travel by sea and carry with us a little fresh water. If we perform ablution with it, we become thirsty. May we perform ablution with seawater?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Its water is purifying, and its dead animals are lawful.”"],[1953,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us out in a party of three hundred, and we were struck by hunger until we reached the sea, and it had cast up a beast. We ate from it until our bodies regained strength. Abu ʿUbaydah took one of its ribs and set it up, then he mounted the tallest man in the army on the largest camel in the army, and the man passed under it.”"],[1954,"We startled a rabbit while we were at Marr al-Ẓahrān. The people ran after it and became exhausted. I caught it and brought it to Abu Ṭalḥah, who slaughtered it and sent its two haunches—or its two thighs, Shuʿbah was unsure—to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he accepted it."],[1955,"He passed by the Prophet ﷺ with two rabbits hanging. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I entered my family's sheep flock and hunted these two rabbits, but I could not find an iron blade to slaughter them with, so I slaughtered them with a sharp stone. May I eat?” He said: “Yes.”"],[1956,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the dabb lizard, and he said: “I am not one to eat it, nor do I declare it forbidden.”"],[1957,"A dabb lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “A nation that was transformed, and Allah knows best.”"],[1958,"He entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who was his maternal aunt and the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas. He found with her a roasted dabb lizard that her sister Hufaydah bt. al-Harith had brought from Najd. She offered the dabb to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he rarely extended his hand to food until it was described to him and named for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached his hand toward the dabb, and a woman among the women present said: Tell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what you have offered him. They said: It is dabb. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ withdrew his hand, so Khalid b. al-Walid said: Do you forbid dabb, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “No, but it is not found in the land of my people, and I find myself averse to it.” Khalid said: So I pulled it over and ate it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching, and he did not forbid me."],[1959,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while the people were cutting off the humps of camels and the fat tails of sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is carrion.”"],[1960,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Mention Allah's name, and eat from what is near you.”"],[1961,"The Prophet ﷺ was eating food with six of his companions when a Bedouin came and ate it up in two mouthfuls. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, if he had mentioned the name of Allah, it would have sufficed you all. So when one of you eats, let him mention the name of Allah. If he forgets to mention the name of Allah, let him say: In the name of Allah at its beginning and at its end.”"],[1962,"My father said to my mother: If you would make food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So she made a tharidah, and he gestured with his hand, indicating little. My father went and invited him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on its top and then said: “Take, in the name of Allah.” They took from its sides. When they had eaten, he supplicated for them, saying: “O Allah, forgive them, have mercy on them, and bless them in their provision.”"],[1963,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate or drank, he would say: “Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise, not rejected, nor left, nor dispensed with, O our Lord.”"],[1964,"“The grateful eater is like the patient fasting person.”"],[1965,"“When one of you eats, let him lick his three fingers.”"],[1966,"“When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks his fingers or has them licked.”"],[1967,"Nubayshah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, came in upon us while we were eating some food. We invited him, and he ate with us, then he said:"],[1968,"“When a morsel of one of you falls, let him wipe off the dust from it, pronounce the name of Allah, and eat it.”"],[1969,"Maʿqil b. Yasār was eating lunch when his morsel fell. He took it, removed whatever dirt was on it, then ate it. Those village chiefs began winking at one another about him, and they said to him, “Do you not see what these non-Arabs are saying? They say, ‘Look at the food in front of him and what he does with this morsel!’” He said, “I will not abandon what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because of the words of these non-Arabs. We were commanded, when a morsel of one of us fell, to remove whatever dirt was on it and to eat it.”"],[1970,"“When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand. Indeed, Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.”"],[1971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Busr b. Rāʿī al-ʿĪr eating with his left hand, so he said, “Eat with your right hand.” He said, “I cannot.” He said, “May you never be able.” And his right hand never reached his mouth after that."],[1972,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to eat with three fingers and would not wipe his hand until he had licked it.”"],[1973,"“He used to eat with his three fingers, and when he finished, he would lick them.”"],[1974,"“Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say what is good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest with his due reward for a day and a night. Hospitality is three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity.”"],[1975,"“Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him be good to his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say what is good or remain silent.”"],[1976,"“Any Muslim who is a guest of a people and wakes up as a deprived guest, then every Muslim is obligated to help him until he takes for him the hospitality of his night from their crops and wealth.”"],[1977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a fly falls into the drink of one of you, let him immerse it completely, then remove it. For in one of its wings is disease and in the other is a cure.”"],[1978,"When a fly falls into the vessel of any of you, let him immerse it, for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other there is healing."],[1979,"The believer eats in one stomach, and the disbeliever eats in seven stomachs."],[1980,"The believer eats in one stomach, and the disbeliever eats in seven stomachs."],[1981,"The food of one suffices two, the food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."],[1982,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Mention the name of Allah and eat from what is near you.'"],[1983,"A large bowl of tharid was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or he said a small bowl, and he said: 'Eat from its edges,' or he said 'its sides, and do not eat from its middle, for the blessing descends in its middle.'"],[1984,"When tharid was brought to her, she ordered that it be covered until its bubbling and steam subsided, and she said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: It is greater for blessing.'"],[1985,"One day the Prophet ﷺ took me by the hand to his house and said: 'Is there any lunch or dinner?' Talhah was uncertain. He said: Then he brought out to him broken pieces of bread and said: 'Is there any condiment?' They said: 'No, except a little vinegar.' He said: 'Bring it, for how excellent a condiment vinegar is.' Jabir said: 'I have not ceased to love vinegar since I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[1986,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'How excellent a condiment is vinegar, or how excellent a relish is vinegar.'"],[1987,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when a broth containing gourd and dried meat was brought to him, and I saw him picking out the gourd and eating it."],[1988,"The Prophet ﷺ used to like gourd. He said: So it was offered to him, and I began to take some and place it before him."],[1989,"Eat olive oil, for it is blessed; use it as a dip and apply it as oil, for it comes from a blessed tree."],[1990,"The Prophet ﷺ said in the Battle of Khaybar, \"Whoever eats from this tree, meaning garlic, should not come to the mosques.\""],[1991,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came down to us, and we went to some trouble to prepare food for him containing some of these herbs. When we brought it, he disliked it and said to his companions: 'Eat, for I am not like any of you; I fear that I may offend my companion.'"],[1992,"We were with Abu Musa when his food was served, and among his food was chicken meat. In the group was a man from Banu Taym Allah who was reddish in complexion, and he kept away. Abu Musa said to him: 'Come close, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat from it.'"],[1993,"Why do you put on the lower garment in this way? He replied: It is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4096)"],[1994,"Do not keep company except with a believer, and let no one eat your food except a pious person."],[1995,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating cucumber with fresh dates."],[1996,"We were in Madinah when a year of famine struck us, and Ibn al-Zubayr was distributing dates as provision. Ibn Umar would pass by us and say: 'Do not pair dates together, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade pairing unless a man seeks permission from his brother.'"],[1997,"O A'ishah, a house with no dates in it has hungry inhabitants - or its inhabitants go hungry - he said it twice or three times."],[1998,"The inhabitants of a house will not go hungry if they have dates."],[1999,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: Dates were gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, and he began to give them as gifts."],[2001,"Whoever sleeps with the smell of grease on his hand and something happens to him should blame no one but himself."],[2002,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf, seeing on him a trace of yellow, “Mahyam?” He said, “I have married.” He said, “Hold a walimah, even if with a sheep.”"],[2003,"“The walimah on the first day is a right, the second is a kindness, and the third is fame and showing off.”"],[2004,"“The worst food is the food of a walimah to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. Whoever abandons the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.”"],[2005,"A man came who had prepared food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, like this,” and he gestured to him with his hand. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Like this,” and he pointed to ʿĀʾishah. He said, “No.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. Then he gestured to him a second time, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. Then he gestured to him a third time, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “And this one?” He said, “Yes.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went with him along with ʿĀʾishah, and they both ate from his food."],[2006,"There was a man called Abū Shuʿayb, and he had a slave boy who was a butcher. He said, “Prepare for me some food so that I may invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as the fifth of five.” He said: He invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as the fifth of five, and a man followed them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You invited us as the fifth of five, and this man has followed me. If you wish, you may permit him, and if you wish, you may leave him.” He said: So he permitted him."],[2007,"“The excellence of ʿĀʾishah over women is like the excellence of tharīd over all other food.”"],[2008,"My father married me off during the emirate of ʿUthmān, and he invited a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Among those he invited was Ṣafwān b. Umayyah, who was a very old man. He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Bite the meat with a proper bite, for it is more appetizing and more wholesome.’”"],[2009,"“I do not eat reclining.”"],[2010,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought the first fruits, he would say, “O Allah, bless us in our Madinah, in our fruits, in our mudd, and in our ṣāʿ, blessing upon blessing.” Then he would give it to the youngest child present."],[2011,"“When the servant of one of you brings the food, let him seat him; if he refuses, let him hand it to him.”"],[2012,"“When one of you’s servant brings him food, let him seat him with him or hand him a morsel or two morsels or a bite or two bites, for he has endured its heat and its smoke.”"],[2013,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love sweets and honey.”"],[2014,"The Prophet ﷺ came out from relieving himself, and food was presented to him. It was said to him, “Will you not perform ablution?” He said, “Should I pray, and then perform ablution?”"],[2015,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was in a state of major ritual impurity and wanted to eat or sleep, he would perform ablution.”"],[2016,"My close friend ﷺ advised me, saying, “When you cook broth, increase its water, then look for a household among your neighbors and ladle out some for them.”"],[2017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When the food is served, remove your shoes, for it is better for your feet.\""],[2018,"“Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, and feed food, and you will enter the gardens.”"],[2019,"“Answer the caller when you are invited.” He said: And 'Abdullah would attend the invitation at a wedding and at other than a wedding, and he would attend it while fasting."],[2020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said, “Throw it away and what is around it, and eat.”"],[2021,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter and died. He said, “Take it and what is around it, and discard it.”"],[2022,"“Whoever eats should use a toothpick, and what he picks out he should spit out, and what he chews with his tongue he should swallow.”"],[2023,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought two cups in Iliya' on the night he was taken on the night journey, one of wine and one of milk. He looked at them and then took the milk. Jibril said, 'Praise be to Allah who guided you to the fitrah. Had you taken the wine, your ummah would have gone astray.'"],[2024,"I was the cupbearer of the people in the house of Abu Talhah. He said: Then the prohibition of wine was revealed. He said: He ordered a caller, and he called out. Abu Talhah said, 'Go out and see what this is.' He said: I went out and said, 'This is a caller calling out: \"Indeed wine has been forbidden.\"' He said to me, 'Go and spill it.' He said: It flowed in the streets of Madinah. He said: Their wine that day was fadikh. Some of the people said, 'Some people have been killed while it was in their bellies.' Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten, if they fear Allah and believe}."],[2025,"\"Whoever drinks wine in this world and does not repent from it will be deprived of it in the Hereafter and will not be given it to drink.\""],[2026,"I entered the garden of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As in Ta'if, which was known as Al-Wahṭ. I found him alongside a young man from the Quraysh, who was suspected of drinking wine. I said, \"There are some things reached to me about you that you report from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said, 'Whoever drinks wine, none of his prayers will be accepted for forty mornings.'\" When the young man heard him mention wine, he pulled his hand away from Abdullah's hand and turned away. Abdullah said, \"O Allah, I do not permit anyone to say something I did not say. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever drinks wine, none of his prayers will be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. But I do not know whether it is on the third or fourth instance that it is incumbent upon Allah to make him drink from the mud of khabal on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[2027,"\"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not sit at a table where wine is being drunk.\""],[2028,"\"The child of adultery, the one who constantly reminds others of his favors, the one who is disobedient to his parents, and the one addicted to wine will not enter Paradise.\""],[2029,"\"The one who is disobedient to his parents, the one who constantly reminds others of his favors, and the one addicted to wine will not enter Paradise.\""],[2030,"Suwayd b. Tariq asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wine, and he forbade him from making it. He said, 'It is a medicine.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not a medicine, but it is a disease.\""],[2031,"\"Wine is from these two trees: the date palm and the grapevine.\""],[2032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about bit'. He said, \"Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.\""],[2033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me and Mu'adh b. Jabal to Yemen and said, \"Drink, but do not drink any intoxicant, for every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[2034,"\"I forbid you from a small amount of that which intoxicates in large amounts.\""],[2035,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Indeed, the first thing that will be forbidden is said to be Zaid, meaning in Islam just like a container is forbidden, meaning alcohol. So it was said, 'How so, O Messenger of Allah, when Allah has clearly stated what is haram in it?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'They will give it a different name and make it permissible.'\""],[2036,"\"The first of your religion is prophethood and mercy, then kingship and mercy, then a dust-colored kingship, then a kingship with tyranny, in which wine and silk are deemed lawful.\""],[2037,"“Whoever sells wine, let him also slaughter pigs.”"],[2038,"I asked Ibn ‘Abbās about selling wine. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a friend from Thaqīf or from Daws, who met him in Makkah in the year of the conquest with a skin of wine, intending to give it to him as a gift. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O so-and-so, do you not know that Allah, Exalted is He, has forbidden it?” He said: The man turned to his servant and said: “Go and sell it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What did you order him to do, O so-and-so?” He said: “I ordered him to sell it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the One who forbade drinking it also forbade selling it.” So he ordered it to be overturned, and it was poured out in al-Baṭḥā’."],[2039,"It reached ‘Umar that Samurah had sold wine, so he said: “May Allah fight Samurah! Does he not know that the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘May Allah curse the Jews. Animal fat was forbidden to them, so they melted it and sold it.’”"],[2040,"“If he becomes drunk, flog him; then if he becomes drunk, flog him; then if he becomes drunk, flog him; then if he becomes drunk, strike his neck.”"],[2041,"“The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the wine drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer.”"],[2042,"Nabīdh would be prepared for the Prophet ﷺ in a water-skin; if no water-skin was available, it would be prepared for him in a stone vessel."],[2043,"That his father, or a man among them, asked the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, we have come out from where you know, and we have settled among people whom you know. Who is our protector?” He said: “Allah and His Messenger.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we used to be owners of vineyards and wine, and Allah has forbidden wine, so what should we do with the vineyards?” He said: “Make them into raisins.” They said: “Then what should we do with the raisins?” He said: “Soak them in water-skins; soak them in the morning and drink them in the evening, and soak them in the evening and drink them in the morning, for when the two times pass, it becomes vinegar before it becomes wine.”"],[2044,"I asked Ibn ‘Umar about nabīdh in earthenware jars. He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it.” Then I met Ibn ‘Abbās and informed him of Ibn ‘Umar’s statement, and he said: “Abū ‘Abd al-Raḥmān spoke the truth.”"],[2045,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not prepare nabīdh in gourds or vessels smeared with pitch.”"],[2046,"I asked Ibn ‘Abbās, or I heard him being asked, about nabīdh in earthenware jars. He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabīdh in earthenware jars and gourds.”"],[2049,"“Tell me what drink is forbidden to us.” He said: “Wine.” I said: “That is in the Qur’an.” He said: “I only relate to you what I heard Muḥammad ﷺ say, beginning with the name or the message.” He said: “He forbade gourds, green jars, and hollowed stumps.”"],[2050,"Do not soak unripe dates and ripe dates together, and do not soak raisins and dried dates together, but soak each one of them separately."],[2051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not say 'al-Karm,' but say 'al-'Inab' or 'al-Habalah.'"],[2052,"There were orphans in the care of Abu Talhah, and he bought wine for them. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, 'Should I make it into vinegar?' He said, 'No.' So he poured it out."],[2053,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drink milk, with Abu Bakr on his left and a Bedouin man on his right. He gave the leftover to the Bedouin, then said, 'The right, then the right.'"],[2054,"He forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."],[2055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."],[2056,"He forbade inverting waterskins."],[2057,"Anas used to breathe in the vessel two or three times, and he claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to breathe in the vessel two or three times."],[2058,"I was with Marwan when Abu Sa'id came and said: A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I cannot quench my thirst with one breath.' He said, 'Then remove the vessel from your mouth, then breathe.' He said, 'I see a speck in it.' He said, 'Then pour it out.'"],[2059,"When one of you urinates, he should not touch his private part with his right hand, nor cleanse himself with his right hand, nor breathe into the vessel."],[2060,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a man among the Ansar to visit him, and a stream was flowing. He said, 'If you have water that has stood overnight in a skin, otherwise we will drink directly from the stream.'"],[2061,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ drank standing from a container.\""],[2062,"“At the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to eat while walking, and drink while standing up.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3301)"],[2063,"He forbade drinking while standing. He said: And I asked him about eating. He said: That is worse."],[2064,"He said to a man whom he saw drinking while standing: Vomit. He said: Why? He said: Would you like to drink with a cat? He said: No. He said: Then one worse than it has drunk with you: Satan."],[2065,"The one who drinks from a vessel of silver only gulps into his belly the fire of Hell."],[2066,"\"We went out with Hudhaifah to Al-Madain, seeking rain. A Bedouin came to him with a silver vessel, and Hudhaifah threw it away. We told him to quiet down, for if we asked him, he would not speak to us. However, later he asked us, 'Do you know why I threw it?' We said, 'No.' He said, 'I was forbidden to drink from vessels made of gold or silver, and forbidden to wear silk and brocade. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Those are for them in this world, and for you in the Hereafter.'"],[2067,"I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some milk, and he said: Why did you not cover it, even if you placed a stick across it?"],[2068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to cover the water container, tie the waterskin, and turn the vessel upside down."],[2069,"Marwan said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: Have you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid blowing into the drink? He said: Yes."],[2070,"He forbade blowing into the drink."],[2071,"The one who gives the people water is the last of them to drink."],[2072,"I said: O Prophet of Allah, the saying of Allah: For them are good tidings in the worldly life. He said: You have asked me about something no one before you or anyone from my nation has asked me. He said: It is the righteous vision that a Muslim sees or is seen for him."],[2073,"The vision of the believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[2074,"Prophethood has departed and the glad tidings remain."],[2075,"“Whoever sees me in a dream has (really) seen me, for Satan cannot appear in my form.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3901)"],[2076,"He who saw me in dream in fact saw the truth (what is true). (Using translation from Muslim 2267a)"],[2077,"The righteous vision is from Allah and the dream is from Satan. So when one of you dreams something he fears, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from Satan, for it will not harm him."],[2078,"I used to see dreams that made me sick. I mentioned that to Abu Qatadah. He said: I too used to see dreams that made me sick until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The good dream is from Allah, so if one of you sees what he loves, let him praise Allah and not tell it except to one he loves. And if he sees what he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from its evil and not tell it to anyone, for then it will not harm him.\""],[2079,"\"The dream is three: a good dream is glad tidings from Allah, a dream is grief from Satan, and a dream is from what a person tells himself. So if one of you sees what he dislikes, let him not speak of it, and let him stand and pray.\""],[2080,"\"When time draws near, the dream of the believer will hardly be false, and the most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful of them in speech.\""],[2081,"From Ali, who attributed the hadith to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever lies about his dream will be charged with tying two grains of barley on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2082,"\"The most truthful dreams are in the early morning hours.\""],[2083,"About the Prophet ﷺ, he used to say, \"Do not interpret dreams except by a knowledgeable person or an advisor.\""],[2084,"\"The dream is on the foot of a bird as long as it is not interpreted; when it is interpreted, it comes to pass.\""],[2085,"\"I saw my Lord in the most beautiful form.\" He said: About what does the Most High Assembly dispute? I said: \"You know best, O Lord.\" He said: Then He placed His palm between my shoulders, and I found its coolness between my breasts, and I learned what is in the heavens and the earth, and He recited: {And thus We showed Abraham the dominion of the heavens and the earth, so that he would be of those who are certain}."],[2086,"\"Whoever sees his Lord in a dream will enter Paradise.\""],[2087,"\"While I was sleeping, I saw people displayed before me wearing shirts, some of which reached the chest and some of which reached less than that. And Umar ibn al-Khattab was displayed before me wearing a shirt that he was dragging.\" Then those around him said: \"How did you interpret that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The religion.\""],[2088,"Musa b. Khalid narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. Muhammad al-Fazari, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar with this hadith. Ibn Umar said: When I slept, I would not get up until morning. Nafi said: Ibn Umar used to pray at night."],[2089,"While I was sleeping, I was brought a cup of milk and drank from it until I saw the moisture in my nail—or he said: in my nails—then I gave the remainder to Umar. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you interpret it? He said: \"Knowledge.\""],[2090,"“Milk is the fitrah, the ship is salvation, the camel is sorrow, greenery is Paradise, and the woman is good.”"],[2091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to his companions: “Whoever among you sees a dream, let him relate it to me and I will interpret it for him.” He said: A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw a canopy between the sky and the earth dripping honey and butter, and I saw a rope extending from the sky to the earth, and I saw people taking from it, some taking much and some taking little, and I saw a rope extending from the sky to the earth. You took hold of it and ascended, and Allah raised you. Then the one after you took hold of it and ascended, and Allah raised him. Then the one after him took hold of it and ascended, and Allah raised him. Then the one after him took hold of it, and it was cut off for him, then it was joined and connected. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to interpret it. He said: “Interpret it.” He was the most skilled of people in interpreting dreams after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: As for the canopy, it is Islam. As for the honey and butter, it is the Qur’an: the sweetness of honey and the softness of butter. As for those taking from it, some much and some little, they are the bearers of the Qur’an. As for the rope extending from the sky to the earth, it is the truth that you are upon. You take hold of it and Allah raises you by it. Then a man after you takes hold of it and rises by it. Then another man takes hold of it and rises by it. Then another man takes hold of it and it is cut off for him, then it is joined for him and he rises by it. So tell me, O Messenger of Allah, may my father be your ransom, did I get it right or wrong? He said: “You got some right and some wrong.” He said: What did I get right and what did I get wrong? He refused to tell him."],[2092,"I saw in a dream as if a sun or a moon – Abu Ja‘far was uncertain – was being raised from the earth to the sky by strong ropes. He mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “That is the death of your nephew.”"],[2093,"“In this dream of mine I saw that I shook a sword and its blade broke. That was what befell the believers on the day of Uhud. Then I shook it again and it returned to the best of what it had been. That was what Allah brought of the conquest and the gathering of the believers. I also saw in it cows, and by Allah, it is good. That was the group of believers on the day of Uhud. And the good is what Allah brought of good and the reward of truthfulness that He gave us after the day of Badr.”"],[2094,"“I saw as if I were in a strong coat of mail, and I saw cows being slaughtered. I interpreted that the coat of mail is Madinah and that the cows are a group – and by Allah, good. If we stay in Madinah, then if they enter upon us, we will fight them.” They said: By Allah, it was not entered upon us in the time of ignorance, so will it be entered upon us in Islam? He said: “Then it is your affair.” The Ansar said to one another: We have opposed the Prophet’s ﷺ opinion. So they came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the affair is yours. He said: “Now? When a prophet has put on his armor, he should not take it off until he fights.”"],[2095,"“I dislike the iron collar and I love the shackle. The shackle is steadfastness in religion.”"],[2096,"“I saw in a dream a black woman with disheveled hair and a foul smell being taken out of Madinah and settled in Mahya‘ah. I interpreted it as the plague of Madinah being transferred by Allah to Mahya‘ah.”"],[2097,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said one day: “I saw in a dream that a man came to me with a lump of dates and I ate it and found in it a date pit that hurt me when I chewed it. Then he gave me another lump.” Abu Bakr said: Your eye slept, O Messenger of Allah. This expedition that you sent out – they obtained booty twice. Both times they found a man invoking your protection. I said to Mujalid: “What does ‘invoking your protection’ mean?” He said: He says: “There is no god but Allah.”"],[2098,"“Good: your husband will return to you, if Allah Almighty wills, as a righteous man, and you will give birth to a dutiful boy.” She used to see it twice or three times, and every time she would come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he would say that to her, and her husband would return and she would give birth to a boy. Then she came one day as she used to come to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was absent, and she had seen that dream. I said to her: What are you asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about, O servant of Allah? She said: A dream that I used to see, and I would come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him about it, and he would say good, and it would happen as he said. I said: Then tell me what it is. She said: Until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ comes and I present it to him as I used to present it. By Allah, I did not leave her until she told me. I said: By Allah, if your dream is true, your husband will die and you will give birth to a wicked boy. She sat down weeping and said: What is wrong with me when I presented my dream to you? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while she was weeping. He said to her: What is wrong with her, O A’ishah? I told him the matter and what I had interpreted for her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Stop, O A’ishah. “When you interpret a dream for a Muslim, interpret it for good, for the dream will be according to how its interpreter interprets it.” So by Allah, her husband died, and I do not think she gave birth except to a wicked boy."],[2099,"“Whoever is able to marry but does not marry is not of us.”"],[2100,"It was narrated that 'Abdullah said: \"The Messenger of Allah said to us: 'O young men, whoever among you can afford it, let him get married, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and guarding chastity, and whoever cannot then he should fast, for it will be a restraint (wija') for him.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3209)"],[2101,"Do you have a young virgin girl who reminds you of Abu Abdurrahman? So he said, \"If you say that, then I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'O youth, whoever among you is able to marry, let him do so, for it is more effective in guarding the gaze and preserving chastity. And whoever is not able, then let him fast, for it will be a shield for him.'\""],[2102,"The Prophet ﷺ prevented ʿUthman bin Mazun from that (not marrying), and had he allowed him, we would have got ourselves castrated. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5074)"],[2103,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade celibacy.”"],[2104,"\"When it came to the matter of Uthman ibn Madhun, who was known for his abstention from women, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a messenger to him and said, 'O Uthman, I have not been commanded to adopt a monastic lifestyle. Have you turned away from my Sunnah?' Uthman replied, 'No, O Messenger of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Verily, it is from my Sunnah to pray, sleep, fast, give charity, get married, and divorce. Whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me, O Uthman. Indeed, your family has rights over you, and you have rights over yourself.' Saad said, 'By Allah, all the men among the Muslims were united in their acknowledgement that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed special preference to Uthman regarding his choice to abstain from women.'\""],[2105,"from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Women are married for four reasons: for religion, beauty, wealth, and lineage. So choose the one with religion—may your hands be dust-covered.”"],[2106,"He proposed to a woman from the Ansar, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Go and look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you two.\""],[2107,"Aqil b. Abi Talib came to Basra and married a woman from Banu Jusham. They said to him, \"With harmony and children.\" He said, \"Do not say that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that and commanded us to say, 'May Allah bless you and bless upon you.'\""],[2108,"When he congratulated someone, he would say, \"May Allah bless you and bless upon you, and bring you together in goodness.\""],[2109,"He forbade a man from proposing to a woman when his brother has already proposed."],[2110,"None of you should propose to a woman when his brother has proposed, nor sell over his brother's sale, until he gives permission."],[2111,"She was married to a man from Quraysh, from Banu Makhzum, and he divorced her with an irrevocable divorce. She sent to his family seeking maintenance, but they said, \"You have no maintenance.\" That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"You have no maintenance, but you must observe the waiting period. Move to the house of Umm Sharik, and do not let us miss your company.\" Then he said, \"Umm Sharik is a woman whom her brothers from the Muhajirun visit. Instead, move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man. If you take off your clothes, he will not see anything. And do not let us miss your company.\" So she went to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum. When her waiting period ended, she mentioned that Mu'awiya and Abu Jahm had proposed to her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"As for Mu'awiya, he is a man with no wealth, and as for Abu Jahm, he does not put his stick down from his shoulder. What about Usama?\" Her family seemed to dislike that, but she said, \"By Allah, I will not marry anyone except the one the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned.\" So she married Usama."],[2112,"He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt, or the paternal aunt in addition to her brother's daughter, or a woman in addition to her maternal aunt, or the maternal aunt in addition to her sister's daughter. The younger is not to be married in addition to the older, nor the older in addition to the younger."],[2113,"He forbade combining a woman with her paternal aunt, and a woman with her maternal aunt."],[2114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade shighar."],[2115,"\"Marry the righteous men and righteous women.\" Abu Muhammad said, \"A part of the hadith fell from me, and what follows them is fine.\""],[2116,"There is no marriage without a guardian."],[2117,"There is no marriage without a guardian."],[2118,"Any woman married without her guardian's permission, her marriage is void, her marriage is void, her marriage is void. If they dispute—Abu 'Asim said, and he said once: if they dispute—then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian. If he has consummated with her, she is entitled to the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part."],[2119,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'An orphan girl should be consulted with regard to marriage, and if she remains silent, that is her permission. If she refuses then she is not to be forced.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3270)"],[2120,"A non-virgin is not to be married until she is consulted, and a virgin is not to be married until her permission is asked. Their said: O Messenger of Allah, what is her permission? He said: Her silence."],[2121,"A previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and a virgin is asked permission concerning herself, and her permission is her silence."],[2122,"The virgin is to be asked permission, and her permission is her silence."],[2123,"A previously married woman has more authority over her affair than her guardian, and a virgin is to be consulted concerning herself, and her silence is her consent."],[2124,"A man from among the Ansar called Khidham married off a daughter of his, and she disliked the marriage arranged by her father. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he annulled her father's marriage, and she married Abu Lubabah b. 'Abd al-Mundhir."],[2125,"Khansa' bt. Khidham's father married her off while she was a non-virgin, and she disliked that. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he annulled her marriage."],[2126,"Any woman married by two guardians—she belongs to the first of them. And any man who sells a sale to two men—it belongs to the first of them."],[2127,"They traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: 'Enjoy these women.' Enjoyment among us means marriage. So we offered that to the women, but they refused unless a term was set between us and them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do it.' So I went out with a cousin of mine; he had a cloak and I had a cloak, his cloak being better than mine, while I was younger than him. We came to a woman, and she was impressed by my youth and by his cloak. She said: 'A cloak like a cloak,' and the term between me and her was ten days. I spent that night with her, then went out in the morning, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing between the corner and the door, saying: 'O people, I had given you permission to enjoy women. Lo, Allah has forbidden it until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever has any of them, let him release her, and do not take back anything of what you gave them.'"],[2128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut'ah marriage in the year of the conquest."],[2129,"He prohibited mutah, the mutah of women, and the meat of domestic donkeys in the year of Khaybar."],[2130,"The muhrim does not marry, nor does he arrange a marriage."],[2131,"I asked `A'ishah, \"How much was the dower of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said, \"His dower to his wives was twelve uqiyah and a nashsh.\" And she said, \"Do you know what a nashsh is?\" He said, \"I said, 'No.'\" She said, \"Half an uqiyah. So this was the dower of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to his wives.\""],[2132,"I heard `Umar b. al-Khattab giving a sermon. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, \"Indeed, do not go to excess in the dowers of women. For if it were a source of honor in this world or piety with Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have been the most entitled to it among you. He did not give as dower to any of his wives, nor was any of his daughters given a dower, more than twelve uqiyah. Indeed, one of you goes to excess in the dower of his wife until she remains in his heart an enmity, until he says, 'I burdened myself for you with the strap of the water-skin, or the sweat of the water-skin.'\""],[2133,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that she had given herself to Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have no need of women.\" A man said, \"Marry me to her.\" He said, \"Give her a garment.\" He said, \"I cannot find one.\" He said, \"Give her even a ring of iron.\" He said, then he made an excuse to him. He said, \"What do you have of the Qur'an?\" He said, \"Such-and-such.\" He said, \"Then I have married you to her for what you have of the Qur'an.\""],[2134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the sermon of need: \"Praise be to Allah - or indeed, praise be to Allah - we praise Him, seek His help, and seek His forgiveness. We seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whoever Allah guides, none can mislead, and whoever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" Then he recites three verses: {O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims} [Al `Imran 102], {O mankind, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul and created from it its mate and dispersed from both of them many men and women. And fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs. Indeed Allah is ever over you an Observer}, {O you who believe, fear Allah and speak a right word. He will amend for you your deeds and forgive you your sins. And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly attained a great attainment} [Al-Ahzab 71]. Then he speaks of his need."],[2135,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The most deserving conditions to be fulfilled are those by which you have made private parts lawful.\""],[2136,"The Prophet ﷺ saw yellowness on Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and said, \"What is this yellowness?\" He said, \"I married a woman for the weight of a date pit of gold.\""],[2137,"\"When one of you is invited to a walimah, let him respond.\""],[2138,"\"Whoever has two wives and inclines to one of them will come on the Day of Resurrection with one side leaning.\""],[2139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to divide and be just, and he would say, \"O Allah, this is my division in what I possess, so do not blame me for what You possess and I do not possess.\""],[2140,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled, he would cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them her arrow came out, he would take her out with him."],[2141,"For the virgin, seven days, and for the previously married, three."],[2142,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah, he stayed with her for three days and said, “It is not that you are held in low esteem by your family. If you wish, I will complete seven days with you, and if I complete seven for you, I will complete seven for the rest of my wives.”"],[2143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me in Shawwal and I was brought to him in Shawwal, so which of his wives was more favored with him than me?"],[2144,"What prevents one of you from saying when he has intercourse with his wife, “In the name of Allah. O Allah, keep us away from Shaytan and keep Shaytan away from what You provide us”? For if Allah decrees a child, Shaytan will not harm it."],[2145,"“Allah is not ashamed of the truth: do not come to women in their rear passages.”"],[2146,"The Jews said to the Muslims, “Whoever comes to his wife while she is turned away, his child will be born cross-eyed.” So Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish}."],[2147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a woman and she pleased him. He went to Sawdah while she was preparing perfume, and with her were women. They left him alone, and he fulfilled his need. Then he said, “Any man who sees a woman who pleases him should go to his wife, for she has the like of what the other has.”"],[2148,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and when we camped, I hurried and someone riding caught up with me. He said, 'I turned back and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with me.' He said to me, 'What made you hurry, Jabir?' I said, 'I am newly married.' He said, 'Did you marry a virgin or a previously married woman?' I said, 'No, a previously married woman.' He said, 'Why didn't you marry a virgin so you could play with her and she could play with you?' Then he said to me, 'When you enter (your wife), do so from the easy direction.' When we entered (Medina), we waited until it was evening, meaning it was time for dinner, so that she could tidy her hair and put on perfume.\""],[2149,"“I had intended to forbid al-ghaylah until I remembered that the Persians and the Romans do that and it does not harm their children.” Abu Muhammad said, “Al-ghaylah is when he has intercourse with her while she is breastfeeding.”"],[2150,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never struck a servant nor did he strike anything with his hand except when striving in the cause of Allah.”"],[2151,"“Do not strike the female slaves of Allah.” Then Umar b. al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “They have become defiant against their husbands.” So he gave them permission to strike them. Then many women went around the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining about their husbands. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Many women have gone around the family of Muhammad complaining about their husbands. Those are not the best of you.”"],[2152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people one day and admonished them about women, saying, “What is the matter with a man who flogs his wife like a slave, yet perhaps he lies with her at the end of his day?”"],[2153,"“The woman was created from a rib. If you try to straighten it, you will break it. So be gentle with her, for in her there is crookedness and a means of livelihood.”"],[2154,"A woman is like a rib: if you straighten it, you break it; if you seek to enjoy it, you enjoy it while there is crookedness in it."],[2155,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about 'azl (withdrawal). He said, \"Do you do that? There is no blame on you if you do not do it, for there is no soul that Allah Most High has decreed to exist but that it will come to be.\""],[2156,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man has a slave girl and has relations with her but dislikes that she become pregnant; should he practice 'azl with her? And he has a wife who is breastfeeding, and he has relations with her but dislikes that she become pregnant; should he practice 'azl with her?\" He said, \"There is no blame on you if you do not do it, for it is only destiny.\""],[2157,"No one is more jealous than Allah; for that reason He forbade immoral deeds. And no one loves praise more than Allah."],[2158,"Some jealousy Allah loves and some He hates. The jealousy Allah loves is jealousy in a matter of suspicion, and the jealousy Allah hates is jealousy in a matter not of suspicion."],[2159,"It reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Sa'd b. 'Ubadah said, \"If I found a man with her, I would strike her with the sword, not with the flat side.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you marvel at the jealousy of Sa'd? I am more jealous than Sa'd, and Allah is more jealous than I. For that reason He forbade immoral deeds, both apparent and hidden. And no person is more jealous than Allah, and nothing is more beloved to Him than excuses. For that reason He sent the prophets as bearers of glad tidings and warners. And no person loves praise more than Allah; for that reason He promised Paradise.\""],[2160,"When a woman spends the night deserting her husband's bed, the angels curse her until she returns."],[2161,"That 'Uwaymir came to 'Asim b. 'Adiyy, and he was the chief of Banu 'Ajlan."],[2162,"I was asked about the two who engage in li'an during the governorship of Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr, whether they are to be separated. I did not know what to say. So I stood up and went to the house of 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar. I said to the servant, \"Ask permission for me to enter.\" He said, \"He is taking a midday nap; you will not be able to enter upon him.\" Ibn 'Umar heard my voice and said, \"Ibn Jubayr?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Enter. Nothing brought you at this hour except a need.\" So I entered upon him and found him using the saddle pad of his mount as a mat and a cushion as a pillow—or he said a small pillow—'Abd Allah was uncertain—stuffed with palm fiber. I said, \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the two who engage in li'an, are they to be separated?\" He said, \"Glory be to Allah, yes. The first person to ask about that was so-and-so. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless you, what do you think if one of us sees his wife committing an indecency, how should he act? If he remains silent, he remains silent about a grave matter, and if he speaks, it is the same.'\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and did not answer him. Then he stood up for his need. After that, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the matter I asked you about has befallen me.'\" He said, \"Then Allah Most High sent down these verses in Surat al-Nur: 'And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves, then the testimony of one of them is four testimonies by Allah that he is truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he is lying. And it will avert the punishment from her if she testifies four testimonies by Allah that he is lying, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is truthful.'\" Until he finished these verses. He said, \"Then he summoned the man and recited them to him, reminded him of Allah, and told him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. The man said, 'I have not lied about her.' Then he summoned the woman, admonished her, reminded her, and told her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. She said, 'By the One who sent you with truth, he is lying.' Then he called the man, and he testified four testimonies by Allah that he was truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he was lying. Then the woman was brought, and she testified four testimonies by Allah that he was lying, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he was truthful. Then he separated them.\""],[2163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated the two who engaged in li'an and attached the child to his mother."],[2164,"Any slave who marries without the permission of his masters or his family is a fornicator."],[2165,"Any slave who marries without the permission of his masters is a fornicator."],[2166,"The child belongs to the bed, and the stone belongs to the adulterer."],[2167,"The child belongs to the bed."],[2168,"Utbah b. Abi Waqqas had instructed his brother Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas to take into his custody the son of the slave woman of Zam'ah, saying, 'He is my son.' When the Prophet ﷺ arrived at the time of the conquest, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas took the son of the slave woman of Zam'ah, and he was the person most resembling Utbah b. Abi Waqqas. The Prophet said, 'He is yours, O 'Abd b. Zam'ah, because he was born on his father's bed.' And the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Veil yourself from him, O Sawdah bt. Zam'ah,' because of the resemblance he saw to Utbah b. Abi Waqqas, and Sawdah was the daughter of Zam'ah."],[2169,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say when the verse of li'an was revealed: 'Any woman who introduces into a people a lineage that is not of them has nothing to do with Allah, and Allah will never admit her to His Paradise. And any man who denies his son while looking at him, Allah will veil Himself from him and disgrace him before the heads of the first and the last.' Abdullah said: Muhammad b. Ka'b al-Qurazi and Sa'id narrated it to him with this, and this hadith has reached me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2170,"I met my uncle, and he had a banner. I said, 'Where are you heading?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and he commanded me to strike his neck and take his property.'"],[2171,"I said to Ubayy b. Ka'b, 'What do you think: if the wives of the Prophet ﷺ were to die, would it be permissible for him to marry?' He said, 'Yes. Allah only made lawful for him a certain category of women and described for him a description, then He said: \"It is not lawful for you to marry women after this description.\"'"],[2172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until Allah made it lawful for him to marry whatever women he wished."],[2173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her manumission her dower."],[2174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and married her, making her manumission her dower."],[2175,"I was with al-Sha'bi when a man from the people of Khurasan came to him and said, 'O Abu 'Amr, those of us in Khurasan say about a man who frees his slave woman and then marries her: he is like one riding his own camel.' Al-Sha'bi said..."],[2176,"About a man who married a woman and had not fixed any dower for her nor consummated the marriage, and then died: he said, she is entitled to a dower equivalent to that of women like her, she must observe the waiting period, and she inherits. Ma'qil al-Ashja'i said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of Birwa' bt. Washiq, a woman of Banu Ru'as, the same as you have ruled.' He said, and he was pleased with that."],[2177,"She was with the Prophet ﷺ in Hafsah's house when she heard a person's voice. She said: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard a person's voice in your house.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I think it is so-and-so, the paternal uncle of Hafsah through breastfeeding.' 'A'ishah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so were alive, her paternal uncle through breastfeeding, would he enter upon me?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes, what is prohibited by breastfeeding is what is prohibited by birth.'"],[2178,"Her paternal uncle, the brother of Abu al-Qu'ays, came asking permission to enter upon her after the veil was prescribed. She refused to permit him until she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked his permission. When the Prophet ﷺ came, she mentioned that to him and said: 'My paternal uncle, the brother of Abu al-Qu'ays, came, and I refused him until I ask your permission.' He said: 'Is he not your paternal uncle?' She said: 'It was the woman who breastfed me; the man did not breastfeed me.' He said: 'He is your paternal uncle, so let him enter upon you.' She said: 'And 'A'ishah used to say: What is prohibited by breastfeeding is what is prohibited by birth.'"],[2179,"What is prohibited by breastfeeding is what is prohibited by birth."],[2180,"One suckling or two sucklings do not make prohibited."],[2181,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have married one woman while I still have another, and the first woman claims that she breastfed the newborn.\" He said, \"Breastfeeding does not make prohibited (marriage) or create the relationship of foster children.\""],[2182,"The Qur'an was revealed with ten known sucklings that make prohibited, then they were abrogated by five known sucklings, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while they were still among what was recited of the Qur'an."],[2183,"He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the reproach of breastfeeding?' He said: 'The ghurrah: a slave or a slave woman.'"],[2184,"I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, and a black slave woman came and said: 'I breastfed both of you.' So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he turned away from me. Abu 'Asim said: He said: 'On the third or the fourth time he said: How, when it has been said?' And he forbade him from her."],[2185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while a man was with her. His face changed and he seemed to dislike that. I said: 'He is my brother through breastfeeding.' He said: 'Consider who your brothers are, for breastfeeding is only from hunger.'"],[2186,"Sahlah bint Suhayl b. 'Amr, who was married to Abu Hudhayfah b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon us while I am in a state of undress, and we regarded him as a son, for Abu Hudhayfah had adopted him as the Prophet ﷺ adopted Zayd.' Then Allah the Exalted revealed: 'Call them by their fathers; that is more just before Allah' [al-Ahzab 5]. So at that the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to breastfeed Salim. Abu Muhammad said: 'This is for Salim specifically.'"],[2187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who makes a woman lawful for her first husband and the one for whom she is made lawful."],[2188,"Hind, the mother of Mu'awiyah, the wife of Abu Sufyan, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man and he does not give me what suffices me and my children except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there any blame on me in that?' He said: 'Take what suffices you and your child in a fair manner.'"],[2189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you are those who are best to their families, and when your companion dies, then leave him be.”"],[2190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was a girl of six years. We came to Madinah and stayed among the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj. I fell ill and my hair fell out, then it grew back thick. Umm Ruman came to me while I was on a swing with my girl companions. She called me loudly, so I went to her, not knowing what she wanted. She took my hand and brought me to the door of the house. I was panting until my breathing calmed down. Then she took some water and wiped my face and head with it. Then she brought me into the house, and there were women of the Ansar in the room. They said, \"Upon goodness and blessing, and upon the best of fortune.\" She handed me over to them, and they prepared me. Then nothing startled me except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the forenoon. They handed me over to him, and I was on that day a girl of nine years."],[2191,"He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. Umar mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Order him to take her back and keep her until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure. Then, if he wishes, he may keep her, and if he wishes, he may divorce her before touching her. That is the prescribed waiting period during which Allah has commanded women to be divorced.\""],[2192,"Umar said to the Prophet ﷺ when Ibn Umar divorced his wife: \"Order him to take her back, then let him divorce her when she is pure.\""],[2193,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah, then took her back.\""],[2194,"The Prophet ﷺ \"divorced Hafsah, then took her back.\""],[2195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen, \"The Quran should not be touched except by one who is pure, and divorce cannot be pronounced before ownership is established, and the freeing of a slave cannot be done until it is bought.\" Abu Muhammad was asked about Sulaiman, and he said, \"I think he is a writer among the writers of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz.\""],[2196,"The wife of Rifa'ah al-Qurazi came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Abu Bakr and Khalid b. Sa'id b. al-'As were at the door, waiting to be granted permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I was married to Rifa'ah, and he divorced me with a final divorce.\" He said: \"Do you want to return to Rifa'ah? No, not until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his sweetness.\" Then Khalid b. Sa'id called out to Abu Bakr: \"Do you not see what she is saying openly in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\""],[2197,"Rifa'ah, a man from Banu Qurayzah, divorced his wife. Then 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Zubayr married her. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has nothing but something like this fringe of mine.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Perhaps you want to return to Rifa'ah. No, not until he tastes your sweetness,\" or he said, \"until you taste his sweetness.\""],[2198,"I asked 'A'ishah about the choice given to women. She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a choice, and was that a divorce?\""],[2199,"\"Any woman who asks her husband for a divorce without a serious reason, the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to her.\""],[2200,"Habibah bt. Sahl was married to Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas. She mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intended to marry her, and she was his neighbor. Thabit struck her, and she went out at dawn to the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and saw someone, so he said: \"Who is this?\" She said: \"I am Habibah bt. Sahl.\" He said: \"What is the matter with you?\" She said: \"Neither I nor Thabit.\" Then Thabit came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah said to him: \"Take from her what you gave her and let her go.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have everything he gave me.\" So he took from her, and she stayed with her family."],[2201,"He divorced his wife with an irrevocable divorce. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \"What did you intend?\" He said: \"One divorce.\" He said: \"By Allah?\" He said: \"By Allah.\" He said: \"It is according to what you intended.\""],[2202,"I was a man who had relations with women in a way that no one else did. When the month of Ramadan entered, I feared that I would do something at night and then continue doing it until morning. He said: So I resolved to abstain until the month ended. While she was serving me one night, something of her was revealed to me, and I did not wait before I fell upon her. When morning came, I went out to my people and told them. I said: \"Come with me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" They said: \"No, by Allah, we will not go with you. We fear that the Qur'an will be revealed concerning you, or that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will say something about you that will bring us shame. We will hand you over for your own offense.\" So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him my story. He said: \"O Salamah, you did that?\" I said: \"I did that.\" He said: \"O Salamah, you did that?\" I said: \"I did that.\" He said: \"O Salamah, you did that?\" I said: \"I did that. Here I am, patient with myself, so judge for me as Allah shows you.\" He said: \"Free a slave.\" He said: I struck the side of my neck, and I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not own any slave other than this.\" He said: \"Fast two consecutive months.\" I said: \"Did what happened to me happen except because of fasting?\" He said: \"Feed sixty poor people a wasq of dates.\" I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, we spent the night without any food.\" He said: \"Go to the collector of charity of Banu Zurayq and have him give it to you. Feed sixty poor people a wasq of dates, and you and your family may eat the rest.\" He said: I went to my people and said: \"I found with you hardship and bad judgment, and I found with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ease and good judgment. He has ordered me to take your charity.\""],[2203,"that her husband divorced her with three pronouncements, and the Prophet ﷺ did not assign her any maintenance or housing."],[2204,"that her husband divorced her with three pronouncements, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to observe her waiting period in the house of her cousin Ibn Umm Maktum."],[2205,"\"We will not abandon the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of His Prophet for the word of a woman. The woman divorced with three pronouncements is entitled to housing and maintenance.\""],[2206,"\"We do not accept the word of a woman in the religion of Allah. The woman divorced with three pronouncements is entitled to housing and maintenance.\""],[2207,"Abu Salamah b. Abd al-Rahman reported to him that he and Ibn Abbas gathered at Abu Hurayrah's, and they mentioned the man whose wife he dies leaving, and she gives birth a few nights after his death. Ibn Abbas said: Her waiting period ends at the later of the two terms. Abu Salamah said: When she gives birth, she becomes lawful. They argued about that between them, and Abu Hurayrah said: I am with my nephew, meaning Abu Salamah. So they sent Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, to Umm Salamah, and he asked her. Umm Salamah mentioned that Subay'ah bt. al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah's husband died, and she gave birth a few nights after his death, and that a man from Banu Abd al-Dar, called Abu al-Sanabil, proposed to her and informed her that she had become lawful, so she wanted to marry someone other than him. Abu al-Sanabil said to her: You are not lawful. Subay'ah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered her to marry."],[2208,"Subay'ah bt. al-Harith's husband died, and she gave birth a few days after her husband's death, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to marry."],[2209,"Subay'ah bt. al-Harith gave birth to her child twenty-some nights after her husband's death. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, she adorned herself, and that was criticized, so her case was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"If she does so, her term has ended.\""],[2210,"Subay'ah gave birth a few days after her husband's death, and she adorned herself, and Abu al-Sanabil criticized her, so she asked, or her case was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered her to marry."],[2211,"\"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day—or who believes in Allah—to mourn for anyone more than three days, except for her husband.\""],[2212,"that a brother of hers or a close relative died, so she took some yellow dye and began rubbing her hands with it, and said: I only do this because the Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn more than three days except for her husband; for him she mourns four months and ten.\""],[2213,"A woman should not mourn more than three days, except for a husband, for whom she mourns four months and ten days. She should not wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb (Yemeni striped cloth), nor apply kohl, nor touch perfume, except when she is closest to her purity after bathing from her menses, a small amount of costus and azfar (a type of perfume)."],[2214,"Al-Furay'ah bint Malik informed that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to return to her family because her husband had gone out in pursuit of some slave girls of his who had fled, and he caught up with them, and when he reached them at the edge of Al-Qudum, they killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Stay in your house until the prescribed period reaches its term.' I said, 'He did not leave me a house that I own or any maintenance.' He said, 'Stay until the prescribed period reaches its term.' So she observed the waiting period for four months and ten days. She said, 'When it was the time of Uthman, he sent for me and asked me about that, and I informed him, so he followed that and upheld it in his judgment.'\""],[2215,"My maternal aunt was divorced and wanted to harvest her palm trees. A man said to her, 'You have no right to go out.' She said, 'So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him.' He said, 'Go out and harvest your palm trees, for perhaps you will give charity or do some good.'"],[2216,"She wanted to buy Barirah, and her masters wanted to stipulate her wala' (clientage). She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Buy her, for the wala' belongs to the one who frees.' So she bought her and freed her, and gave her the choice regarding her husband, who was a free man. And the Prophet ﷺ was brought some meat and said, 'Where is this from?' It was said, 'It was given as charity to Barirah.' He said, 'It is charity for her and a gift for us.'"],[2217,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me and I brought him some food without meat. He said, 'Did I not see a pot set up for you?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is meat given as charity to Barirah, and she gave it to us as a gift.' He said, 'It is charity for her and a gift for us.' She had a husband, and when she was freed, she was given the choice."],[2218,"When 'A'ishah freed Barirah, her husband was a slave, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urged her to stay with him. She kept saying to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Do I not have the right to separate from him?' He said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Then I have separated from him.'"],[2219,"Barirah's husband was a slave called Mughith. It is as if I am looking at him walking behind her, crying, with his tears flowing onto his beard. The Prophet ﷺ said to al-'Abbas, 'O 'Abbas, are you not amazed at the intensity of Mughith's love for Barirah and the intensity of Barirah's hatred for Mughith?' He said to her, 'If only you would take him back, for he is the father of your child.' She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, are you commanding me?' He said, 'I am only interceding.' She said, 'I have no need of him.'"],[2220,"I was with Abu Hurayrah when a woman came to him and said, 'My husband wants to take away my child.' Abu Hurayrah said, 'I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a woman came to him and said, \"My husband wants to take away my child, or my son, who has benefited me and given me water from the well of Abu 'Inabah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Draw lots,\" or he said, \"Let them draw lots\" – Abu 'Asim was the one who doubted. Then her husband came and said, \"Who will dispute with me regarding my child, or my son?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O boy, this is your father and this is your mother, so take the hand of whichever of them you wish.\" And Abu 'Asim said, \"Follow whichever of them you wish.\" So he took his mother's hand and she left with him.'"],[2221,"For a slave woman there are two divorces, and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles."],[2222,"Regarding the captives of Awtas, he said, 'A pregnant woman is not to be had intercourse with until she gives birth, nor a non-pregnant woman until she has menstruated once.'"],[2223,"The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the child until he reaches puberty, and from the insane until he regains his sanity."],[2224,"The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three reasons: disbelief after faith, adultery after being married, or killing a person without right, in which case he is killed."],[2225,"The blood of a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for one of three persons: a life for a life, a previously married person who commits adultery, and one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."],[2226,"Safwan bin Umayyah was sleeping in the mosque, then a man came to him while he was also sleeping. He took his cloak from under his head and woke him up. Safwan caught up with him and took it back, then he went to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I was sleeping in the mosque and this man came to me and took my cloak from under my head. I caught up with him and took it back. He ordered for it to be cut, so Safwan said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, my cloak has not reached the point where it should be cut.\" He said, \"Why didn't you accept it before bringing it to me?\""],[2227,"The hand is cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[2228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut off (the hand) for a shield worth three dirhams."],[2229,"The Quraysh were concerned about the case of the Makhzumi woman who had stolen. They said, \"Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her?\" They said, \"Who would dare (to do so) except Usama b. Zayd, the beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" So Usama spoke to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you intercede regarding one of the limits set by Allah?\" Then he stood and delivered a sermon, saying, \"Those before you were destroyed only because when a noble person among them stole, they left him alone, but when a weak person among them stole, they carried out the punishment on him. By Allah, if Fatima bt. Muhammad were to steal, I would cut off her hand.\""],[2230,"A thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who confessed, but no goods were found with him. He said, \"I do not think you stole.\" He said, \"Yes, I did.\" He said, \"I do not think you stole.\" He said, \"Yes, I did.\" He said, \"Go and cut off his hand, then bring him to me.\" So they cut off his hand and then brought him. He said, \"Ask Allah for forgiveness and repent to Him.\" He said, \"I ask Allah for forgiveness and I repent to Him.\" He said, \"O Allah, accept his repentance. O Allah, accept his repentance.\""],[2231,"There is no cutting off (of the hand) for fruit nor for palm pith."],[2232,"There is no cutting off (of the hand) for fruit nor for palm pith."],[2233,"“The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2593)"],[2234,"There is no cutting off (of the hand) for fruit nor for palm pith."],[2235,"There is no cutting off (of the hand) for palm pith."],[2236,"There is no cutting off (of the hand) for the one who plunders openly, nor for the one who snatches away, nor for the betrayer."],[2237,"A man who had drunk wine was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he struck him with two palm branches. Then Abu Bakr did likewise. When it was Umar's time, he consulted the people, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said, \"The lightest of the prescribed punishments is eighty (lashes).\" He said, \"So he did that.\""],[2238,"I witnessed Uthman b. Affan when al-Walid b. Uqba was brought to him. Ali said, \"The Prophet ﷺ flogged forty lashes, Abu Bakr flogged forty, and Umar eighty, and each is a Sunnah.\""],[2239,"When one of you drinks, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns a fourth time, kill him."],[2240,"It is not lawful for anyone to strike anyone more than ten lashes except in a hadd from the hudud of Allah."],[2241,"A man from Aslam came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that he had committed adultery, and he testified against himself four times that he had committed adultery. So he ordered his stoning, and he had been married."],[2242,"Ma'iz b. Malik was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, a short man wearing only a lower garment and no cloak, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining on a pillow to his left. He spoke to him, and I do not know what he said to him, as I was far from him, with people between me and him. Then he said, \"Take him and stone him.\" Then he said, \"Bring him back.\" He spoke to him again, and I could hear, though people were between me and him. Then he said, \"Take him and stone him.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ stood and delivered a sermon, and I could hear him. Then he said, \"Whenever we go out in the way of Allah, one of them stays behind and bleats like a he-goat, granting one of them a small amount of milk. By Allah, if I get hold of any of them, I will make an example of him.\""],[2243,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I beseech you to judge us according to Allah's Laws.\" Then his opponent who was wiser than he, got up and said, \"He has spoken the truth. So judge us according to Allah's Laws and please allow me (to speak), O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Speak.\" He said, \"My son was a laborer for the family of this man and he committed illegal sexual intercourse with his wife, and I gave one-hundred sheep and a slave as a ransom (for my son), but I asked the religious learned people (regarding this case), and they informed me that my son should be flogged onehundred stripes, and be exiled for one year, and the wife of this man should be stoned (to death).\"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, I will Judge you (in this case) according to Allah's Laws. The one-hundred (sheep) and the slave shall be returned to you and your son shall be flogged one-hundred stripes and be exiled for one year. And O Unais! Go in the morning to the wife of this man and ask her, and if she confesses, stone her to death.\" She confessed and he stoned her to death. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6859)"],[2244,"I was among those who stoned him. Abu Muhammad said: meaning Ma'iz b. Malik. When he felt the touch of the stones, he panicked severely. He said: We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Why did you not leave him?\""],[2245,"\"Go with Ma'iz b. Malik and stone him.\" So we went with him to Baqi' al-Gharqad. By Allah, we did not tie him or dig for him, but he stood and we threw at him with bones, pottery shards, and stones."],[2246,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man called Ma'iz b. Malik came to him and confessed adultery to him. He turned him away three times. Then he came a fourth time and confessed. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that a pit be dug for him, and he was placed in it up to his chest, and he ordered the people to stone him."],[2247,"\"Indeed, the Jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a man and a woman from among them who had committed adultery. The Messenger said, 'What should be done with those who have committed adultery among you?' They replied, 'We do not find anything mentioned about it in our scripture.' Abdullah bin Salam said, 'You have lied regarding stoning in the Torah. Bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful.' So they brought the Torah, and he placed his hand on the verse of stoning and asked, 'What is this?' When they saw that, they said, 'It is the verse of stoning.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they be stoned near the site where funeral processions are placed near the mosque.' Abdullah said, 'I saw the man shielding the woman with his body from the stones.'\""],[2248,"ʿUmar said: Allah, may He be exalted, sent Muhammad ﷺ and sent down the Book to him. Among that which was revealed to him was the verse of stoning. We recited it and understood it. But I fear that with the passage of time, some people will say: We do not find the verse of stoning in the Book of Allah, and as a result an obligation that Allah revealed will be forsaken. Stoning is the due punishment in the Book of Allah for those who commit zina, both men and women, if they have been married and if proof is established, or there is a pregnancy or a confession. (Using translation from Aḥmad 276)"],[2250,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a woman from Banu Ghamid came to him and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have committed adultery, and I want you to purify me.\" He said to her, \"Go back.\" The next day she came to him again and confessed adultery to him. She said, \"O Prophet of Allah, purify me. Perhaps you will turn me away as you turned away Ma'iz b. Malik. By Allah, I am pregnant.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"Go back until you give birth.\" When she gave birth, she came with the child, carrying him in a cloth, and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have given birth to this.\" He said, \"Go and nurse him, then wean him.\" When she had weaned him, she came with the child, in his hand a piece of bread, and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have weaned him.\" The Prophet ﷺ ordered that the child be handed over to a man among the Muslims, and he ordered about her, and a pit was dug for her, and she was placed in it up to her chest. Then he ordered the people to stone her. Khalid b. al-Walid came forward with a stone and threw it at her head, and blood splattered onto Khalid b. al-Walid's cheek, and he cursed her. The Prophet ﷺ heard his cursing her and said, \"Gently, Khalid, do not curse her. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, she has repented such a repentance that if a tax collector repented like that, he would be forgiven.\" Then he ordered about her, and the funeral prayer was offered for her, and she was buried."],[2251,"A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ while pregnant from adultery and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a sin meriting a hadd, so carry it out on me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called her guardian and said, \"Go and treat her well, and when she gives birth, bring her to me.\" He did so, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that her clothes be fastened about her, then he ordered her to be stoned. Then he prayed over her. Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over her when she committed adultery?\" He said, \"She has repented such a repentance that if it were divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, it would suffice them. Have you found anything better than her giving her life for Allah ﷻ?\""],[2252,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a slave woman who commits adultery but is not married. He said, 'If she commits adultery, then flog her, and if she commits adultery again, then flog her.' He said, 'I do not know about the third or fourth time, sell her, even if it is for a lock of hair.'\""],[2253,"\"Take from me, take from me. Allah has made a way for them: the virgin with the virgin, and the previously married with the previously married. The virgin: one hundred lashes and exile for a year. The previously married: one hundred lashes and stoning.\""],[2254,"\"I will spend in it a year of medical treatment if it is permissible for him.\" If she made it permissible for him, he would receive one hundred lashes. And if she did not make it permissible for him, she would be stoned. Her husband was asked, and he said, \"Indeed, I have made it permissible for him.\" So he struck him one hundred times. Yahya said, \"He is elevated.\""],[2255,"Whoever has a prescribed punishment carried out upon him, that sin is forgiven for him."],[2256,"A woman vowed to perform Hajj and then died. Her brother came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"If she had a debt, would you pay it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then pay Allah, for Allah is more deserving of fulfillment.\""],[2257,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I made a vow in the pre-Islamic era, then Islam came.\" He said, \"Fulfill your vow.\""],[2258,"My sister vowed to perform Hajj for Allah walking and not covering her head. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Tell your sister to cover her head, ride, and fast three days.\""],[2259,"Uqbah's sister vowed to walk to the House. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah is surely free from need of your sister's vow. Let her ride and offer a sacrificial animal.\""],[2260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon an elderly man walking between his two sons. He said, \"What is the matter with this elderly man?\" His two sons said, \"He vowed to walk.\" He said, \"Ride, for Allah is free from need of you and of your vow.\""],[2261,"There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in what the son of Adam does not possess."],[2262,"Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."],[2263,"\"O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah grants you victory, I will pray in Jerusalem.\" He said, \"Pray here.\" He repeated it to him three times, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Then it is your affair.\""],[2264,"A vow does not repel anything; it only extracts from the miserly and stingy."],[2265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon Umar b. al-Khattab while he was traveling in a caravan and swearing by his father. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Whoever must swear, let him swear by Allah or remain silent.\""],[2266,"Whoever swears an oath and then says, 'If Allah wills,' has made an exception."],[2267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes an oath by a right hand and then says, 'If Allah wills,' then he is choosing the best way. And if He wills otherwise, then he will not do it.\""],[2268,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, “Do not swear.”"],[2269,"A man asked Adi b. Hatim? Then he swore that he would not give him anything. Then he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever swears an oath and then sees something else better than it, let him do that which is better and expiate for his oath.”"],[2270,"O Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, “Do not ask for authority, for if you are given it because of asking, you will be left to it, and if you are given it without asking, you will be helped with it. And when you swear an oath and then see something else better than it, expiate for your oath and do that which is better.”"],[2271,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My mother owes a slave, and I have a black Nubian slave girl. Will she suffice for her? He said, “Bring her.” Then he asked, “Do you testify that there is no god but Allah?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “Free her, for she is a believer.”"],[2272,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Your oath is only according to what your companion believes you to mean by it.”"],[2273,"The oath by which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to swear was, “No, by the Turner of the hearts.”"],[2274,"Whoever is afflicted by blood or injury—and injury is a wound—has the choice of one of three things. If he wants a fourth, then restrain his hands: either he retaliates, or he forgives, or he takes the blood money. If he takes any of that and then transgresses after that, then for him is the Fire, abiding therein eternally."],[2275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen, and in his letter was: “Whoever kills a believer deliberately with clear evidence, then it is retaliation by his hand, unless the heirs of the slain person agree otherwise.” Abu Muhammad said: “Iʿtabaṭa means he killed without cause.”"],[2276,"Abdullah was attacked and killed, and his neck was broken until it was dislocated, then he was thrown into one of the watering places of Khaybar. His companions were called for help and they took him out and buried him. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah. His brother Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl came forward—he had seniority with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—and his two cousins were with him, Huwayyisah b. Masʿud and Muhayyisah. Abd al-Rahman spoke, and he was the youngest of them in age, but he was the blood relative and had seniority among the people. When he spoke, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The elder, the elder.” So he stepped back, and Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah spoke, then he spoke. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Name your killer, then swear fifty oaths against him, and we will hand him over to you.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot swear about what we do not know; we do not know who killed him except that the Jews are our enemy and he was killed among them. He said, “Then they will swear to you by Allah that they are innocent of the blood of your companion, and then they will be free of it.” They said: We will not accept the oaths of the Jews, for there is nothing greater among them than to swear falsely. He said, “Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid his blood money from his own resources: one hundred camels.”"],[2277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen, and in his letter was: “A man may be killed for a woman.”"],[2278,"A slave girl had her head crushed between two stones. It was said to her: Who did this to you? Was it so-and-so? Was it so-and-so? Until the Jew was named. She nodded her head. He was sent for and brought, and he confessed. So the Prophet ﷺ ordered that his head be crushed between two stones."],[2279,"I said to 'Ali: O Commander of the Faithful, have you learned anything of revelation other than what is in the Book of Allah, the Exalted? He said: No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, I do not know it except an understanding that Allah gives a man in the Qur'an, and what is in the scroll. I said: And what is in the scroll? He said: The blood money, the ransoming of the captive, and a Muslim should not be killed for a polytheist."],[2280,"The prescribed punishments are not to be carried out in mosques, and a parent is not to be subjected to retaliation for killing his child."],[2281,"Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates him, we will mutilate him."],[2282,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when the killer was brought to him, being led in a leather strap. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the guardian of the slain: 'Do you pardon?' He said: No. He said: 'Then will you take the blood money?' He said: No. He said: 'Then will you kill him?' He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you pardon him, he will bear your sin and the sin of your companion.' He said: So he left him. He said: Then I saw him dragging his leather strap, having pardoned him."],[2283,"The major sins: associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and killing a soul. Shu'bah the doubter said: or the false oath."],[2284,"Cursing a believer is like killing him, and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be tormented with it on the Day of Resurrection."],[2285,"Whoever kills himself with an iron weapon, his iron weapon will be in his hand, thrusting it into his belly in the Fire of Hell, remaining therein forever. Whoever kills himself with poison, his poison will be in his hand, sipping it in the Fire of Hell, remaining therein forever. Whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself, he will be throwing himself in the Fire of Hell, remaining therein forever."],[2286,"A man killed a man during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ set his blood money at twelve thousand. That is His saying: {They swear by Allah that they did not say it, while they had certainly said the word of disbelief and disbelieved after their Islam and planned that which they were not to attain. And they were not resentful except because Allah and His Messenger had enriched them of His bounty.} [At-Tawbah: 74] because of their taking the blood money."],[2287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen: 'And upon the people of gold is one thousand dinars.'"],[2288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad the Prophet ﷺ to Shurahbil b. 'Abd Kulal, al-Harith b. 'Abd Kulal, and Nu'aym b. 'Abd Kulal, the chieftains of Dhu Ru'ayn, Ma'afir, and Hamdan. And in his letter was: 'For the life, the blood money is one hundred camels.'"],[2289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen, and in his letter was: 'For the nose, if it is completely cut off, the full blood money; for the tongue, the full blood money; for the two lips, the full blood money; for the two testicles, the full blood money; for the penis, the full blood money; for the backbone, the full blood money; for the two eyes, the full blood money; for one leg, half the blood money; for a head wound reaching the brain, one third of the blood money; for a wound reaching the interior of the body, one third of the blood money; and for a wound that exposes the bone, fifteen camels.'"],[2290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the blood money for accidental killing in fifths."],[2291,"A slave belonging to poor people cut off the hand of a boy belonging to wealthy people, so his family came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is for poor people?\" So the Prophet ﷺ did not impose anything on him."],[2292,"\"The fingers are equal.\" He said: I said, \"Ten, ten?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[2293,"\"This and this are equal,\" and he said, \"with his little finger and his thumb.\""],[2294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen: \"And for every finger of the fingers of the hand and the foot, ten camels.\""],[2295,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for wounds that expose bone: five, five camels.\""],[2296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen: \"And for every finger of the fingers of the hand and the foot, ten camels, and for the wound that exposes bone, five camels.\""],[2297,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for teeth: five, five camels.\""],[2298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen, \"And in the year, there are five types of camels.\""],[2299,"He pulled his hand away and his two fingers got dislocated, so they argued with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Will one of you bite his brother as a stallion bites?\" You have no compensation.\""],[2300,"\"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure, one-fifth is due.\""],[2301,"\"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure, one-fifth is due.\""],[2302,"\"The mine is without liability, and the grazing livestock is without liability, and the well is without liability, and on buried treasure, one-fifth is due.\""],[2303,"Two women were married to one man, and they became jealous, so one of them struck the other with a tent pole and killed her and what was in her belly. They brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled for the fetus a ghurrah (a slave, male or female) and made it the liability of the woman's 'aqilah (paternal relatives)."],[2304,"'Umar adjured the people about the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the fetus, whereupon Hamal b. Malik b. al-Nabighah stood up and said: \"I was between two wives of mine, and one of them struck the other with a tent pole, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for her fetus a ghurrah and that she be killed for it.\""],[2305,"Messenger of Allah, why should I play blood-wit for one who neither drank, nor ate, nor spoke, nor made any noise; it is like a nonentity (it is, therefore, not justifiable to demand blood-wit for it). Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He seems to be one of the brothers of soothsavers on account of the rhymed speech which he has composed. (Using translation from Muslim 1681c)"],[2306,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The diyya for one killed by mistake, semi-intentional, and what is done with a whip or stick — among them are forty in whose bellies are their young.”"],[2307,"If I were to know that you had been peeping through the door, I would have thrust that into your eyes, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Permission is needed as a protection against glance. (Using translation from Muslim 2156a)"],[2308,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a room, and with him was a comb with which he was scratching his head, a man looked in upon him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “If I knew that you were looking, I would have thrust it into your eyes. Permission was made only for the sake of looking.”"],[2309,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day Makkah was conquered: “No Quraishi shall be killed patiently after this day until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2310,"I came to Madinah with a son of mine, and we had not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I went to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out wearing two green garments. When I saw him, I recognized him by the description. I went up to him, and he said: “Who is this with you?” I said: “My son, by the Lord of the Ka‘bah.” He said: “Your son?” I said: “I testify to it.” He said: “Indeed this son of yours will not commit a crime against you, nor will you commit a crime against him.”"],[2311,"I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to my father: “Is this your son?” He said: “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘bah.” He said: “Truly?” He said: “Truly, I testify to it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing at how strong my resemblance to my father was, and at my father’s oath about me. Then he said: “Indeed this son of yours will not commit a crime against you, nor will you commit a crime against him.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.”"],[2312,"A group of us from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and discussed, saying: “If only we knew which deeds are most beloved to Allah, the Exalted, we would do them.” Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed: “Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth exalts Allah, and He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise. O you who have believed, why do you say what you do not do? Great is hatred…” [al-Saff: 2], until He completed it. Abdullah said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to us until he completed it.” Abu Salamah said: “Ibn Salam recited it to us.” Yahya said: “Abu Salamah recited it to us, and Yahya recited it to us, and al-Awza‘i recited it to us, and Muhammad recited it to us.”"],[2313,"“Allah has guaranteed for the one who goes out from his house, nothing driving him out except jihad in the path of Allah and belief in His words, that He will admit him to Paradise or return him to his dwelling from which he went out, along with whatever he attained of reward or spoils.”"],[2314,"It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best?” He said: “The one whose horse is hamstrung and his blood is spilled.”"],[2315,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, \"Which is the best deed?\" He said, \"To believe in Allah and His Apostle.\" He was then asked, \"Which is the next (in goodness)?\" He said, \"To participate in Jihad in Allah's Cause.\" He was then asked, \"Which is the next?\" He said, \"To perform Hajj-Mabrur. \" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1519)"],[2316,"“Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a camel, Paradise is guaranteed for him — and that is the amount of time it takes for her milk to flow for the one who milks her.”"],[2317,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to them while they were sitting and said: “Shall I tell you about the best of people in rank?” We said: “Yes.” He said: “A man holding the head of his horse — or he said: a horse — in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed.” Then he said: “Shall I tell you about the one who comes after him?” We said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “A man withdrawing into a mountain pass, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and keeping away from people’s evils.” Then he said: “Shall I tell you about the worst of people in rank?” We said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The one who is asked by Allah, the Almighty, and does not give by Him.”"],[2318,"“A man’s standing in the ranks in the path of Allah is better than a man’s worship for sixty years.”"],[2319,"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever's two feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Allah forbids him to the Fire.”"],[2320,"“A morning's journey in the path of Allah or an evening's journey in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains.”"],[2321,"“There is no servant who fasts a day in the path of Allah, seeking the face of Allah, except that Allah distances between his face and the Fire by seventy autumns.”"],[2322,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and one night he heard him saying: “The Fire is forbidden to an eye that stayed awake in the path of Allah, and the Fire is forbidden to an eye that wept from fear of Allah.” He said: And he said the third, but I forgot it."],[2324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “For it on the Day of Resurrection you will have seven hundred she-camels, all of them bridled.”"],[2325,"I met Abu Dharr while he was driving a camel of his, or leading it, with a water-skin on his neck. I said, “O Abu Dharr, what is wrong with you?” He said, “My work is with me.” I said, “What is wrong with you?” He said, “My work is with me.” I said, “Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There is no Muslim who spends a pair from his wealth in the path of Allah except that the gatekeepers of Paradise rush to meet him.’” Abu Muhammad said: “It means two dirhams, or two slave women, or two slaves, or two riding animals.”"],[2326,"That he recited this verse: {And prepare against them whatever you are able of power} [Al-Anfal 60]. “Verily, power is archery.”"],[2327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ admits three people to Paradise by a single arrow: its maker, who seeks reward in making it for good; the one who hands it to the archer; and the one who shoots it.”"],[2331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no wounded person who is wounded in the path of Allah ﷻ except that Allah ﷻ will raise him on the Day of Resurrection while his wound bleeds, its scent the scent of musk and its color the color of blood.”"],[2332,"“Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from his heart, Allah will cause him to reach the stations of the martyrs, even if he dies on his bed.”"],[2333,"“The martyr finds no pain from being killed except as one of you finds from the pain of a pinch.”"],[2334,"“There is no soul that dies and enters Paradise and wishes that it returned to you, even if it had the world and what it contains, except the martyr; for he wishes that he were killed again and again, because of what he has seen of the reward.”"],[2335,"\"Regarding the souls of the martyrs, if it were not for Abdullah, no one would have informed us. He said that the souls of the martyrs are with Allah on the Day of Judgment in the bodies of green birds, with lanterns hanging from the throne, freely roaming in the gardens of paradise as they please. Then they return to their lanterns, and their Lord honors them and asks, 'Do you have any need? Is there anything you desire?' They respond, 'No, except that we want to return to the world and be killed again.'\""],[2336,"The slain are three: a believer who strove with his self and his wealth in the path of Allah; when he met the enemy he fought until he was killed. The Prophet ﷺ said concerning him: 'That is the tested martyr in the tent of Allah beneath His Throne, none surpassing him except the prophets by the degree of prophethood. And a believer who mixed a righteous deed with another evil one, who strove with his self and his wealth in the path of Allah; when he met the enemy he fought until he was killed.' The Prophet ﷺ said concerning him: 'A cleansing purifier that wiped away his sins and his errors; indeed the sword is an eraser of errors, and he will be admitted to Paradise from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes. And a hypocrite who strove with his self and his wealth; when he met the enemy he fought until he was killed, then that one is in the Fire; indeed the sword does not erase hypocrisy.'\""],[2337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and gave a sermon, praised Allah and extolled Him, then mentioned jihad and did not leave anything more virtuous than it except the obligatory duties. A man stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of one who is killed in the path of Allah—does that expiate his sins?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes, if he is killed patiently, expectant of reward, advancing and not retreating—except for debt, for he will be taken to account for it, as Jibril ﷺ asserted to me.'\""],[2338,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'The plague is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, military expedition is martyrdom, and the belly and the woman in childbirth.'\""],[2339,"'Being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, the plague is martyrdom, the belly is martyrdom, and the woman whose child kills her in a full pregnancy is martyrdom.'\""],[2340,"'We used to raid with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ having no food except this samur and the leaves of the hubala, until one of us would defecate as a sheep does, with no mixture. Then the Banu Asad came to reprimand me; I would then have failed and my deed gone astray.'\""],[2341,"'Whoever raids in the path of Allah intending in his raid nothing but a hobbling camel rope, then he will have what he intended.'\""],[2342,"'Raiding is of two kinds: as for one who raids seeking the face of Allah, obeys the leader, spends his precious possessions, is easy with his partner, and avoids corruption, then his sleep and his wakefulness are all reward. As for one who raids for pride, showing off, reputation, disobeys the leader, and corrupts in the land, then he will not return with even enough.'\""],[2343,"'Whoever does not raid or equip a raider or look after a raider's family with good, Allah will strike him with a calamity before the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[2344,"'Whoever equips a raider in the path of Allah or looks after his family, Allah will write for him the like of his reward, except that it does not diminish anything from the reward of the raider.'\""],[2345,"I heard al-Bara' saying: When this verse was revealed—{Not equal are those who sit among the believers} [al-Nisa' 95]—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Zayd, and he brought a shoulder blade, and he wrote it. Ibn Umm Maktum complained of his disability, so it was revealed: {Not equal are those who sit among the believers, other than those with a handicap} [al-Nisa' 95].\""],[2346,"The Prophet ﷺ was in her house one day and woke up laughing. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what makes you laugh?' He said: 'I was shown a people of my community riding the surface of this sea like kings on thrones.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.' He said: 'You are one of them.' Then he slept again and woke up laughing. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what makes you laugh?' He said: 'I was shown a people of my community riding the surface of this sea like kings on thrones.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.' He said: 'You are one of them.' Then he slept again and woke up laughing. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what makes you laugh?' He said: 'I was shown a people of my community riding this sea like kings on thrones.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.' He said: 'You are one of the first ones.' He said: Then 'Ubadah b. al-Samit married her, and he raided in the sea and carried her with him. When they arrived, a mule was brought near for her to ride, and it threw her, and her neck was broken, and she died.\""],[2347,"'I raided with the Prophet ﷺ in seven raids, treating the wounded or the injured, making food for them, and looking after their baggage.'\""],[2348,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, he drew lots among his wives, and the lot fell upon Aisha and Hafsa, so they both went out with him."],[2349,"I heard Uthman on the pulpit saying: I had concealed from you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, disliking that you disperse from me. Then it occurred to me to narrate it to you so that each person may choose for himself what seems best to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A day of ribat in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days elsewhere.”"],[2350,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Every deceased person is sealed upon his actions, except for the one who is stationed in the path of Allah, for his actions continue to be recorded for him until he is resurrected.\""],[2351,"Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection—reward and booty."],[2352,"Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection—reward and booty."],[2353,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to buy a horse; which one should I buy? He said: “Buy a dark bay with a white spot on its upper lip, white stockings, and a white right foreleg, or a chestnut with the same markings; you will gain booty and be safe.”"],[2354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to race the trained horses from al-Hafya' to the gorge, and the untrained ones from the gorge to the mosque of Banu Zurayq. Ibn Umar was among those who raced them."],[2355,"Horses were raced in the time of al-Hajjaj, and al-Hakam b. Ayyub was over Basra. We came to the race, and when the horses arrived, we said: Let us go to Anas b. Malik and ask him whether they used to bet on races during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We came to him in his palace in the corner and asked him, saying: O Abu Hamza, did you bet on races during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bet? He said: “Yes, by Allah, he bet on a horse of his called Subha; it outpaced the people, and he was delighted and pleased by that.”"],[2356,"Strive against the polytheists with your wealth, your lives, and your tongues."],[2357,"A group of my nation will remain dominant over the people until the command of Allah comes, while they are dominant."],[2358,"People of my nation will remain dominant upon the truth."],[2359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “After me, there will be a people from my nation who recite the Quran but it will not go beyond their throats. They will go out of the religion as an arrow goes out of the game, then they will not return to it. They are the worst of creation and creatures.” Sulayman said: Humayd said: Abdullah b. al-Samit said: I met Rafi', the brother of al-Hakam b. Amr al-Ghifari, and narrated this hadith to him. Rafi' said: I also heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2360,"“O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition, he would send it at the beginning of the day. He said: This man was a merchant, and he used to send his servants at the beginning of the day, and his wealth increased."],[2361,"It was seldom that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would set out when he intended a journey except on Thursday."],[2362,"The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best of neighbors in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."],[2363,"The best of companions are four, the best of armies are four thousand, and the best of raiding parties are four hundred. And any [force] that reaches twelve thousand, and they are patient and sincere, they will not be defeated due to small numbers."],[2364,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man over a raiding party, he would advise him concerning his own self to fear Allah and to treat well those Muslims with him. And he said: \"Raid in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah. Fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Raid, but do not act treacherously, do not steal from the spoils, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child.\""],[2365,"Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being. But if you meet them, then be steadfast and remember Allah much. And if they shout and make a clamor, then you must keep silent."],[2366,"He used to supplicate during the days of Hunayn: \"O Allah, by You I attack, by You I defend, and by You I fight.\""],[2367,"Muslim b. Haysam narrated to me from al-Nu'man b. Muqarrin from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[2368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fight any people until he called them."],[2369,"He used to raid at the time of the dawn prayer, and he would listen. If he heard the call to prayer, he would refrain; if he did not hear the call to prayer, he would raid."],[2370,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the delegation of Thaqif. He said: I was at the bottom of the tent, and there was no one in it except the Prophet ﷺ sleeping, when a man came to him and whispered to him. He said: \"Go and kill him.\" Then he said: \"Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah?\" Shu'bah said: \"And I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but Allah.' If they say it, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me except for its due.\""],[2371,"The blood of a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah is not lawful except for one of three persons: a life for a life, a previously married adulterer, and one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."],[2372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out the army of the commanders. He said: They set out and remained as long as Allah willed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and gave the order, and it was called out: \"The prayer is to be gathered.\""],[2373,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The advisor is trustworthy.\""],[2374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he intended a military expedition, would give the impression of a different destination."],[2375,"I fought a man in single combat and killed him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me his spoils as an extra share. Our slogan with Khalid b. al-Walid was \"Amit,\" meaning \"Kill.\""],[2376,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of Hunayn on a scorching, intensely hot day. We dismounted beneath the shade of the trees. He mentioned the story, then he took a handful of dust. He said: The one who was closer to him than I was told me that he threw it in their faces and said: \"May the faces be disfigured!\" So Allah routed the polytheists. Ya'la said: Their sons told me that their fathers said: Not one of us remained but his eyes and mouth were filled with dust."],[2377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us while we were with him in a gathering: \"Pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill your children, and do not bring a slander that you fabricate between your hands and feet. Whoever among you fulfills, his reward is with Allah. Whoever commits any of that and Allah conceals him, his affair is with Allah: if He wills, He punishes him, and if He wills, He forgives him. And whoever commits something and is punished for it in this world, it is an expiation for him.\" He said: So we pledged allegiance to him on that."],[2378,"On the day of al-Hudaybiyah we were one thousand four hundred, and we pledged allegiance to him while Umar was holding his hand beneath the tree, which was a samurah tree. He said: \"We pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee, and we did not pledge allegiance to him upon death.\""],[2379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was carrying earth with us on the day of the Confederates, and the earth had covered the whiteness of his armpits, while he was saying: \"O Allah, had it not been for You, we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. So send down tranquility upon us and make our feet firm when we meet. The forebears have transgressed against us, and if they desire tribulation, we refuse.\" And he raised his voice with it."],[2380,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah in the year of the conquest with a helmet on his head. When he took it off, a man came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this is Ibn Khatal clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Kill him.\""],[2381,"The pommel of the Prophet's ﷺ sword was made of silver."],[2382,"When he appeared before a people, he liked to stay in their open space for three days."],[2383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ burned the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir."],[2384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military detachment and said: \"If you capture so-and-so and so-and-so, burn them with fire.\" Then when the next day came, he sent to us and said: \"I had ordered you to burn these two men, but then I considered that it is not appropriate for anyone to punish with fire except Allah. So if you capture them, kill them.\""],[2385,"‘Abd Allaah bin (mas’ud) said “A woman was found slain in one of the battles of the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ. The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ forbade to kill women and children. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2668)"],[2386,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a raid, and we defeated the polytheists. The people hastened in killing until they killed the offspring. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"What is the matter with people whom killing has carried away until they killed the offspring? Indeed, offspring must never be killed,\" three times."],[2387,"\"We were presented to the Prophet ﷺ on that day. Whoever had pubic hair was killed, and whoever had not was left. I was among those who had not pubic hair, so they did not kill me.\""],[2388,"\"Free the captive and feed the hungry.\""],[2389,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ransomed one man for two men."],[2390,"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black; the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification; spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me; I was aided with terror for a month, the enemy being terrified of me from a month's journey; and it was said to me, 'Ask and you will be given,' so I reserved my supplication as intercession for my community, and it will reach whoever of you, God willing, did not associate anything with Allah."],[2391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided the spoils of Hunayn at al-Ji'ranah."],[2392,"From the Prophet ﷺ something similar. He said: \"So I was joined to them.\" Abu Muhammad said: The correct view according to me is what Zakariyya said regarding the chain."],[2393,"Najdah of Banu 'Amir wrote to Ibn 'Abbas asking him about some matters. He wrote to him: You asked about the share of the near relatives whom Allah mentioned. We used to think that the relatives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were them, but our people refused that to us."],[2394,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted on the day of Khaybar to the horseman three shares and to the foot soldier one share.\""],[2395,"\"I did not witness any booty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he allotted me a share, except on the day of Khaybar, for it was exclusively for the people of al-Hudaybiyyah. Abu Musa and Abu Hurayrah had come between al-Hudaybiyyah and Khaybar.\""],[2396,"I attended Khaybar while I was an owned slave, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me from the odds and ends of the baggage and gave me a sword, saying, “Gird yourself with this.”"],[2397,"He forbade that shares be sold until they are distributed."],[2398,"We raided the Maghrib under the command of Ruwayfiʿ b. Thābit al-Anṣārī, and we conquered a village called Jarbah. Ruwayfiʿ b. Thābit al-Anṣārī stood among us as a preacher and said: I do not stand among you except with what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he stood among us on the day of Khaybar when we conquered it. He said, “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not approach any of the captives until he has sought to make sure she is not pregnant.”"],[2399,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a woman who was pregnant—meaning with child—at the entrance of a tent, and he said, “Perhaps he has had intercourse with her?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “I was about to curse him with a curse that would enter his grave with him. How can he make him an heir while he is not permissible for him, and how can he employ him while he is not permissible for him?”"],[2400,"Abū Ayyūb was in an army, and the children were separated from their mothers. He saw them weeping and began returning each child to its mother, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever separates a mother and her child, Allah will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2401,"I took the paternal aunt of al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah and brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ asked about his aunt, and he said, “O Ṣakhr, when people accept Islam, they secure their wealth and their blood, so hand her over to him.” And there was a water source belonging to Banū Sulaym. They accepted Islam and came to him asking for it, so he called me and said, “O Ṣakhr, when people accept Islam, they secure their wealth and their blood, so hand it over to them.” So I handed it over."],[2402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party which included Ibn ʿUmar. They captured many camels, and their shares were twelve camels or eleven camels, and they were given an extra camel each."],[2403,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided in enemy territory, he would give a quarter as extra share, and when he returned and the people were weary, he would give a third as extra share."],[2404,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a third as extra share after the fifth."],[2405,"“Whoever kills an unbeliever, his belongings are his.” On that day Abū Ṭalḥah killed twenty and took their belongings."],[2406,"I fought a man in single combat and killed him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me his belongings as extra share."],[2407,"He used to dislike extra shares and say, “Let the strong among the Muslims return them to their weak.”"],[2408,"«Pay the tailor and the seamstress, and beware of stealing from the spoils, for it is a disgrace upon its people on the Day of Resurrection.»"],[2409,"We raided the Maghrib, and Ruwayfi' b. Thabit al-Ansari was over us. We conquered a village called Jarbah. Ruwayfi' b. Thabit al-Ansari stood among us as a speaker and said: I do not stand among you except with what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood among us on the day of Khaybar when we conquered it: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not ride any riding animal from the spoils of the Muslims until, when he has exhausted it — or he said, made it lean — Abu Muhammad said: I doubt it — he returns it. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear a garment from the spoils of the Muslims until, when he has worn it out, he returns it."],[2410,"Some people were killed on the day of Khaybar, and they said: So-and-so is a martyr, until they mentioned a man and said: So-and-so is a martyr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «No, indeed I saw him in the Fire, in an 'aba'ah or a burdah that he had stolen from the spoils.» Then he said to me: O Ibn al-Khattab, stand and call out among the people that none will enter Paradise except the believers. So I stood and called out among the people."],[2412,"No plundering, no stealing from the spoils, and no treachery. {And whoever steals from the spoils will bring what he stole on the Day of Resurrection.}"],[2413,"«Hands are not cut off during a military expedition.» I would cut them off."],[2414,"He informed him that the Prophet ﷺ appointed a worker over the sadaqah. The worker came to him when he finished his work and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is what belongs to you, and this was gifted to me. The Prophet ﷺ said: «Why did you not sit in the house of your father and mother, and see whether you would be given a gift or not?» Then the Prophet ﷺ stood in the evening after the prayer on the pulpit, pronounced the tashahhud, praised Allah and extolled Him with what He is worthy of, then said: To proceed: What is the matter with the worker whom we appoint, then he comes to us and says: This is from your work, and this was gifted to me? Why did he not sit in the house of his father and mother, and see whether he would be given a gift or not? By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, none of you will steal anything from it except that he will bring it on the Day of Resurrection, carrying it on his neck. If it is a camel, he will bring it bellowing; if it is a cow, he will bring it mooing; if it is a sheep, he will bring it bleating. I have conveyed. Abu Humayd said: Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hands until we could see the whiteness of his armpits. Abu Humayd said: Zayd b. Thabit heard that with me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so ask him."],[2415,"The king of Dhu Yazan gifted the Prophet ﷺ a hullah which he had acquired for thirty-three camels or thirty-three she-camels, and he accepted it."],[2416,"«The ruler of Aylah sent a letter to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and gifted him a white mule. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to him and gifted him a burdah.»"],[2417,"«Indeed, we do not seek help from a polytheist.»"],[2418,"Among the last things the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke, he said: «Expel the Jews from the Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula.»"],[2419,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book, and we eat in their vessels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «If you are in a land as you mentioned, then do not eat in their vessels unless you find no alternative. If you find no alternative, then wash them and then eat in them.»"],[2420,"A leather bag of fat was lowered on the day of Khaybar. He said: I went to it and clung to it. He said: Then I said, “I will not give anyone anything from this today.” Then I turned around, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiling at me. Abdullah said: “I hope that Humayd heard it from Abdullah.”"],[2421,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it from the Magi of Hijar.\""],[2422,"She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the conquest and said, “O Messenger of Allah, my cousin claims that he will kill a man I have granted protection to, Fulan b. Hubayrah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “We grant protection to the one you have protected, O Umm Hani’.”"],[2423,"I went out early in the morning to exercise a horse of mine, and I passed by a mosque among the mosques of the Banu Hanifah and heard them testifying that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah. I returned to Abdullah b. Mas'ud and informed him. He sent the police to them, and they seized them and brought them to him. The people repented and retracted their statement, so he released them. He brought forward a man from among them called Abdullah b. al-Nuwahah and struck his neck. They said to him, “You released the people and killed this one?” He said, “I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when this man and another entered as two delegates from Musaylimah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, ‘Do you both testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?’ They said to him, ‘We testify that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah.’ He said, ‘I believe in Allah and His messengers. If I were to kill a delegate, I would have killed you both.’ So for that reason I killed him.” And he ordered their mosque to be demolished, so it was torn down."],[2424,"“Whoever kills a person under treaty not in its due manner, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[2425,"Al-Adba' belonged to a man from Banu 'Uqayl. He was taken captive and al-Adba' was seized. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while he was in bonds. He said, “O Muhammad, why do you take me and take the foremost of the pilgrims' camels, when I have become Muslim?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If you had said it while you were in control of your affairs, you would have attained every success.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “We take you because of the crime of your allies.” Thaqif had captured two men from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came on a donkey with a velvet cloth over it. He said, “O Muhammad, I am hungry, so feed me, and thirsty, so give me water.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This is your need.” Then the man was ransomed for two men, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept al-Adba' for his saddle, and it was one of the foremost camels of the pilgrims. Then the polytheists raided the grazing livestock of Madinah and took it, including al-Adba', and they captured a Muslim woman. When they camped, Abu Muhammad said—then he mentioned a word—their camels were in their courtyards. One night, the woman got up while they were asleep, and she would not place her hands on any camel except that it grumbled, until she came to al-Adba'. She came to a docile, belled she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mounted it, then headed toward Madinah. She vowed that if Allah saved her, she would surely slaughter it. When she arrived, the camel was recognized, and it was said, “The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” They brought her to the Prophet ﷺ, and the woman told him of her vow. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What a bad reward you have given it—or what a bad reward it has received—if Allah saved her, she would surely slaughter it. There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in what a son of Adam does not own.”"],[2426,"I was with Ali b. Abi Talib when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him, and he proclaimed four things until his voice became hoarse: “Indeed, none will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul. No polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year, and no one shall circumambulate the House naked. And whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, its term is four months. When the four months have passed, Allah is free from the polytheists, and so is His Messenger.”"],[2427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'Umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah, but the people of Makkah refused to let him enter Makkah until he made a treaty with them that he would stay for three days. When they wrote, “This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, has agreed upon,” they said, “We do not acknowledge this. If we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would not have prevented you from anything. But you are Muhammad b. Abdullah.” He said, “I am the Messenger of Allah and I am Muhammad b. Abdullah.” He said to Ali, “Erase ‘Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah.’” Ali said, “No, by Allah, I will never erase it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the document, and he did not know how to write, so he wrote in place of “Messenger of Allah”: “This is what Muhammad b. Abdullah has agreed upon: that he will not enter Makkah with weapons except the sword in its sheath, and that he will not take out any of its people who wishes to follow him, nor prevent any of his companions who wishes to remain there.” When he entered it and the term expired, they came to Ali and said, “Tell your companion to leave us, for the term has expired.”"],[2428,"“Two slaves from al-Ta'if came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he freed them; one of them was Abu Bakrah.”"],[2429,"On the day of the Confederates, Sa'd b. Mu'adh was shot and they severed his vein. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized it with fire, and his hand swelled, so he bled it. He cauterized it again, and his hand swelled. When he saw that, he said, “O Allah, do not take my soul until my eye is cooled by the Banu Qurayzah.” His vein held, and not a drop fell until they surrendered to the judgment of Sa'd. He sent for him, and he ruled that their men be killed and their women and children be spared so that the Muslims might benefit from them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You have hit upon Allah's judgment regarding them.” They were four hundred. When their killing was finished, his vein burst open and he died."],[2430,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing on his mount at al-Hazwarah, saying, “By Allah, you are the best land of Allah and the most beloved land of Allah to Allah. Were it not that I was expelled from you, I would not have left.”"],[2431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not revile the dead, for they have reached what they sent ahead.”"],[2432,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no emigration after the conquest, but there is jihad and intention. And when you are called to mobilize, then mobilize.”"],[2433,"They discussed migration in the presence of Mu'awiyah while he was on his couch, so he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Migration will not cease until repentance ceases,” three times, “and repentance will not cease until the sun rises from its west.”"],[2434,"“Were it not for migration, I would have been a man of the Ansar.”"],[2435,"“There is no commander of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hands bound to his neck; the truth will release him or destroy him.”"],[2436,"“Beware of injustice, for injustice will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2437,"“Indeed, Allah supports this religion with the wicked man.”"],[2438,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and said, 'Indeed, those who came before you from the people of the Scripture divided into seventy-two sects. And indeed, this nation will divide into seventy-three sects, seventy-two of them in the Hellfire and one in Paradise.' Abdullah said, 'Al-Haraz is a tribe from the people of Yemen.'\""],[2439,"“Whoever sees something he dislikes from his commander should be patient, for there is no one who separates from the community by a handspan and then dies except that he dies a death of ignorance.”"],[2440,"“Whoever draws a weapon against us is not one of us.”"],[2441,"“Indeed, this affair is in Quraysh; no one opposes them except that Allah will cast him down on his face, as long as they uphold the religion.”"],[2442,"“Quraysh, the Ansar, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Aslam, Ghifar, and Ashja' have no patron besides Allah and His Messenger.”"],[2443,"“Do you think that if Aslam and Ghifar were better than the two allies, Asad and Ghatafan, would you consider them to have lost?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, they are better than them.\" He said, \"Do you think that if Muzaynah and Juhaynah were better than Tamim and 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah,\" and he extended his voice with it, \"would you consider them to have lost?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, they are better than them.\""],[2444,"“Ghifar, may Allah forgive her, and Aslam, may Allah grant her peace.”"],[2445,"“Ghifar, may Allah forgive her, and Aslam, may Allah grant her peace, and 'Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.”"],[2446,"«There is no confederation in Islam, and any confederation from the pre-Islamic era is only increased in strength and freshness by Islam.»"],[2447,"I said to Muʿāwiyah b. Qurrah, “Did Anas mention that the Prophet ﷺ said to al-Nuʿmān b. Muqarrin, ‘The son of a people’s sister is one of them?’” He said, “Yes.”"],[2448,"«The client of a people is one of them, the confederate of a people is one of them, and the son of a people’s sister is one of them.»"],[2449,"I was under the camel of the Prophet ﷺ, and I heard him say, «Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or affiliates himself with other than his patrons out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory deed will be accepted from him.»"],[2450,"«Whoever claims descent from other than his father, while he knows that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him.»"],[2451,"«The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are ambiguous matters that many people do not know. Whoever guards against the ambiguous matters has kept his honor and religion clear. Whoever falls into the ambiguous matters falls into the unlawful, like a shepherd grazing around a sanctuary, soon to trespass into it. Indeed, every king has a sanctuary, and Allah’s sanctuary is His prohibitions. Indeed, in the body there is a lump of flesh; when it is sound, the whole body is sound, and when it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt. Indeed, it is the heart.»"],[2452,"I said to al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī, “What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “A man asked him about a matter, and I do not know what it was. He said, ‘Leave what unsettles you for what does not unsettle you.’”"],[2453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Wābiṣah, “Have you come to ask about righteousness and sin?” He said, “I said, ‘Yes.’” He said, “Then he gathered his fingers and struck his chest with them, and said, ‘Consult your heart, consult yourself, O Wābiṣah’ — three times — ‘Righteousness is what the soul is at ease with and the heart is at ease with. Sin is what chafes in the soul and wavers in the chest, even if people give you a ruling and they give you a ruling again.’”"],[2454,"I was holding the rein of the camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the middle of the days of Tashrīq, driving the people away from him. He said, «Indeed, every ribā from the pre-Islamic era is abolished. Indeed, Allah has decreed that the first ribā to be abolished is the ribā of ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib. Yours is your principal capital; you shall not wrong nor be wronged.»"],[2455,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the consumer of ribā and the one who feeds it to others.»"],[2456,"«A time will surely come when a man will not care whether he takes wealth lawfully or unlawfully.»"],[2457,"«The most rightful thing a man eats is from his good earnings, and his child is from his good earnings.»"],[2458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to al-Baqi' and said, “O assembly of merchants!” until they craned their necks. He said, “Merchants will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection as wicked sinners, except those who fear Allah, act righteously, and speak truthfully.”"],[2459,"“The truthful, trustworthy merchant will be with the prophets, the steadfast affirmers of truth, and the martyrs.”"],[2460,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakat, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"],[2461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some food in the market of Madinah and was pleased by its appearance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ inserted his hand into its interior and brought out something unlike the exterior. He expressed disapproval to the owner of the food, then said, “There is no fraud between Muslims. Whoever defrauds us is not of us.”"],[2462,"“Every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so.”"],[2463,"“No one monopolizes except a sinner,” twice."],[2464,"“The importer is provided for, and the monopolizer is cursed.”"],[2465,"Prices rose during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, so the people said, “O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen, so set prices for us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed Allah is the Creator, the Withholder, the Expander, the Provider, the Setter of prices. I hope to meet my Lord with none of you seeking recompense from me for an injustice I committed against him in blood or property.”"],[2466,"The angels received the soul of a man from among those before you. They said, “Did you do any good?” He said, “No.” They said, “Remember.” He said, “I used to lend to people and would order my young men to give respite to the one in difficulty and to overlook the one who was well-off.” He said, “Allah said: Overlook him.”"],[2467,"“The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they do not separate. If they are truthful and make things clear, they will be blessed in their sale. If they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale will be effaced.”"],[2468,"“If the two parties to a sale disagree while the object of sale is still present and there is no evidence between them, then the statement to be accepted is what the seller says, or they may return the sale.”"],[2469,"It is not lawful for a person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to sell against the sale of his brother until he leaves it."],[2470,"The guarantee for slaves is three days."],[2471,"The guarantee for slaves is three days."],[2472,"Whoever buys a sheep or milch animal that has been left unmilked for a while, he has the option for three days. If he returns it, he must return with it a sa' of food, not wheat."],[2473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of fraud (gharar)."],[2474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fruits until their ripeness appears. He forbade both the seller and the buyer."],[2475,"Whoever buys fruit and a calamity strikes it, he must not take anything from him. How can you take your brother's wealth without right?"],[2476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muhāqalah and muzābanah."],[2477,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of 'arāyā for dried dates and fresh dates, and did not permit anything else."],[2478,"Whoever buys food, he must not sell it until he takes possession of it."],[2479,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a loan and a sale, and two conditions in a sale, and profit on what is not guaranteed."],[2480,"Whoever buys a slave and does not stipulate his wealth, he gets nothing."],[2481,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two sales and two ways of dress: the sale of munabadhah and mulamasah."],[2482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of uncertainty and the sale of pebbles."],[2483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."],[2484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ borrowed a young camel. Then camels from the zakat camels came. Abu Rafi' said: He ordered me to repay the man his young camel. I said: I found among the camels only a fine four-year-old camel. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Give it to him, for the best of people are those who are best in repayment."],[2485,"Do not go out to meet the caravans. Whoever meets them and buys something from them, then when he enters the market, he has the option."],[2486,"None of you should sell against the sale of another. And do not go out to meet the goods until they are brought down to the markets. And do not bid against each other to raise the price."],[2487,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the payment of a soothsayer."],[2488,"When the verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah concerning usury were revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and recited them to the people, then he forbade trading in wine."],[2489,"When the verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah were revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and recited them to the people, then he forbade trading in wine."],[2490,"I asked Ibn Abbas about the skins of animals that die naturally. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Its tanning is its purification."],[2492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling loyalty and giving it as a gift."],[2493,"A man among us freed a slave of his after his death. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for him and sold him. Jabir said: He only died the previous year."],[2494,"When a man's slave woman gives birth to a child from him, she becomes free upon his death or after him."],[2495,"O Allah, bless them in their measuring vessel and bless them in their sa' and their mudd."],[2496,"I had a mudd of dates belonging to the Prophet ﷺ, and I found something better than it, a sa' for two sa's, so I bought it and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"Where did you get this, O Bilal?\" I said, \"I bought a sa' for two sa'.\" He said, \"Return it and give us back our dates.\""],[2497,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the brother of Banu 'Adiyy al-Ansari and appointed him over Khaybar. He came with fine dates. Ibn Maslamah said, meaning good ones. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Is all the dates of Khaybar like this?\" He said, \"No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we buy a sa' for two sa' of the mixed dates.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not do that; rather like for like, or sell this and buy with its price from this, and likewise the scale.\""],[2498,"Gold for gold, hand to hand; silver for silver, hand to hand; dates for dates, hand to hand; wheat for wheat, hand to hand; barley for barley, hand to hand; and there is no excess between them."],[2499,"Some people during the rule of Mu'awiyah stood up selling vessels of gold and silver for a deferred payment. 'Ubadah b. al-Samit stood up and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, dates for dates, barley for barley, and salt for salt, except like for like, equal for equal. Whoever increases or asks for an increase has engaged in riba.\""],[2500,"Riba is only in debt."],[2501,"I used to sell camels at al-Baqi', selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars—or perhaps he said, I receive—so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, wait a moment, let me ask you: I sell camels at al-Baqi', selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars.\" He said, \"There is no harm in taking at the rate of your day as long as you do not part while there is something between you.\""],[2502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while his shield was pawned with a Jewish man for thirty sa' of barley."],[2503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while they were lending in fruits for two and three years. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Lend in fruits with a known measure and a known weight.\""],[2504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ weighed dirhams for him and made them heavier."],[2505,"Makhramah al-'Abdi and I brought cloth from al-Bahrayn to Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us walking and bargained with us for a pair of trousers, or bought a pair of trousers from us. There was a weigher weighing for a fee, so he said to the weigher, \"Weigh and give more.\" When he left walking, they said, \"This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2506,"\"Delay (in payment) by a rich man is injustice, and if one of you is referred for payment to a wealthy man, let him accept the transfer.\""],[2507,"He demanded repayment of a debt owed to him by Ibn Abi Hadrad in the mosque, and their voices rose until the Prophet ﷺ heard them while he was in his house. He came out to them and called, \"O Ka'b!\" He said, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Reduce your debt,\" and he gestured to him, meaning by half. He said, \"I have done so.\" He said, \"Stand and settle it.\""],[2508,"\"Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or waives it for him, Allah will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade.\" He said: Then he spat on his document and said, \"Go, for it is yours,\" to his debtor, and he mentioned that he was in difficulty."],[2509,"\"Whoever relieves his debtor or cancels it for him will be in the shade of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2510,"\"Whoever finds his exact property with a person who has become bankrupt, or with a man who has become bankrupt, he is more entitled to it than others.\""],[2511,"\"The soul of a believer is suspended as long as he owes a debt.\""],[2512,"Whoever departs this life with his soul free from three things enters Paradise: from arrogance, misappropriation of spoils, and debt."],[2513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a man to offer the funeral prayer over him, and he said, \"Pray over your companion, for he owes a debt.\" Abu Qatadah said, \"It is upon me, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"In full settlement?\" He said, \"In full settlement.\" So he prayed over him."],[2514,"\"By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no believer on earth but I am the closest of people to him. So whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents, let them call upon me, for I am his patron. And whoever leaves wealth, it belongs to his heirs, whoever they may be.\""],[2515,"\"Indeed, Allah is with the creditor until his debt is repaid, as long as it is not in something Allah dislikes.\" He said: Abdullah b. Ja'far used to say to his treasurer, \"Go and collect a debt for me, for I dislike spending a night except with Allah with me, after what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2516,"\"The hand is responsible for what it takes until it returns it.\""],[2517,"\"Return the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you.\""],[2518,"Some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ presented him with a dish containing fish while he was in the house of one of his wives. The dish broke and the Prophet ﷺ took a piece of the fish and placed it on a tray, saying, \"Eat, your mother's sins have been forgiven.\" He then waited until a new dish arrived, took it, and gave it to the owner of the broken dish. Abdullah said, \"This is what we say about it.\""],[2519,"Sufyan b. Abdullah found a saddlebag and brought it to Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ . He said, \"Announce it for a year; if it is recognized, then that is that, otherwise it is yours.\" It was not recognized, and he met him with it the following year during the season and mentioned it to him. Umar said, \"It is yours, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to do that.\" He said, \"I have no need of it.\" So Umar took possession of it and placed it in the public treasury."],[2520,"In the year Makkah was conquered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said, \"Indeed, Allah held back the elephant from Makkah and gave authority over its people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the believers. Verily, it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be lawful for anyone after me. Verily, it is sacred at this very hour of mine; its fresh herbage is not to be cut, its trees are not to be lopped, and its fallen objects are not to be picked up except by one who announces them.\""],[2521,"\"The stray animal of a Muslim is a brand of the Fire.\""],[2522,"\"The stray animal of a Muslim is a brand of the Fire. The stray animal of a Muslim is a brand of the Fire. The stray animal of a Muslim is a brand of the Fire. Do not go near it.\" Then a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, lost property that we find?\" He said, \"Announce it, do not conceal it, and do not hide it. If its owner comes, then hand it over to him; otherwise, it is the property of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.\""],[2523,"\"Whoever seizes the right of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has made the Fire obligatory for him and forbidden Paradise to him.\" A man said to him, \"Even if it is something insignificant, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Even if it is a stick of arak.\""],[2524,"\"There are three whom Allah will not speak to, nor look at, on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and they will have a painful punishment.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are they? They have failed and lost.\" He repeated it. I said, \"Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"The one who lets his garment hang below his ankles, the one who reminds others of his favors, and the one who sells his goods by means of a false oath.\""],[2525,"\"Whoever wrongfully takes a span of land, it will be made to encircle his neck from seven earths.\""],[2526,"\"Whoever revives dead land, he has a reward in it, and whatever the wild animals eat from it is charity for him.\""],[2527,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to grant him the salt flat called the salt of Ma'rib, and he granted it to him. Then al-Aqra' b. Habis al-Tamimi said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I came to the salt spring in the pre-Islamic era, and it is in a land with no water. Whoever comes to it takes from it, and it is like perennial water.\" So the Prophet ﷺ asked al-Abyad to rescind his grant of the salt flat. I said, \"I have rescinded it on the condition that you make it a charity from me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is a charity from you, and it is like perennial water; whoever comes to it takes from it.\" He said, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him land and palm trees in the Jawf, the Jawf of Murad, in place of it when he rescinded it from him. Al-Faraj said, \"So it remains like that; whoever comes to it takes from it.\""],[2528,"It is narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed a piece of land. He said, \"Send Muawiyah with me.\" He said, \"Give it to him.\" Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Gündar narrated to us about this narration."],[2529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered my walled garden and said, \"O Umm Mubashshir, did a Muslim plant this or a disbeliever?\" I said, \"A Muslim.\" He said, \"There is no Muslim who plants a plant and a human, animal, or bird eats from it but that it is charity for him.\""],[2530,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the protected area of arak trees. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no protected area for arak trees.\" He said, \"An arak tree within my enclosure?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no protected area for arak trees.\" Faraj said, meaning al-Abyad, \"Within my enclosure\" refers to the land in which crops are grown and which is surrounded."],[2531,"Do not sell water, for I heard the Prophet ﷺ forbidding the sale of water."],[2532,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission, and he entered between him and his shirt. Uthman said: He embraced him and said: What is the thing which it is not lawful to withhold? He said: \"Salt and water.\" He said: What is the thing which it is not lawful to withhold? He said: \"If you do good, it is better for you.\" He said: What is the thing which it is not lawful to withhold? He said: \"If you do good, it is better for you.\" And he ended with salt and water."],[2533,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dealt with the people of Khaybar for half of what comes out of it of fruit or crops."],[2534,"We used to engage in sharecropping for two or three years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from sharecropping on the basis of one-third, one-half, and something of straw. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"Whoever has land should cultivate it; if he dislikes cultivating it, he should give it to his brother; if he dislikes giving it to his brother, he should leave it.\""],[2535,"I asked Abdullah b. Ma'qil about sharecropping, and he said:"],[2536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of barren land for two or three years."],[2537,"We used to lease land at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for what grew on the water channels and for what the water reached of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that and allowed us—or he said granted us a concession—to lease it for gold and silver."],[2538,"When you estimate the produce, take it and leave some; leave one-third, and if you do not leave one-third, then leave one-fourth."],[2539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the earnings of slave women."],[2540,"The earnings of a cupper are vile, the dowry of a prostitute is vile, and the price of a dog is vile."],[2541,"The translation of the sentence \"أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ﷺ «حَجَمَهُ أَبُو طَيْبَةَ وَأَمَرَ لَهُ بِصَاعَيْنِ مِنْ طَعَامٍ»\" into English is: \"It is narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj and ordered him to give him two Sa' of food\"."],[2542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the stud fee of a stallion."],[2543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the stud fee of a stallion and the wages of a prostitute."],[2544,"“Whoever of you sells a house or real estate, it is likely that he will not be blessed in it unless he puts it into something like it.”"],[2545,"“Whoever digs a well, no one may dig around it for forty cubits as a watering place for his livestock.”"],[2546,"Regarding preemption when their path is one? He said: “It is to be waited for, even if its owner is absent.”"],[2547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in favor of preemption in every unpartitioned share, whether a dwelling or a garden. It is not lawful for him to sell until he notifies his partner. If he wishes, he may take it, and if he wishes, he may leave it. If he sells without notifying him, then he (the partner) has more right to it.” It was said to Abu Muhammad: “Do you hold this opinion?” He said: “Yes.”"],[2548,"Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari sought permission from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, three times, but he was not granted permission. So he returned and said, \"What made you come back?\" Abu Musa replied, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, saying, 'If someone seeks permission three times and is not granted it, then let them return.' So Umar said, 'Bring someone to testify with you or I will do something [harsh].' Abu Sa'eed said, 'Umar called me while I was in the mosque, fearing Umar's anger towards me. He stood up and said, 'I swear by Allah, among you there is a man who heard this from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, except that he did not testify to it.' I lifted my head and said, 'Let me inform Umar that I am with you on this.' Others also said the same, and Abu Musa's problem was resolved.\""],[2549,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and knocked on his door. He said, “Who is it?” I said, “Me.” He said, “Me? Me?” and he disliked that."],[2550,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to come to his family at night unexpectedly, or to suspect them, or to seek out their faults.” Sufyan said: “His saying, ‘or to suspect them, or to seek out their faults’—I do not know whether it is something Muharib said or something in the hadith.”"],[2551,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Medina, the people gathered around and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has arrived.\" I went out among those who went out, and when I saw his face, I recognized that his face is not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him say was, \"O people, spread peace, feed the hungry, maintain family ties, and pray while the people are asleep. You shall enter Paradise in peace.\""],[2552,"A Muslim has six rights over another Muslim: he greets him with peace when he meets him, responds to his sneeze, visits him when he is ill, answers his invitation, attends his funeral, loves for him what he loves for himself, and advises him sincerely in his absence."],[2553,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The horseman gives Salam to the walking person, the walking person to the one standing and the few to the many.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2705)"],[2554,"When one of the Jews greets, he only says, “As-samu ‘alayk” (death be upon you), so say, “Upon you.”"],[2555,"I was walking with Thabit al-Bunani, and he passed by some boys and greeted them. Thabit narrated that he was with Anas, and he passed by some boys and greeted them, and Anas narrated that he was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he passed by some boys and greeted them."],[2556,"While she was among some women, the Prophet ﷺ passed by them and greeted them."],[2557,"Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Aish, this is Jibril reciting peace to you.” She said, “And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.” She said, “And he sees what I do not see.”"],[2558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and I came to him when he finished his prayer, and I was the first to greet with the greeting of Islam. He said, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. From whom are you?” He said: I said, “From Ghifar.” He said, and he lowered his hand. I said to myself, “He disliked that I attributed myself to Ghifar.”"],[2559,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Peace be upon you,” so he returned the greeting and said, “Ten.” Then a man came and greeted, saying, “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” so he returned the greeting and said, “Twenty.” Then a man came and greeted, saying, “Peace be upon you, the mercy of Allah, and His blessings,” so he returned the greeting and said, “Thirty.”"],[2560,"He greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating, so he did not return the greeting to him until he had performed ablution. When he had performed ablution, he returned it to him."],[2561,"“Do not enter upon women.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, what about the brother-in-law?” He said, “The brother-in-law is death.”"],[2562,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the sudden glance? He said, “Avert your gaze.”"],[2563,"From Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a woman's hem, so he said, “A handspan.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, then their feet will show?” He said, “The length of a forearm, not to exceed that.” Abdullah said: People narrate it from Nafi' from Sulayman b. Yasar."],[2564,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said, “O assembly of women, do you not have silver with which to adorn yourselves? Indeed, there is no woman among you who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[2565,"“Any woman who perfumes herself and then goes out so that her scent is noticed is an adulteress, and every eye is adulterous.”"],[2566,"“Allah has cursed the women who tattoo and those who ask to be tattooed, and the women who pluck facial hair, and those who ask for it to be done, and the women who file gaps between their teeth for beauty, altering the creation of Allah.” This reached a woman from Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub, so she came and said, “It has reached me that you cursed such-and-such and such-and-such?” He said, “Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed and whom are in the Book of Allah?” She said, “I have read what is between the two covers and I did not find in it what you say.” He said, “If you have read it, you have certainly found it. Have you not read: ‘Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you from, abstain from it, and fear Allah. Indeed, Allah is severe in punishment’ [al-Hashr 7]?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “For he did forbid it.” She said, “But I see your family doing it?” He said, “Go in and look.” So she went in and looked, and she did not see any of what she needed. He said, “If she were like that, I would not have had intercourse with her.”"],[2567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid ten characteristics: a man lying with a man in a single undergarment with nothing between them, and a woman lying with a woman in a single undergarment with nothing between them, and plucking hair, and tattooing, and plundering, and riding on leopard skins, and wearing brocade here on the two shoulders and on the lower part of the garments. Abdullah said: Abu Amir is a shaykh of theirs, and mukama'ah means lying together."],[2568,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed effeminate men and masculine women, and he said, “Expel them from your houses.” He said, “So the Prophet ﷺ expelled so-and-so, and Umar expelled so-and-so or so-and-so (a woman).”"],[2569,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat with us while my thigh was uncovered. He said, “Cover yourself. Do you not know that the thigh is private?”"],[2570,"Some women from the people of Hims entered upon Aishah to ask her for a religious ruling. She said, “Perhaps you are among the women who enter bathhouses?” They said, “Yes.” She said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There is no woman who takes off her clothes in other than her husband’s house except that she tears apart what is between her and Allah ﷻ.’”"],[2571,"A man should not make his brother get up from his seat and then sit in it, but make room and spread out."],[2572,"\"When one of you—or a man—gets up from his seat and then returns to it, he is more entitled to it.\""],[2573,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some people of the Ansar sitting and said, \"If you must do so, then guide the way, spread the salam, and help the oppressed.\""],[2574,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lying on his back in the mosque with one of his legs over the other."],[2575,"\"When you are three, let not two converse privately without their companion, for that grieves him.\""],[2576,"Toward the end of his life, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in a gathering and wanted to get up, he would say, \"Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you now say words you did not say before.\" He said, \"This is an atonement for what occurs in gatherings.\""],[2577,"The sneezer says: Al-hamdu lillah 'ala kulli hal (Praise be to Allah in every situation). The one who responds to him says: Yarhamukum Allah (May Allah have mercy on you). And he replies to him: Yahdikum Allah wa yuslihu balakum (May Allah guide you and set your affairs right)."],[2578,"Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he responded to one of them and did not respond to the other. It was said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, you responded to this one and did not respond to the other?\" He said, \"This one praised Allah, and that one did not praise Allah.\""],[2579,"A man sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Yarhamuk Allah (May Allah have mercy on you).\" Then he sneezed again, and he said, \"The man has a cold.\""],[2580,"We had a garment with images on it, and I placed it in front of the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he forbade me—or she said, he disliked it. She said, \"So I made it into cushions.\""],[2581,"\"The angel does not enter a house in which there is a dog, an image, or a person in a state of major ritual impurity.\""],[2582,"The Muslim, when he spends an expense on his family while seeking reward for it, it is charity for him."],[2583,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, he would be met by me and al-Hasan or al-Husayn. He said: “I think he said al-Hasan.” He carried me in front of him and al-Hasan behind him until we entered Madinah, and we were on the mount that the Prophet ﷺ was riding."],[2584,"We came to Qays b. Saʿd b. ʿUbādah in his house. The muezzin called for prayer and we said to Qays, “Stand and lead us in prayer.” He said, “I will not lead a people over whom I am not in command.” A man not inferior to him, called ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥanẓalah b. al-Ghasīl, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man is more entitled to the chest of his mount and the chest of his bed, and to lead prayer in his own dwelling.” So Qays b. Saʿd said at that, “O so-and-so,” to a client of his, “stand and pray with them.”"],[2585,"On the peak of every camel there is a devil, so when you ride them, invoke the name of Allah and do not fall short in your needs."],[2586,"Ride these beasts sound and do not take them as chairs."],[2587,"Travel is a piece of punishment: it denies one of you his sleep, food, and drink. So when one of you has fulfilled his need from his journey, let him hasten his return to his family."],[2588,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said to him, “O Prophet of Allah, I intend to travel.” He said to him, “When?” He said, “Tomorrow, if Allah wills.” He came to him, took his hand, and said to him, “In Allah’s keeping and in His protection. May Allah provide you with piety, forgive you your sin, and direct you to good wherever you aim or wherever you turn.”"],[2589,"When the Prophet ﷺ traveled he would say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, change after stability, the supplication of the wronged, and an evil sight in family and property.”"],[2590,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled and mounted his riding camel, he would say “Allāhu akbar” three times and say: “Glory be to the One Who subjected this to us, for we could not have subdued it, and to our Lord we will return” [43:14]. O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine for righteousness and piety, and for deeds that please You. O Allah, make the journey easy for us and fold up for us the distance of the land. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Deputy among the family. O Allah, accompany us in our journey and be our deputy among our family with good.”"],[2591,"When we ascended we said “Allāhu akbar,” and when we descended we said “Subḥān Allāh.”"],[2592,"The caravan that has a bell is not accompanied by angels."],[2593,"\"The angels do not accompany a group among whom there is a dog or a bell.\""],[2594,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and heard a woman cursing, so he said, \"What is this?\" They replied, \"So-and-so has cursed her riding camel.\" He said, \"Unload her, for she is cursed.\" He said: So they unloaded her. 'Imran said, \"It is as if I am looking at her, a grayish she-camel.\""],[2595,"\"A woman should not travel a journey of three days or more unless accompanied by her father, her brother, her husband, or a mahram of hers.\""],[2596,"\"If people knew what is in solitude, no rider would ever travel alone at night.\""],[2597,"If any of you stops at a place and says, 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,' nothing will harm him at that place until he departs from it."],[2598,"When he stopped at a place, he would not leave it until he prayed two rak'ahs, or he would bid farewell to the place with two rak'ahs."],[2599,"When he returned from his journey, he would say: \"Returning, if Allah wills, repentant, worshipping, praising our Lord.\""],[2600,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded a man, when he took to his bed, to say: \"O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affairs to You, and relied upon You, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed and Your Prophet whom You sent.\" For if he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."],[2601,"When any of you goes to his bed, let him shake out his bed with the inner part of his waist-wrapper, for he does not know what has come into it after him. And let him say: \"O Allah, with Your name I lay down my side, and with Your name I raise it. O Allah, if You take my soul, forgive it; and if You release it, guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants.\""],[2602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and placed his foot between me and Fatimah, and taught us what to say when we took to our beds: thirty-three tasbihs, thirty-three tahmids, and thirty-four takbirs. 'Ali said, \"I have not omitted them since.\" A man said to him, \"Not even on the night of Siffin?\" He said, \"Not even on the night of Siffin.\""],[2603,"When the Prophet ﷺ woke up, he would say: \"Praise be to Allah who gave us life after causing us to die, and to Him is the resurrection.\""],[2604,"Whoever wakes up at night and says: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs the praise, and He is over all things capable. Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, and there is no power or strength except with Allah.' Then he says, 'My Lord, forgive me' — or he said, 'Then he supplicates' — his prayer is answered. If he resolves and performs ablution and then prays, his prayer is accepted."],[2605,"When morning came, the Prophet ﷺ would say: aṣbaḥnā ʿalā fiṭrati al-islām, wa-ʿalā kalimati al-ikhlāṣ, wa-ʿalā dīni nabiyyinā muḥammadin ﷺ, wa-ʿalā millati abīnā ibrāhīm, ḥanīfan musliman, wa-mā kāna mina al-mushrikīn (We have entered the morning upon the natural disposition of Islam, the word of sincerity, the religion of our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and the creed of our father Ibrahim, upright and Muslim.)"],[2606,"Abu Bakr said, “O Messenger of Allah, command me with something I should say when I reach morning and when I reach evening.” He said, “Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self, and from the evil of Satan and his entrapment.” He said, “Say it when you reach morning, when you reach evening, and when you take to your bed.”"],[2607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever wears a garment and says, 'Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided it for me without any power or strength from me,' his previous sins will be forgiven.\""],[2608,"“When one of you enters the mosque, let him say: O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy. And when he leaves, let him say: O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty.”"],[2609,"“Whoever enters the market and says: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death, and He is ever-living and does not die; in His hand is all good, and He is over all things capable — Allah will record for him a thousand thousand good deeds, and erase from him a thousand thousand bad deeds, and raise him a thousand thousand degrees.” He said, “Then I came to Khurasan and met Qutaybah b. Muslim, and I said, ‘I have brought you a gift,’ and I narrated it to him. So he would ride out in his procession, come to the market, stand there and say it, then return.”"],[2610,"“Call yourselves by my name, and do not hide behind my title.”"],[2611,"“You will be called on the Day of Resurrection by your names and the names of your fathers, so make your names beautiful.”"],[2612,"“The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman.”"],[2613,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade us from naming our slaves four names: Aflah, Nafi, Rabah, and Yasar."],[2614,"“Umm Asim used to be called Asiyah, so the Prophet ﷺ named her Jamilah.”"],[2615,"“Zaynab’s name was Barrah, so the Prophet ﷺ named her Zaynab.”"],[2616,"A man from the polytheists said to a man from the Muslims, “What an excellent people you are, were it not that you say: Whatever Allah wills and whatever Muhammad wills.” The Prophet ﷺ heard, so he said, “Do not say: Whatever Allah wills and whatever Muhammad wills, but say: Whatever Allah wills, then whatever Muhammad wills.”"],[2617,"“Do not say to the grapevine ‘generosity’; rather generosity is the Muslim man.”"],[2618,"A boy was driving the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said, “O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels.”"],[2619,"Woe to the one who narrates and lies in order to make people laugh; woe to him, woe to him."],[2620,"The Prophet ﷺ affirmed Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt in two verses of his poetry, saying: [al-tawil meter] 'A man and a bull under his right foot, and the eagle for the other, and a watching lion.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He has spoken truth.' He said: 'And the sun rises at the end of every night, red, its color becoming rosy.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He has spoken truth.' Then a speaker said: 'It refuses; it does not rise for us in its gentleness except tormented and unless it is whipped.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He has spoken truth.'"],[2621,"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."],[2622,"That the belly of one of you be filled with pus or blood is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."],[2623,"Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion."],[2624,"Indeed, health and leisure are two blessings among the blessings of Allah, in which many people are deceived."],[2625,"Whoever listens to the conversation of a people while they dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ear."],[2626,"Do not follow one glance with another, for the first is for you and the next is against you."],[2627,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed in Islam about which I will not ask anyone. He said: 'Fear Allah, then remain upright.' He said: I said: Then what? He said: Then he pointed to his tongue."],[2628,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with something I may hold fast to. He said: 'Say: My Lord is Allah, then remain upright.' He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you fear most for me? He said: Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ took hold of his tongue, then said: 'This.'"],[2629,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best? He said: 'The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.'"],[2630,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever is silent, he is saved."],[2631,"It was said to him: What is backbiting? He said: 'Your mentioning your brother with what he dislikes.' It was said: What if what I say about my brother is true? He said: 'If it is in him, then you have backbitten him, and if it is not in him, then you have slandered him.'"],[2632,"Indeed, the worst of riding beasts are the riding beasts of falsehood. Neither seriousness nor jest is acceptable in lying, nor should a man promise his son something and then not fulfill it. Verily, truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. Verily, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. It is said of the truthful one: 'He spoke the truth and acted righteously,' and it is said of the liar: 'He lied and acted wickedly.' A man continues to speak the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a veracious one (ṣiddīq), and he continues to lie until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."],[2633,"\"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\""],[2634,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O you people! Indeed Allah is Tayyib (good) and he does not accept but what is good. And indeed Allah ordered the believers with what He ordered the Messengers. He ﷺ said: 'O you Messengers! Eat of the good things and do righteous deeds. Verily I am well acquainted with what you do (23:51).' And He said: 'O you who believe! Eat from the good things We have provided you (2:172).' He said: \"And he mentioned a man: 'Who is undertaking a long journey, whose hair is dishevelled and he is covered with dust. He raises his hands to the heavens and says: \"O Lord! O Lord!\" Yet his food is from the unlawful, his drink is from the unlawful, his clothing is from the unlawful, and he was nourished by the unlawful. So how can that be accepted?'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2989)"],[2635,"\"A servant and a riding mount are sufficient for any of you from this world.\""],[2636,"\"The righteous will depart one after another, and there will remain the dregs of people, like the dregs of barley.\""],[2637,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “How many a fasting person gains nothing from his fast except thirst, and how many a person who stands (in prayer at night) gains nothing from his standing except sleeplessness.”"],[2638,"He mentioned prayer one day and said, \"Whoever guards it, it will be for him a light, a proof, and a salvation from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever does not guard it, it will not be for him a light, nor a salvation, nor a proof, and on the Day of Resurrection he will be with Qārūn, Pharaoh, Hāmān, and Ubayy b. Khalaf.\""],[2639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to encourage the night vigil until he said, \"Even if it is one rakʿah.\""],[2640,"I had a sharp tongue toward my family, and it did not go beyond them to others. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? Indeed, I seek forgiveness from Allah one hundred times every day.\""],[2642,"From the Prophet ﷺ , that he recited, \"He is the owner of piety and forgiveness\" [Al-Muddathir 56]. He said: \"Your Lord says: I am the owner of piety, so whoever fears Me, I am worthy to forgive him.\""],[2643,"Indeed I know a verse which, if the people were to act upon it, would suffice them: {Then when they have reached their term, either retain them according to what is acceptable or part with them according to what is acceptable. And take as witnesses two just men from among you and establish the testimony for Allah. That is instructed to whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day. And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out} [al-Ṭalāq: 2]."],[2644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O ʿĀʾish, beware of sins that are regarded as insignificant, for they have a seeker from Allah.\""],[2645,"\"Every son of Adam sins, and the best of those who sin are those who repent.\""],[2646,"\"A man traveled in a desolate land,\" he said, \"and stopped under a tree, with his mount carrying his provisions and food. Then he woke up and his mount had gone. He climbed a high place and saw nothing; then he climbed another high place and saw nothing; then he climbed another high place and saw nothing.\" He said, \"Then he turned around and there it was, dragging its halter. He was not more joyful at finding it than Allah is at the repentance of His servant when he turns to Him in repentance.\""],[2647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a square line for us, then drew a line in its middle, then drew lines around it, and drew a line extending outside the line. Then he said, \"This is the human being, for the middle line; and this is his lifespan, surrounding him; and these are his ailments, for the surrounding lines—if one misses him, another strikes him; and this is his hope, for the line extending outside.\""],[2648,"Two hungry wolves sent among sheep are not more destructive to them than a man's eagerness for wealth and honor is to his religion."],[2649,"I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes."],[2650,"The Prophet ﷺ stood when Allah the Almighty sent down {And warn your closest relatives} [al-Shu'ara' 214], and said: \"O assembly of Quraysh, purchase your own selves from Allah; I cannot avail you before Allah in anything. O Banu 'Abd Manaf, I cannot avail you before Allah in anything. O 'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, I cannot avail you before Allah in anything. O Safiyyah, paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah, I cannot avail you before Allah in anything. O Fatimah bt. Muhammad, ask me whatever you wish; I cannot avail you before Allah in anything.\""],[2651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Draw near and be steadfast, and know that none of you will be saved by his deeds.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, not even you?\" He said: \"Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy and grace from Him.\""],[2652,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is not one of you except that he has a companion from the jinn and a companion from the angels.\" They asked: \"Even you?\" He replied: \"Yes, even me. But Allah has aided me against him, so he has submitted.\" Abu Muhammad said: \"Among the people is someone who says, 'I have submitted' but he means, 'I have given up'.\""],[2653,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[2654,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a scabby kid that its owners had cast out, and said: \"Do you consider this one insignificant to its owners?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"By Allah, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this one is to its owners.\""],[2655,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"Which deeds are best?\" He said: \"Faith in Allah and striving in the cause of Allah.\""],[2656,"The best of deeds in the sight of Allah is faith in which there is no doubt."],[2657,"None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[2658,"None of you believes until I am dearer to him than his father, his child, and all people."],[2659,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best?\" He said: \"The one whose life is long and whose deeds are good.\" He said: \"Then which of the people is worst?\" He said: \"The one whose life is long and whose deeds are evil.\""],[2660,"We had lunch with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah was with us. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is anyone better than us? We embraced Islam and struggled alongside you.' He said, 'Yes, a people who come after you, who believe in me though they have not seen me.'"],[2661,"How bad it is for one of you to say, 'I forgot such-and-such a verse.' Rather, he was made to forget. So keep reminding yourselves of the Quran, for it escapes from the hearts of men faster than camels escape from their hobbles."],[2662,"None of you should say, 'I am better than Yunus b. Matta.'"],[2663,"He ﷺ said, 'Every Muslim owes charity.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what if he cannot or does not do it?' He said, 'He works with his hands, so he eats from it and gives charity.' They said, 'What if he does not do that?' He said, 'He helps the one in desperate need.' They said, 'What if he does not do that?' He said, 'He commands what is good.' They said, 'What if he does not do that?' He said, 'He refrains from evil, for that is charity for him.'"],[2664,"He ﷺ said, 'Whoever stands in a position of showing off and seeking reputation, Allah will expose him on the Day of Resurrection and make his deeds known.'"],[2665,"The example of the believer is like the example of a tender plant of a crop: the winds bend it, at times setting it upright and at other times laying it low, until death comes to him. The example of the disbeliever is like the example of a firmly rooted cedar that nothing can affect until it is uprooted all at once."],[2666,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he gave me; then I asked him and he gave me; then I asked him and he gave me; then I asked him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Hakim, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with a generous soul will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it with a greedy soul will not be blessed in it, and he will be like the one who eats but never feels full. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.'"],[2667,"He ﷺ said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade burying infant girls alive, disobeying mothers, withholding and demanding, idle talk and asking too many questions, and wasting wealth.'"],[2668,"He ﷺ said, 'What I fear most for my Ummah is the misguided leaders.'"],[2669,"He ﷺ said, 'A man should help his brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. If he is an oppressor, he should stop him, for that is help for him; and if he is oppressed, he should support him.'"],[2670,"He ﷺ said, 'Religion is sincere advice.' He said, 'We said, to whom, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'To Allah, to His Messenger, to His Book, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common people.'"],[2671,"\"Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange. I think Hafs said: 'So glad tidings to the strangers.'\" It was said, \"And who are the strangers?\" He said, \"Those who withdraw from the tribes.\""],[2672,"\"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him.\" So 'A'ishah or one of his wives said, \"But we dislike death.\" He said, \"It is not that. But when death comes to the believer, he is given glad tidings of Allah's pleasure and honor, so nothing is more beloved to him than what is ahead of him; thus he loves to meet Allah, and Allah loves to meet him. And when death comes to the disbeliever, he is given tidings of Allah's punishment and penalty, so nothing is more hateful to him than what is ahead of him; thus he hates to meet Allah, and Allah hates to meet him.\""],[2673,"Indeed Allah, Exalted is He, will say on the Day of Resurrection: \"Where are those who loved one another for My majesty? Today I will shade them in My shade, on a day when there is no shade but My shade.\""],[2674,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"None of you should wish for death. If he is a doer of good, perhaps he may increase in goodness; and if he is a doer of evil, perhaps he may seek to make amends.\""],[2675,"\"I have been sent and the Hour is like these two.\" Wahb pointed with his index and middle fingers."],[2676,"\"You have completed seventy nations; you are the last of them and the most honored of them before Allah.\""],[2677,"\"Where is so-and-so?\" A man among them nudged him and said, \"He is such and such.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Did he not witness Badr?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: 'Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.'\""],[2678,"If Allah were to withhold rain from my ummah for ten years and then send it down, a group of my ummah would become disbelievers because of it, saying: \"It is by the rain-star of Mijdah.\""],[2679,"We came to Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah to visit him when he was ill. He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A good deed is rewarded ten times its like.'\""],[2680,"\"Whoever has two faces in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2681,"\"O Allah, I am only a human being. Whichever Muslim I have cursed, insulted, or flogged, make it for him a prayer, a mercy, and a means of nearness by which You bring him close to You on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2682,"It would not please me that Mount Uhud be mine in gold, and that I die on the day I die with a dinar or half a dinar by me, except for a debtor."],[2683,"You are certainly engaging in deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair, which we used to count at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among the destructive sins. It was mentioned to Muhammad—meaning Ibn Sirin—and he said, 'He spoke the truth, and I consider dragging the lower garment to be of that.'"],[2684,"Fever is from the breath of Hell—or from the heat of Hell—so cool it with water."],[2685,"No Muslim is afflicted by a tribulation in his body except that Allah commands the guardian angels who protect him, saying, 'Write for My servant, every day and night, the like of the good he used to do while he was confined in My bond.'"],[2686,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was suffering from a fever. I placed my hand on him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you have a severe fever.' He said, 'Indeed I suffer a fever like two men of you.' I said, 'Is that because you have twice the reward?' He said, 'Yes, and no Muslim is afflicted with any harm—illness or what is other than that—except that sins are shed from him just as a tree sheds its leaves.'"],[2687,"Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him."],[2688,"One day the Prophet ﷺ came and joy was visible on his face. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we see joy on your face that we have not seen before?' He said, 'Yes, an angel came to me and said, \"O Muhammad, your Lord says to you: Would it not please you that no one from your ummah sends blessings upon you except that I send ten blessings upon him, and no one greets you with peace except that I greet him with peace ten times?\" I said, \"Yes.\" '"],[2689,"Allah has angels who roam the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my ummah."],[2690,"I have several names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Mahi—the one by whom Allah erases disbelief, I am al-Hashir—the one after whom people are gathered, and I am al-‘Aqib, and the ‘Aqib is the one after whom there is no prophet."],[2691,"O Ka‘b b. ‘Ujrah, flesh nurtured from ill-gotten gain will never enter Paradise."],[2692,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, he laughed and said, 'Will you not ask me what makes me laugh?' They said, 'What makes you laugh?' He said, 'I marvel at the affair of the believer—all of it is good for him. If what he loves befalls him, he praises Allah, and that is good for him. If what he dislikes befalls him and he is patient, that is good for him. No one's affair is entirely good except the believer's.'"],[2693,"I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and not know whether it was something revealed to him or something he said, while he was saying, 'If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the son of Adam's belly except dust. And Allah relents to the one who repents.'"],[2694,"«None should tell stories except a commander, one commanded, or one showing off.»"],[2695,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «That I sit in a gathering like this is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves.» He said: I said, “Which gathering does he mean?” He said: At that time he was telling stories."],[2696,"«The believer is not bitten from the same hole twice.»"],[2697,"«Do not enter upon women whose husbands are absent, for the devil runs through the son of Adam like the running of blood.» They said, “And from you?” He said, «Yes, but Allah helped me against him, so I stay safe.»"],[2698,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Which people are most severely tried?” He said, «The prophets, then the most exemplary, then the most exemplary. A man is tried according to his religion. If his religion is firm, his trial is increased, and if his religion is weak, it is lightened for him. The servant continues to be tried until he walks on the earth with no sin upon him.»"],[2699,"Do not praise me excessively as the Christians praised ʿĪsā b. Maryam, but say, “Allah’s servant and His messenger.”"],[2700,"«Allah made mercy into one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine with Himself and sent down one part to the earth. From that one part, creatures show mercy to each other, so that a mare lifts her hoof from her foal lest she injure it.»"],[2701,"Indeed, your Lord is merciful. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is written for him; if he does it, it is written for him tenfold, up to seven hundredfold, up to many multiples. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, a good deed is written for him; if he does it, it is written as one, or He wipes it away. None is ruined before Allah except the ruined."],[2702,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but cannot do deeds like theirs?” He said, «You, O Abū Dharr, are with the one you love.» I said, “I love Allah and His Messenger.” He said, «You are with the one you love.»"],[2703,"«O son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for what is in you, and I do not mind. O son of Adam, if you meet Me with earth-filling sins, I meet you with earth-filling forgiveness, so long as you do not associate anything with Me. O son of Adam, if you sin until your sin reaches the clouds of the sky, then you seek My forgiveness, I forgive you, and I do not mind.»"],[2704,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about righteousness and sin. He said, «Righteousness is good character, and sin is what stirs in your soul and you dislike for people to know it.»"],[2705,"«Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good deed and it will wipe it out, and behave towards the people with a good character.»"],[2706,"«The most complete of the believers in faith are those with the best character.»"],[2707,"«Indeed Allah is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness.»"],[2708,"«Indeed Allah loves gentleness in every affair.»"],[2709,"«Whoever I take his two beloved ones and he remains patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied for him with any reward less than Paradise.»"],[2710,"Ubaidullah b Ziyad visited Ma'qil b. Yasir al-Muzani in his last iliness. Ma'qil said (to him): I am narrating to you a tradition I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If I knew that I am to survive this illness. I would, not narrate it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: If God appointed anyone ruler over a people and he died while he was still treacherous to his people, God would forbid his entry into Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 142e)"],[2711,"«The best of your leaders are those whom you love and they love you, and you pray for them and they pray for you. And the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and they hate you, and you curse them and they curse you.» We said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not then oppose them? He said: «No, as long as they establish the prayer among you. Indeed, whoever is appointed over him a ruler and sees him committing something of disobedience to Allah, let him hate what he commits of disobedience to Allah, but let him not withdraw his hand from obedience.»"],[2712,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the Trumpet, and he said, «A horn into which it will be blown.»"],[2713,"«Allah will seize the earth and fold up the heaven with His Right Hand, then He will say: I am the King; where are the kings of the earth?»"],[2714,"It was said to him: What is the Praiseworthy Station? He said: That is the day when Allah, Exalted is He, will descend upon His Throne, which will creak as a new saddle creaks from being constrained by Him, and it is as wide as what is between the heaven and the earth. And you will be brought barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. The first one to be clothed will be Ibrahim. Allah, Exalted is He, will say: Clothe My intimate friend. Then two white garments from the garments of Paradise will be brought, and I will be clothed after him. Then I will stand at a station to the right of Allah which the first and the last will envy me for."],[2715,"The people said to the Prophet ﷺ: Will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Prophet ﷺ said: «Do you dispute about seeing the moon on the night of the full moon when there is no cloud below it?» They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: «Do you dispute about seeing the sun when there is no cloud below it?» They said: No. He said: «Then you will see Him just like that.»"],[2716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and said: «O people, indeed you will be gathered to Allah, Exalted is He, barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.» Then he recited: {As We began the first creation, We will repeat it. A promise binding on Us. Indeed, We will do it.}"],[2717,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When Allah gathers the servants on one plain, a caller will call out: Let every people join what they used to worship. So every people will join what they used to worship, and the people will remain as they are. Then He will come to them and say: What is the matter with the people? They have gone, and you are still here? They will say: We are waiting for our Lord. He will say: Do you recognize Him? They will say: If He makes Himself known to us, we will recognize Him. Then He will uncover His shin to them, and they will fall down in prostration. That is the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {The Day the shin will be uncovered and they are invited to prostration but they will not be able} [al-Qalam 42]. Every hypocrite will remain and will not be able to prostrate, then He will lead them to Paradise."],[2718,"When Allah gathers the first and the last and judges between them and finishes the judgment, the believers say, \"Our Lord has judged between us, so who will intercede for us with our Lord?\" They say, \"Go to Adam, for Allah created him with His hand and spoke to him.\" They come to him and say, \"Arise and intercede for us with our Lord.\" Adam says, \"You should go to Nuh.\" They come to Nuh, and he directs them to Ibrahim. They come to Ibrahim, and he directs them to Musa. They come to Musa, and he directs them to 'Isa. They come to 'Isa, and he says, \"I will direct you to the unlettered Prophet.\" He said, \"They come to me, and Allah ﷻ permits me to stand before Him. My seat emits the finest fragrance anyone has ever smelled, until I come to my Lord. He will grant me intercession and make for me a light from the hair of my head to the toenail of my foot. At that point, the disbelievers say to Iblis, 'The believers have found someone to intercede for them, so you arise and intercede for us with your Lord, for you are the one who led us astray.'\" He said, \"He arises, and his seat emits the foulest odor anyone has ever smelled. Then Hell is magnified, and at that point he says, {And Satan will say when the matter has been decided, 'Indeed, Allah promised you a promise of truth, and I promised you, but I betrayed you'} [Ibrahim 22] to the end of the verse.\""],[2719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There is for every apostle a prayer, and I intend (if Allah so willed) that I would reserve my prayer for the intercession of my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Muslim 198b)"],[2720,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without any reckoning.\" Ukasha said, \"O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to include me among them.\" The Prophet ﷺ supplicated, \"O Allah, make him among them.\" Another person then requested the Prophet ﷺ to supplicate for him, but the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Ukasha has surpassed you in this.\""],[2721,"\"There will certainly enter Paradise by the intercession of a man from my Ummah more than the tribe of Tamim.\" They said, \"Other than you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Other than me.\""],[2722,"I said to 'A'ishah, \"O Mother of the Believers, what do you think about the statement of Allah the Exalted, {On the Day the earth will be replaced by another earth and the heavens, and they will come forth before Allah, the One, the Prevailing}? Where will the people be on that day?\" She said, \"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said, 'Upon the Sirat.'\""],[2723,"About the statement of Allah ﷻ {And there is none of you except he will come to it. This is upon your Lord an inevitability decreed} [Maryam 71], he narrated to me that 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud narrated to them, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The people will come to the Fire, then they will depart from it according to their deeds. The first of them will be like a flash of lightning, then like the wind, then like the speed of a horse, then like a rider in his saddle, then like a man's running, then like his walking.\""],[2724,"Death will be brought as a dusty ram and made to stand between Paradise and the Fire. It will be said, 'O people of Paradise,' and they will stretch their necks and look. It will be said, 'O people of the Fire,' and they will stretch their necks and look, seeing that relief has come. Then it will be slaughtered, and it will be said, 'Eternal life, no death.'"],[2725,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon, and he said, \"I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire.\" He kept saying it until, if he were in this position of mine, the people of the market would have heard it, and until a cloak that was upon him fell at his feet."],[2726,"There was a servant among the servants of Allah who did not practice any religion for Allah. He remained until a lifetime had passed and a lifetime remained. He realized that he had not stored up any good with Allah, so he called his sons and said, \"What kind of father do you know me to be?\" They said, \"The best, O our father.\" He said, \"Indeed, I will not leave with any of you any wealth that is mine except that I take it, or you must do what I command you.\" He said, \"He took a covenant from them, by my Lord.\" He said, \"As for me, when I die, take me and burn me with fire until I become charcoal, then crush me, then scatter me in the wind.\" He said, \"They did that to him, by the Lord of Muhammad, when he died. Then he was brought back in the best form he had ever been, and was presented to his Lord. He said, 'What made you do what you did with the fire?' He said, 'Fear of You, O Lord.' He said, 'I hear that you were indeed fearful.' He said, 'He was forgiven.'\""],[2727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat. It was said, \"You neither fed it nor gave it water, and you did not let it loose to eat from the vermin of the earth.\""],[2728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Ninety-nine serpents will be set upon the disbeliever in his grave, biting and stinging him until the Hour rises. If one of those serpents were to blow upon the earth, it would not grow any greenery.\""],[2729,"\"Indeed, in Hell there is a valley called Habhab, inhabited by every tyrant.\" So beware lest you be among them."],[2730,"\"As for the people of the Fire who are its inhabitants, they will not die in the Fire. But as for some people, the Fire will touch them according to their sins, and they will be burned in it until they become charcoal. Then permission for intercession will be given, and they will come out of the Fire in groups, and will be scattered upon the rivers of Paradise. It will be said to the people of Paradise, 'Pour water upon them.'\" He said, \"They will pour water upon them, and their flesh will grow as a seed grows in the silt of a flood.\""],[2731,"Paradise has eight gates."],[2732,"Whoever enters Paradise will enjoy bliss and never suffer; his clothes will never wear out and his youth will never fade. In Paradise there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never crossed the mind of any human."],[2733,"The place of a whip of one of you in Paradise is better than this world and everything in it. Recite, if you wish: “Every soul will taste death, and you will only be given your full reward on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever is drawn away from the Fire and admitted to Paradise has truly succeeded. And the life of this world is nothing but the enjoyment of delusion” (Al ʿImrān 185)."],[2734,"We said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is Paradise built of?” He said, “A brick of gold and a brick of silver; its mortar is fragrant musk, its pebbles are rubies and pearls, and its soil is saffron. Whoever enters it will abide eternally; he will enjoy bliss and never suffer; their youth will not fade and their clothes will not wear out.”"],[2735,"The Gardens of Firdaws are four: two of gold—their ornaments, vessels, and whatever is in them—and two of silver—their ornaments, vessels, and whatever is in them. Nothing stands between the people and looking at their Lord except the veil of pride over His face in the Gardens of ʿAdn. These rivers gush forth from the Gardens of ʿAdn into a hollow, then afterwards rise up as rivers. ʿAbdullāh said: jawbah means what the earth is pierced through for."],[2736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, the first group from my Ummah to enter Paradise will be like the full moon on a clear night, then those who follow them will be like the brightest star in the sky.\" Ukashah stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me among them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, make him among them.\" Then another man stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me among them.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Ukashah has surpassed you in that.\""],[2737,"\"From the Prophet ﷺ: {And it will be said, \"Indeed, this is for you a reward, and your effort has been appreciated.\"} [Al-A'raf 43] He said, 'Be glad, so as not to be saddened. Be generous, so as not to be stingy. Age gracefully, so as not to be weakened. And live eternally, so as not to die.'\""],[2738,"A man from the people of Paradise will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, intercourse, and desire.” A Jewish man said, “One who eats and drinks will need to relieve himself?” He said, “Sweat will flow from his skin, and then his belly will shrink.”"],[2739,"The people of Paradise are young, hairless, beardless, with kohl-lined eyes; their clothes do not wear out and their youth does not fade."],[2740,"The people of Paradise do not urinate, blow their noses, or defecate. That comes out of them as a belch. They eat and drink and are inspired with glorification and praise just as they are inspired with breath."],[2741,"I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never crossed the mind of any human. Recite, if you wish: “No soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for the eyes as a reward for what they used to do” (al-Sajdah 17)."],[2742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the lowest rank of the people of Paradise is the one who desires something from Allah, and it will be said to him, 'You have that and its equivalent along with it, except that you will have much more.' It will be said to him, 'That is yours and its equivalent along with it.' Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It will be said to him, 'That is yours and ten times its equivalent.'\""],[2743,"The people of Paradise will see the people of the upper chambers just as you see the brilliant star in the sky."],[2744,"There is no one in Paradise but has two wives; indeed he can see the marrow of their shins from behind seventy garments, and there is no unmarried person therein."],[2745,"\"The tent is a hollow pearl, its height in the sky sixty miles; in each of its corners are people for the believer, whom the others do not see.\""],[2746,"\"When a believer desires a child in Paradise, its conception, birth, and age will be in an hour, as he desires.\""],[2747,"The people of Paradise will be one hundred and twenty rows; eighty of them from my Ummah, and forty from the rest of the people."],[2748,"\"In Paradise there is a sea of milk, a sea of honey, and a sea of wine; then rivers split off from them.\""],[2749,"When 'Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is a river in Paradise; its banks are of gold, and it flows over pearls and rubies. Its soil is more fragrant than musk, its taste sweeter than honey, and its water whiter than snow.\""],[2750,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it; and recite if you wish: 'And extended shade.'"],[2751,"\"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it; it is the tree of eternity.\""],[2752,"\"The 'ajwah is from Paradise, and it is a cure for poison.\""],[2753,"\"There is a market in Paradise.\" They said, \"What is it?\" He said, \"Dunes of musk; they will come out to it and gather there. Then Allah will send upon them a breeze that will enter them into their homes, and their spouses will say to them, 'You have increased in beauty after us,' and they will say the like to their spouses.\""],[2754,"\"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires.\""],[2755,"While I was sitting in the mosque, and a circle of poor Emigrants was seated, the Prophet ﷺ entered and sat with them, so I stood up to join them. The Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"Let the poor Emigrants rejoice in what will delight their faces, for they will enter Paradise forty years before the rich.\" He said, \"I saw their faces brighten.\" 'Abdullah b. 'Amr said, \"So much so that I wished I were one of them.\""],[2756,"The Fire complained to its Lord and said, 'My Lord, parts of me have consumed other parts.' So Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, granted it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. That is the most intense heat you experience and the most intense cold (zamharir) you experience."],[2757,"“Indeed this fire of yours is one part of seventy parts of the Fire of Hell.”"],[2758,"“The person with the least severe punishment in Hell will have two sandals, from which his brain will boil.”"],[2759,"Its inhabitants will be thrown into the Fire, and it will say, 'Is there any more? Is there any more? Is there any more?' three times, until its Lord, Exalted is He, comes to it and places His foot upon it, and it shrinks back and says, 'Enough, enough, enough.'"],[2760,"“Learn the obligatory shares of inheritance, the art of grammatical errors, and the Sunnahs, just as you learn the Quran.”"],[2761,"“Learn the obligatory shares of inheritance, for they are part of your religion.”"],[2762,"“If Uthman and Zayd were to perish in some age, the knowledge of the obligatory shares of inheritance would perish. Indeed, a time came upon the people when none knew it except those two.”"],[2763,"“Learn the Quran and the obligatory shares of inheritance, for it is near that a man will become poor in respect to knowledge he used to know, or he will remain among a people who do not know.”"],[2764,"“Whoever knows the Quran but does not know the obligatory shares of inheritance, his likeness is that of a burnus with no face—or it has no face.”"],[2765,"He said, “I do not know what you are asking me about.” He said, “Kill your neighbors.”"],[2766,"“Learn the obligatory shares of inheritance, divorce, and Hajj, for they are part of your religion.”"],[2767,"They used to encourage the teaching of the Qur'an, the obligatory shares of inheritance, and the rites of Hajj."],[2768,"\"Whoever reads the Quran, let him learn the obligations, for if he meets an Arab, and the Arab asks, 'Do you read the Quran?' If he says 'Yes,' then he asks, 'Do you fulfill the obligations?' If he says 'Yes,' then it is something additional and good. But if he says 'No,' then the Arab asks, 'What is your superiority over me, O emigrant?'\""],[2769,"We asked Masruq: Was A'ishah proficient in the obligatory shares of inheritance? He said: \"By the One besides whom there is no god, I saw the senior companions of Muhammad ﷺ asking her about the obligatory shares of inheritance.\""],[2770,"Whoever claims descent from other than his father, knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden for him."],[2771,"Claiming a lineage that is not known is disbelief in Allah, and disavowing a lineage, even if it is distant, is disbelief in Allah."],[2772,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, but I arrived after he had passed away, and Abu Bakr was standing in his place. He prolonged the praise and wept profusely, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Disavowing a lineage, even if it is distant, is disbelief in Allah, and claiming a lineage that is not known is disbelief in Allah.\""],[2773,"Any man who claims descent from other than his father, or allies himself with other than his patrons who freed him, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people until the Day of Resurrection. Neither an obligatory act nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him."],[2774,"Whenever Umar took us along a path, we found it easy. He said regarding a husband and two parents: \"The husband receives half, and the mother receives one-third of what remains.\""],[2775,"A man who left behind his wife and his parents? He said: \"Zayd b. Thabit divided it into four parts.\""],[2776,"Regarding a woman and two parents: \"The woman receives one-fourth, and the mother receives one-third of what remains.\""],[2777,"The woman receives one-fourth: one share out of four; the mother receives one-third of what remains: one share; and the father receives two shares."],[2778,"Regarding a woman who left behind her husband and her two parents: “For the husband is half, and for the mother is one-third of what remains.”"],[2779,"Regarding a woman and two parents, he said: “From four shares: for the woman is one-fourth, for the mother is one-third of what remains, and what remains is for the father.”"],[2780,"Umar, when he took us along a path, we would follow him in it, and we found it easy. He ruled concerning a woman and two parents from four shares: he gave the woman one-fourth, the mother one-third of what remained, and the father two shares."],[2781,"Allah would not see me favor a mother over a father."],[2782,"Ibn Abbas sent to Zayd b. Thabit: “Do you find in the Book of Allah for the mother one-third of what remains?” Zayd said: “You are only a man who speaks according to his opinion, and I am a man who speaks according to my opinion.”"],[2783,"\"From Ibn Abbas, they said about a husband and parents: 'The husband is entitled to half of the wealth, while the mother is entitled to one-third of the total wealth, and whatever is left belongs to the father.'\""],[2784,"“For the mother is one-third of the entire estate in the case of a woman and two parents, and in the case of a husband and two parents.”"],[2785,"Ibn Abbas opposed the people of the Qiblah concerning a woman and two parents: he gave the mother one-third of the entire estate."],[2786,"Mu'adh ibn Jabal decided in Yemen in favor of a girl and a sister, so he gave half to the girl and half to the sister."],[2787,"Ibn al-Zubayr did not give inheritance to a full sister along with a daughter until al-Aswad narrated to him that Mu'adh b. Jabal gave the daughter half and the sister half. He said: “You are my messenger to Abdullah b. Utbah, so inform him of that.” He was his judge in Kufah."],[2788,"A man who left behind a daughter and a sister? He said: “For his daughter is half, and for his sister is what remains.”"],[2789,"Regarding a husband, a mother, full siblings, and maternal siblings? He said: Umar, Abdullah, and Zayd used to make them partners. Umar said: “The father only increased them in closeness.”"],[2790,"“He used not to make them partners.”"],[2791,"that Uthman used to make [them] partners"],[2792,"that Zayd used to make [them] partners"],[2793,"that he used to make [them] partners"],[2794,"Umar said regarding al-musharraka, \"The father only increased them in closeness.\""],[2795,"Abdullah came concerning the obligation of the half-brothers from the mother's side. He said that all the property belongs to his brother, his mother's son, so he distributed it to him according to the share of a full brother from the father's side and the mother's side. When Ali arrived, I asked him about it and informed him of Abdullah's statement. He said, \"May Allah have mercy on him. If he was a jurist, then perhaps I would have increased his share beyond what Allah had prescribed for him, which is one-sixth. Then he would have divided it among them like a man from among them.\""],[2796,"A case was brought to him concerning two paternal cousins, one of whom was a maternal brother. It was said to Ali, \"Ibn Mas'ud used to give him all the wealth.\" Ali said, \"Indeed he was a jurist. Had it been me, I would have given him the sixth and whatever remained would be between them.\""],[2797,"A man came to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari and Salman b. Rabi'a and asked them about a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister. They said, \"For the daughter is half, and what remains is for the sister. Go to Ibn Mas'ud, for he will agree with us.\" The man came to Abdullah and asked him about that. He said, \"I would then be astray and not of the rightly guided. I judge by what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged: for the daughter half, for the son's daughter a sixth, and what remains is for the sister.\""],[2798,"He used to say concerning full sisters and half-brothers and half-sisters through the father: for the full sisters two-thirds, and what remains is for the males without the females. Masruq came to Madinah and heard the statement of Zayd concerning it, and it pleased him. One of his companions said to him, \"Will you abandon the statement of Abdullah?\" He said, \"I came to Madinah and found Zayd b. Thabit among those firmly grounded in knowledge.\" Ahmad said: I said to Abu Shihab, \"How did Zayd rule concerning it?\" He said, \"He made them partners.\""],[2799,"We mentioned in the presence of Hakim b. Jabir that Ibn Mas'ud said concerning full sisters and half-brothers and half-sisters through the father: \"He used to give the full sisters two-thirds, and what remained was for the males without the females.\" Hakim said: Zayd b. Thabit said, \"This is from the practice of the pre-Islamic era, that men inherit instead of women. Indeed their brothers are returned to them.\""],[2800,"She used to make partners between two daughters, a son's daughter, and a son's son, giving the two daughters two-thirds, and whatever remained she made them partners in."],[2802,"He used to say concerning a daughter, son's daughters, and a son's son, \"If the division between them is less than a sixth, he gives them a sixth; and if it is more than a sixth, he gives them a sixth.\""],[2803,"He used to make [them] partners. Alqama said to him, \"Is any of them more reliable than Abdullah?\" He said, \"No, but I saw Zayd b. Thabit and the people of Madinah making partners in two daughters, a son's daughter, a son's son, and two sisters.\""],[2804,"Concerning a woman who left her husband, her mother, her full sister, her paternal half-sister, and her maternal siblings: he made it from six, then raised it until it reached ten. For the husband is half: three shares; for the full sister is half: three shares; for the mother is a sixth: one share; for the maternal siblings is a third: two shares; and for the paternal half-sister is one share to complete the two-thirds."],[2805,"Ali and Zaid used to not be hindered by the disbelievers or the slaves, and they would not inherit anything from them. Abdullah, on the other hand, would be hindered by the disbelievers and the slaves, and he would not inherit anything from them."],[2806,"Ali and Zaid used to not be hindered by the disbelievers or the slaves, and they would not inherit anything from them. Abdullah, on the other hand, would be hindered by the disbelievers and the slaves, and he would not inherit anything from them."],[2807,"That ʿAlī and Zayd said: “The mamluks and the People of the Book do not veil and do not inherit.” And ʿAbdullāh said: “They veil and do not inherit.”"],[2808,"That ʿAlī and Zayd said: “The mamluks and the People of the Book do not veil and do not inherit.” And ʿAbdullāh said: “They veil and do not inherit.”"],[2809,"That ʿUmar had written down the inheritance of the grandfather until when he was stabbed, he called for it and erased it. Then he said: “You will see your own opinion regarding it.”"],[2810,"\"I manage eighty different cases in seriousness.\""],[2811,"A man came to him and asked him about an obligatory share, so he said: “If there is no grandfather in it, then bring it.”"],[2812,"A man came to him and asked him about an obligatory share, so he said: “If there is no grandfather in it, then bring it.”"],[2813,"“Whoever would like to plunge into the depths of Hell, let him judge between the grandfather and the brothers.”"],[2814,"From Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī."],[2815,"“That Abū Bakr made the grandfather a father.”"],[2816,"That Abū Bakr “used to make the grandfather a father.”"],[2817,"That Abū Bakr used to make the grandfather a father."],[2818,"\"Indeed, a grandfather does not hold the same position as a father in your eyes, and you do not deny.\" He (the interrogator) said, \"I said, even if you were (the father), you would not deny.\" Marwan said, \"I bear witness regarding Uthman bin Affan that he testified regarding Abu Bakr that he made the grandfather (as) a father when there is no father.\""],[2819,"That Abū Bakr “used to make the grandfather a father.”"],[2820,"He made him the one whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to take anyone as a close friend, I would have taken him as a close friend, but the brotherhood of Islam is better”—meaning “Abū Bakr”—he made him a father, meaning the grandfather."],[2821,"He made the grandfather a father.\""],[2822,"\"Indeed, the grandfather's established practice has passed, and indeed Abu Bakr made the grandfather a father, but the people chose otherwise.\""],[2823,"\"Indeed, the first grandfather to inherit in Islam was Umar.\""],[2824,"Indeed, the first grandfather to inherit in Islam was Umar. He took his wealth, then Ali and Zayd came to him and said, \"You do not have that; you are only like one of the two brothers.\""],[2825,"\"Umar used to divide the estate with the grandfather along with one brother or two brothers; when they increased, he gave him one-third, and he used to give him one-sixth along with a child.\""],[2826,"When Umar b. al-Khattab was stabbed, he consulted them regarding the grandfather. He said, \"I had formed an opinion concerning the grandfather, so if you see fit to follow it, then follow it.\" Uthman said to him, \"If we follow your opinion, it is sound; and if we follow the opinion of the elder (Abu Bakr), then what a fine man of opinion he was.\""],[2827,"Ibn Abbas wrote to Ali while Ibn Abbas was in Basra: I have been brought a case of a grandfather and six brothers. Ali wrote to him: \"Give the grandfather one-sixth, and do not give him anything after that.\""],[2828,"Regarding six brothers and a grandfather, he said: \"Give the grandfather one-sixth.\""],[2829,"Ali used to consider seriousness as a sixth sense."],[2830,"Ali \"used to make the grandfather share with the brothers up to one-sixth.\""],[2831,"\"Ali used to make the grandfather share with the brothers until he would be a sixth.\""],[2832,"\"Ali used to make the grandfather share up to six along with the brothers, giving each entitled heir his share, and he would not allow an uterine brother to inherit along with a grandfather, nor an uterine sister. He would not increase the grandfather's share beyond one-sixth along with a child unless there was someone else, and he would not divide with a paternal brother along with a full brother. When there was a full sister and a paternal brother, he would give the sister half and the remaining half between the grandfather and the brother in equal halves. When there were brothers and sisters, he would make them share with the grandfather up to one-sixth.\""],[2833,"Ibn Abbas was asked about the grandfather. He said, \"Which father of yours is greater?\" I said, \"Adam.\" He said, \"Have you not heard the words of Allah, Exalted is He: {O children of Adam}\""],[2834,"I wish that I and those who disagree with me regarding the grandfather would invoke mutual curses as to which of us is worse in speech."],[2835,"He made the grandfather a father."],[2836,"Do I have any sisters? I said no. He said that the husband's share is a half and the mother's share is a third. He said, \"So I tried my best to answer me and he did not answer me except by that.\" Ibrahim and 'Amir and 'Abdul-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah said, \"No one has ever come with a obligation more confusing than the obligation you came with.\" He said, \"So I came to 'Ubaidah As-Salmani and it was said that no one in Kufa knows more about a obligation than 'Ubaidah and Al-Harith Al-A'war. 'Ubaidah used to sit in the mosque, and when Shurayh came with an obligation that had a difficulty, he would refer it to 'Ubaidah, and he would give a ruling. So I asked him and he said, \"If you want, I can tell you about the obligation of Abdullah ibn Mas'ood in this matter. He said, \"For the husband, there are three shares, half for the wife, a third for the mother, and a sixth of the remaining capital for the father-in-law.\" Abu Ishaq said, \"The father-in-law is the grandfather.\""],[2837,"Zaid used to make the grandfather a sharer with the siblings up to one-third."],[2838,"He used to divide with the grandfather along with the siblings up to one-third, then he would not diminish him."],[2839,"Take concerning the matter of the grandfather what the people have agreed upon."],[2840,"Zaid b. Thabit said regarding a sister, mother, husband, and grandfather: he made it from twenty-seven: to the mother six, to the husband nine, to the grandfather eight, and to the sister four."],[2841,"The first grandmother to be given a share in Islam was the father's mother while her son was alive."],[2842,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a grandmother one-sixth."],[2843,"It means: \"Umar inherited a grandmother with her son.\""],[2844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave three grandmothers one-sixth. He said: I said to Ibrahim: Who are they? He said: Your two grandmothers on your father's side and your grandmother on your mother's side."],[2845,"The grandmother inherits while her son is alive."],[2846,"The mother of the father of the mother does not inherit; her son through whom she is connected does not inherit, so how could she inherit?"],[2847,"The grandmother inherits while her son is alive."],[2848,"A grandmother, the mother of a father or the mother of a mother, came to Abu Bakr and said, “The son of my son, or the son of my daughter, has died, and I have heard that I have a share. So what is for me?” Abu Bakr said, “I have not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say anything about her, and I will ask the people.” When he prayed Zuhr, he said, “Which of you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say anything about the grandmother?” Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said, “I did.” He said, “What?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a sixth.” He said, “Does anyone other than you know that?” Muhammad b. Maslamah said, “He has spoken the truth.” So Abu Bakr gave her the sixth. Then a similar case came to Umar, and he said, “I do not know; I have not heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her, and I will ask the people.” They told him the hadith of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah and Muhammad b. Maslamah. Umar said, “Whichever of you two she is alone with, she gets the sixth; but if you both come together, it is between you.”"],[2849,"“When the grandmothers are equal, three grandmothers inherit: the two grandmothers of his father—the mother of his mother and the mother of his father—and the grandmother of his mother. But if one of them is closer, the share belongs to the nearest of kin.”"],[2850,"“They both did not allow the grandmother, the mother of the father, to inherit along with the father.”"],[2851,"That Uthman “did not allow the grandmother to inherit while her son was alive.”"],[2852,"“Grandmothers have no inheritance; it is only a provision given to them. The nearest and the farthest of grandmothers are equal.”"],[2853,"“The grandmother inherits while her son is alive.”"],[2854,"Four grandmothers came racing to Masruq, and he set aside the mother of the father of the mother and allowed three to inherit: the two grandmothers of his father—the mother of his mother and the mother of his father—and the grandmother of his mother."],[2855,"Regarding a daughter and a son's daughter, he said: “A half and a sixth, and what remains is returned to the daughter.”"],[2856,"That he was asked about maternal siblings and a mother, so he gave the maternal siblings a third and the mother the rest of the wealth, and he said: “The mother is the residuary heir of one who has no residuary heir.”"],[2857,"About a man who died and left his daughter, with no heir known other than her, he said: “She gets all the wealth.”"],[2858,"Ibn Mas'ud “did not return to a maternal brother along with a mother, nor to a grandmother when there was with her someone else entitled to a fixed share, nor to a son's daughter along with a full daughter, nor to a wife and husband.” Ali used to return to every holder of a fixed share except the wife and the husband."],[2859,"Ibn Mas'ud “did not return to a maternal brother along with a mother, nor to a grandmother when there was with her someone else entitled to a fixed share, nor to a son's daughter along with a full daughter, nor to a wife and husband.” Ali used to return to every holder of a fixed share except the wife and the husband."],[2860,"“That he was asked about a daughter or a sister, so he gave her a half and placed what remained in the public treasury.”"],[2861,"About the cursed son, he said: \"His inheritance belongs to his mother.\""],[2862,"I heard a man ask 'Ata' b. Abi Rabah about the child of two who cursed each other: To whom does his inheritance belong? He said: \"To his mother and her family.\""],[2863,"About the cursed son: \"If he leaves a maternal brother and his mother, the brother gets one-sixth and the mother one-third, then the remainder is returned to them, so the brother gets one-third and the mother two-thirds.\" Ibn Mas'ud said: \"The brother gets one-sixth and whatever remains goes to the mother.\""],[2864,"About the cursed son who leaves a paternal nephew and a grandfather, he said: \"The wealth belongs to the paternal nephew.\""],[2865,"About the inheritance of the cursed son: \"His mother gets one-third and two-thirds go to the public treasury.\""],[2866,"\"His inheritance belongs to his mother; the agnates of his mother pay blood money on his behalf.\""],[2867,"About the child of a woman who was cursed by her husband, who leaves his grandmother and his maternal brothers: He said: \"The grandmother gets one-third and the brothers get two-thirds.\" Zayd b. Thabit said: \"The grandmother gets one-sixth, the maternal brothers get one-third, and whatever remains goes to the public treasury.\""],[2868,"\"His mother inherits him,\" meaning the cursed son."],[2869,"\"His mother inherits him.\""],[2870,"I wrote to a brother of mine from Banu Zurayq asking him: To whom did the Prophet ﷺ rule for the cursed son? He wrote back to me that the Prophet ﷺ \"ruled it for his mother; she is in the position of both his mother and his father.\" Sufyan said: \"All the wealth belongs to the mother; she is in the position of his father and mother.\""],[2871,"About the cursed son who leaves his mother and his mother's agnates, he said: \"One-third belongs to his mother and whatever remains goes to his mother's agnates.\""],[2872,"About the cursed son, they both said: \"His agnates are his mother's agnates.\""],[2873,"“The inheritance of the child of a cursed (li‘ān) mother belongs to his mother.” I said, “What if he has a brother from his mother?” He said, “He gets one-sixth.”"],[2874,"“The child of a cursed (li‘ān) mother belongs to his mother: she inherits her prescribed share from him, and the rest goes to the public treasury.”"],[2875,"“When they curse each other (li‘ān), they are separated and never reunited, and the child is attributed to his mother: he is called ‘son of So-and-so,’ she is his ‘aṣaba (residuary heir); she inherits from him and he inherits from her. Whoever attributes him to adultery is flogged.”"],[2876,"Concerning the child of two who have cursed each other (li‘ān): “His mother’s ‘aṣaba inherit from him, and they pay his blood-money on his behalf.”"],[2877,"Concerning the child of a cursed (li‘ān) mother – he is the one who has no father – “his mother inherits from him, as do his brothers from his mother, and his mother’s ‘aṣaba. If someone slanders him, the slanderer is flogged.”"],[2878,"He was asked about the inheritance of the child of a cursed (li‘ān) mother: to whom does it belong? He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned it to his mother, because of the affliction she suffered, and to his brothers from his mother.”"],[2879,"Some people brought a dispute before ‘Alī ؓ concerning the child of two who had cursed each other (li‘ān). His father’s ‘aṣaba came seeking his inheritance. He said, “His father had disowned him, so you have no right to any of his inheritance.” He ruled that his inheritance belonged to his mother, and made her his ‘aṣaba."],[2880,"Concerning a person who has both male and female organs: from which of them is he to be given inheritance? He said, “From whichever of them he urinates.”"],[2881,"Concerning the hermaphrodite (khunthā): he said, “He is given inheritance according to the organ from which he urinates.”"],[2882,"‘Āmir was asked about a newborn who is neither male nor female, who has neither male nor female organs, and who excretes urine and feces from his navel. He was asked about his inheritance. He said, “Half the share of a male and half the share of a female.”"],[2883,"Abū Bakr was asked about kalāla. He said, “I will state my own opinion about it. If it is correct, it is from Allah; if it is wrong, it is from me and from Satan. I think it means anyone other than the parent and the child.” When ‘Umar became caliph, he said, “I would be ashamed before Allah to reject anything that Abū Bakr said.”"],[2884,"“Nothing ever perplexed the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as much as kalāla perplexed them.”"],[2885,"Al-kalalati is anyone other than the parent and the child."],[2886,"He used to recite this verse: “And if a man or a woman is inherited by a kalalah, and he has a brother or a sister” [al-Nisaʾ 12] — Saʿd said: “to a mother.”"],[2887,"ʿUmar b. al-Khattab sought someone to inherit Ibn al-Dahdahah but found no heir, so he gave the wealth of Ibn al-Dahdahah to the maternal uncles of Ibn al-Dahdahah."],[2888,"Allah and His Messenger are the patron of one who has no patron, and the maternal uncle is the heir of one who has no heir."],[2889,"ʿUmar was brought a case concerning a maternal uncle through the mother and a maternal aunt, and he gave the maternal uncle through the mother two thirds and gave the maternal aunt one third."],[2890,"ʿUmar b. al-Khattab gave the maternal aunt one third and the paternal aunt two thirds."],[2891,"He said: ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwan was brought a case concerning a maternal aunt and a paternal aunt, and an old man stood up and said: “I witnessed ʿUmar b. al-Khattab give the maternal aunt one third and the paternal aunt two thirds.” He said: He was about to write according to that, then he said: “Where is Zayd on this?”"],[2892,"\"The aunt is in the position of the mother, and the uncle is in the position of the father, and the niece is in the position of the sibling, and every relative is in the position of the womb, by which he asserts his rights if he is not an inheritor with close kinship.\""],[2893,"ʿUmar ruled concerning the people of the plague of ʿAmawas that if they were equal from the father's side, then the children of the mother are more entitled, and if some of them were closer to others through a father, then they are more entitled to the wealth."],[2894,"Salim, the mawla of Abu Hudhayfah, was struck on the day of al-Yamamah, and his inheritance amounted to two hundred dirhams. ʿUmar said: “Hold it back for his mother until she consumes it all.”"],[2895,"Brothers through the mother inherit from one another, to the exclusion of half-brothers through the father: a man inherits from his full brother, to the exclusion of his half-brother through the father."],[2896,"Muhammad bin Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Amr bin Murrah who said: \"I asked Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah: 'Did you remember anything from Abdullah?' He said, 'No'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 624)"],[2897,"The mother is the ʿasabah of one who has no ʿasabah, and the sister is the ʿasabah of one who has no ʿasabah."],[2898,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Give the Fara'id (the shares of the inheritance that are prescribed in the Qur'an) to those who are entitled to receive it. Then whatever remains, should be given to the closest male relative of the deceased .\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6732)"],[2899,"A paternal aunt of his died as a Jew in Yemen, and he mentioned that to ʿUmar b. al-Khattab, who said: “The closest of the people to her from among the people of her religion inherits from her.”"],[2900,"The paternal aunt of al-Ash'ath b. Qays died while she was a Jew. He went to Umar b. al-Khattab, and he said, \"The people of her religion inherit from her.\""],[2901,"Umar ibn Al-Khattab said, \"Those who associate partners with God, we do not inherit from them nor do they inherit from us.\""],[2902,"\"The people of two different religions do not inherit from one another.\""],[2903,"\"The people of two different communities do not inherit from one another.\""],[2904,"\"We do not inherit from the People of the Book, nor do they inherit from us, except that a man inherits from his male slave or his female slave when they die.\""],[2905,"\"We do not inherit from the People of the Book, nor do they inherit from us, except that a man inherits from his male slave or his female slave.\""],[2906,"\"Mu'awiyah used to allow a Muslim to inherit from a disbeliever, but he did not allow a disbeliever to inherit from a Muslim.\""],[2907,"Al-Mu'zilah bt. al-Harith died in Yemen while she was a Jew. Al-Ash'ath b. Qays, who was her paternal nephew, rode to Umar concerning her inheritance. Umar said, \"That is not for you. The closest of people to her from the people of her religion inherit from her. Two communities do not inherit from one another.\""],[2908,"\"Two separate communities do not inherit from one another, and one who does not inherit does not block others from inheriting.\""],[2909,"\"A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.\""],[2910,"\"When the deceased dies, the rights become due to their rightful owners, and nothing is given to one who accepted Islam or was manumitted before the inheritance is divided.\""],[2911,"\"A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.\""],[2912,"\"A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.\""],[2913,"\"The mukatab has no inheritance as long as any of his kitabah remains upon him.\""],[2914,"About a man who has sons and he freed half of some of them, a third of some of them, and a quarter of some. He said, \"They do not inherit until they are fully freed.\""],[2915,"About a man who bought his son during his illness. He said, \"If it comes out of the third, he inherits from him; but if the si'ayah is imposed on him, he does not inherit.\""],[2916,"\"The hadd of the mukatab is the hadd of a slave until he is freed.\""],[2917,"\"The mawla is a brother in religion and a blessing, and the most entitled of people to his inheritance is the closest of them to the one who freed him.\""],[2918,"About a man who freed a slave, then the mawla and the slave died, and the one who freed left his father and his son. They both said, \"The wealth belongs to the son.\""],[2919,"About a man who left his father and his son's son. He said, \"The wala' belongs to the son's son.\""],[2920,"A woman freed a slave of hers, then she died and left her son and her brother; then her mawla died. The woman's son and her brother came to the Prophet ﷺ about his inheritance. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"His inheritance belongs to the woman's son.\" Her brother said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if he had committed a grave offense, upon whom would it be?\" He said, \"Upon you.\""],[2921,"I asked Ibrahim about a man who freed a slave of his, then the slave died and the mawla died, and the one who freed left his father and his son. He said, \"To his father such-and-such, and what remains is for his son.\""],[2922,"\"It belongs to the son.\""],[2923,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to al-Baqi' and saw a man being sold. He came to him and bargained for him, then left him. Another man saw him, bought him, and freed him. Then he brought him to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I bought this man and freed him, so what do you think about him?\" He said, \"He is your brother and your mawla.\" He said, \"What do you think about his companionship?\" He said, \"If he is grateful to you, it is good for him and bad for you; and if he is ungrateful to you, it is good for you and bad for him.\" He said, \"What do you think about his wealth?\" He said, \"If he dies and leaves no 'asabah, then you are his heir.\""],[2924,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave of hers, then he died and left his daughter and his mawlat, the daughter of Hamzah. \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided his inheritance between his daughter and his mawlat, the daughter of Hamzah, into two halves.\""],[2925,"I brought a dispute before Ali concerning a father who died leaving no one besides me and his freed slave. He gave me half and gave his freed slave half."],[2926,"A case was brought to him involving a daughter and a freed slave. He gave the daughter half and the freed slave half."],[2927,"\"He died and left behind his daughter and his followers, so Ali gave his daughter half and his followers half.\""],[2928,"Her father died, and Ali assigned half to her and half to his freed slaves."],[2929,"He was asked about two sisters, one of whom purchased her father and then set him free, after which he died. He said, \"They receive two-thirds as their fixed share in the Book of Allah, and what remains belongs to the one who freed him, to the exclusion of the other.\""],[2930,"Regarding a woman who freed her father and the father then died leaving four daughters, she being one of them. He said, \"No favor is owed by him; they receive two-thirds, and she shares with them.\""],[2931,"I was with Suwayd b. Ghafalah when a man came to him and asked about the share of a man who left behind his daughter and his wife. He said, \"I shall inform you of the ruling of Ali.\" The man said, \"The ruling of Ali is sufficient for me.\" He said, \"Ali ruled that his wife receives one-eighth and his daughter one-half, then he returned the remainder to his daughter.\""],[2932,"A female client of Ibrahim died leaving property. I said to Ibrahim, and he said, \"She has a relative.\""],[2933,"\"Loyalty belongs to the closest elder,\" meaning by elder the nearest through father or mother."],[2934,"A letter was written to Umar concerning Fukayhah bt. Sam'an that she died leaving her nephew through her father and mother and her nephew through her father. Umar wrote: \"Loyalty belongs to the closest elder.\""],[2935,"Abdullah and Shurayh said, \"for the inheritors.\""],[2936,"\"Umar, Abdullah, Ali, and Zayd ruled that loyalty belongs to the closest elder.\""],[2937,"Fukayhah bt. Sam'an died leaving her nephew through her father and the sons of her nephew through her father and mother. \"Umar gave inheritance to the sons of her nephew through her father.\""],[2938,"\"Loyalty belongs to the closest elder.\""],[2939,"From Ibrahim regarding two brothers who inherited a freedman that their father had manumitted, then one of them died and left children: He said, 'Ali, Zayd, and 'Abdullah used to say, \"Loyalty belongs to the eldest.\""],[2940,"\"Loyalty belongs to the eldest.\""],[2941,"\"Loyalty belongs to the eldest.\""],[2942,"\"Loyalty belongs to the eldest.\""],[2943,"Regarding the man who supports another man, they said: \"He is among the Muslims.\" Sufyan said: \"And that's what we say as well.\""],[2944,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the Sunnah regarding a man from the people of disbelief who becomes Muslim at the hands of a man from the Muslims?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is the closest of people to him in his life and in his death.\""],[2945,"He was asked about a man from the people of the Sawad when he becomes Muslim at the hands of a man. He said, \"He pays blood money on his behalf and inherits from him.\""],[2946,"\"A woman inherits from the blood money of her husband, whether intentional or accidental.\""],[2947,"\"The blood money is according to the obligatory shares prescribed by Allah ﷻ.\""],[2948,"\"The blood money follows the same course as inheritance.\""],[2949,"\"That maternal brothers be made heirs from the blood money.\""],[2950,"\"The blood money is an inheritance among the heirs of the slain, according to the Book of Allah and its obligatory shares.\""],[2951,"\"Indeed, he has wronged who does not make maternal brothers heirs from the blood money.\""],[2952,"Blood money is inherited as wealth is inherited, its accidental and its deliberate."],[2953,"Ali did not give inheritance from blood money to brothers from the mother, nor to the husband, nor to the wife at all."],[2954,"Brothers from the mother do not inherit from blood money."],[2955,"Any people who inherit from one another whose deaths are obscured in a collapse or drowning do not inherit from one another; the living inherit them."],[2956,"I read in one of the books of Umar b. Abd al-Aziz concerning a people upon whom a house falls and it is not known which of them died first: The dead do not inherit from one another, and the living inherit from the dead."],[2957,"Umm Kulthum and her son Zayd died on the same day, and the two wailing women met in the road, and neither of them inherited from the other. The people of al-Harrah did not inherit from one another, and the people of Siffin did not inherit from one another."],[2958,"A house in Syria collapsed upon some people, and Umar made some of them inherit from the others."],[2959,"He made two brothers who were killed at Siffin inherit from one another, each from the other."],[2960,"A man perished and left his paternal aunt and his maternal aunt, so Umar gave the paternal aunt the share of a brother and gave the maternal aunt the share of a sister."],[2961,"Whoever is connected by a womb relation is given according to the womb relation through which he is connected."],[2962,"Regarding a man who left his paternal aunt and his brother's daughter, he said: The wealth belongs to his brother's daughter."],[2963,"The maternal uncle is an heir."],[2964,"That ʿUmar and ʿAbdullāh considered it appropriate to give a maternal uncle a share of inheritance."],[2965,"Concerning a paternal aunt and a brother's daughter, he said: \"The wealth goes to the brother's daughter.\""],[2966,"\"The paternal aunt [receives].\""],[2967,"Concerning a brother's daughter and a paternal aunt, he said: \"I would give the wealth to the brother's daughter.\""],[2968,"Concerning a man who died leaving no heir except his brother's daughter and his maternal uncle, he said: \"The maternal uncle gets the share of his sister, and the brother's daughter gets the share of her father.\""],[2969,"Masrūq used to place the paternal aunt in the position of the father when there was no father, and the maternal aunt in the position of the mother when there was no mother."],[2970,"The son of al-Daḥdāḥa died, and he was an atī (a person of unknown lineage) with no known origin. He was among the Banū al-ʿAjlān and left no offspring. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿĀṣim b. ʿAdī: \"Do you know of any lineage for him among you?\" He replied: \"We do not know him, O Messenger of Allah.\" So he called his sister's son and gave him his inheritance."],[2971,"That he gave the wealth to a maternal uncle."],[2972,"ʿĀmir was asked about a woman or a man who died leaving a maternal aunt and a paternal aunt, with no other heir or relative. He said: \"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd used to place the maternal aunt in the position of his mother and the paternal aunt in the position of her brother.\""],[2973,"Concerning a man who, at his death, acknowledged a debt of one thousand dirhams to a man, while another man established proof of one thousand dirhams, and the deceased left one thousand dirhams. He said: \"The wealth is divided between them in halves, unless he was insolvent, in which case his acknowledgment is not valid.\""],[2974,"I said to Sharīk: \"How did you mention regarding the two brothers, when one of them claims a brother?\" He said: \"He enters into his share.\""],[2975,"Concerning brothers, when some of them claim a brother and the others deny him, he said: \"He enters with them, taking the position of a slave owned jointly by brothers, when one of them frees his share.\" He said: \"ʿĀmir, al-Ḥakam, and their companions used to say: 'He does not enter except into the share of the one who acknowledged him.'\""],[2976,"When they are two brothers, and one of them claims a [third] brother while the other denies him? He said: Ibn Abi Layla used to say, 'It is from six: to the one who did not claim, three; to the claimant, two shares; and to the one claimed, one share.'"],[2977,"About a man who had three sons and said, 'Two thirds of my property are for the youngest of my sons.' The middle one said, 'I approve it,' and the eldest said, 'I do not approve it.' He said, 'It is from nine: he takes out his third, so he gets his share and the share of the one who approved.' Hammad said, 'He returns the share to all of them.' Amir said, 'The one who rejected only rejected against himself.'"],[2978,"About a man who acknowledged a brother, he said, 'His proof is that he is his brother.'"],[2979,"About a man who, at his death, acknowledged one thousand dirhams as a partnership investment and one thousand as a debt, and left only one thousand dirhams. He said, 'The debt is paid first, and if anything remains, it belongs to the partner in the investment.'"],[2980,"About a man who died and left three hundred dirhams and three sons. A man came claiming one hundred dirhams against the deceased, and one of the sons acknowledged it for him. He said, 'It is charged to them proportionally.' Then al-Sha'bi said, 'I do not think it should be an inheritance until the debt is paid.'"],[2981,"About a man who died and left two sons and two thousand dirhams. They divided the two thousand dirhams, and one of the sons went absent. Then a man came and established a rightful claim of one thousand dirhams against the deceased. He said, 'He takes all that is in the hand of the one present, and it is said to him: pursue your absent brother and take half of what is in his hand.'"],[2982,"If some of the heirs acknowledge a debt, it is upon him according to his share."],[2983,"If two of the heirs testify to a debt, it is from the entire estate if they are upright. Al-Sha'bi said, 'It is upon them in their portions.'"],[2984,"Ibn Mas'ud used to give inheritance to the family of an apostate if he was killed."],[2985,"Ali b. Abi Talib made the inheritance of an apostate for his Muslim heirs."],[2986,"Ali ruled that the inheritance of an apostate goes to his Muslim family."],[2987,"If a man kills his brother intentionally, he does not inherit from his estate nor from his blood money. But if he kills him accidentally, he inherits from his estate but does not inherit from his blood money. He said: Ata used to say that."],[2988,"A man threw a stone at his mother and killed her, then sought his inheritance from his brothers. His brothers said to him, 'You have no inheritance.' They went up to Ali, and he imposed the blood-money on him and excluded him from the inheritance."],[2989,"When a man kills his wife mistakenly, he is prevented from inheriting her blood-money and anything else."],[2990,"The killer does not inherit anything from the one he killed."],[2991,"Regarding a man who slandered his wife and brought witnesses, so she was stoned: he said, 'He inherits from her.'"],[2992,"Regarding a man who was flogged with the prescribed punishment – I think he died, Abu al-Nu'man was uncertain – he said, 'They inherit from each other.'"],[2993,"The killer does not inherit and does not block others from inheritance."],[2994,"The killer is not made an heir."],[2995,"No killer inherits, whether by mistake or intentionally."],[2996,"The killer does not inherit."],[2997,"When two relationships are combined, inheritance is according to the closer of them."],[2998,"He inherits from the side that is valid and does not inherit from the side that is not valid."],[2999,"Regarding the Magians: when they embrace Islam, they inherit from both relationships together."],[3000,"Concerning the wife of the prisoner: “She inherits from him and he inherits from her.”"],[3001,"Concerning the prisoner who makes a bequest, he said: “I permit his bequest as long as he remains upon his religion and has not changed from his religion.”"],[3002,"“The prisoner is treated as an heir when he is in the hands of the enemy.”"],[3003,"“The prisoner is treated as an heir.”"],[3004,"He did not treat the prisoner as an heir.”"],[3005,"“Umar b. al-Khattab wrote to Shurayh not to treat the foundling as an heir except with clear proof, even if she brought him in her swaddling cloths.”"],[3006,"“Treat the foundling as an heir.”"],[3007,"“Foundlings are not treated as heirs.”"],[3008,"Mention was made in his presence of the statement of one who spoke about the foundling, and he rejected that and said: “The Muhajirun and the Ansar inherited from one another by their lineage which was in the Jahiliyyah.”"],[3009,"“The foundling is not treated as an heir except with clear proof.”"],[3010,"“Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman did not treat the foundling as an heir.”"],[3011,"“A woman from Muharib, a captive, acknowledged the lineage of a brother of hers, also a captive, so Abdullah b. Utbah made him inherit from his sister.”"],[3012,"From a man: he said at the point of departure from this world, 'I am the client of so-and-so.' He said: \"His inheritance is returned to the one whom he named as his patron at the point of departure from this world, unless they bring evidence against him to the contrary by which they rebut his statement, in which case his inheritance is returned to what the evidence established.\""],[3013,"Regarding Ali and Abdullah, they said, \"The child of adultery is considered like the son of condemnation.\""],[3014,"\"That a child born of fornication is not inherited by the one who claims him, nor does the child inherit from that one.\""],[3015,"He used not to give inheritance to a child born of fornication even if a man claimed him.\""],[3016,"\"Any man who comes to a boy claiming that he is his son and that he committed fornication with his mother, and no one else claims that boy, then he inherits from him.\" Bukayr said: I asked Urwah about that and he said the like of the statement of Sulayman b. Yasar."],[3017,"\"The child of a woman divorced by li'an is like a child born of fornication: his mother inherits from him, and his heirs are the heirs of his mother.\""],[3018,"\"A child born of fornication is not given inheritance.\""],[3019,"Regarding children born of fornication, he said: \"They inherit from one another on the mother's side. If she gives birth to twins and one dies, he inherits the sixth.\""],[3020,"\"A child born of fornication does not inherit. Only one whose father had not had the hadd punishment established upon him, or whose mother was owned through marriage or purchase, inherits.\""],[3021,"Regarding a man who commits fornication with a woman then marries her, he said: \"There is no harm, unless she is pregnant, in which case the child is not attributed to him.\""],[3022,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"ruled that every child claimed after his father to whom he is attributed, if his heirs after him claim him, then he ruled: if he was from a slave woman whom he owned on the day he had intercourse with her, then he is attached to the one who claimed him, and he has nothing of the inheritance that was divided before him, and whatever inheritance he reaches that has not been divided, he has his share. He is not attached if the one to whom he is attributed denied him. And if he was from a slave woman he did not own or a free woman with whom he committed adultery, then he is not attached and does not inherit, even if the one to whom he is attributed claimed him, for he is a child of fornication belonging to the people of his mother, whether they were free or slave.\""],[3023,"I asked al-Sha'bi about a slave of mine who was a child of fornication. He said: \"Do not sell him, do not consume his price, and employ him.\""],[3024,"He was asked about a child born out of wedlock who dies. He said, \"If he is the son of an Arab woman, his mother inherits one-third, and the remainder of his wealth is placed in the public treasury. If he is the son of a freedwoman, his mother inherits one-third, and those who freed her inherit the rest.\" Marwan said, \"And I heard Malik say that.\""],[3025,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"ruled the inheritance of the child of a woman divorced by li'an entirely for his mother, because of the hardship she endured in bearing him.\""],[3026,"He said regarding the child of zina: To his mother's guardians, \"Take him, for you will inherit from him and pay his blood money, and he will not inherit from you.\""],[3027,"\"The sa'ibah places his wealth wherever he wishes.\""],[3028,"He was asked about the inheritance of the sa'ibah. He said, \"Every freed slave is a sa'ibah.\""],[3029,"\"The sadaqah and the sa'ibah are for their day or their time.\""],[3030,"Amir was asked about a slave who is freed as a sa'ibah. To whom does his wala' belong? He said, \"To the one who freed him.\""],[3031,"\"Mawlā died during the time of Uthman without having a heir, so he commanded for his wealth to be entered into the treasury.\""],[3032,"Regarding a man who died and had no patron of manumission, he said, \"His wealth goes where he bequeathed it. If he did not bequeath, then it goes to the bayt al-mal.\""],[3033,"Regarding one freed as a sa'ibah: \"His wala' belongs to the one who freed him. He only released him from slavery and did not release him from wala'.\""],[3034,"\"There is no harm in selling the wala' of a sa'ibah or giving it as a gift.\""],[3035,"\"A man emancipated a runaway boy and then came to Abdullah and said, 'I have emancipated a runaway boy for myself, and this is his belonging.' He said, 'It is yours.' He said, 'I have no need for it.' He said, 'Put it, as there are many inheritors here.'\""],[3036,"\"When the infant cries out, it is inherited from and prayed over.\""],[3037,"\"If a boy receives an inheritance and is inherited and prayers are offered for him.\""],[3038,"\"There is no newborn except that it cries out, and its crying out is by Satan squeezing its belly so it screams, except Isa son of Maryam ﷺ .\""],[3039,"\"The newborn does not inherit until it cries out screaming, even if it was born alive.\""],[3040,"\"When the newborn cries out, it is prayed over and inherited from.\""],[3041,"I consider the sneeze a cry."],[3042,"A newborn is not inherited from until he cries, and no funeral prayer is offered over him until he cries. When he cries, prayer is offered over him, he is inherited from, and the full blood money is paid."],[3043,"\"He is not offered prayers and a newborn is not offered prayers until he starts crying.\""],[3044,"When two mukatabs buy each other—this one from his master and that one from his master—the sale is for the first, and the people of Madinah say: The wala belongs to the master of the seller. They say: He only bought what the mukatab owed, so the wala belongs to the master."],[3045,"Any free man who marries a slave woman has enslaved half of himself, and any slave who marries a free woman has freed half of himself. Abu Muhammad said: Meaning the child."],[3046,"Regarding a slave who marries a woman, then divorces her while he has a child from her: He said: If she is free, the maintenance is upon his mother, and if he is a slave—meaning the child—then upon his patrons."],[3047,"From Ibrahim, they both said, \"His loyalty is to whoever begins with freeing a slave for the first time.\""],[3048,"If he guarantees, the wala is his, and if the slave is made to work to pay off his value, the wala is between them."],[3049,"Regarding a slave owned by two men, one of whom frees his share: He said: His emancipation is to be completed. If he has no wealth, the slave is made to work for the half at a fair value, and the wala belongs to the one who freed him."],[3050,"Regarding a slave owned by two men, one of whom frees his share and the other retains his: He said: His inheritance is between them."],[3051,"His inheritance belongs to the one who retained him. Qatadah said: It belongs entirely to the one who freed him, and his value is upon him. The people of Kufa say that."],[3052,"Regarding a man who dies leaving a mukatab and has sons and daughters: Do women have any right to the wala? He said: Women inherit from what remains of his kitabah upon him, and the wala belongs to men apart from women, except what they themselves contracted or freed."],[3053,"Women do not inherit from the wala except what they freed or what was freed by those they freed."],[3054,"A man died leaving a mukatab, then the mukatab died leaving wealth. Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah b. Abd al-Rahman allocated what remained of his kitabah among the male and female children of his patron according to their inheritance shares, and what remained of the wealth after his kitabah belonged to the males among the children of his patron rather than the females."],[3055,"Clientage belongs to the eldest, and women do not inherit from clientage except what they themselves have manumitted or have contracted for manumission."],[3056,"\"From Abu Qilabah\""],[3057,"Women do not inherit from clientage except what they themselves have manumitted or what those whom they manumitted have manumitted, except for the woman of li'an, for she inherits from the one whom her son manumits, the son from whom his father has disavowed himself."],[3058,"That he used to inherit the clients of 'Umar instead of 'Umar's daughters."],[3059,"Regarding a woman who died and left behind her sons, and they inherited wealth and clients from her, then her sons died. He said, \"The clientage returns to the woman's male relatives.\""],[3060,"I asked Ibrahim about a man who contracted a slave of his for manumission, then died and left behind sons and daughters. He said, \"It belongs to the males, not the females.\""],[3061,"Regarding a woman who died and left behind a client. He said, \"The clientage belongs to her sons, and when they die it returns to her male relatives.\""],[3062,"Women have no share in clientage except what she herself has manumitted personally."],[3063,"A client of 'Umar died, and Ibn 'Umar asked Zayd b. Thabit, \"Do 'Umar's daughters have any share of his inheritance?\" He said, \"I do not think they have anything. If you wish to give them something, you may give it to them.\""],[3064,"Whoever secures the inheritance secures the clientage."],[3065,"A woman from Muharib granted the clientage of her slave to himself, so she manumitted him, and he granted the clientage of himself to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Amr b. Hazm. Then she died, and the clients brought a dispute before 'Uthman. 'Uthman called for evidence regarding what he said. The evidence was brought, and 'Uthman said to him, \"Go and ally yourself with whomever you wish.\" Abu Bakr said, \"So he allied himself with 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Amr b. Hazm.\""],[3066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of allegiance and its gift."],[3067,"He prohibited the sale of allegiance and its gift."],[3068,"Allegiance is not to be sold nor given as a gift, and allegiance belongs to the one who manumits."],[3069,"Allegiance is a tie like the tie of kinship; it is not to be sold nor given as a gift."],[3070,"They both disliked the sale of allegiance."],[3071,"Ibn Abbas, loyalty cannot be sold, meaning it cannot be consumed by the enslavement of a person twice."],[3072,"The obligations are from six; we do not make them awl."],[3073,"A dispute was brought to Shurayh concerning two daughters, two parents, and a husband, and he judged in it. The husband then came complaining about him in the mosque. So he sent Abdullah b. Rabah to him, and he seized him and sent to Shurayh, saying, 'What do you say about this?' He said, 'This man thinks me an unjust man, and I think him a wicked man: he displays complaint and conceals a just judgment.' The man said to him, 'What do you say about two daughters, two parents, and a husband?' He said, 'The husband gets one-fourth of all the property, the parents get two sixths, and what remains is for the two daughters.' 'For what reason did you diminish me?' He said, 'It is not I who diminished you; Allah diminished you. For the two daughters is two-thirds, for the parents two sixths, and for the husband one-fourth. Thus it is from seven and a half as an obligation; your obligation is awl.'"],[3074,"The father draws the allegiance of his child."],[3075,"\"Aljad du yajurru alwala’a\" translates to \"Generosity leads to loyalty\" in English."],[3076,"The father draws the allegiance of his child."],[3077,"About a slave who died having a free father and sons from a free woman: to whom belongs the allegiance of his child? He said, 'To the patrons of the grandfather.'"],[3078,"About a mukatab who died having paid half of his kitabah and having a child from a free woman, he said, 'I do not see but that he has drawn the allegiance of his child.'"],[3079,"Shurayh would not retract a judgment he had made. Then al-Aswad narrated to him that Umar said, 'When a slave marries a free woman and she bears free children, then he is manumitted after that, the allegiance reverts to the patrons of their father.' So Shurayh adopted it."],[3080,"Regarding a slave who has a free woman as his wife: \"The child is freed by the manumission of his mother; then when the father is freed, he draws the wala'.\""],[3081,"Regarding a free woman under a slave, he said: \"As for what she bore from him while he was a slave, their wala' belongs to her patrons; and what she bore from him while he was free, their wala' belongs to his patrons.\""],[3082,"\"If a free woman is under a slave and she bears him a boy, then he is freed by the manumission of his mother, and his wala' belongs to his mother's mawali. Then when the father is freed, he draws the wala' to his father's mawali.\""],[3083,"My mother was a mawla of al-Huraqa, and my father Ya'qub was a mukatab of Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan al-Nasri. Then my father paid his kitaba, so al-Huraqi entered upon Uthman and asked for the right for me, meaning the stipend, while Malik b. Aws was with him. He said: \"That is my mawla.\" They disputed before Uthman, and he ruled in favor of al-Huraqi."],[3084,"A man died leaving no heir. It was written about him to Umar b. Abd al-Aziz while he was caliph, and he wrote: \"Distribute his inheritance among those who receive the stipend with them.\" So his inheritance was distributed among those who received the stipend with them in his administrative unit."],[3085,"\"It is not fitting for a Muslim man to spend two nights while he has something to bequeath without his will being written down with him.\""],[3086,"\"The believer does not eat to the full of both his bellies, and his will remains under his side.\""],[3087,"He said: Thumama b. Hazn said to me: \"What happened to your father?\" I said: \"He died.\" He said: \"Did he make a will? For it used to be said: When a man makes a will, his will compensates for what he neglected of his zakat.\""],[3088,"Whoever makes a will and does not act unjustly or unfairly, he has the like of the reward he would have had if he had given it in charity during his lifetime."],[3089,"It was said to Harim b. Hayyan: \"Instruct us.\" He said: \"I instruct you with the last verses of Surat al-Nahl.\" Ibn Hayyan then recited: {Invite to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good instruction, and argue with them in a way that is best. Indeed, your Lord is most knowing of who has strayed from His way, and He is most knowing of the rightly guided. And if you punish, punish with an equivalent of that with which you were harmed. But if you are patient, it is better for those who are patient. And be patient, and your patience is not but through Allah. And do not grieve over them and do not be in distress over what they conspire. Indeed, Allah is with those who fear Him and those who are doers of good.}"],[3090,"I asked Abdullah b. Abi Awfa: \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ make a will?\" He said: \"No.\" I said: \"Then how was the will prescribed for people, or were they commanded to make a will?\" He said: \"He bequeathed the Book of Allah, Mighty and Sublime.\" And Huzayl b. Shurahbil said: \"Abu Bakr was acting as executor over the successor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Abu Bakr wished that he had found a covenant from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and had pierced his nose with a nose ring for it.\""],[3091,"\"About Qatadah, it is written that when death approaches you, it is obligatory upon the God-conscious individuals to leave a will for their parents and close relatives, according to the custom of good deeds. This is a right upon the righteous individuals.\" [Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 180]. The phrase \"Al-khayr (the good) referred to wealth of one thousand or more (dirhams) and beyond.\""],[3092,"That {fear Allah and set things right between you, and obey Allah and His Messenger, if you are believers} and he instructed them with what Ibrahim instructed his sons and Ya'qub: {O my sons, indeed Allah has chosen for you this religion, so do not die except while you are Muslims} [al-Baqarah 132]. And he instructed them not to disdain being mawali of the Ansar and their brothers in religion, and that chastity and truthfulness are better and more pious than fornication and lying. If any event befalls me in this illness of mine before I change this will of mine, then he mentioned his need."],[3093,"This is how they used to make their wills: This is what so-and-so, son of so-and-so, bequeathed: that he bears witness that there is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that the Hour is coming, there is no doubt about it, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves. And he enjoined those of his family he leaves behind to fear Allah, to reconcile their differences, and to obey Allah and His Messenger, if they are believers. And he enjoined them with what Ibrahim enjoined his sons, and Ya'qub: {O my sons, Allah has chosen the religion for you, so do not die except as Muslims} [al-Baqarah 132]. And he bequeathed, if an event befalls him in this illness of his, that his need is such and such."],[3094,"The testimony: This is what he testified to: We bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. And he believes in Allah and disbelieves in the taghut. Upon that he lives, if Allah wills, and dies, and is resurrected. And he bequeathed, regarding what Allah has provided him, regarding what he left, if an event befalls him, while it is such and such, unless he changes any of what is in this will."],[3095,"Al-Rabi' b. Khuthaym wrote his will: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. This is what al-Rabi' b. Khuthaym bequeathed, and he called Allah as witness over it — and Allah suffices as witness and rewarder of His righteous servants and bestower of reward. Indeed I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Prophet. And I command myself and whoever obeys me that we worship Allah among the worshippers, praise Him among the praisers, and be sincere to the community of Muslims."],[3096,"That 'Ali entered upon a sick man, and they mentioned the will to him. 'Ali said: Allah said {If he leaves wealth} [al-Baqarah 180], and I do not think he leaves wealth. Hammad said: “I remembered that he left more than seven hundred.”"],[3097,"'Ali b. Abi Talib entered upon a man of his people to visit him. The man said: Should I make a will? He said: “No, you have not left wealth, so leave your wealth to your children.”"],[3098,"Concerning a man who made a will while the heirs were present, acknowledging that they were witnesses, he said: “It is not permissible.”"],[3099,"I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about heirs who approve the will, then when he dies they do not approve. They said: “It is not permissible.”"],[3100,"Concerning a man who bequeaths more than a third, he said: If the heirs permit it, we permit it. And if the heirs say we permit it, they have the choice when they lower their hands from the grave."],[3101,"That he bequeaths more than a third, and they permitted it for him, then they retracted it after he died. 'Abdullah was asked about that, and he said: “This is unwillingness; it is not permissible.”"],[3102,"Concerning a man who bequeaths more than a third and the heirs consented, he said: “It is permissible.” Abu Muhammad said: We permit it, meaning during life."],[3103,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered upon him while he was in Makkah and he had only a daughter. I said to him: I have only one daughter, so should I bequeath all my wealth? The Prophet ﷺ said: “No.” I said: Then should I bequeath half? The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “No.” He said: Should I bequeath a third? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A third, and a third is a lot.”"],[3104,"I fell ill along with the Prophet ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, until I became seriously ill. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me to visit me, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I think that I am dying, and I have a lot of wealth, and none will inherit from me except a daughter of mine. Should I give all my wealth in charity?” He said, “No.” I said, “Then half of it?” He said, “No.” I said, “Then a third?” He said, “A third, and a third is a lot. If you leave your heirs wealthy, it is better than leaving them poor, begging people with their hands. And you do not spend any expenditure except that Allah rewards you for it, even the morsel you put into your wife’s mouth.”"],[3105,"That his father Ziyad b. Matar made a will, saying, “My will is what the jurists of Basra agree upon.” So I asked, and they agreed upon one fifth."],[3106,"That a man asked Umar b. al-Khattab, saying, “My heirs are only distant relatives (kalalah), so should I bequeath half?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then a third?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then a quarter?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then a fifth?” He said, “No.” Until he reached a tenth, then he said, “Bequeath a tenth.”"],[3107,"\"They used to impose taxes at a rate of one-fifth and one-fourth, and the one-third was the highest tax. Abu Muhammad said that by 'al-jamih' [the highest tax], it means a spirited horse.\""],[3108,"I made a will to Humayd b. Abd al-Rahman, and he said, “I would not accept the will of a man who has children and bequeaths a third.”"],[3109,"“A third is a hardship, but it is permissible.”"],[3110,"“A sixth was more beloved to them than a third.”"],[3111,"“The guardian is a trustee regarding what is entrusted to him.”"],[3112,"“The guardian’s action is valid in everything except in buying; and when he has made a sale, he cannot revoke it.” This is the opinion of Yahya b. Hamza."],[3113,"“The guardian is a trustee in everything except in manumission, for he must establish the patronage (wala’).”"],[3114,"“Regarding the wealth of the orphan, the guardian may use it if he is appointed as guardian for the man.”"],[3115,"\"The guardian of the orphan shall take his right through intercession, and the absent one shall also be interceded for.\""],[3116,"\"So he laid down his words and turned to his father Qilabah and said, 'What are you saying?' He said, 'Answer the boy's request to give him his land.' He said, 'Then our wealth will be destroyed?' He said, 'You are the one who destroyed it.'\""],[3117,"Regarding a man who bequeathed to one man half of his wealth and to another a third of his wealth, he said: “They are both entitled to that within the third, this one with the half and this one with the third.”"],[3118,"“The testator may change whatever he wishes of the will, except manumission.”"],[3119,"\"A man may make whatever changes he wishes in his will, and the controlling part of the will is its last [provision].\""],[3120,"His father manumitted some slaves of his during his illness, then he decided to revoke their manumission and manumit others instead. He said: \"They took me before 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan, and he upheld the manumission of the latter ones and invalidated the manumission of the former ones.\""],[3121,"\"A man may make whatever changes he wishes in his will, and the controlling part of the will is its last [provision].\""],[3122,"About a man who makes one bequest and then makes another, he said: \"Both are valid from his wealth.\""],[3123,"\"The controlling part of the will is its last [provision].\""],[3124,"\"If the judge suspects the executor, he should not remove him, but instead appoint someone else alongside him.\" This is the view of al-Awza'i."],[3125,"\"The sick person's sale, purchase, and marriage are valid, and it is not taken from the third.\""],[3126,"\"Whatever the sick person gives as a preferential price in his illness, whether in a sale or purchase, is counted toward his third at fair value.\""],[3127,"A woman from our family gave a gift while she was pregnant. Al-Qasim was asked about it, and he said: \"It is from the entire wealth.\" Yahya said: \"Our view is that if labor pains had begun, then what she gave is from the third.\""],[3128,"About a man who said to his slave, 'If I enter so-and-so's house, then my slave is free,' and then he entered it while he was ill, he said: \"He is manumitted from the third, and if he entered it while he was healthy, he is manumitted from the entire wealth.\""],[3129,"\"If the heirs are needy, I see no harm in returning something to them from the third.\" Yahya said: \"I mentioned that to al-Awza'i, and he liked it.\""],[3130,"\"If two of the heirs testify, it is valid against all of them, and if one testifies, then it is valid only for his own share.\""],[3131,"“If one of the heirs bears witness, then in his share according to his portion.” Then he said, “Thereafter in the whole of his portion.”"],[3132,"“If a man bequeaths the third and the fourth, it is in the concrete property and the debt; and if he bequeaths fifty or sixty up to a hundred, it is in the concrete property until it reaches the third.”"],[3133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A man is most entitled to a third of his wealth, to place it in whichever of his wealth he wishes.”"],[3134,"I asked Abu al-Darda about a man who set aside dirhams in the path of Allah. Abu al-Darda said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘The example of one who gives charity at his death or emancipates is like one who gives a gift after he is full.’”"],[3135,"Concerning the matter of a man, Hassan advises certain things, including setting slaves free, and goes beyond one-third? He said, \"It begins with freeing slaves.\""],[3136,"“Whoever bequeaths or emancipates, and in his bequest there is excess, the excess falls upon the people of emancipation and the people of the bequest.” Ata said, “The people of Madinah overruled us: they begin with emancipation before.”"],[3137,"Regarding one who bequeaths emancipation and other things, and it exceeds the third, he said, “By shares.”"],[3138,"Regarding a man who bequeaths more than the third and in it there is emancipation, he said, “Begin with emancipation.”"],[3139,"“Begin with emancipation before the bequest.”"],[3140,"Regarding a man who bequeaths to the sons of Fulan, he said, “Their rich and their poor, their male and their female are equal.”"],[3141,"“If he bequeaths to the sons of Fulan, the male and the female in it are equal.”"],[3142,"A man came to Shurayh and asked him about a man who bequeathed a share of his wealth. He said, “The obligatory share is calculated, and whatever its allotted portions amount to, the legatee is given a share like one of them.”"],[3143,"“When a man gives charity to some of his inheritors while he is healthy, with more than half, it is returned to one-third. If he gives half, that is permitted for him.” Sa‘īd said, “The judges of the people of Damascus used to rule by that.”"],[3144,"“The shroud is taken from all of the wealth.”"],[3145,"Regarding a man who died and left property worth two thousand dirhams, while he owed the same amount or more, he said, “He is shrouded from it, and his debt is not paid.”"],[3146,"“One begins with the shroud, then the debt, then the bequest.”"],[3147,"Regarding a woman who dies, he said, “She is shrouded from her own wealth; the husband is not responsible for anything.”"],[3148,"“The perfume and the shroud come from the capital.”"],[3149,"“The shroud is taken from the middle of the wealth. He is shrouded according to what he used to wear during his life. Then the debt is paid, then the one-third.”"],[3150,"If a man entrusts a bequest to another man while he is absent, he should accept his bequest. If he is present, he has the choice: if he wishes, he accepts, and if he wishes, he leaves it."],[3151,"I asked al-Ḥasan and Muḥammad about a man who entrusts a bequest to another man. They said, “We prefer that he accept.”"],[3152,"“If a man entrusts a bequest to another man while he is absent, then when he arrives, if he wishes, he accepts. Once he accepts, he may not reject it.”"],[3153,"“If a man entrusts a bequest to another man, and the bequest is presented to him while he was absent, and he accepts, he may not retract.”"],[3154,"\"If a man gives instructions to someone while he is absent and he is dead and unaware, it is binding.\""],[3155,"“If he bequeaths to his slave one-third of his wealth, or one-fourth of his wealth, or one-fifth of his wealth, it is from his wealth and includes emancipation.”"],[3156,"A man may be deprived of the blessing of his wealth during his life, and when death approaches he provides for an act of wickedness."],[3157,"Abdullah al-Murrān: withholding during life and squandering at death. Abu Muhammad said: It is said: bitter in life and bitter at death."],[3158,"If a man bequeaths to another the like of his son's share, he does not receive the like of his share until it is reduced from it."],[3159,"Concerning a man who had three sons and bequeathed to a man the like of the share of one of them if they were four. Al-Sha'bi said: He is given a fifth."],[3160,"We asked 'Amir about a man who left two sons and bequeathed the like of the share of one of them if they were three. He said: He bequeathed a fourth."],[3161,"Concerning a man who bequeathed the like of the share of some of the heirs. He said: It is not permissible, even if it is less than a third."],[3162,"Concerning a man who bequeathed from the produce of his slave a dirham, while his produce is six. He said: He has a sixth of it."],[3163,"If he acknowledges for an heir and for a non-heir one hundred dirhams. He said: I think I should invalidate both of them."],[3164,"An acknowledgment for an heir is not valid."],[3165,"A bequest for an heir is not valid."],[3166,"A man whose kunya is Abu Thabit acknowledged at his death that his wife had against him four hundred dirhams from her dower, and al-Hasan permitted it."],[3167,"I was under the she-camel of the Prophet ﷺ while it was chewing its cud, and its saliva was dripping between my shoulders. I heard him say: Indeed, Allah has given every rightful person his right, so no bequest to an heir is valid."],[3168,"When death approaches one of you, if he leaves good, the bequest to the parents and near relatives (al-Baqarah 180) with what is proper, a duty upon the righteous. He was commanded to bequeath to his parents and near relatives. Then that was abrogated afterwards in Surat al-Nisa, so He appointed for the parents a known share and attached to every inheritor his share from it, and there is no bequest for them. So the bequest became for one who does not inherit, from near relative or otherwise."],[3169,"The property belonged to the children, and the bequest was for the parents and near relatives. Then Allah abrogated of that what He willed, and He appointed for the male the like of the share of two females, and appointed for the parents for each one of them the sixth and the third, and appointed for the wife the eighth and the fourth, and for the husband the half and the fourth."],[3170,"From Ikrimah and al-Hasan: {If he leaves good, the bequest to the parents and near relatives} [al-Baqarah 180]. The bequest was thus until the verse of inheritance abrogated it."],[3171,"About a man who left a will, and he had a wealthy brother. Should he leave a will for him? He said, \"Yes, even if his wealth is twenty thousand (dirhams).\" Then he said, \"And if his wealth is one hundred thousand, surely his richness will not prevent him from giving his brother his rights.\""],[3172,"About a man who said: 'My sword is for so-and-so; and if so-and-so dies, then for so-and-so; and if so-and-so dies, then its return is to me.' They both said: 'It is for the first.' He said: And Humayd b. Abd al-Rahman said: 'It is carried out as he said.'"],[3173,"About the man who gives a man a gift and says: 'It is yours, and when you die, then for so-and-so; and when so-and-so dies, then for so-and-so; and when so-and-so dies, then its return is to me.' He said: 'It is carried out as he said, even if they were a hundred.'"],[3174,"We asked Salim b. Abdullah about a man who bequeaths to others outside his relatives. Salim said: 'It is where he placed it.' He said: We said: 'Al-Hasan says: It is returned to the near relatives.' He rejected that and spoke harshly."],[3175,"If a man bequeaths to his relatives, it is for the closest of them by lineage; the male and female are equal in it."],[3176,"About a man who said: 'One of my two slaves is free,' then died without clarifying. He said: 'The heirs are in his position; they free whichever of them they like.'"],[3177,"That a man said during his illness: 'For so-and-so such-and-such, and for so-and-so such-and-such, and my slave so-and-so is free,' and he did not say: 'If something happens to me,' then he recovered. He said: 'He remains a slave.'"],[3178,"About a man who freed his slave at death and had nothing else and owed a debt. He said: 'He strives for the creditors in his price.'"],[3179,"That a man bought a slave for nine hundred dirhams and freed him, and did not pay the price of the slave, and left nothing. Ali said: 'The slave strives for his price.'"],[3180,"The mudabbar is from the third."],[3181,"The mudabbar (slave manumitted upon the owner's death) is from the third."],[3182,"The one freed after death is from the third."],[3183,"The female slave freed after death and her child are from the third."],[3184,"The one freed after death is from the third."],[3185,"The mudabbar is from the entire wealth."],[3186,"The one freed after death is from the entire wealth."],[3187,"Do not witness a will until it is recited to you, and do not witness for someone you do not know."],[3188,"That Umar b. al-Khattab willed to the mothers of his children four thousand, four thousand for each woman among them."],[3189,"That he permitted the will of a thirteen-year-old boy."],[3190,"A boy from the tribe, seven years old, made a will, and Shurayh said: \"If the boy is correct in his will, it is valid.\""],[3191,"That he witnessed Shurayh permit the will of Abbas b. Ismail b. Marthad for his wet nurse from the people of al-Hirah, while Abbas was a young boy."],[3192,"If the young boy is wary of the well, his will is valid."],[3193,"A boy of theirs when he came of age, called Marthad, bequeathed to a wet nurse of his from the people of al-Ḥīrah forty dirhams, and Shurayḥ permitted it, saying, “Whoever attains the right, we permit it.”"],[3194,"A boy in Madinah was on his deathbed while his heirs were in Syria. They mentioned to ʿUmar that he was dying and asked him to make a will. ʿUmar ordered him to make a will, and he bequeathed a well called Biʾr Jusham. Its owners later sold it for thirty thousand. Abū Bakr mentioned that the boy was ten or twelve years old."],[3195,"A boy’s will concerning his property is permissible up to one-third or less. His guardian may prevent him from that in health out of fear of poverty for him, but at death he may not prevent him."],[3196,"He was brought concerning a slave girl who had made a will, and they kept belittling her, so he said, “Whoever attains the right, we permit it.”"],[3197,"Sulaym al-Ghassānī died at ten or twelve years old and bequeathed a well of his worth thirty thousand, which ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb permitted."],[3198,"His will is not permissible except what is of no consequence."],[3199,"The divorce of a boy, his will, his gift, his charity, and his manumission are not permissible until he reaches puberty."],[3200,"The divorce of a minor boy, his manumission, his will, his purchase, his sale, or anything else are not permissible."],[3201,"Divorce and will are not permissible except with sound mind, except the intoxicated, meaning the drunkard, for his divorce is permissible and his back is beaten."],[3202,"I asked al-Qāsim b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Muʿāwiyah b. Qurrah about a man who said in his will, “Every slave I own is free,” while he had a runaway slave. They both said, “He is free.” Al-Ḥasan, Iyās, and Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh said, “He is not free.”"],[3203,"ʿUmar appointed Ḥafṣah, the Mother of the Believers, as his executrix."],[3204,"Safiyya bequeathed to a Jewish relative of hers."],[3205,"A boy from the tribe called Abbas b. Marthad, seven years old, bequeathed forty dirhams to a Jewish foster mother of his from the people of al-Hira. Shurayh said: “If the boy hits the mark in his bequest, it is valid, and he only bequeathed to one entitled to it.”"],[3206,"Al-Zubayr made his houses a perpetual charity for his sons, not to be sold or inherited, and for the divorced one of his daughters to live in without causing harm or being harmed, so if she is self-sufficient with a husband, she has no right."],[3207,"Regarding a man who bequeaths dinars to another man in the way of Allah, and the beneficiary dies before he takes them out from his family, he said: “They go to the heirs of the deceased testator, to spend them in the way of Allah.”"],[3208,"Regarding a man who bequeaths to a man, and the beneficiary dies before the testator, he said: “It is valid for the heirs of the beneficiary.”"],[3209,"A man came to Ibn Umar and said: A man made a bequest to me and arranged a she-camel in the way of Allah, and this is not a time to go out for battle, so should I carry people on it for Hajj? Ibn Umar said: “Hajj and Umrah are in the way of Allah.”"],[3210,"A man bequeathed his wealth in the way of Allah. The executor asked Umar about that, and he said: “Give it to Allah's workers.” He asked: Who are Allah's workers? He said: “The pilgrims of Allah's House.”"],[3211,"A man who has nothing of the Quran in his interior is like a ruined house."],[3212,"This Quran is Allah's banquet, so take from it what you can. I know nothing more devoid of good than a house in which there is nothing of Allah's Book, and the heart in which there is nothing of Allah's Book is ruined like the ruin of a house with no inhabitant."],[3213,"Learn this Quran, for you will be rewarded for its recitation: for every letter, ten good deeds. Indeed, I do not say that Alif Lam Mim is a letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter, each letter ten good deeds."],[3214,"A house expands for its people, angels attend it, devils abandon it, and its good increases when the Quran is recited in it; and a house constricts for its people, angels abandon it, devils attend it, and its good decreases when the Quran is not recited in it."],[3215,"«If the Quran were placed in a hide and then thrown into the fire, it would not burn.»"],[3216,"I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Recite the Quran, for it is an excellent intercessor on the Day of Resurrection. It will say on the Day of Resurrection: O Lord, adorn him with the adornment of honor, so he will be adorned with the adornment of honor. O Lord, clothe him with the garment of honor, so he will be clothed with the garment of honor. O Lord, crown him with the crown of honor. O Lord, be pleased with him, for there is nothing after Your pleasure."],[3217,"The Quran comes to intercede for its companion, saying: \"O Lord, for every worker there is wages from his work, and indeed I prevented him from pleasure and sleep, so honor him.\" It will be said: \"Extend your right hand and you will be filled with the pleasure of Allah.\" Then it will be said: \"Extend you left hand and you will be filled with the pleasure of Allah.\" And he will be dressed in the garment of generosity, adorned with the adornment of honor, and he will be crowned with the crown of honor."],[3218,"The Quran will intercede for its companion, and he will be clothed with the robe of honor. Then it will say: O Lord, give him more, so he will be crowned with the crown of honor. He said: Then it will say: O Lord, give him more, and give him more. He said: It will say: My pleasure."],[3219,"«Would any of you love, when he goes to his family, to find three fat pregnant she-camels?» They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: «Then three verses that one of you recites are better for him than them.»"],[3220,"Indeed this Quran is the banquet of Allah, so learn from His banquet as much as you can. Indeed this Quran is the rope of Allah, the clear light, and the beneficial healing. It is a protection for whoever clings to it, and salvation for whoever follows it. It does not deviate so as to be corrected, nor does it become crooked so as to be straightened. Its wonders never cease, and it does not wear out from much repetition. So recite it, for Allah will reward you for its recitation: for every letter, ten good deeds. Indeed, I do not say that {Alif Lam Mim} [al-Baqarah 1] is one letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter."],[3221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood one day as a speaker, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, I am only a human being. It is near that the messenger of my Lord will come to me and I will answer him. I am leaving among you the two weighty things. The first of them is the Book of Allah, in which there is guidance and light, so hold fast to the Book of Allah and adhere to it. He urged them regarding it and encouraged them in it. Then he said: «And my household. I remind you of Allah concerning my household,» three times."],[3222,"This path is attended, and the devils attend it, calling out: O servants of Allah, this is the way. So hold fast to the rope of Allah, for the rope of Allah is the Quran."],[3223,"«Indeed the reciter of the Quran and the learner—the angels send blessings upon them until they finish the surah. So when one of you recites a surah, let him delay two verses from it until he finishes it at the end of the day, so that the angels send blessings upon the reciter and the teacher from the beginning of the day to its end.»"],[3224,"He used to say: «Recite the Quran, and do not let these hanging mushafs deceive you, for Allah will never punish a heart that has contained the Quran.»"],[3225,"«Recite the Quran, and do not let these hanging mushafs deceive you, for Allah will not punish a heart that has contained the Quran.»"],[3226,"«There is no educator except that he loves his discipline to be followed, and indeed the discipline of Allah is the Quran.»"],[3227,"«Indeed this Quran is the banquet of Allah, so whoever enters into it is safe.»"],[3228,"Whoever loves the Quran, let him receive glad tidings."],[3229,"\"Whoever loves the Quran, let him rejoice.\""],[3230,"The Quran will come on the Day of Resurrection and intercede for its companion, and it will be a guide for him to Paradise, and it will testify against him, and it will be a driver for him to the Fire."],[3231,"\"Indeed Allah has people from among mankind.\" It was said, \"Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"The people of the Quran.\""],[3232,"On you is the Quran, for it is the understanding of the intellect, the light of wisdom, the springs of knowledge, and the most recent of books, bearing the promise of the Most Merciful. And it was said in the Torah, \"O Muhammad, I have revealed to you a new Torah, in which blind eyes, deaf ears, and sealed hearts will be opened.\""],[3233,"\"Indeed this Quran is a reward for you, and a reminder for you, and a burden upon you. Follow the Quran, and do not let the Quran follow you. For whoever follows the Quran, it will lead him to the gardens of Paradise, and whoever the Quran follows, it will push him from behind and cast him into Hell.\""],[3234,"Ali b. Abi Talib took me by the hand and said, \"If you remain, the Quran will be recited by three groups: a group for Allah, a group for dispute, and a group for worldly gain. And whoever seeks by it, he will attain.\""],[3235,"A man said to Abu al-Darda', \"Your brothers from the people of Kufa, the people of remembrance, send you greetings of peace.\" He said, \"And upon them be peace. Tell them to give the Quran their full attention, for it will carry them to moderation and ease, and keep them away from tyranny and hardship.\""],[3236,"I entered the mosque and found people engaging in talk. I went to Ali and said, \"Do you not see that people are engaging in talk in the mosque?\" He said, \"Have they done that?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'There will be trials.' I said, 'What is the way out of them?' He said, 'The Book of Allah, the Book of Allah. In it is the news of those before you, and the report of those after you, and the judgment of what is between you. It is the decisive criterion, not a jest. It is that which if any tyrant abandons it, Allah will break him, and whoever seeks guidance in other than it, Allah will lead him astray. It is the firm rope of Allah, and it is the wise reminder, and it is the straight path. It is that by which desires do not deviate, and tongues do not become confused, and scholars never have enough of it, and it does not become worn out by much repetition, and its wonders do not cease. It is that which the jinn did not finish hearing before they said, \"Indeed we have heard a wonderful Quran\" [Quran 72:1]. It is that by which whoever speaks it speaks truth, and whoever judges by it is just, and whoever acts upon it is rewarded, and whoever calls to it is guided to a straight path. Take it, O one-eyed.'\""],[3237,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, your community will be tested after you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, or it was asked, \"What is the way out of it?\" He said, \"The Mighty Book, which falsehood cannot come to it from before it or from behind it, a revelation from the Wise, the Praiseworthy [Quran 41:42]. Whoever seeks guidance in other than it, Allah has led him astray. And whoever takes charge of this matter from a tyrant and judges by other than it, Allah will break him. It is the wise reminder, and the clear light, and the straight path. In it is the news of those before you, and the report of those after you, and the judgment of what is between you. It is the decisive criterion, not a jest. It is that which the jinn heard and did not finish before they said, \"Indeed we have heard a wonderful Quran that guides to right conduct\" [Quran 72:1-2]. It does not become worn out by much repetition, and its lessons do not cease, and its wonders do not perish.\" Then Ali said to al-Harith, \"Take it, O one-eyed.\""],[3238,"From Ibrahim regarding {And whoever is given wisdom has been given much good} [Quran 2:269], he said, \"Understanding of the Quran.\""],[3239,"From Mujahid regarding {He gives wisdom to whom He wills} [Quran 2:269], he said, \"The Book; He gives its correct understanding to whom He wills.\""],[3240,"He said to his wife, \"Beware of admitting into my house anyone who drinks wine, since the Quran used to be recited in it every three days.\""],[3241,"\"What prevents any of you, when he returns from his market or from his need and reclines on his bed, from reciting three verses of the Quran?\""],[3242,"The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it."],[3243,"Indeed, the best of you is the one who teaches the Quran or learns it."],[3244,"The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches the Quran."],[3245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no person who learns the Quran and then forgets it, except that he will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection and he will be dumbfounded.\""],[3246,"\"Increase your recitation of the Quran before it is lifted.\" They said, \"[[When] these copies of the Quran are lifted, how will it remain in the hearts of the people?\" He said, \"A night will come when by the morning their hearts will be empty of it. They will [even] forget the statement: There is no god worthy of worship other than Allah. They will return back to the times of ignorance and their poetry. That will be when Word (command of Allah) will take effect.\""],[3247,"\"Fill your hearts with it and fill your houses with it.\" He said: I think he means the Quran."],[3248,"\"Layusryan ala al-Qur'ani that laylatin, wa la yutraku ayatun fi mus-hafin, wa la fi qalbi ahadin illa rufi'at.\" \"He will recite the Quran on a particular night, and not a single verse will be left in a Mus'haf (copy of the Quran) or in the heart of any person except that it will be raised.\""],[3249,"\"No one sits with the Quran and then rises from it except with an increase or a decrease.\" Then he recited: {And We send down of the Quran that which is a healing and a mercy for the believers, but it does not increase the wrongdoers except in loss}."],[3250,"Indeed, Allah intends punishment for the people of the earth, but when He hears the teaching of wisdom to children, He turns that away from them."],[3251,"The Quran will wear out in the chests of some people as a garment wears out, and it will crumble. They will recite it without finding any desire or pleasure in it. They will wear the skins of sheep over the hearts of wolves. Their deeds are greed unmixed with fear. If they fall short, they say, 'We will attain.' If they do wrong, they say, 'We will be forgiven. We do not associate anything with Allah.'"],[3252,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"How bad it is for one of you to say, 'I forgot such-and-such a verse.' Rather, he was made to forget. Keep recalling the Quran, for it is swifter in slipping away from the chests of men than camels from their tethers.\""],[3253,"\"Learn the Book of Allah, keep it in your hearts, recite it melodiously, and acquire it. By the One in whose hand is my soul—or by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad—it is swifter in slipping away than pregnant camels from their tethers.\""],[3254,"\"Learn the Book of Allah, keep it in your hearts, acquire it, and recite it melodiously. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is swifter in slipping away than pregnant camels from their tethers.\""],[3255,"Ikrimah b. Abi Jahl used to place the mushaf on his face and say: \"The Book of my Lord, the Book of my Lord.\""],[3256,"\"Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, when he prayed the morning prayer, would read the mushaf until the sun rose.\" He said: \"And Thabit used to do that.\""],[3257,"Allah does not shy away from striking a similitude even of a gnat or that which is above it. As for those who believe, they know it is the truth from their Lord; and as for those who disbelieve, they say: What does Allah intend by such a similitude? He misleads many by it and guides many by it, and He misleads none by it except the defiantly disobedient. [al-Baqarah 26] He said: i.e., they know that it is the Speech of the Most Merciful."],[3258,"There is no speech greater in the sight of Allah than His speech, and the servants do not refer back to Allah any speech more beloved to Him than His speech."],[3259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to present himself in the season at the standing place to the people, saying: “Is there any man who will carry me to his people? For Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the speech of my Lord.”"],[3260,"Indeed this Quran is the speech of Allah, so let me not find you bending it according to your desires."],[3261,"Whoever is occupied by reciting the Quran from asking Me and remembering Me, I give him the best reward of those who ask. And the excellence of the speech of Allah over all other speech is like the excellence of Allah over His creation."],[3262,"The excellence of the speech of Allah over the speech of His creation is like the excellence of Allah over His creation."],[3263,"The Quran is more beloved to Allah than the heavens and the earth and those within them."],[3264,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Recite the Quran as long as you agree upon it, but when you differ about it, then stand up.”"],[3265,"Recite the Quran as long as your hearts agree upon it, but when you differ about it, then stand up."],[3266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Recite the Quran as long as your hearts agree upon it, but when you differ about it, then stand up.”"],[3267,"Among the people are those who are given faith but not given the Quran, among them are those given the Quran but not given faith, among them are those given the Quran and faith, and among them are those given neither the Quran nor faith.” Then he struck for them a similitude and said: “As for the one given faith but not given the Quran, his example is that of a date: sweet in taste but no fragrance. As for the example of the one given the Quran but not given faith, his example is that of the myrtle: pleasant in fragrance but bitter in taste. As for the one given the Quran and faith, his example is that of the citron: pleasant in fragrance and sweet in taste. And as for the one given neither the Quran nor faith, his example is that of the colocynth: bitter in taste and no fragrance.”"],[3268,"The example of the believer who recites the Quran is that of a citron: its taste is good and its fragrance is good. The example of the believer who does not recite the Quran is that of a date: its taste is sweet but it has no fragrance. The example of the hypocrite who recites the Quran is that of sweet basil: its fragrance is good but its taste is bitter. And the example of the hypocrite who does not recite the Quran is that of the colocynth: it has no fragrance and its taste is bitter."],[3269,"The example of the one who was given faith and was not given the Qur’an is the example of the date-palm: its taste is good and it has no smell. The example of the one who was given the Qur’an and was not given faith is the example of the basil (rayhānah al-āsah): its smell is pleasant and its taste is bitter. The example of the one who was given the Qur’an and faith is the example of the citron (utrujjah): its smell is pleasant and its taste is pleasant. The example of the one who was not given faith nor the Qur’an is the example of the colocynth (ḥanẓalah): its smell is foul and its taste is foul."],[3270,"Nāfiʿ b. ʿAbd al-Ḥārith met ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb at ʿUsfān—and ʿUmar had appointed him over the people of Makkah—so he greeted ʿUmar. ʿUmar said to him, “Whom did you leave as your deputy over the people of the valley?” Nāfiʿ said, “I left Ibn Abzā as deputy over them.” ʿUmar said, “And who is Ibn Abzā?” He said, “A mawlā from among our mawālī.” ʿUmar said, “You left a mawlā as deputy over them?” He said, “O Commander of the Believers, indeed he is a reciter of the Book of Allah, knowledgeable in the obligatory shares (farāʾiḍ).” ʿUmar said, “Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Indeed Allah raises with this Book some peoples and lowers with it others.’”"],[3271,"“Indeed the one who recites the Qur’an has a reward, and the one who listens to it has two rewards.”"],[3272,"“Whoever listens to a verse from the Book of Allah, it will be a light for him.”"],[3273,"“The one who recites the Qur’an and is proficient in it will be with the noble, righteous scribe-angels (al-safarah al-kirām al-bararah). And the one who recites it and finds it difficult for him, he has two rewards.”"],[3274,"“Whoever Allah gave the Qur’an, and he stood with it in the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and acted according to what is in it, and died upon obedience, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the safarah and the aḥkām.” Saʿīd said: “Al-safarah are the angels, and al-aḥkām are the prophets.” He said: “And whoever was eager for it while it slips away from him, and he does not abandon it, he will be given its reward twice. And whoever was eager for it while it slips away from him, and died upon obedience, he is among their nobles, and they were preferred over people as vultures were preferred over the rest of the birds, and as a green meadow was preferred over the surrounding tracts of land. When it is the Day of Resurrection, it will be said: ‘Where are those who used to recite My Book and were not distracted by following livestock?’ Then he will be given eternal life and bliss. And if his parents died upon obedience, a crown of kingship will be placed upon their heads, and they will say: ‘Our Lord, did our deeds reach this?’ He will say: ‘Yes, indeed your son used to recite My Book.’”"],[3275,"“In the Fātiḥah of the Book there is healing from every disease.”"],[3276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me and said: “Did not Allah, Exalted be He, say, {O you who believe, respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you to that which gives you life, and know that Allah intervenes between a man and his heart, and that to Him you will be gathered} [al-Anfāl: 24]?” He said: “Shall I not teach you the greatest sūrah in the Qur’an before I leave the mosque?” When he intended to leave, he said: “Al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi l-ʿālamīn. It is the seven oft-repeated verses and the great Qur’an that you were given.”"],[3277,"“The Fātiḥah of the Book is the seven oft-repeated verses.”"],[3278,"“Nothing like it was sent down in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Qur’an—meaning the Mother of the Qur’an (Umm al-Qur’an). Indeed it is seven of the oft-repeated verses and the great Qur’an which I was given.”"],[3279,"“Al-ḥamdu lillāh is the Mother of the Qur’an, the Mother of the Book, and the seven oft-repeated verses.”"],[3280,"“There is no house in which Sūrat al-Baqarah is recited except that the devil leaves it, and he has a farting sound (ḍarīṭ).”"],[3281,"Surat Al-Baqarah: learning it is a blessing and abandoning it is a regret, and the idle ones cannot master it, and it is the canopy of the Qur'an."],[3282,"Indeed, everything has a peak, and the peak of the Qur'an is Surat Al-Baqarah. And indeed, everything has a pure essence, and the pure essence of the Qur'an is the Mufassal."],[3283,"Whoever recites Surat Al-Baqarah will be crowned with it as a crown in Paradise."],[3284,"Indeed, when Satan hears Surat Al-Baqarah being recited in a house, he leaves it."],[3285,"A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which surah of the Qur'an is greatest?' He said: 'Say: He is Allah, the One.' He said: 'Then which verse in the Qur'an is greatest?' He said: 'The Verse of the Kursi: {Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence.} [Al-Baqarah 255].' He said: 'Then which verse, O Prophet of Allah, do you love to reach you and your nation?' He said: 'The conclusion of Surat Al-Baqarah, for it is from the treasures of Allah's mercy beneath His Throne; He gave it to this nation, and it has not left out any good from the good of this world or the Hereafter except that it encompasses it.'"],[3286,"A man from the companions of Muhammad ﷺ met a man from the Jinn and wrestled him, and the human threw him. The human said to him: 'I see you as small and feeble, as if your two forearms are the forearms of a dog. Is that how all of you Jinn are, or are you alone like that among them?' He said: 'No, by Allah, I am among them robust, but wrestle me a second time; if you throw me, I will teach you something that will benefit you.' So he wrestled him again and threw him. He said: 'Come, teach me.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do you recite {Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence.} [Al-Baqarah 255]?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Indeed, you will not recite it in a house except that Satan leaves it with a sound like the braying of a donkey, and then he will not enter it until morning.'"],[3287,"Whoever recites ten verses from Surat Al-Baqarah in a night, no devil will enter that house that night until morning: four from its beginning, the Verse of the Kursi, two verses after it, and three at its end, the first of which is: {To Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth. And whether you reveal what is within yourselves or conceal it, Allah will bring you to account for it. Then He will forgive whom He wills and punish whom He wills, and Allah is over all things competent.}"],[3288,"Whoever recites four verses from the beginning of Surah Al-Baqarah, Ayat Al-Kursi, two verses after Ayat Al-Kursi, and three verses from the end of Surah Al-Baqarah, Satan will not approach him or his family that day, and nothing will harm him. And it will not be recited over a person who is insane except that he will be cured."],[3289,"I would not think that anyone who has reason would sleep until he recites these verses from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah, for they are from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[3290,"Whoever recites ten verses from Al-Baqarah at his sleep will not forget the Qur'an: four verses from its beginning, the Verse of the Kursi, two verses after it, and three from its end."],[3291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi and the opening of Ha-Mim al-Mumin up to His saying, \"Forgiver of sin and Accepter of repentance, severe in punishment, Possessor of bounty. There is no god except Him; to Him is the destination,\" [Ghafir 40:3], will not see anything he dislikes until evening. And whoever recites it in the evening will not see anything he dislikes until morning.\""],[3292,"Indeed, Allah wrote a Book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, then He sent down from it two verses with which He sealed Surat Al-Baqarah. They are not recited in a house for three nights except that no devil approaches it."],[3293,"Whoever recites the last two verses of Surat Al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him."],[3294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Greatest Name of Allah is contained in these two verses: 'Allah! There is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence' (Surah Al-Baqarah, 2:255) and 'Your god is one God' (Surah Al-Baqarah, 2:163).\""],[3295,"Indeed, Allah sealed Surat Al-Baqarah with two verses that were given to me from His treasure beneath the Throne. So learn them and teach them to your women, for they are a prayer, a Qur'an, and a supplication."],[3296,"I was sitting with the Prophet (pbuh) and I heard him say, \"Learn Surah Al-Baqarah, for its recitation is a blessing, and its abandonment is a source of remorse. It is not easily overcome by falsehood.\" Then he remained silent for a while, and then said, \"Learn Surahs Al-Baqarah and Al-Imran, for they are the two radiant ones and they will shade their companion on the Day of Resurrection, like two clouds, or two gardens, or two flocks of birds spreading their wings. Indeed, the Quran will come to its companion on the Day of Resurrection, when the grave opens up for him, in the form of a pale man, and will say to him, 'Do you recognize me?' He will reply, 'I do not recognize you.' It will then say, 'I am your companion, the Quran, who made you thirsty in the heat and kept you awake at night. Every trader will have behind his merchandise, and today you will have behind every transaction.' The person will then be presented with the kingdom in his right hand, and immortality in his left hand. A crown of honor will be placed on his head, and his parents will be clothed in two garments that the world will not equal. They will say, 'Why have we been dressed in this?' It will be said to them, 'Because of your child's recitation of the Quran.' Then it will be said to him, 'Recite and ascend through the ranks of Paradise and its chambers.' So he will continue to ascend as long as he recites, whether in a measured tone or melodiously.\""],[3297,"Indeed a brother of yours saw in a dream that people were traversing a long rugged mountain pass, and at the top of the mountain were two green trees calling out: Is there any among you who recites Surah al-Baqarah? Is there any among you who recites Surah Al-Imran? When a man said yes, they lowered their branches until he clung to them, and they carried him across the mountain."],[3298,"A man read at the house of Abdullah Al-Baqara and Al-Imran, then he said, \"I have read two surahs in which is the greatest name of Allah. When invoked with it, he answers, and when asked with it, he gives.\""],[3299,"Whoever recites al-Baqarah and Al-Imran, they will come on the Day of Resurrection saying: Our Lord, there is no way against him."],[3300,"Whoever recites Al-Imran is wealthy, and al-Nisa' is adorned."],[3301,"Whoever recites the end of Al-Imran in a night, the standing of a night is written for him."],[3302,"Whoever recites Surah Al-Imran on Friday, the angels will send blessings upon him until nightfall."],[3303,"What a good treasure for the poor is Surah Al-Imran; he stands with it at the end of the night."],[3304,"He sought refuge in the valley of Majannah, a valley where no one walked except that he was afflicted by jinn, and on the edge of the valley were two monks. When evening came, one of them said to his companion: By Allah, the man is doomed. He said: Then he began Surah Al-Imran. They said: He recited a good surah; perhaps he will be saved. He said: And he awoke safe. Abu Muhammad said: Abu al-Salil is Durayb b. Nuqayr, and it is said Ibn Nuqayr."],[3305,"The seven long ones are like the Torah, the hundreds are like the Gospel, the repeated ones are like the Psalms, and the rest of the Quran after that is a merit."],[3306,"Al-An'am is among the required parts of the Quran."],[3307,"The opening of the Torah is al-An'am and its conclusion is Hud."],[3308,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Recite Surah Hud on Friday."],[3309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Recite Surah Hud on Friday."],[3310,"“Whoever recites ten verses from al-Kahf will not be harmed by the Dajjal.”"],[3311,"“Whoever recites the end of Surah al-Kahf at an hour he intends to rise during the night, he will rise at it.” ‘Abdah said, “We tried it and found it to be so.”"],[3312,"\"Whoever recites Surah Al-Kahf on the night of Friday, a light will shine for him from among his own light until the next Friday.\""],[3313,"Recite the delivering one, which is alif lam mim tanzil, for it has reached me that a man used to recite it and nothing else, and he had many sins. It spread its wing over him and said, “Lord, forgive him, for he used to recite me often.” So the Lord made it intercede for him and said, “Write for him a good deed for every sin and raise him a degree.”"],[3314,"“Whoever recites tanzil al-sajdah and tabaraka alladhi bi yadihi al-mulk, seventy good deeds are written for him, seventy sins are removed from him, and he is raised seventy degrees.”"],[3315,"Indeed, alif lam mim tanzil al-kitab, no doubt about it, from the Lord of the worlds, will argue on behalf of its companion in the grave, saying: “O Allah, if I am from Your Book, make me intercede for him; and if I am not from Your Book, erase me from him.” And it becomes like a bird, placing its wing over him, and it intercedes for him and protects him from the punishment of the grave. And in tabaraka alladhi bi yadihi al-mulk there is the like of it. So Khalid did not sleep until he had recited both of them."],[3316,"The Prophet ﷺ “would not sleep until he recited alif lam mim and tabaraka.”"],[3317,"“They were given excellence over every surah in the Quran by sixty good deeds.”"],[3318,"I heard Murrah say, “A man was approached in his grave, and it was approached from the side of his grave. Then a surah of the Quran of thirty verses began to argue on his behalf,” until he said, “So Masruq and I looked and we did not find in the Quran a surah of thirty verses except tabaraka.”"],[3319,"Indeed, Allah, blessed and exalted, recited Taha and Yasin a thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth. When the angels heard the Quran, they said, “Glad tidings to a nation upon whom this is sent down, glad tidings to hearts that carry this, and glad tidings to tongues that speak this.”"],[3320,"“Whoever recites Yasin in a night seeking the countenance of Allah, he will be forgiven.” And he said, “It has reached me that it equals the entire Quran.”"],[3321,"“Indeed, everything has a heart, and the heart of the Quran is Yasin. Whoever recites it, it is as if he recited the Quran ten times.”"],[3322,"“Whoever recites Yasin in a night seeking the countenance of Allah will be forgiven in that night.”"],[3323,"Whoever recites Yā Sīn at the beginning of the day, his needs will be fulfilled."],[3324,"Whoever recites Yā Sīn in the morning is granted ease for his day until evening, and whoever recites it at the beginning of his night is granted ease for his night until morning."],[3325,"\"Whoever recites Surah Ad-Dukhan on the night of Friday with faith and belief in it, shall be forgiven.\""],[3326,"Whoever recites Sūrat Ḥā Mīm on the night of Friday will wake up forgiven, and will be married to the wide-eyed maidens (al-ḥūr al-ʿīn)."],[3327,"The Ḥawāmīm are called the brides."],[3328,"Whoever recites three verses from the end of Sūrat al-Ḥashr in the morning and dies that day is sealed with the seal of the martyrs, and if he recites them in the evening and dies that night is sealed with the seal of the martyrs."],[3329,"He used to recite the Musabbiḥāt at bedtime and said, \"Verily in them is a verse that equals a thousand verses.\""],[3330,"Whoever says in the morning: I seek refuge with Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from the accursed Shayṭān, and recites three verses from the end of Sūrat al-Ḥashr, Allah appoints seventy thousand angels over him to send blessings upon him until evening; and if he says it in the evening, the like of that until morning."],[3331,"A man came to Kufa in the time of Ziyād, and I heard him narrate that he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey of his. He said: My knee touched or grazed his knee, and he heard a man reciting Qul yā ayyuhā al-kāfirūn. He said, \"He is free of shirk.\" And he heard a man reciting Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad. He said, \"He is forgiven.\""],[3332,"What has brought you? He said: I came so that you may teach me something I say at bedtime. He said, \"When you take to your bed, recite Qul yā ayyuhā al-kāfirūn, then sleep upon its conclusion, for it is a disavowal of shirk.\""],[3333,"Indeed, Allah divided the Qur'an into three parts, and He made Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad one third of the Qur'an."],[3334,"Whoever recites Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad ten times, a palace is built for him in Paradise; whoever recites it twenty times, two palaces are built for him in Paradise; and whoever recites it thirty times, three palaces are built for him in Paradise. 'Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, then we will increase our palaces. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah is more expansive than that.\""],[3335,"When he recited a surah and completed it, he would follow it with Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad."],[3336,"Is any of you unable to recite one third of the Qur'an in a night? They said: We are more unable and weaker than that. He said, \"Indeed, Allah divided the Qur'an into three parts, and He made Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad one third of the Qur'an.\""],[3337,"“Say: He is Allah, the One” equals one third of the Quran."],[3338,"“Say: He is Allah, the One” equals one third of the Quran."],[3339,"A man said, “By Allah, I love this surah: ‘Say: He is Allah, the One.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Your love of it will admit you into Paradise.”"],[3340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about “Say: He is Allah, the One,” and he said, “It is one third of the Quran, or it equals it.”"],[3341,"He came to her and said, “Do you not see what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has brought us?” She said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has brought us much good. What is it?” He said, “He said to us: ‘Would one of you be unable to recite one third of the Quran in a night?’” He said, “We feared that he would impose upon us something we could not do, so we did not respond to him at all until he said it three times. Then he said: ‘Is not one of you able to recite: “Say: He is Allah, the One, Allah, the Eternal Refuge”?’”"],[3342,"“Whoever recites ‘Say: He is Allah, the One’ fifty times, Allah forgives his sins of fifty years.”"],[3343,"I clung to the foot of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, teach me Surah Hud and Surah Yusuf.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “O Uqbah, you will never recite a surah of the Quran more beloved to Allah, nor more effective in His sight, than ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.’”"],[3344,"I walked with the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me, “Say, O Uqbah.” I said, “What should I say?” He fell silent for a moment, then said, “O Uqbah, say.” I said, “What should I say?” He said, “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.” So I recited it until I reached its end. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, “No one has ever asked with anything like it, nor has anyone sought refuge with anything like it.”"],[3345,"“There have been revealed to me verses the like of which has never been seen, or the like of which has never been seen.”"],[3346,"“Whoever recites ten verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless.”"],[3347,"“Whoever recites ten verses in a night will be recorded among the devoted worshippers.”"],[3348,"«Whoever recites ten verses will not be recorded among the heedless.»"],[3349,"«Whoever recites ten verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless.»"],[3350,"«Whoever recites fifty verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless.»"],[3351,"«Whoever recites fifty verses in a night will be recorded among the preservers.»"],[3352,"«Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless.»"],[3353,"«Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night will be recorded among the devoutly obedient.»"],[3354,"«Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night will have the devout obedience of a night recorded for him.»"],[3355,"«Whoever recites one hundred verses will be recorded among the devoutly obedient.»"],[3356,"«Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night will be recorded among the devoutly obedient.»"],[3357,"«Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night will be recorded among the devoutly obedient.»"],[3358,"«Whoever recites one hundred verses will not be recorded among the heedless.»"],[3359,"I heard Abu Umamah say: «Whoever recites two hundred verses will be recorded among the devoutly obedient.»"],[3360,"\"Whoever recites two hundred verses in a night will be recorded among the devoutly obedient.\""],[3361,"\"Whoever recites ten verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless, and whoever recites one hundred verses in a night will be recorded among the devoutly obedient, and whoever recites two hundred verses will be recorded among the successful.\""],[3362,"\"Whoever recites ten verses in a night will be recorded among those who remember Allah, and whoever recites one hundred verses will be recorded among the devoutly obedient, and whoever recites five hundred verses up to one thousand will enter the morning with a qintar of reward.\" It was asked, \"And what is the qintar?\" He said, \"A bull's hide filled with gold.\""],[3363,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night, the Quran will not dispute with him that night; and whoever recites two hundred verses in a night, the devotion of a night will be recorded for him; and whoever recites five hundred verses up to one thousand in a night will enter the morning with a qintar in the Hereafter.\" They asked, \"And what is the qintar?\" He said, \"Twelve thousand.\""],[3364,"\"Whoever recites three hundred verses in a night will have a qintar recorded for him, and whoever recites seven hundred verses\" — I do not know what Abu Nu'aym said about it."],[3365,"\"Whoever recites one thousand verses will have a qintar of reward recorded for him, and a qirat of that qintar cannot be matched by your worldly possessions.\""],[3366,"\"Whoever recites one thousand verses in a night will have a qintar recorded for him, and a qirat of the qintar is better than the world and whatever is in it, and he will gain reward as much as Allah wills.\""],[3367,"\"Whoever recites one thousand verses will have a qintar of reward recorded for him, a qirat of which is like a great mountain.\""],[3368,"\"The qintar is twelve thousand.\""],[3369,"\"The qintar is a bull's hide filled with gold.\""],[3370,"\"The qintar is forty thousand.\""],[3371,"\"The qintar is the blood money of one of you: twelve thousand.\""],[3372,"The quintal is seventy thousand dinars."],[3373,"The quintal is one thousand uqiyyahs and two hundred uqiyyahs."],[3374,"The quintal is seventy thousand mithqals."],[3375,"Whoever attends the Quran when it is commenced, it is as if he attended a conquest in the path of Allah, and whoever attends its completion when it is completed, it is as if he attended the spoils when they are distributed."],[3376,"A man used to recite in the mosque of Madinah, and Ibn Abbas had placed someone to watch for him, so when it was the day of his completion, he stood and went over to him."],[3377,"When Anas b. Malik was close to completing the Quran at night, he would leave some of it until morning, then gather his family and complete it with them."],[3378,"When Anas completed the Quran, he gathered his children and the people of his household and supplicated for them."],[3379,"When a man completes the Quran during the day, the angels send blessings upon him until evening, and if he finishes it at night, the angels send blessings upon him until morning."],[3380,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked which deed is best. He said, \"The one who alights and then sets out again.\" It was said, \"And what is the one who alights and then sets out again?\" He said, \"The companion of the Quran who strikes from the beginning of the Quran to its end, and from its end to its beginning; whenever he alights, he sets out again.\""],[3381,"When a man recites the Quran during the day, the angels send blessings upon him until evening, and if he recites it at night, the angels send blessings upon him until morning. Sulayman said, \"I saw our companions like to complete it at the beginning of the day and the beginning of the night.\""],[3382,"Whoever recites the Quran from memory has a supplication in this world or in the Hereafter."],[3383,"“Whoever recites the Quran at night or by day, the angels send blessings upon him until nightfall.” And the other said, “He is forgiven.”"],[3384,"“Whoever recites the Quran and then supplicates, four thousand angels say Amin to his supplication.”"],[3385,"Mujahid sent for me, saying, “We only invited you because we wanted to complete the Quran, and it has reached us that supplication is answered at the completion of the Quran.” He said, “They made supplications.”"],[3386,"“If the completion of the Quran coincides with the beginning of the night, the angels send blessings upon him until morning. If its completion coincides with the end of the night, the angels send blessings upon him until evening. Perhaps one of us would have a portion left, so he would delay it until evening or morning.”"],[3387,"“The bearers of the Quran are the leaders of the people of Paradise.”"],[3388,"\"He used to complete the recitation of the Quran every two nights.\""],[3389,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, in how many days should I complete the Quran?” He said, “Complete it in a month.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I can do more.” He said, “Complete it in twenty-five.” I said, “I can do more.” He said, “Complete it in twenty.” I said, “I can do more.” He said, “Complete it in fifteen.” I said, “I can do more.” He said, “Complete it in ten.” I said, “I can do more.” He said, “Complete it in five.” I said, “I can do more.” He said, “No.”"],[3390,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me not to recite the Quran in less than three days.”"],[3391,"“He is not one of us who does not chant the Quran.”"],[3392,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Which of the people has the best voice for the Quran and the best recitation?” He said, “The one whom, when you hear him recite, you think he fears Allah.”"],[3393,"“Allah has not permitted for anything what He has permitted for a Prophet to chant the Quran.”"],[3394,"“Allah has not permitted for anything as He has permitted for a Prophet to chant the Quran.”"],[3395,"He used to say to Abu Musa, who had a beautiful voice for the Quran, “This one has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud.”"],[3396,"When ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb saw Abū Mūsā, he would say, “Remind us of our Lord, O Abū Mūsā,” and he would recite in his presence."],[3397,"“Let me not find any one of you placing one leg over the other, singing, and neglecting to recite Sūrat al-Baqarah, for Satan flees from a house in which Sūrat al-Baqarah is recited. And the emptiest of houses is the hollow one, empty of the Book of Allah.”"],[3398,"Salamah al-Bayḍaq came to Madinah and stood to lead them in prayer. It was said to Sālim, “If you would come and listen to his recitation.” When he was at the door of the mosque, he heard his recitation and turned back, saying, “Singing, singing.”"],[3399,"Abū Mūsā would come to ʿUmar, and ʿUmar would say to him, “Remind us of our Lord,” and he would recite in his presence."],[3400,"“Allah does not listen attentively to anything as He does to a prophet who chants the Quran, reciting it aloud.”"],[3401,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Abu Musa has indeed been given a flute from the flutes of the family of David.\""],[3402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and heard a man reciting. He said, “Who is this?” It was said, “ʿAbdullāh b. Qays.” He said, “This one has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dāwūd.”"],[3403,"“Adorn the Quran with your voices.”"],[3404,"“Beautify the Quran with your voices, for a beautiful voice increases the Quran in beauty.”"],[3405,"“A man recited in the presence of Anas with one of these melodies, and Anas disliked that.”"],[3406,"“They used to consider these melodies in the Quran to be an innovation.”"]]);
